QData("search/trans-clearai",["In the name of God, the Most Compassionate, the Most Merciful.","All praise belongs to God, Lord of all worlds.","The Most Compassionate, the Most Merciful.","Master of the Day of Judgment.","You alone we worship, and You alone we ask for help.","Guide us to the straight path.","The path of those You have blessed, not those who earned Your wrath, nor those who went astray.","Alif Lam Mim.","This is the Book in which there is no doubt, a guidance for the righteous.","Those who believe in the unseen, establish prayer, and spend from what We have provided them.","And those who believe in what was sent down to you and what was sent down before you, and of the Hereafter they are certain.","Those are upon guidance from their Lord, and those are the successful.","Truly, those who disbelieved—it is the same to them whether you warned them or did not warn them—they will not believe.","God has sealed their hearts and their hearing, and over their eyes is a veil, and for them is a great punishment.","Among people are those who say, “We believe in God and the Last Day,” yet they are not believers.","They try to deceive God and those who believe, but they deceive only themselves, and they do not realize it.","In their hearts is a disease, and God has increased them in disease. For them is a painful punishment because they used to lie.","When they are told, “Do not spread corruption on earth,” they say, “We are only peacemakers.”","Surely it is they who are the corrupters, but they do not realize it.","When they are told, “Believe as the people have believed,” they say, “Should we believe as the fools have believed?” Surely it is they who are the fools, but they do not know.","When they meet those who believe, they say, “We believe.” But when they are alone with their devils, they say, “We are with you; we were only mocking.”","God mocks them and extends them in their transgression, wandering blindly.","Those are the ones who purchased misguidance for guidance, so their trade brought no profit, and they were never guided.","Their example is like one who kindled a fire, and when it lit up what was around him, God took away their light and left them in darkness, unable to see.","Deaf, mute, blind—so they will not return.","Or like a rainstorm from the sky, in which is darkness, thunder, and lightning. They press their fingers into their ears against the thunderbolts in fear of death. And God encompasses the disbelievers.","The lightning nearly snatches their sight. Whenever it flashes for them, they walk in it, and when it darkens over them, they stand still. Had God willed, He could have taken their hearing and their sight. Truly, God is Capable of all things.","O people, worship your Lord, who created you and those before you, so that you may be righteous.","He who made the earth a bed for you and the sky a canopy, and sent down rain from the sky, bringing out fruits as provision for you. So do not set up rivals to God while you know.","If you are in doubt about what We sent down upon Our servant, then produce a chapter like it and call upon your witnesses besides God, if you are truthful.","But if you do not—and you never will—then fear the Fire whose fuel is people and stones, prepared for the disbelievers.","And give good news to those who believe and do good deeds: that they will have gardens beneath which rivers flow. Every time they are provided with fruit from them, they will say, “This is what we were provided before.” They will be given things alike in appearance. They will have purified spouses there, and there they will remain forever.","God is not ashamed to strike a parable of a mosquito or what is above it. As for those who believe, they know it is the truth from their Lord. As for those who disbelieve, they say, “What did God intend by this as a parable?” He leads many astray by it and guides many by it. And He leads astray by it only the defiantly disobedient.","Those who break God’s covenant after it was sealed, and sever what God has commanded to be joined, and spread corruption on earth—those are the losers.","How can you disbelieve in God when you were dead and He gave you life? Then He will cause you to die, then bring you to life, then to Him you will be returned.","It is He who created for you all that is on the earth, then turned to the sky and fashioned it into seven heavens. And He is All-Knowing of all things.","When your Lord said to the angels, “I am placing a successor on the earth,” they said, “Will You place on it one who will spread corruption there and shed blood, while we glorify You with praise and declare Your holiness?” He said, “I know what you do not know.”","He taught Adam the names, all of them, then presented them to the angels and said, “Tell Me the names of these, if you are truthful.”","They said, “Glory be to You! We have no knowledge except what You have taught us. You are the All-Knowing, the All-Wise.”","He said, “O Adam, tell them their names.” And when he told them their names, He said, “Did I not tell you that I know the unseen of the heavens and the earth, and I know what you reveal and what you have been concealing?”","When We said to the angels, “Prostrate before Adam,” they all prostrated except Iblis. He refused and was arrogant, and he was among the disbelievers.","We said, “O Adam, dwell, you and your wife, in the Garden, and eat freely from it wherever you wish, but do not approach this tree, or you will be among the wrongdoers.”","But Satan caused them to slip from it and removed them from what they had been in. We said, “Go down, some of you enemies to others. And on the earth you will have a dwelling place and provision for a time.”","Then Adam received words from his Lord, and He turned to him in mercy. Truly, He is the Ever-Relenting, the Most Merciful.","We said, “Go down from it, all of you. And when guidance comes to you from Me, whoever follows My guidance — no fear will be upon them, nor will they grieve.”","But those who disbelieve and deny Our signs — they are the companions of the Fire. They will abide in it forever.","O Children of Israel, remember My blessing that I bestowed upon you, and fulfill My covenant and I will fulfill your covenant, and Me alone — fear Me.","Believe in what I have sent down, confirming what is with you, and do not be the first to deny it. Do not sell My verses for a petty price, and be mindful of Me alone.","Do not mix truth with falsehood, and do not conceal the truth while you know.","Establish prayer, give charity, and bow with those who bow.","Do you command people to righteousness while forgetting yourselves, even as you recite the Scripture? Will you not reason?","Seek help through patience and prayer. It is truly a burden, except for the humble.","Those who know they will meet their Lord and that to Him they will return.","O Children of Israel, remember My blessing that I bestowed upon you, and that I favored you over all peoples.","And fear a Day when no soul will avail another in the least, no intercession will be accepted from it, no ransom will be taken from it, and they will not be helped.","And when We saved you from Pharaoh’s people, who were inflicting on you the worst torment — slaughtering your sons and sparing your women. In that was a tremendous trial from your Lord.","And when We parted the sea for you, saving you and drowning Pharaoh’s people as you looked on.","And when We appointed for Moses forty nights, then you took the calf after him, and you were wrongdoers.","Then We pardoned you after that, so that you might be grateful.","When We gave Moses the Book and the criterion, so that you might be guided.","When Moses said to his people, “O my people, you have wronged yourselves by taking the calf. So repent to your Maker and kill yourselves. That is better for you with your Maker.” Then He accepted your repentance. Truly, He is the Ever-Accepting, the Most Merciful.","When you said, “O Moses, we will never believe you until we see God openly.” So the thunderbolt struck you while you looked on.","Then We raised you after your death, so that you might be grateful.","We shaded you with clouds and sent down to you manna and quails. “Eat from the good things We have provided you.” They did not wrong Us, but they were wronging themselves.","When We said, “Enter this town and eat freely from it wherever you wish, and enter the gate in prostration, and say, ‘Relieve us,’ and We will forgive your sins. And We will give more to those who do good.”","But those who wronged substituted a word other than what they were told, so We sent down upon those who wronged a plague from the sky for their defiance.","When Moses sought water for his people, We said, “Strike the rock with your staff.” Twelve springs burst from it. Each group knew its drinking place. “Eat and drink from God’s provision, and do not spread corruption in the land.”","When you said, “O Moses, we cannot endure one kind of food, so call upon your Lord to bring out for us what the earth grows — its herbs, its cucumbers, its garlic, its lentils, and its onions.” He said, “Would you exchange what is better for what is lesser? Go down to any town, and you will have what you asked for.” Humiliation and poverty were stamped upon them, and they drew upon themselves wrath from God. That was because they used to reject God’s signs and kill the prophets without right. That was because they disobeyed and kept transgressing.","Surely those who believe, and those who are Jewish, and the Christians, and the Sabians — whoever believed in God and the Last Day and did good — they will have their reward with their Lord. No fear will be upon them, nor will they grieve.","When We took your covenant and raised the mountain above you: “Hold firmly to what We have given you and remember what is in it, so that you might be mindful.”","Then you turned away after that. Were it not for God’s grace upon you and His mercy, you would have been among the losers.","You certainly knew those among you who transgressed regarding the Sabbath. So We said to them, “Be despised apes!”","We made it a deterring example for those present at the time and those after it, and a lesson for the God-conscious.","And when Moses said to his people, “God commands you to slaughter a cow.” They said, “Are you mocking us?” He said, “I seek refuge in God from being among the ignorant.”","They said, “Call upon your Lord for us to make clear to us what she is.” He said, “He says she is a cow neither old nor young, but middle-aged between that. So do what you are commanded.”","They said, “Call upon your Lord for us to make clear to us what her color is.” He said, “He says she is a bright yellow cow, vivid in color, pleasing to those who see her.”","They said, “Call upon your Lord for us to make clear to us what she is. The cows all look alike to us, and if God wills, we will surely be guided.”","He said, “He says she is a cow not broken to plow the earth nor to water the fields — unblemished, with no marking on her.” They said, “Now you have brought the truth.” So they slaughtered her, though they nearly did not.","And when you killed a man and disputed over it, but God was to bring out what you were concealing.","So We said, “Strike him with a piece of her.” Thus God brings the dead to life and shows you His signs, so that you may understand.","Then your hearts hardened after that, and they became like stones or even harder. For surely among stones are those from which rivers burst. And surely among them are those that split open and water flows from them. And surely among them are those that fall down in awe of God. And God is not unaware of what you do.","Do you hope that they will believe you, when a group of them used to hear God’s words then distort them after they had understood them, knowingly?","When they meet those who believe, they say, “We believe.” But when they are alone with one another, they say, “Do you tell them what God has revealed to you, so they can argue against you with it before your Lord? Do you not understand?”","Do they not know that God knows what they conceal and what they declare?","Among them are the unlettered who know nothing of the Scripture but wishful thinking, and they do nothing but speculate.","So woe to those who write the Scripture with their own hands then say, “This is from God,” to trade it for a small price. Woe to them for what their hands have written, and woe to them for what they earn.","They say, “The Fire will not touch us except for a few days.” Say, “Have you taken a covenant with God — for God never breaks His covenant — or do you say about God what you do not know?”","Yes — whoever earns evil and is engulfed by his sin, those are the companions of the Fire; they will remain in it forever.","Those who believe and do good deeds, those are the companions of the Garden; they will remain in it forever.","When We took the covenant of the Children of Israel: “You will worship none but God, and be good to your parents, to relatives, to orphans, and to the needy. Speak kindly to people, establish prayer, and give charity.” Then you turned away, except a few of you, and you were resistant.","When We took your covenant: “You will not shed your own blood, nor expel your own people from your homes.” Then you affirmed it, and you were witnesses.","Yet here you are, killing your own people, expelling a group of you from their homes, conspiring against them in sin and aggression. And if they come to you as captives, you ransom them — though their very expulsion was forbidden to you. Do you believe in part of the Scripture and reject the rest? The recompense for those among you who do that is nothing but disgrace in this life, and on the Day of Resurrection they will be driven to the harshest punishment. God is not unaware of what you do.","Those are the ones who purchased this life at the cost of the Hereafter. Their punishment will not be lightened, nor will they be helped.","Truly We gave Moses the Scripture and followed him with messengers after him. We gave Jesus son of Mary clear proofs and strengthened him with the Holy Spirit. Is it that whenever a messenger came to you with what your souls did not desire, you grew arrogant? Some you denied, and some you killed?","They said, “Our hearts are wrapped.” No, God has cursed them for their disbelief, so little do they believe.","When a Book came to them from God, confirming what was with them — and they used to pray for victory over the disbelievers before — yet when what they recognized came to them, they disbelieved in it. So God’s curse is upon the disbelievers.","Wretched is what they sold their souls for — disbelieving in what God sent down, out of envy that God would send down His grace upon whomever He wills of His servants. So they brought upon themselves wrath upon wrath. And for the disbelievers is a humiliating punishment.","When they are told, “Believe in what God has sent down,” they say, “We believe in what was sent down to us,” and they disbelieve in what came after it, though it is the truth confirming what is with them. Say, “Then why did you kill God’s prophets before, if you were believers?”","Certainly Moses came to you with clear proofs, then you took the calf after him, and you were wrongdoers.","And when We took your covenant and raised the mountain above you: “Hold firmly to what We have given you and listen.” They said, “We hear and we disobey.” And the calf was made to soak into their hearts because of their disbelief. Say, “Wretched is what your faith commands you, if you are believers.”","Say, “If the Home of the Hereafter with God is yours alone, excluding all other people, then wish for death, if you are truthful.”","But they will never wish for it, because of what their hands have sent ahead. And God is All-Knowing of the wrongdoers.","You will surely find them the most greedy of all people for life — even more than the polytheists. Each one of them wishes he could live a thousand years, yet being granted long life would not remove him from the punishment. And God is All-Seeing of what they do.","Say, “Whoever is an enemy of Gabriel — it is he who brought it down upon your heart by God’s permission, confirming what came before it, and as guidance and glad tidings for the believers.”","Whoever is an enemy of God, His angels, His messengers, Gabriel, and Michael — then truly God is an enemy of the disbelievers.","We have sent down to you clear verses, and none disbelieve in them except the defiantly disobedient.","Is it not that every time they made a covenant, a group among them cast it aside? Rather, most of them do not believe.","When a messenger from God came to them confirming what they had, a group of those who were given the Scripture threw God’s Book behind their backs as though they did not know.","They followed what the devils recited over Solomon’s kingdom. Solomon did not disbelieve, but the devils disbelieved, teaching people sorcery and what was sent down to the two angels in Babylon, Harut and Marut. Yet those two would not teach anyone without saying, “We are only a trial, so do not disbelieve.” Still, they learned from them what separates a man from his wife. But they could not harm anyone with it except by God’s permission. They learned what harmed them and did not benefit them. They certainly knew that whoever purchased it would have no share in the Hereafter. How wretched is what they sold their souls for—if only they knew.","Had they believed and been mindful, a reward from God would have been far better—if only they knew.","O you who believe, do not say “Attend to us” but say “Look upon us,” and listen. For the disbelievers there is a painful punishment.","Neither the disbelievers among the People of the Scripture nor the polytheists wish that any good be sent down to you from your Lord. But God singles out with His mercy whom He wills, and God is the Possessor of immense grace.","Whatever verse We abrogate or cause to be forgotten, We bring one better than it or equal to it. Do you not know that God is Capable of all things?","Do you not know that to God belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth, and that you have no protector or helper besides God?","Or do you wish to question your Messenger as Moses was questioned before? Whoever exchanges faith for disbelief has truly strayed from the right path.","Many of the People of the Scripture wish they could turn you back to disbelief after your faith, out of envy from within themselves, even after the truth has become clear to them. So pardon and overlook until God brings His command. Truly, God is Capable of all things.","Establish the prayer and give the charity. Whatever good you send ahead for yourselves, you will find it with God. Surely God is All-Seeing of what you do.","They said, “No one will enter Paradise except those who are Jews or Christians.” Those are their wishful thoughts. Say, “Produce your proof, if you are truthful.”","Rather, whoever submits his face to God while being a doer of good will have his reward with his Lord. No fear will be upon them, nor will they grieve.","The Jews said, “The Christians stand on nothing,” and the Christians said, “The Jews stand on nothing,” yet they both recite the Scripture. So too, those who have no knowledge said the same as their words. God will judge between them on the Day of Resurrection regarding what they used to differ over.","Who is more unjust than one who prevents God’s houses of worship from having His name remembered in them and strives for their ruin? Those should not have entered them except in fear. For them in this world is disgrace, and for them in the Hereafter is a tremendous punishment.","To God belong the East and the West. Wherever you turn, there is God’s face. Truly, God is All-Encompassing, All-Knowing.","They said, “God has taken a son.” Glory be to Him! Rather, to Him belongs whatever is in the heavens and the earth. All are devoutly obedient to Him.","Originator of the heavens and the earth — when He decrees a matter, He only says to it, “Be,” and it is.","Those who have no knowledge said, “Why does God not speak to us, or a sign come to us?” So too, those before them said the same as their words. Their hearts are alike. We have made the signs clear for a people who are certain.","We have sent you with the truth, as a bearer of good news and a warner, and you will not be asked about the companions of the Blaze.","The Jews will never be pleased with you, nor the Christians, until you follow their creed. Say, “God’s guidance is the true guidance.” If you were to follow their desires after the knowledge that has come to you, you would have no protector or helper against God.","Those to whom We gave the Scripture recite it as it should be recited — those truly believe in it. And whoever disbelieves in it — those are the losers.","O Children of Israel, remember My favor that I bestowed upon you, and that I preferred you over all peoples.","Fear a Day when no soul will avail another in the least, nor will any ransom be accepted from it, nor will any intercession benefit it, nor will they be helped.","When his Lord tested Abraham with certain words and he fulfilled them, He said, “I am making you a leader for mankind.” He said, “And from my descendants?” He said, “My covenant does not extend to the wrongdoers.”","When We made the House a place of return for mankind and a sanctuary — take the station of Abraham as a place of prayer — and We charged Abraham and Ishmael: “Purify My House for those who circle it, those who devote themselves there, and those who bow and prostrate.”","When Abraham said, “My Lord, make this a secure land and provide its people with fruits — those of them who believe in God and the Last Day.” He said, “And whoever disbelieves, I will grant him enjoyment for a little while, then I will drive him to the punishment of the Fire — and what a wretched destination!”","As Abraham was raising the foundations of the House, along with Ishmael: “Our Lord, accept this from us. You are the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.","Our Lord, make us both submissive to You, and from our descendants a community submissive to You. Show us our rites and turn to us in mercy. You are the Ever-Relenting, the Most Merciful.","Our Lord, send among them a messenger from themselves who will recite to them Your verses, teach them the Book and wisdom, and purify them. You are the All-Mighty, the All-Wise.”","Who would turn away from the creed of Abraham except one who debases himself? We chose him in this world, and in the Hereafter he is surely among the righteous.","When his Lord said to him, “Submit,” he said, “I have submitted to the Lord of all worlds.”","Abraham charged his sons with this, as did Jacob: “O my sons, God has chosen this religion for you, so do not die except as those who have submitted.”","Were you witnesses when death came to Jacob, when he said to his sons, “What will you worship after me?” They said, “We will worship your God and the God of your fathers — Abraham, Ishmael, and Isaac — one God, and to Him we submit.”","That was a community that has passed away. To them is what they earned, and to you is what you have earned, and you will not be asked about what they used to do.","They said, “Be Jews or Christians, and you will be guided.” Say, “Rather, the creed of Abraham, a monotheist, and he was not of those who associate others with God.”","Say, “We believe in God and what was sent down to us, and what was sent down to Abraham, Ishmael, Isaac, Jacob, and the tribes, and what Moses and Jesus were given, and what the prophets were given from their Lord. We make no distinction between any of them, and to Him we submit.”","So if they believe in the like of what you believe in, they are guided. But if they turn away, they are only in opposition. God will suffice you against them. He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.","The coloring of God! And who is better than God in coloring? And we are worshippers of Him.","Say, “Do you argue with us about God, when He is our Lord and your Lord? To us are our deeds and to you are your deeds, and we are devoted to Him alone.”","Or do you say that Abraham, Ishmael, Isaac, Jacob, and the tribes were Jews or Christians? Say, “Are you more knowing, or is God?” And who is more unjust than one who conceals a testimony he has from God? God is not unaware of what you do.","That was a community that has passed away. To it belongs what it earned, and to you belongs what you earned. You will not be asked about what they used to do.","The foolish among people will say, “What turned them away from the direction they used to face?” Say, “To God belong the east and the west. He guides whom He wills to a straight path.”","And so We made you a middle community, that you may be witnesses over humanity, and the Messenger may be a witness over you. We did not appoint the direction you used to face except to distinguish those who follow the Messenger from those who turn back on their heels. It was indeed a great trial, except for those whom God guided. God would never let your faith go to waste. Truly, God is Compassionate and Merciful toward people.","We see the turning of your face toward the sky. So We will turn you toward a direction that pleases you. Turn your face toward the Sacred Mosque. Wherever you are, turn your faces toward it. Those who were given the Scripture certainly know that it is the truth from their Lord. God is not unaware of what they do.","Even if you brought those who were given the Scripture every verse, they would not follow your direction. You are not a follower of their direction, nor are they followers of one another’s direction. If you were to follow their desires after the knowledge that has come to you, then you would surely be among the wrongdoers.","Those to whom We gave the Scripture recognize him as they recognize their own sons. Yet a group of them knowingly conceal the truth.","The truth is from your Lord, so never be among the doubters.","Each has a direction to which he turns. So race toward good deeds. Wherever you may be, God will bring you all together. Truly, God is Capable of all things.","From wherever you set out, turn your face toward the Sacred Mosque. It is certainly the truth from your Lord. And God is not unaware of what you do.","From wherever you set out, turn your face toward the Sacred Mosque. And wherever you may be, turn your faces toward it, so that people will have no argument against you — except those among them who do wrong — so do not fear them, but fear Me, and so that I may complete My favor upon you, and that you may be guided.","Just as We sent among you a messenger from among you, reciting Our verses to you, purifying you, teaching you the Scripture and wisdom, and teaching you what you did not know.","So remember Me, and I will remember you. Be grateful to Me and do not deny Me.","O you who believe, seek help through patience and prayer. Surely, God is with the patient.","Do not say of those who are killed in God’s cause that they are dead. Rather, they are alive, but you do not perceive it.","We will surely test you with something of fear, hunger, and loss of wealth, lives, and crops. So give good news to the patient.","Those who, when calamity strikes them, say, “Truly, we belong to God, and to Him we return.”","Upon them are blessings from their Lord, and mercy. Those are the rightly guided.","Truly, Safa and Marwa are among God’s rites. So whoever makes pilgrimage to the House or performs the lesser visit, there is no blame on him in walking between them. And whoever volunteers good, God is Appreciative, All-Knowing.","Those who conceal what We sent down of clear proofs and guidance after We made it clear to people in the Book—God curses them, and the cursers curse them.","Except those who repented, reformed, and made clear—those I will accept in repentance. I am the Ever-Accepting, the Most Merciful.","Those who disbelieved and died as disbelievers—upon them is the curse of God, the angels, and all of mankind.","Abiding in it forever. The punishment will not be lightened for them, nor will they be reprieved.","Your God is one God. There is no god but Him, the Most Compassionate, the Most Merciful.","Truly, in the creation of the heavens and the earth, the alternation of night and day, the ships that sail the sea with what benefits people, the water God sent down from the sky—reviving the earth after its death and spreading in it every kind of creature—the shifting of the winds, and the clouds pressed into service between the sky and the earth, are signs for people who reason.","Yet among people are those who take rivals besides God, loving them as they love God. But those who believe are stronger in their love for God. If only the wrongdoers could see—when they see the punishment—that all power belongs to God, and that God is severe in punishment.","When those who were followed disowned those who followed them, and they saw the punishment, and all ties between them were severed.","Those who followed said, “If only we could have another turn, so we could disown them as they disowned us.” Thus God shows them their deeds as anguish upon them, and they will never leave the Fire.","O people, eat from what is on the earth, lawful and good, and do not follow the footsteps of Satan. He is truly a clear enemy to you.","He only commands you to evil and indecency, and to say about God what you do not know.","When they are told, “Follow what God has sent down,” they say, “No, we follow what we found our fathers upon.” Even if their fathers understood nothing and were not guided?","The example of those who disbelieve is like one who calls out to what hears nothing but cries and shouts. Deaf, mute, blind — they do not understand.","O you who believe, eat from the good things We have provided you and give thanks to God, if it is Him you worship.","He has only forbidden you carrion, blood, the flesh of swine, and what has been offered to other than God. But whoever is compelled, neither craving nor transgressing, no sin falls upon him. Truly, God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","Those who conceal what God has sent down of the Book and sell it for a small price — they fill their bellies with nothing but Fire. God will not speak to them on the Day of Resurrection, nor will He purify them, and for them is a painful punishment.","Those are the ones who purchased misguidance in exchange for guidance, and punishment in exchange for forgiveness. How patient they are for the Fire!","That is because God sent down the Book with the truth. And those who differ over the Book are in extreme discord.","Righteousness is not that you turn your faces toward the east or the west, but righteous is he who believes in God, the Last Day, the angels, the Book, and the prophets; and gives wealth despite his love for it to relatives, orphans, the needy, the traveler, those who ask, and for freeing slaves; and establishes prayer and gives charity; and those who fulfill their covenant when they make one; and the patient in hardship, adversity, and in the heat of battle. Those are the ones who are truthful, and those are the righteous.","O you who believe, retribution is prescribed for you in cases of killing: the free for the free, the slave for the slave, the female for the female. But whoever is pardoned anything by his brother, let there be adherence to what is fair and payment to him with good grace. That is a relief from your Lord and a mercy. Whoever transgresses after that — for him is a painful punishment.","In retribution there is life for you, O people of understanding, so that you may be mindful.","Prescribed for you, when death approaches any of you and he leaves wealth behind, is the bequest to parents and close relatives in a fair manner — a duty upon the righteous.","Whoever alters it after hearing it, the sin falls only upon those who alter it. Surely, God is All-Hearing, All-Knowing.","But whoever fears bias or sin from a testator and reconciles between them, no sin falls upon him. Truly, God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","O you who believe, fasting has been prescribed for you as it was prescribed for those before you, so that you may become God-conscious.","For a counted number of days. Whoever among you is ill or on a journey, then an equal number of other days. And for those who can barely endure it, a compensation: the feeding of a needy person. Whoever volunteers more good, it is better for him. And that you fast is better for you, if only you knew.","The month of Ramadan in which the Quran was sent down as guidance for people and as clear proofs of guidance and the criterion. So whoever among you witnesses the month, let him fast it. And whoever is ill or on a journey, then an equal number of other days. God intends ease for you and does not intend hardship for you, and so that you may complete the number and glorify God for having guided you, and so that you may be grateful.","When My servants ask you about Me, I am near. I answer the call of the caller when he calls upon Me. So let them respond to Me and believe in Me, that they may be rightly guided.","Permitted for you on the night of the fast is intimacy with your wives. They are a garment for you and you are a garment for them. God knew that you were betraying yourselves, so He turned to you and pardoned you. So now lie with them and seek what God has written for you. And eat and drink until the white thread becomes distinct to you from the black thread of dawn. Then complete the fast until nightfall. And do not lie with them while you are in retreat in the mosques. These are God’s limits, so do not go near them. Thus does God make His verses clear to people, so that they may become God-conscious.","Do not consume one another’s wealth unjustly, nor offer it to judges so that you may consume a portion of people’s wealth through sin while you know.","They ask you about the crescents. Say, “They are time-markers for people and for the pilgrimage.” Righteousness is not that you enter houses from their backs, but righteousness is in whoever is God-conscious. Enter houses from their doors, and be mindful of God so that you may succeed.","Fight in God’s cause those who fight you, but do not transgress. Truly, God does not love the transgressors.","Kill them wherever you find them and drive them out from where they drove you out. Persecution is worse than killing. Do not fight them at the Sacred Mosque unless they fight you there. But if they fight you, then kill them. Such is the recompense of the disbelievers.","But if they cease, then God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","Fight them until there is no more persecution and religion belongs to God. But if they cease, then there is no hostility except against the wrongdoers.","The sacred month for the sacred month, and all sanctities are subject to retaliation. Whoever transgresses against you, transgress against him in the same measure. Be mindful of God, and know that God is with the God-conscious.","Spend in God’s cause and do not throw yourselves with your own hands into destruction. Do good, for God loves those who do good.","Complete the pilgrimage and the lesser pilgrimage for God. But if you are prevented, then whatever offering is easy to obtain. And do not shave your heads until the offering reaches its place of sacrifice. Whoever among you is ill or has an ailment of the head, then a ransom of fasting, charity, or ritual sacrifice. When you are secure, whoever enjoys the lesser pilgrimage leading up to the pilgrimage, then whatever offering is easy to obtain. Whoever cannot find one, then a fast of three days during the pilgrimage and seven when you return — that is ten in full. That is for those whose families are not present at the Sacred Mosque. Be mindful of God, and know that God is severe in punishment.","The pilgrimage is in appointed months. Whoever undertakes the pilgrimage in them — then no sexual talk, no wickedness, and no quarreling during the pilgrimage. Whatever good you do, God knows it. And take provision, for surely the best provision is righteousness. So be mindful of Me, O people of understanding.","There is no blame on you for seeking bounty from your Lord. When you pour down from Arafat, remember God at the Sacred Monument. Remember Him as He guided you, though before that you were among the astray.","Then pour down from where the people pour down, and seek God’s forgiveness. Truly, God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","When you have completed your rites, remember God as you remember your fathers — or with even greater remembrance. Among the people are those who say, “Our Lord, give us in this world,” and they have no share in the Hereafter.","And among them are those who say, “Our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire.”","Those will have a share of what they earned. And God is swift in reckoning.","Remember God during the appointed days. Whoever hurries in two days, there is no sin on him, and whoever stays longer, there is no sin on him — for the one who is mindful. Be mindful of God, and know that to Him you will be gathered.","Among the people is one whose speech impresses you in the life of this world, and he calls God to witness what is in his heart, yet he is the fiercest of opponents.","When he turns away, he strives through the land to spread corruption in it and destroy crops and livestock. And God does not love corruption.","When he is told, “Fear God,” pride in sin seizes him. Hell is enough for him — and what a wretched resting place!","And among the people is one who sells his own self seeking God’s pleasure. And God is Compassionate to His servants.","O you who believe, enter into peace wholly, and do not follow the footsteps of Satan. He is a clear enemy to you.","If you slip after the clear proofs have come to you, then know that God is All-Mighty, All-Wise.","Are they waiting for nothing but that God should come to them in canopies of cloud, and the angels, and the matter is settled? To God all matters are returned.","Ask the Children of Israel how many clear signs We gave them. Whoever alters God’s blessing after it has come to him — truly God is severe in punishment.","The life of this world has been made alluring to those who disbelieve, and they mock those who believe. But the God-conscious will be above them on the Day of Resurrection. God provides for whoever He wills without measure.","Humanity was one community, so God sent the prophets as bearers of good news and as warners, and He sent down with them the Book in truth to judge between people in what they disagreed over. Yet none disagreed over it except those who were given it, after the clear proofs had come to them, out of rivalry among themselves. So God guided those who believed to the truth of what they had disagreed over, by His permission. God guides whoever He wills to a straight path.","Do you think you will enter Paradise without having faced what those before you faced? They were struck by hardship and adversity and were shaken until the messenger and those who believed with him said, “When will God’s help come?” Truly, God’s help is near.","They ask you what they should spend. Say, “Whatever good you spend should be for parents, relatives, orphans, the needy, and the traveler.” Whatever good you do, God is All-Knowing of it.","Fighting is prescribed for you, though you dislike it. Yet you may dislike something that is good for you, and you may love something that is bad for you. God knows, and you do not know.","They ask you about the sacred month—fighting in it. Say, “Fighting in it is grave, but blocking the way to God, denying Him, barring access to the Sacred Mosque, and driving its people out are graver in God’s sight. Persecution is graver than killing.” They will not stop fighting you until they turn you back from your religion, if they can. Whoever among you turns back from his religion and dies as a disbeliever—those are the ones whose deeds are nullified in this world and the Hereafter. Those are the companions of the Fire; they will remain in it forever.","Surely those who believed, and those who emigrated and strove in God’s cause—those hope for God’s mercy. God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","They ask you about wine and gambling. Say, “In both there is great sin and some benefit for people, but their sin is greater than their benefit.” They ask you what they should spend. Say, “The surplus.” This is how God makes the verses clear to you, so that you may reflect.","On this world and the Hereafter. They ask you about orphans. Say, “Setting their affairs right is best. And if you mix your affairs with theirs, they are your brothers.” God knows the corrupter from the reformer. Had God willed, He could have made things difficult for you. Truly, God is All-Mighty, All-Wise.","Do not marry polytheist women until they believe. A believing slave woman is better than a polytheist woman, even if she pleases you. And do not give your women in marriage to polytheist men until they believe. A believing slave man is better than a polytheist man, even if he pleases you. Those invite to the Fire, while God invites to Paradise and forgiveness by His permission. He makes His verses clear to people so that they may remember.","They ask you about menstruation. Say, “It is a harm, so keep away from women during menstruation and do not approach them until they are clean. Then when they have purified themselves, come to them from where God has commanded you. Truly, God loves those who repent and loves those who purify themselves.”","Your women are a tillage for you, so come to your tillage however you wish. Send ahead for yourselves, be mindful of God, and know that you will meet Him. Give glad tidings to the believers.","Do not make God an excuse in your oaths against doing good, being mindful, and making peace between people. God is All-Hearing, All-Knowing.","God does not hold you accountable for idle talk in your oaths, but He holds you accountable for what your hearts have earned. God is All-Forgiving, All-Forbearing.","For those who swear to abstain from their wives, there is a waiting period of four months. If they return, then God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","But if they resolve on divorce, then God is All-Hearing, All-Knowing.","Divorced women wait by themselves for three cycles. It is not lawful for them to conceal what God has created in their wombs, if they believe in God and the Last Day. Their husbands have more right to take them back during that period, if they desire reconciliation. They have rights similar to what is expected of them, according to what is fair. Yet men have a degree over them. God is All-Mighty, All-Wise.","Divorce is twice — then either retention with fairness or release with kindness. It is not lawful for you to take back anything of what you have given them, unless both fear that they cannot maintain God’s limits. If you fear that they cannot maintain God’s limits, there is no blame on either of them for what she gives back. These are God’s limits, so do not transgress them. Whoever transgresses God’s limits — those are the wrongdoers.","If he divorces her, she is not lawful to him after that until she marries another husband. If he then divorces her, there is no blame on either of them for returning to each other, provided they believe they can uphold God’s limits. These are God’s limits, which He makes clear to a people who know.","When you divorce women and they reach the end of their waiting period, either retain them in kindness or release them in kindness. Do not retain them to cause harm and transgress. Whoever does that has wronged himself. Do not take God’s verses in mockery. Remember God’s blessing upon you and what He sent down to you of the Book and wisdom, admonishing you through it. Be mindful of God, and know that God is All-Knowing of everything.","When you divorce women and they reach the end of their waiting period, do not prevent them from marrying their husbands if they agree among themselves in kindness. This is an admonition for whoever among you believes in God and the Last Day. That is more wholesome for you and more pure. God knows, and you do not know.","Mothers nurse their children for two full years, for those who wish to complete the nursing. The father is responsible for their provision and clothing in kindness. No soul is burdened beyond its capacity. No mother is harmed on account of her child, nor is a father on account of his child. The same obligation falls on the heir. If both parents wish to wean by mutual consent and consultation, there is no blame on them. And if you wish to have your children nursed by others, there is no blame on you provided you hand over what you have given in kindness. Be mindful of God, and know that God is All-Seeing of what you do.","Those among you who die and leave wives behind — their wives wait by themselves for four months and ten days. When they reach the end of their waiting period, there is no blame on you for what they do with themselves in kindness. God is All-Aware of what you do.","There is no blame on you for what you hint at in proposing to women, or for what you conceal in your hearts. God knows that you will think of them, but do not make secret promises to them except to speak in kindness. Do not resolve on the marriage tie until the prescribed period reaches its end. Know that God knows what is in your hearts, so beware of Him. And know that God is All-Forgiving, All-Forbearing.","There is no blame on you if you divorce women before you have touched them or set a dowry for them. But provide for them — the wealthy according to his means and the poor according to his means — a fair provision. This is a duty upon the good-doers.","If you divorce them before you have touched them but after you have set a dowry for them, then half of what you set is due — unless they waive it or the one in whose hand is the marriage tie waives it. That you waive is closer to righteousness. And do not forget generosity between you. Truly God is All-Seeing of what you do.","Guard your prayers, especially the middle prayer, and stand before God in devout obedience.","If you are in fear, then on foot or riding. But when you are secure, remember God as He taught you what you did not know.","Those of you who die and leave wives behind — a bequest for their wives: provision for a year without being expelled. But if they leave of their own accord, there is no blame on you for what they do with themselves in a fair manner. God is All-Mighty, All-Wise.","Divorced women are entitled to fair provision — a duty upon the righteous.","Thus God makes His verses clear to you, so that you may understand.","Have you not seen those who fled their homes in their thousands, fearing death? God said to them, “Die!” Then He brought them back to life. Surely God is full of grace toward people, but most people are not grateful.","Fight in God’s cause, and know that God is All-Hearing, All-Knowing.","Who will lend God a good loan, that He may multiply it for him many times over? God withholds and extends, and to Him you will be returned.","Have you not seen the chiefs of the Children of Israel after Moses, when they said to a prophet of theirs, “Appoint a king for us so we may fight in God’s cause”? He said, “Is it possible that, if fighting is prescribed for you, you will not fight?” They said, “Why would we not fight in God’s cause when we have been driven from our homes and our children?” Yet when fighting was prescribed for them, they turned away — all but a few of them. God is All-Knowing of the wrongdoers.","Their prophet said to them, “God has appointed Saul as king over you.” They said, “How can he have kingship over us when we have more right to kingship than him, and he has not been given abundance of wealth?” He said, “God has chosen him over you and increased him abundantly in knowledge and stature. God grants His kingship to whom He wills. God is All-Encompassing, All-Knowing.”","Their prophet said to them, “The sign of his kingship is that the Ark will come to you, in which is tranquility from your Lord and relics of what the family of Moses and the family of Aaron left behind, borne by the angels. Surely in that is a sign for you, if you are believers.”","When Saul set out with the troops, he said, “God will test you with a river. Whoever drinks from it is not of me, and whoever does not taste it is of me — except one who scoops a handful with his hand.” They drank from it, all but a few of them. And when he and those who believed with him crossed it, they said, “We have no strength today against Goliath and his troops.” Those who were certain they would meet God said, “How many a small force has defeated a large force by God’s permission! And God is with the steadfast.”","When they faced Goliath and his troops, they said, “Our Lord, pour patience upon us, steady our feet, and grant us victory over the disbelieving people.”","So they defeated them by God’s permission, and David killed Goliath. God gave him kingship and wisdom and taught him what He willed. Were it not for God driving people back, some by means of others, the earth would have been corrupted. But God is full of grace to all the worlds.","These are God’s verses. We recite them to you in truth, and you are truly among the messengers.","Those messengers — We favored some of them over others. Among them were those to whom God spoke, and He raised some of them in degrees. We gave Jesus son of Mary the clear proofs and supported him with the Holy Spirit. Had God willed, those who came after them would not have fought one another after the clear proofs had come to them. But they differed — some of them believed and some of them disbelieved. Had God willed, they would not have fought one another, but God does what He wills.","O you who believe, spend from what We have provided you before a Day comes in which there is no bargaining, no friendship, and no intercession. And the disbelievers — they are the wrongdoers.","God—there is no god but He, the Ever-Living, the Self-Sustaining. Neither drowsiness overtakes Him nor sleep. To Him belongs what is in the heavens and what is on the earth. Who can intercede with Him except by His permission? He knows what is before them and what is behind them, and they encompass nothing of His knowledge except what He wills. His Throne extends over the heavens and the earth, and preserving them does not burden Him. He is the Most High, the Most Great.","There is no compulsion in religion. Right guidance has become clear from error. So whoever rejects false gods and believes in God has grasped the firmest handhold, one that never breaks. God is All-Hearing, All-Knowing.","God is the Protector of those who believe—He brings them out of darkness into light. And those who disbelieve, their protectors are false gods—they bring them out of light into darkness. Those are the companions of the Fire; they will remain in it forever.","Have you not seen the one who argued with Abraham about his Lord because God had given him kingship? When Abraham said, “My Lord is the One who gives life and causes death,” he said, “I give life and cause death.” Abraham said, “God brings the sun from the east—bring it from the west.” So the disbeliever was dumbfounded. God does not guide the wrongdoing people.","Or the one who passed by a town that had collapsed upon its roofs. He said, “How will God bring this back to life after its death?” So God caused him to die for a hundred years, then raised him. He said, “How long have you remained?” He said, “I remained a day, or part of a day.” He said, “No, you have remained a hundred years. Look at your food and drink—they have not spoiled. And look at your donkey. And We will make you a sign for people. And look at the bones, how We raise them then clothe them with flesh.” When it became clear to him, he said, “I know that God has power over all things.”","When Abraham said, “My Lord, show me how You give life to the dead,” He said, “Have you not believed?” He said, “Yes, but so that my heart may be at rest.” He said, “Then take four birds and draw them to you, then place a part of them on each mountain, then call them—they will come to you in haste. And know that God is All-Mighty, All-Wise.”","The example of those who spend their wealth in God’s way is like a grain that sprouts seven ears, in each ear a hundred grains. God multiplies for whoever He wills. God is All-Encompassing, All-Knowing.","Those who spend their wealth in God’s way and then do not follow what they spent with reminders or harm — their reward is with their Lord. No fear will be upon them, nor will they grieve.","A kind word and forgiveness are better than charity followed by harm. God is Self-Sufficient, All-Forbearing.","O you who believe, do not nullify your charity with reminders and harm, like one who spends his wealth to be seen by people and does not believe in God and the Last Day. His example is like a smooth stone covered with soil — a downpour strikes it and leaves it bare. They gain nothing from what they earned. God does not guide the disbelieving people.","The example of those who spend their wealth seeking God’s pleasure and to strengthen their own souls is like a garden on a hilltop — a downpour strikes it and it yields double its fruit. And if no downpour strikes it, then a drizzle suffices. God is All-Seeing of what you do.","Would any of you wish to have a garden of palms and grapevines, rivers flowing beneath it, with every kind of fruit in it for him, then old age strikes him while he has feeble children, and a fiery whirlwind strikes it and it burns up? Thus God makes the signs clear to you, so that you may reflect.","O you who believe, spend from the good things you have earned and from what We have brought out for you from the earth. Do not aim for the worthless of it to spend, when you yourselves would not take it unless you closed your eyes to it. And know that God is Self-Sufficient, All-Praiseworthy.","Satan promises you poverty and commands you to indecency, but God promises you forgiveness from Him and bounty. God is All-Encompassing, All-Knowing.","He grants wisdom to whoever He wills, and whoever is granted wisdom has been given abundant good. Yet none take heed except people of understanding.","Whatever you spend in charity or vow as a vow, God knows it. And the wrongdoers have no helpers.","If you disclose your charitable gifts, that is good. But if you conceal them and give them to the poor, that is better for you, and He will remove some of your misdeeds from you. God is All-Aware of what you do.","Their guidance is not upon you, but God guides whoever He wills. Whatever good you spend is for your own souls, and you do not spend except seeking God’s face. Whatever good you spend will be repaid to you in full, and you will not be wronged.","For the poor who are confined in God’s cause, unable to travel in the land — the ignorant would think them wealthy because of their restraint. You recognize them by their mark: they do not beg people persistently. Whatever good you spend, God is truly Knowing of it.","Those who spend their wealth by night and by day, secretly and openly — they have their reward with their Lord. No fear will be upon them, nor will they grieve.","Those who consume usury will not stand except as one stands whom Satan has struck with madness. That is because they said, “Trade is just like usury.” But God has permitted trade and forbidden usury. Whoever receives a warning from his Lord and stops, he may keep what is past, and his affair rests with God. But whoever returns — those are the companions of the Fire, dwelling in it forever.","God destroys usury and nourishes charity. God does not love any ungrateful sinner.","Truly, those who believed, did righteous deeds, established prayer, and gave charity — their reward awaits them with their Lord. No fear will come upon them, nor will they grieve.","O you who believe, be mindful of God and give up whatever remains of usury, if you are believers.","If you do not, then be warned of war from God and His Messenger. But if you repent, you may have your principal — you do no wrong and are not wronged.","If the debtor is in hardship, then grant respite until a time of ease. And to give it as charity is better for you, if only you knew.","And be mindful of a Day when you will be returned to God. Then every soul will be paid in full what it earned, and they will not be wronged.","O you who believe, when you contract a debt with one another for a stated term, write it down. Let a scribe write between you with justice. No scribe should refuse to write as God has taught him. So let him write, and let the one upon whom the obligation falls dictate, and let him be mindful of God, his Lord, and not diminish anything from it. If the one upon whom the obligation falls is feeble-minded, or weak, or unable to dictate himself, then let his guardian dictate with justice. Call two witnesses from among your men. If there are not two men, then one man and two women from those you approve as witnesses — so that if one of them errs, the other may remind her. Witnesses must not refuse when they are called. Do not grow weary of writing it down, whether small or large, along with its term. That is more just in God’s sight, more reliable for testimony, and more likely to prevent your doubt — unless it is an immediate transaction you conduct among yourselves, in which case there is no blame on you if you do not write it down. Have witnesses when you trade with one another. No scribe or witness should be harmed. If you do so, it is truly wickedness on your part. Be mindful of God, and God teaches you. God is All-Knowing of all things.","If you are on a journey and cannot find a scribe, then a pledge held in hand. But if you trust one another, then let the one who is trusted fulfill his trust, and let him be mindful of God, his Lord. Do not conceal testimony. Whoever conceals it — truly his heart is sinful. God is All-Knowing of what you do.","To God belongs what is in the heavens and what is on the earth. Whether you reveal what is in yourselves or conceal it, God will hold you to account for it. He forgives whom He wills and punishes whom He wills. God is Capable of all things.","The Messenger believed in what was sent down to him from his Lord, and so did the believers. Each believed in God, His angels, His books, and His messengers. “We make no distinction between any of His messengers.” They said, “We hear and we obey. Your forgiveness, our Lord. To You is the return.”","God does not burden a soul beyond its capacity. It receives what it has earned, and upon it is what it has earned. Our Lord, do not hold us accountable if we forget or err. Our Lord, do not lay upon us a burden like that which You laid upon those before us. Our Lord, do not burden us with what we have no strength to bear. Pardon us, forgive us, and have mercy on us. You are our Protector, so grant us victory over the disbelieving people.","Alif Lam Mim.","God — there is no god but He, the Ever-Living, the Self-Sustaining.","He sent down to you the Book in truth, confirming what came before it, and He sent down the Torah and the Gospel.","Before it, as guidance for people, and He sent down the Criterion. Truly, those who disbelieved in God’s signs — for them is a severe punishment. And God is Almighty, Possessor of retribution.","Nothing on earth or in heaven is hidden from God.","It is He who shapes you in the wombs however He wills. There is no god but He, the Almighty, the All-Wise.","It is He who sent down to you the Book. In it are verses that are precise — they are the mother of the Book — and others that are ambiguous. As for those in whose hearts is deviation, they follow what is ambiguous of it, seeking discord and seeking its interpretation. But none knows its interpretation except God. And those firm in knowledge say, “We believe in it; all of it is from our Lord.” And none take heed except people of understanding.","“Our Lord, do not let our hearts swerve after You have guided us, and grant us mercy from You. You are the Ever-Giving.”","“Our Lord, You will gather all people on a Day about which there is no doubt.” Surely God does not break His promise.","Those who disbelieved—their wealth and their children will never avail them anything against God. Those are the fuel of the Fire.","Like the way of Pharaoh’s people and those before them: they denied Our signs, so God seized them for their sins. And God is severe in punishment.","Say to those who disbelieved, “You will be defeated and gathered into Hell—what a wretched resting place!”","There was a sign for you in two armies that met: one fighting in God’s cause and another disbelieving. They saw them as twice their number with their own eyes. And God supports with His victory whom He wills. Surely in that is a lesson for those with insight.","The love of desires has been made alluring to people: women, sons, heaped-up hoards of gold and silver, fine horses, livestock, and farmland. That is the enjoyment of this worldly life, but with God is the best return.","Say, “Shall I tell you of something better than that? For the reverent, with their Lord, are gardens beneath which rivers flow, dwelling there forever, and purified spouses, and pleasure from God.” And God is All-Seeing of His servants.","Those who say, “Our Lord, we have believed, so forgive us our sins and protect us from the punishment of the Fire.”","The patient, the truthful, the devout, the charitable, and those who seek forgiveness at dawn.","God has testified that there is no god but He—and so have the angels and those of knowledge—upholding justice. There is no god but He, the All-Mighty, the All-Wise.","Truly, the religion with God is Islam. Those who were given the Scripture did not differ except after knowledge had come to them, out of envy among themselves. And whoever denies God’s verses—God is swift in reckoning.","If they argue with you, say, “I have surrendered my face to God, and so have those who follow me.” And say to those who were given the Scripture and the unlettered, “Have you surrendered?” If they surrender, they are guided. But if they turn away, your duty is only to convey. And God is All-Seeing of His servants.","Those who deny God’s verses, kill the prophets without right, and kill those among the people who command justice — give them tidings of a painful punishment.","Those are the ones whose deeds have come to nothing in this world and the Hereafter, and they have no helpers.","Have you not seen those who were given a share of the Scripture? They are called to God’s Book to judge between them, then a group of them turns away in rejection.","That is because they said, “The Fire will never touch us except for a few days.” What they used to fabricate has deluded them in their religion.","So how will it be when We gather them for a Day about which there is no doubt, and every soul is paid in full what it earned, and they are not wronged?","Say, “O God, Master of all sovereignty, You give sovereignty to whom You will and strip sovereignty from whom You will. You honor whom You will and humiliate whom You will. In Your hand is all good. Truly, You have power over all things.","You merge the night into the day and merge the day into the night. You bring the living from the dead and bring the dead from the living. And You provide for whom You will without measure.”","Believers must not take disbelievers as allies instead of believers. Whoever does that has nothing to do with God — unless you are guarding yourselves against them as a precaution. God warns you of Himself, and to God is the final return.","Say, “Whether you conceal what is in your hearts or reveal it, God knows it. He knows what is in the heavens and what is in the earth, and God is Capable of all things.”","The Day every soul finds what it did of good brought before it, and what it did of evil — it will wish there were a vast distance between itself and that. God warns you of Himself, and God is Compassionate to His servants.","Say, “If you love God, then follow me, and God will love you and forgive you your sins. God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.”","Say, “Obey God and the Messenger.” But if they turn away, then truly God does not love the disbelievers.","God chose Adam, Noah, the family of Abraham, and the family of Imran over all people.","Descendants, one from another. And God is All-Hearing, All-Knowing.","When the wife of Imran said, “My Lord, I have vowed to You what is in my womb, dedicated entirely, so accept it from me. You are the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.”","When she gave birth to her, she said, “My Lord, I have given birth to a girl” — and God knew best what she had delivered — “and the male is not like the female. I have named her Mary, and I seek Your protection for her and her offspring from Satan the accursed.”","So her Lord accepted her with a gracious acceptance and made her grow a beautiful growth, and placed her in the care of Zechariah. Every time Zechariah entered the sanctuary to see her, he found provision with her. He said, “O Mary, where did this come from?” She said, “It is from God. Truly God provides for whoever He wills without limit.”","It was there that Zechariah called upon his Lord. He said, “My Lord, grant me from You good offspring. You are the Hearer of prayer.”","The angels called out to him while he stood praying in the sanctuary, “God gives you glad tidings of John, confirming a word from God, a leader, chaste, and a prophet among the righteous.”","He said, “My Lord, how can I have a boy when old age has overtaken me and my wife is barren?” He said, “So it is — God does what He wills.”","He said, “My Lord, give me a sign.” He said, “Your sign is that you will not speak to people for three days except by gesture. And remember your Lord often, and glorify Him in the evening and the early morning.”","When the angels said, “O Mary, God has chosen you and purified you and chosen you above the women of all peoples.","O Mary, be devout to your Lord, prostrate, and bow with those who bow.”","That is from the news of the unseen which We reveal to you. You were not with them when they cast their pens to decide which of them would take charge of Mary, and you were not with them when they disputed.","When the angels said, “O Mary, God gives you glad tidings of a word from Him, whose name is the Messiah, Jesus son of Mary, distinguished in this world and the Hereafter, and among those brought near.","He will speak to people in the cradle and in maturity, and he will be among the righteous.”","She said, “My Lord, how can I have a child when no man has touched me?” He said, “So it is. God creates what He wills. When He decrees a matter, He only says to it, ‘Be,’ and it is.","He will teach him the Scripture, wisdom, the Torah, and the Gospel.","And a messenger to the Children of Israel: ‘I have come to you with a miracle from your Lord. I fashion for you from clay the shape of a bird, then I breathe into it, and it becomes a bird by God’s leave. I heal the blind and the leper, and I bring the dead to life by God’s leave. I tell you what you eat and what you store in your homes. Surely in that is a sign for you, if you are believers.","And confirming what came before me of the Torah, and to make lawful for you some of what was forbidden to you. I have come to you with a sign from your Lord, so be mindful of God and obey me.","God is my Lord and your Lord, so worship Him. This is a straight path.’”","When Jesus sensed disbelief from them, he said, “Who are my supporters for God’s cause?” The disciples said, “We are God’s supporters. We believe in God, and bear witness that we are submitters.","Our Lord, we believe in what You have revealed and we follow the messenger, so record us among the witnesses.”","They plotted, and God plotted, and God is the best of plotters.","When God said, “O Jesus, I will take you and raise you to Me and purify you from those who disbelieved, and I will place those who follow you above those who disbelieved until the Day of Resurrection. Then to Me is your return, and I will judge between you in what you used to differ over.","As for those who disbelieved, I will punish them with a severe punishment in this world and the Hereafter, and they will have no helpers.","But as for those who believed and did righteous deeds, He will pay them their rewards in full.” God does not love the wrongdoers.","That is what We recite to you of the verses and the wise reminder.","Truly, the example of Jesus before God is like the example of Adam — He created him from dust, then said to him, “Be,” and he was.","The truth is from your Lord, so do not be among the doubters.","Whoever argues with you about him after the knowledge that has come to you, say, “Come, let us call our sons and your sons, our women and your women, ourselves and yourselves, then let us earnestly pray and invoke God’s curse upon the liars.”","Surely this is the true account. There is no god but God, and God is truly the All-Mighty, the All-Wise.","If they turn away, then God is All-Knowing of the corrupters.","Say, “O People of the Book, come to a word common between us and you: that we worship none but God, that we associate nothing with Him, and that none of us takes others as lords besides God.” If they turn away, then say, “Bear witness that we are those who submit.”","O People of the Book, why do you argue about Abraham when the Torah and the Gospel were not revealed until after him? Do you not reason?","Here you are — you argued about what you had some knowledge of, so why do you argue about what you have no knowledge of? God knows, and you do not know.","Abraham was neither a Jew nor a Christian, but he was a monotheist, one who submitted, and he was not of those who associate others with God.","Surely the people closest to Abraham are those who followed him, and this Prophet, and those who believe. God is the Ally of the believers.","A faction of the People of the Book wished they could lead you astray, but they lead astray none but themselves, and they do not realize it.","O People of the Book, why do you deny God’s verses while you yourselves bear witness?","O People of the Book, why do you mix truth with falsehood and conceal the truth while you know?","A faction of the People of the Book said, “Believe in what was sent down upon the believers at the start of the day and deny it at its end, so that they might turn back.","And do not trust anyone except those who follow your religion.” Say, “Truly, guidance is God’s guidance — that anyone should be given the like of what you were given, or that they should argue against you before your Lord.” Say, “Truly, all bounty is in God’s hand. He gives it to whom He wills.” God is All-Encompassing, All-Knowing.","He singles out with His mercy whom He wills. God is the Possessor of immense bounty.","Among the People of the Book is one who, if you entrust him with a heap of gold, will return it to you. And among them is one who, if you entrust him with a single coin, will not return it to you unless you keep standing over him. That is because they said, “We have no obligation toward the unlettered.” They speak lies about God, and they know it.","But yes — whoever fulfills his covenant and is mindful, then God loves the mindful.","Those who sell God’s covenant and their oaths for a small price — they will have no share in the Hereafter. God will not speak to them, nor look at them on the Day of Resurrection, nor purify them, and for them is a painful punishment.","Among them is a group who twist their tongues with the Book so you would think it is from the Book, when it is not from the Book. They say, “It is from God,” when it is not from God. They speak lies about God, and they know it.","It is not for any human being that God should give him the Book, authority, and prophethood, and then he would say to people, “Be servants to me instead of God.” Rather, “Be people of the Lord, since you have been teaching the Book and since you have been studying it.”","Nor would he command you to take the angels and the prophets as lords. Would he command you to disbelief after you have submitted?","When God took the covenant of the prophets: “Whatever I have given you of a Book and wisdom, then a messenger comes to you confirming what is with you — you must believe in him and you must support him.” He said, “Do you affirm this and accept My binding pledge on that?” They said, “We affirm it.” He said, “Then bear witness, and I am with you among the witnesses.”","So whoever turns away after that — those are the defiantly disobedient.","Do they seek other than God’s religion, when to Him has submitted everyone in the heavens and the earth, willingly or unwillingly, and to Him they will be returned?","Say, “We believe in God, in what was sent down to us, in what was sent down to Abraham, Ishmael, Isaac, Jacob, and the tribes, and in what Moses, Jesus, and the prophets were given from their Lord. We make no distinction between any of them, and to Him we submit.”","Whoever seeks a religion other than submission to God, it will never be accepted from him, and in the Hereafter he will be among the losers.","How will God guide a people who disbelieved after their faith, who witnessed that the Messenger is true, and to whom clear proofs came? God does not guide the wrongdoing people.","Those — their recompense is that upon them falls the curse of God, the angels, and all of mankind.","They will remain in it forever. The punishment will not be lightened for them, nor will they be given respite.","Except those who repent after that and make amends — truly God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","Those who disbelieved after their faith and then grew in disbelief — their repentance will never be accepted. Those are the ones astray.","Those who disbelieved and died as disbelievers — never would the earth’s fill of gold be accepted from any one of them, even if he offered it as ransom. Those will have a painful punishment, and they will have no helpers.","You will never attain righteousness until you spend from what you love. And whatever you spend, God is fully aware of it.","All food was lawful to the Children of Israel except what Israel forbade himself before the Torah was sent down. Say, “Then bring the Torah and recite it, if you are truthful.”","So whoever fabricates lies about God after that — those are the wrongdoers.","Say, “God has spoken the truth. So follow the creed of Abraham, a monotheist, and he was not of those who associate others with God.”","Truly, the first house established for mankind is the one at Bakkah—blessed and a guidance for all peoples.","In it are clear signs: the station of Abraham. Whoever enters it is safe. And pilgrimage to the House is a duty owed to God by all people who can find a way to it. And whoever disbelieves—God is beyond need of all peoples.","Say, “O People of the Book, why do you reject God’s verses when God is witness to all you do?”","Say, “O People of the Book, why do you turn those who believe away from God’s path, seeking to make it crooked, while you yourselves are witnesses? God is not unaware of what you do.”","O you who believe, if you obey a faction of those given the Book, they will turn you back into disbelievers after your faith.","How can you disbelieve when God’s verses are recited to you and His Messenger is among you? Whoever holds fast to God has been guided to a straight path.","O you who believe, be mindful of God as He truly deserves, and do not die except as those who have submitted.","Hold fast to God’s rope, all together, and do not be divided. Remember God’s blessing upon you: you were enemies, and He united your hearts, so by His blessing you became brothers. You were on the edge of a pit of Fire, and He rescued you from it. Thus God makes His verses clear to you, so that you may be guided.","Let there be among you a community that calls to good, commands what is right, and forbids what is wrong. Those are the successful.","Do not be like those who divided and disagreed after clear proofs had come to them. Those will have a terrible punishment.","On the Day when faces turn white and faces turn black. As for those whose faces turn black: “Did you disbelieve after your faith? Then taste the punishment for your disbelief.”","But as for those whose faces turn white—they are in God’s mercy, dwelling there forever.","These are God’s verses; We recite them to you in truth. God does not desire any injustice for all peoples.","To God belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth. And to God all matters are returned.","You are the best nation ever brought out for humanity: you enjoin what is right, forbid what is wrong, and believe in God. Had the People of the Book believed, it would have been better for them. Among them are believers, but most of them are defiantly disobedient.","They will never harm you except with minor annoyance. If they fight you, they will turn their backs to you, and then they will not be helped.","Humiliation is stamped upon them wherever they are found, except through a rope from God and a rope from people. They drew upon themselves wrath from God, and wretchedness is stamped upon them. That is because they used to reject God’s signs and kill the prophets without right. That is because they disobeyed and used to transgress.","They are not all alike. Among the People of the Book is an upright community who recite God’s verses through the hours of the night, prostrating.","They believe in God and the Last Day, enjoin what is right, forbid what is wrong, and race toward good deeds. Those are among the righteous.","Whatever good they do will never be denied them. God is All-Knowing of the God-conscious.","Truly, those who disbelieve — their wealth and their children will avail them nothing against God. Those are the companions of the Fire; they will remain in it forever.","The example of what they spend in this worldly life is like a wind bearing frost that struck the harvest of a people who wronged themselves and destroyed it. God did not wrong them, but they wrong themselves.","O you who believe, do not take as intimates those outside your own. They spare no effort to ruin you and wish for your suffering. Hatred has already shown from their mouths, and what their chests conceal is far greater. We have made the signs clear to you, if you would reason.","Here you are, loving them while they do not love you, and you believe in the Scripture — all of it. When they meet you, they say, “We believe,” but when they are alone, they bite their fingertips at you in rage. Say, “Die in your rage!” Truly, God is All-Knowing of what is within the chests.","If something good touches you, it grieves them, and if misfortune strikes you, they rejoice at it. But if you are patient and God-conscious, their scheming will not harm you at all. Truly, God encompasses all that they do.","Remember when you set out from your family at dawn, positioning the believers at their battle stations. And God is All-Hearing, All-Knowing.","When two groups among you were about to lose heart, though God was their protector. And in God let the believers place their trust.","God had already granted you victory at Badr when you were few and weak. So be mindful of God, that you may be grateful.","When you said to the believers, “Is it not enough for you that your Lord reinforces you with three thousand angels sent down?","Yes, if you are patient and mindful, and they come at you in this rush of theirs, your Lord will reinforce you with five thousand angels, distinctly marked.”","God made this only as good news for you and to put your hearts at ease. Victory comes only from God, the All-Mighty, the All-Wise.","To cut off a flank of those who disbelieved, or crush them so they turn back defeated.","It is no concern of yours whether He turns to them in mercy or punishes them, for they are wrongdoers.","To God belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth. He forgives whom He wills and punishes whom He wills. And God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","O you who believe, do not consume usury, doubled and multiplied. Be mindful of God, so that you may prosper.","Fear the Fire that has been prepared for the disbelievers.","Obey God and the Messenger, so that you may be shown mercy.","Race toward forgiveness from your Lord and a Garden as wide as the heavens and the earth, prepared for the reverent.","Those who spend in ease and hardship, who restrain their anger and pardon people. God loves those who do good.","And those who, when they commit an indecency or wrong themselves, remember God and seek forgiveness for their sins—and who forgives sins but God?—and do not persist in what they did while they know.","Those—their recompense is forgiveness from their Lord and Gardens beneath which rivers flow, dwelling therein forever. How excellent is the reward of those who act.","Ways of life have passed before you, so travel through the earth and see how the deniers met their end.","This is a declaration for humanity, and a guidance and counsel for the mindful.","Do not weaken and do not grieve—you are the superior ones, if you are believers.","If a wound has touched you, a similar wound has touched the other people. These are days We alternate among people, so that God may distinguish those who believe and take martyrs from among you. God does not love the wrongdoers.","And so that God may purify those who believe and destroy the disbelievers.","Or did you think you would enter the Garden while God has not yet known those among you who struggled, and known the steadfast?","You used to wish for death before you met it—now you have seen it while you were looking on.","Muhammad is nothing but a messenger; messengers have passed before him. If he dies or is killed, will you turn back on your heels? Whoever turns back on his heels will never harm God in the least. And God will recompense the grateful.","No soul can die except by God’s permission, at a decreed term. Whoever desires the reward of this world, We will give him of it, and whoever desires the reward of the Hereafter, We will give him of it. And We will recompense the grateful.","How many a prophet fought alongside whom were many devout men, and they never faltered for what struck them in God’s cause, nor did they weaken, nor did they submit. And God loves the steadfast.","Their only words were: “Our Lord, forgive us our sins and our excess in our affairs, and plant our feet firmly, and grant us victory over the disbelieving people.”","So God gave them the reward of this world and the finest reward of the Hereafter. And God loves those who do good.","O you who believe, if you obey those who disbelieve, they will turn you back on your heels, and you will become losers.","Rather, God is your protector, and He is the best of helpers.","We will cast terror into the hearts of those who disbelieve because they associated with God what He sent down no authority for. Their refuge is the Fire, and wretched is the abode of the wrongdoers.","God certainly fulfilled His promise to you when you were cutting them down by His permission—until you lost courage, disputed over the command, and disobeyed after He had shown you what you love. Among you were those who desired this world, and among you were those who desired the Hereafter. Then He turned you away from them to test you. And He has pardoned you. God is full of grace toward the believers.","When you were fleeing uphill, not turning back for anyone, while the Messenger was calling you from behind, He repaid you with grief upon grief so that you would not grieve over what escaped you or what struck you. And God is All-Aware of what you do.","Then after the grief, He sent down upon you security—a drowsiness overtaking a group of you—while another group cared only about themselves, harboring thoughts about God other than the truth, thoughts of ignorance. They say, “Do we have any say in the matter?” Say, “The matter belongs entirely to God.” They conceal within themselves what they do not reveal to you. They say, “If we had any say in the matter, we would not have been killed here.” Say, “Even if you had been in your homes, those for whom killing was decreed would have gone out to their deathbeds.” And so that God might test what is in your chests and purify what is in your hearts. God is All-Knowing of what lies within the chests.","Those of you who turned back on the day the two armies met—it was Satan who made them slip through something they had earned. But God has pardoned them. Truly, God is All-Forgiving, All-Forbearing.","O you who believe, do not be like those who disbelieved and said of their brothers when they traveled the land or went on raids, “Had they stayed with us, they would not have died or been killed”—so that God would make that a source of anguish in their hearts. God gives life and causes death. And God is All-Seeing of what you do.","If you are killed in God’s cause or die, forgiveness from God and mercy are far better than all they amass.","And if you die or are killed, it is to God you will be gathered.","It was by mercy from God that you were gentle with them. Had you been harsh and hard-hearted, they would have scattered from around you. So pardon them, seek forgiveness for them, and consult them in the matter. Then, when you have resolved, put your trust in God. Truly, God loves those who put their trust in Him.","If God helps you, none can overcome you. But if He forsakes you, who then can help you after Him? So let the believers put their trust in God.","It is not for a prophet to defraud. Whoever defrauds will bring what he defrauded on the Day of Resurrection. Then every soul will be paid in full what it earned, and they will not be wronged.","Is one who pursues God’s pleasure like one who has brought upon himself wrath from God, whose refuge is Hell? What a wretched destination!","They are of varying degrees before God. And God is All-Seeing of what they do.","Certainly God bestowed a favor upon the believers when He raised among them a messenger from themselves, reciting to them His verses, purifying them, and teaching them the Book and wisdom—though before that they were clearly astray.","When a disaster struck you after you had inflicted twice as much, you said, “How is this?” Say, “It is from yourselves.” Truly, God is Capable of all things.","What struck you on the day the two armies met was by God’s permission, and so that He might distinguish the believers.","And so that He might distinguish the hypocrites. They were told, “Come, fight in God’s cause, or at least defend.” They said, “If we knew there would be fighting, we would have followed you.” They were closer to disbelief that day than to faith. They say with their mouths what is not in their hearts. And God knows best what they conceal.","Those who sat back and said of their brothers, “Had they obeyed us, they would not have been killed.” Say, “Then avert death from yourselves, if you are truthful.”","Do not think those killed in God’s cause are dead. They are alive with their Lord, provided for.","Rejoicing in what God has given them of His grace, and delighted for those who have not yet joined them from behind — that no fear will be upon them, nor will they grieve.","They rejoice in a blessing from God and grace, and that God does not waste the reward of the believers.","Those who answered God and the Messenger after wounds had struck them — for those among them who did good and were mindful, a great reward.","Those whom people told, “The people have gathered against you, so fear them,” but it only increased them in faith, and they said, “God is enough for us, and what an excellent Guardian.”","So they returned with a blessing from God and grace, no harm having touched them, and they pursued God’s pleasure. God is the possessor of great grace.","That is only Satan frightening his allies. So do not fear them, but fear Me, if you are believers.","Do not let those who rush into disbelief grieve you. They will never harm God in the least. God intends to give them no share in the Hereafter, and for them is a great punishment.","Surely those who purchased disbelief at the price of faith will never harm God in the least, and for them is a painful punishment.","Let not those who disbelieve think that Our granting them respite is good for them. We only grant them respite so they increase in sin, and for them is a humiliating punishment.","God would never leave the believers in the state you are in until He separates the wicked from the good. And God would never reveal to you the unseen, but God chooses from His messengers whom He wills. So believe in God and His messengers. And if you believe and are mindful, for you is a great reward.","Let not those who hoard what God has given them of His grace think it is good for them. Rather, it is bad for them. They will be collared with what they hoarded on the Day of Resurrection. To God belongs the inheritance of the heavens and the earth, and God is All-Aware of what you do.","God has heard the words of those who said, “God is poor and we are rich.” We will record what they said and their killing of the prophets without right, and We will say, “Taste the punishment of the Blaze.”","That is for what your hands have sent ahead, and God is never unjust to His servants.","Those who said, “God has made a covenant with us not to believe in any messenger until he brings us an offering consumed by fire.” Say, “Messengers before me came to you with clear proofs and with what you demanded — so why did you kill them, if you are truthful?”","If they deny you, messengers before you were denied too — they came with clear proofs, the scriptures, and the illuminating Book.","Every soul will taste death. You will only be paid your full rewards on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever is pulled away from the Fire and admitted into Paradise has truly triumphed. The life of this world is nothing but the enjoyment of delusion.","You will surely be tested in your wealth and yourselves, and you will surely hear much abuse from those who were given the Book before you and from those who associate partners with God. But if you endure and remain God-conscious, that is truly a matter of resolve.","When God took the covenant of those who were given the Book — “You must make it clear to people and not conceal it” — they cast it behind their backs and sold it for a petty price. Wretched is what they purchase!","Do not think that those who rejoice in what they have done and love to be praised for what they did not do — do not think they are safe from the punishment. For them is a painful punishment.","To God belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth. God is Capable of all things.","Truly in the creation of the heavens and the earth and the alternation of night and day are signs for people of understanding.","Those who remember God standing, sitting, and on their sides, and reflect on the creation of the heavens and the earth: “Our Lord, You did not create this in vain. Glory be to You. Protect us from the punishment of the Fire.","Our Lord, whoever You admit into the Fire, You have truly disgraced him, and the wrongdoers have no helpers.","Our Lord, we heard a caller calling to faith: ‘Believe in your Lord,’ and we believed. Our Lord, forgive us our sins, erase our misdeeds, and take our souls with the righteous.","Our Lord, grant us what You promised us through Your messengers, and do not disgrace us on the Day of Resurrection. You never break Your promise.”","So their Lord answered them, “I do not let the work of any worker among you go to waste, male or female — you are of one another. Those who emigrated and were driven from their homes and were harmed in My cause and fought and were killed, I will surely erase their misdeeds and I will surely admit them into gardens beneath which rivers flow — a reward from God.” And with God is the finest reward.","Do not be deceived by the movement of the disbelievers throughout the land.","A brief enjoyment, then their refuge is Hell — and what a wretched resting place!","But those who were mindful of their Lord will have gardens beneath which rivers flow, dwelling there forever — a welcome from God. And what is with God is better for the righteous.","Among the People of the Book are those who believe in God and what was sent down to you and what was sent down to them, humbling themselves before God, never trading God’s verses for a small price. Those will have their reward with their Lord. Truly God is swift in reckoning.","O you who believe, be patient, outdo others in patience, stand firm, and be mindful of God, so that you may succeed.","O people, be mindful of your Lord, who created you from a single soul and created from it its mate and spread from them both many men and women. And be mindful of God, in whose name you appeal to one another, and of family ties. Truly, God is ever a Watcher over you.","Give the orphans their wealth, and do not exchange the bad for the good, and do not consume their wealth into your own. It is surely a great sin.","If you fear you cannot deal justly with the orphans, then marry what pleases you of women — two, three, or four. But if you fear you will not be fair, then one, or what your right hands possess. That is more likely to keep you from injustice.","Give women their bridal gifts freely. But if they willingly give up any part of it to you, then consume it with pleasure and ease.","Do not give the feeble-minded your wealth that God has made a means of support for you. Provide for them from it, clothe them, and speak to them with kind words.","Test the orphans until they reach the age of marriage. If you find sound judgment in them, hand over their wealth to them. Do not consume it wastefully or in haste before they grow up. Whoever is wealthy should abstain, and whoever is poor may consume reasonably. When you hand over their wealth to them, have it witnessed. And God suffices as a Reckoner.","For men is a share of what parents and close relatives leave behind, and for women is a share of what parents and close relatives leave behind — whether little or much — an obligated share.","When relatives, orphans, and the needy are present at the division, provide for them from it and speak to them with kind words.","Let those fear who, had they left behind weak offspring, would worry for them. So let them be mindful of God and speak words of justice.","Those who consume the wealth of orphans unjustly are only filling their bellies with fire, and they will burn in a Blaze.","God instructs you regarding your children: the male receives the share of two females. If they are women, more than two, they receive two-thirds of what he left. If she is one, she receives half. For each of his parents, a sixth of what he left, if he had a child. If he had no child and his parents inherit from him, then his mother receives a third. If he had siblings, then his mother receives a sixth — after any bequest he made or debt. Your fathers and your children — you do not know which of them is closer to you in benefit. An obligation from God. Truly, God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.","You receive half of what your wives left, if they had no child. If they had a child, you receive a fourth of what they left — after any bequest they made or debt. They receive a fourth of what you left, if you had no child. If you had a child, they receive an eighth of what you left — after any bequest you made or debt. If a man or woman is inherited from with no direct heir, and he has a brother or sister, each of them receives a sixth. If they are more than that, they share in a third — after any bequest made or debt, without causing harm. A directive from God. God is All-Knowing, All-Forbearing.","These are God’s limits. Whoever obeys God and His Messenger, He will admit him into Gardens beneath which rivers flow, dwelling therein forever. That is the supreme triumph.","Whoever disobeys God and His Messenger and oversteps His limits, He will admit him into a Fire, dwelling therein forever, and for him is a humiliating punishment.","Those of your women who commit indecency — call four witnesses from among you against them. If they testify, then confine them to their houses until death takes them or God makes a way for them.","The two among you who commit it — punish them both. But if they repent and reform, then leave them alone. Truly, God is ever Accepting of repentance, Most Merciful.","Repentance with God is only for those who do evil in ignorance and then repent soon after — those are the ones God accepts in repentance. God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.","But repentance is not for those who go on doing evil until, when death comes upon one of them, he says, “I repent now,” nor for those who die as disbelievers. For those, We have prepared a painful punishment.","O you who believe, it is not lawful for you to inherit women against their will. Do not pressure them to take back part of what you gave them, unless they commit a clear indecency. Live with them in kindness. If you dislike them, it may be that you dislike something in which God places much good.","If you wish to replace one wife with another and you have given one of them a fortune, take nothing back from it. Would you take it through slander and open sin?","How could you take it back when you have been intimate with one another, and they have taken from you a solemn covenant?","Do not marry women your fathers married — except what has already passed. It was indeed an indecency, a hateful thing, and a wretched path.","Forbidden to you are your mothers, your daughters, your sisters, your paternal aunts, your maternal aunts, your brother’s daughters, your sister’s daughters, your mothers who nursed you, your sisters through nursing, your wives’ mothers, your stepdaughters under your care from wives you have consummated marriage with — but if you have not consummated with them, there is no blame on you — and the wives of your sons from your own loins, and marrying two sisters at the same time, except what has already passed. Truly God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","And married women, except those your right hands possess. This is God’s decree upon you. Lawful to you is all beyond that, provided you seek them with your wealth in marriage, not in fornication. Whatever you have enjoyed from them, give them their due compensation as an obligation. There is no blame on you in whatever you mutually agree upon after the obligation. Truly God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.","Whoever among you cannot afford to marry free believing women, then from your believing slave girls that your right hands possess — and God knows best about your faith; you are of one another — so marry them with their families’ permission and give them their due compensation fairly, as chaste women, not fornicators or those who take secret lovers. Once they are married, if they commit an indecency, their punishment is half that of free women. That is for whoever among you fears falling into sin. But that you be patient is better for you. God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","God wants to make things clear to you, guide you to the ways of those before you, and turn to you in mercy. God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.","God wants to turn to you in mercy, but those who follow their desires want you to deviate greatly.","God wants to lighten your burden, for the human being was created weak.","O you who believe, do not consume one another’s wealth unjustly, unless it is through trade by mutual consent among you. And do not kill yourselves. Truly, God is ever Merciful to you.","Whoever does that out of aggression and injustice, We will burn him in a Fire. And that is easy for God.","If you avoid the major sins you are forbidden from, We will absolve your lesser offenses and admit you into a noble entrance.","Do not covet what God has favored some of you with over others. Men have a share of what they have earned, and women have a share of what they have earned. Ask God for His bounty. Surely, God is ever All-Knowing of all things.","For each We have appointed heirs to what parents and close relatives leave behind. And those with whom your oaths have made a pledge, give them their share. Truly, God is ever a Witness over all things.","Men are caretakers of women, by what God has favored some of them over others and by what they spend of their wealth. So righteous women are devoutly obedient, guarding in absence what God has guarded. As for those whose defiance you fear, admonish them, forsake them in bed, and strike them. But if they obey you, seek no way against them. Surely, God is ever Most High, Most Great.","If you fear a rift between the two of them, send an arbiter from his family and an arbiter from her family. If they both desire reconciliation, God will bring them into accord. Truly, God is ever All-Knowing, All-Aware.","Worship God and associate nothing with Him. Show kindness to parents, to relatives, to orphans, to the needy, to the near neighbor, to the distant neighbor, to the companion at your side, to the traveler, and to those your right hands possess. Truly, God does not love anyone arrogant and boastful.","Those who are stingy and urge others to be stingy and conceal what God has given them of His bounty — We have prepared for the disbelievers a humiliating punishment.","And those who spend their wealth to be seen by people and believe neither in God nor in the Last Day. Whoever has Satan as a companion — what a wretched companion!","What would it have cost them to believe in God and the Last Day and spend from what God has provided them? God is All-Knowing of them.","God does not wrong anyone by even an atom’s weight. If it is a good deed, He multiplies it and grants from Himself a great reward.","So how will it be when We bring a witness from every nation and bring you as a witness over these?","On that Day, those who disbelieved and disobeyed the Messenger will wish the earth were leveled over them, and they will not be able to hide a single word from God.","O you who believe, do not approach prayer while you are intoxicated until you know what you are saying, nor while in a state of major impurity — unless you are passing through — until you have bathed. If you are ill, or on a journey, or one of you has come from relieving himself, or you have touched women, and you find no water, then turn to clean earth and wipe your faces and your hands. Truly, God is Ever-Pardoning, All-Forgiving.","Have you not seen those who were given a share of the Scripture? They purchase misguidance and want you to stray from the path.","God knows best your enemies. God suffices as a Protector, and God suffices as a Helper.","Among those who are Jewish, some distort words from their places and say, “We hear and we disobey,” and “Hear, may you not be heard,” and “Ra’ina,” twisting with their tongues and slandering the religion. Had they said, “We hear and we obey,” and “Hear,” and “Look upon us,” it would have been better for them and more upright. But God cursed them for their disbelief, so they believe not, except a few.","O you who were given the Scripture, believe in what We have sent down, confirming what is with you, before We obliterate faces and turn them backward, or curse them as We cursed the people of the Sabbath. God’s command is always carried out.","Truly, God does not forgive that partners be ascribed to Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whoever He wills. Whoever ascribes partners to God has fabricated a tremendous sin.","Have you not seen those who declare themselves pure? Rather, God purifies whom He wills, and they will not be wronged by so much as a thread.","Look how they fabricate lies against God. That alone suffices as a clear sin.","Have you not seen those who were given a share of the Scripture? They believe in idols and false gods and say of those who disbelieve, “These are more rightly guided than the believers in path.”","Those are the ones God has cursed, and whoever God curses, you will never find for him a helper.","Or do they have a share of sovereignty? Then they would not give people even the speck on a date stone.","Or do they envy people for what God has given them of His bounty? We gave the family of Abraham the Scripture and wisdom, and We gave them a great kingdom.","Some of them believed in it, and some of them turned away from it. Hell suffices as a blaze.","Those who disbelieve in Our signs — We will roast them in a Fire. Every time their skins are burned through, We will replace them with other skins so they may taste the punishment. Truly, God is All-Mighty, All-Wise.","Those who believe and do righteous deeds — We will admit them into Gardens beneath which rivers flow, dwelling therein forever. For them therein are purified spouses, and We will admit them into deep, cool shade.","God commands you to return trusts to their rightful owners, and when you judge between people, to judge with justice. Truly, how excellent is what God instructs you with. God is All-Hearing, All-Seeing.","O you who believe, obey God and obey the Messenger and those in authority among you. If you disagree over anything, refer it to God and the Messenger, if you believe in God and the Last Day. That is better and more sound in outcome.","Have you not seen those who claim they believe in what was sent down to you and what was sent down before you, yet they wish to seek judgment from false authority, though they were commanded to reject it? Satan wants to lead them far astray.","When they are told, “Come to what God has sent down and to the Messenger,” you see the hypocrites turning away from you in utter aversion.","So how will it be when disaster strikes them because of what their own hands have done, then they come to you swearing by God, “We intended nothing but goodness and reconciliation”?","Those are the ones whose hearts God knows well. So turn away from them, admonish them, and speak to them words that cut deep into their souls.","We never sent a messenger except to be obeyed by God’s leave. If only, when they wronged themselves, they had come to you and asked God’s forgiveness, and the Messenger had asked forgiveness for them, they would have found God Ever-Relenting, Most Merciful.","But no, by your Lord, they will not believe until they make you judge in their disputes, then find no resistance in themselves toward your verdict, and submit fully.","Had We prescribed for them, “Kill yourselves” or “Leave your homes,” only a few of them would have done it. Yet had they done what they were advised to do, it would have been better for them and more strengthening.","And then We would have given them from Us a great reward.","And We would have guided them to a straight path.","Whoever obeys God and the Messenger — they are with those God has blessed: the prophets, the truthful, the martyrs, and the righteous. What excellent companions they are!","That is the bounty of God, and God suffices as All-Knowing.","O you who believe, take your precautions, then march out in detachments or march out all together.","Among you is he who will surely lag behind. If a calamity strikes you, he says, “God has blessed me, since I was not present with them.”","But if a bounty from God comes to you, he will surely say — as if there were no affection between you and him — “If only I had been with them, I would have won a great triumph!”","So let those who sell the life of this world for the Hereafter fight in God’s cause. Whoever fights in God’s cause and is killed or prevails — We will grant him a great reward.","What is wrong with you that you do not fight in God’s cause and for the oppressed among men, women, and children who say, “Our Lord, take us out of this town whose people are oppressors, and appoint for us from Yourself a protector, and appoint for us from Yourself a helper”?","Those who believe fight in God’s cause, and those who disbelieve fight in the cause of false gods. So fight the allies of Satan. Truly, Satan’s scheming is weak.","Have you not seen those who were told, “Restrain your hands, establish the prayer, and give charity”? But when fighting was prescribed for them, a group of them feared people as they fear God — or with even greater fear — and said, “Our Lord, why have You prescribed fighting for us? If only You had granted us a brief reprieve!” Say, “The enjoyment of this world is little, and the Hereafter is better for the God-conscious. You will not be wronged by so much as a thread.”","Wherever you may be, death will overtake you, even if you are in fortified towers. If something good befalls them, they say, “This is from God,” but if something bad befalls them, they say, “This is from you.” Say, “All is from God.” What is wrong with these people that they can hardly understand a word?","Whatever good befalls you is from God, and whatever bad befalls you is from yourself. We have sent you to mankind as a messenger, and God suffices as a witness.","Whoever obeys the Messenger has obeyed God. And whoever turns away — We have not sent you as a guardian over them.","They say, “Obedience,” but when they leave your presence, a group of them plots by night something other than what you say. God records what they plot by night. So turn away from them and put your trust in God. God is sufficient as a Guardian.","Do they not reflect on the Quran? Had it been from anyone other than God, they would have found in it much contradiction.","When news of security or fear reaches them, they spread it. Had they referred it to the Messenger and to those in authority among them, those who can draw conclusions among them would have known it. Were it not for God’s grace upon you and His mercy, you would have followed Satan, all but a few.","So fight in God’s cause — you are not responsible except for yourself — and urge on the believers. Perhaps God will restrain the might of those who disbelieve. God is greater in might and greater in punishment.","Whoever intercedes with a good intercession will have a share of it, and whoever intercedes with an evil intercession will bear a portion of it. God is a Keeper over all things.","When you are greeted with a greeting, greet back with something better or return it. Truly, God keeps account of all things.","God — there is no god but Him. He will surely gather you on the Day of Resurrection, about which there is no doubt. And who is more truthful in speech than God?","What is wrong with you that you are two groups regarding the hypocrites, when God has cast them back for what they earned? Do you want to guide those whom God has led astray? Whoever God leads astray — you will never find a way for him.","They wish you would disbelieve as they have disbelieved, so you would be alike. So do not take allies from among them until they emigrate in God’s cause. But if they turn away, then seize them and kill them wherever you find them, and do not take from among them any ally or helper.","Except those who reach a people between whom and you there is a treaty, or those who come to you with their hearts shrinking from fighting you or fighting their own people. Had God willed, He would have given them power over you, and they would have fought you. So if they withdraw from you and do not fight you and offer you peace, then God has given you no way against them.","You will find others who want to be safe from you and safe from their own people. Every time they are returned to temptation, they plunge back into it. So if they do not withdraw from you, offer you peace, and restrain their hands, then seize them and kill them wherever you encounter them. Against those, We have given you clear authority.","It is not for a believer to kill a believer except by mistake. Whoever kills a believer by mistake must free a believing slave and pay blood money to the victim’s family, unless they waive it as charity. If the victim belonged to a people hostile to you but was himself a believer, then the freeing of a believing slave. If he belonged to a people with whom you have a treaty, then blood money delivered to his family and the freeing of a believing slave. Whoever cannot find the means, then fasting for two consecutive months — a repentance from God. God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.","Whoever kills a believer deliberately, his recompense is Hell, abiding in it forever. God’s wrath is upon him, He has cursed him, and He has prepared for him a tremendous punishment.","O you who believe, when you go out in God’s cause, verify carefully. Do not say to anyone who offers you peace, “You are not a believer,” seeking the fleeting gains of this worldly life — with God are abundant spoils. You yourselves were like that before, then God bestowed His favor upon you. So verify carefully. Truly God is fully Aware of what you do.","Not equal are those believers who sit back — other than those with disabilities — and those who strive in God’s cause with their wealth and their lives. God has favored those who strive with their wealth and their lives over those who sit back by a degree. To each God has promised the best reward. Yet God has favored those who strive over those who sit back with a tremendous reward.","Degrees from Him, and forgiveness, and mercy. God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","Those whose souls the angels take while they were wronging themselves — they say, “What state were you in?” They reply, “We were oppressed in the land.” They say, “Was God’s earth not spacious enough for you to emigrate in it?” Their refuge is Hell — and what a wretched destination!","Except the truly helpless among men, women, and children who have no means and find no way.","Those — God may well pardon them. God is All-Pardoning, All-Forgiving.","Whoever emigrates in God’s cause will find on the earth many a refuge and abundance. Whoever leaves his home emigrating to God and His Messenger, then death overtakes him, his reward has already fallen upon God. God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","When you travel through the land, there is no blame on you if you shorten the prayer, if you fear that those who disbelieve may attack you. Truly, the disbelievers have always been a clear enemy to you.","When you are among them and lead them in prayer, let a group of them stand with you and let them carry their weapons. When they have prostrated, let them move to the rear, and let another group who has not yet prayed come and pray with you, and let them take their precautions and their weapons. Those who disbelieve wish you would neglect your weapons and your supplies so they could sweep down on you in a single assault. There is no blame on you if you are troubled by rain or are ill to set down your weapons, but take your precautions. God has prepared for the disbelievers a humiliating punishment.","When you have finished the prayer, remember God standing, sitting, and lying on your sides. Then when you are secure, establish the prayer. Surely the prayer has been a timed obligation upon the believers.","Do not weaken in pursuing the enemy. If you suffer, they too suffer as you suffer, but you hope from God what they do not hope. God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.","We have sent down the Book to you in truth so that you may judge between people by what God has shown you. Do not be an advocate for the treacherous.","Seek God’s forgiveness. God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","Do not argue on behalf of those who betray themselves. God does not love anyone who is a persistent traitor, steeped in sin.","They hide from people but do not hide from God, and He is with them when they plot by night with words He does not approve. God encompasses everything they do.","Here you are, arguing on their behalf in the life of this world — but who will argue with God on their behalf on the Day of Resurrection, or who will be their guardian?","Whoever does evil or wrongs himself then seeks God’s forgiveness will find God All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","Whoever earns a sin earns it only against himself. God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.","Whoever earns a fault or a sin then casts it upon an innocent person has burdened himself with slander and a clear sin.","Were it not for God’s grace upon you and His mercy, a group of them would have resolved to lead you astray. But they lead astray none but themselves, and they cannot harm you in the least. God has sent down to you the Book and wisdom and taught you what you did not know. God’s grace upon you has been immense.","There is no good in most of their private conversations, except for whoever commands charity, or kindness, or reconciliation between people. Whoever does that seeking God’s pleasure, We will give him a great reward.","Whoever opposes the Messenger after guidance has become clear to him and follows a path other than that of the believers, We will turn him to what he has turned to and burn him in Hell — what a wretched destination!","Truly, God does not forgive that partners be ascribed to Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whoever He wills. Whoever ascribes partners to God has strayed far, far astray.","They call upon none besides Him but females, and they call upon none but a rebellious Satan.","God cursed him. And he said, “I will surely take from Your servants an appointed share.","I will surely lead them astray, I will surely fill them with false hopes, I will surely command them and they will slit the ears of cattle, and I will surely command them and they will alter God’s creation.” Whoever takes Satan as a protector instead of God has suffered a clear loss.","He makes them promises and fills them with hopes, but Satan promises them nothing but delusion.","Those — their refuge is Hell, and they will find no escape from it.","But those who believe and do righteous deeds, We will admit them into Gardens beneath which rivers flow, dwelling there forever. God’s promise is true — and who is more truthful in word than God?","It is not by your wishful thinking, nor by the wishful thinking of the People of the Book. Whoever does evil will be repaid for it, and he will find for himself no protector or helper besides God.","Whoever does righteous deeds, whether male or female, while being a believer — those will enter Paradise and will not be wronged even by the speck on a date stone.","Who is better in faith than one who submits his face to God while doing good and follows the creed of Abraham, a monotheist? And God took Abraham as a close friend.","To God belongs what is in the heavens and what is on the earth. And God encompasses all things.","They ask you for a ruling concerning women. Say, “God gives you a ruling concerning them, and what is recited to you in the Book concerning orphan women to whom you do not give what is prescribed for them yet desire to marry them, and concerning the oppressed among children, and that you stand for orphans with justice.” Whatever good you do, God is truly All-Knowing of it.","If a woman fears ill-treatment or neglect from her husband, there is no blame on them if they reach a settlement between themselves. Settlement is better. Souls are prone to greed. If you do good and are mindful, then God is truly All-Aware of what you do.","You will never be able to treat women with perfect equality, no matter how hard you try. So do not incline entirely toward one, leaving the other like one suspended. If you make amends and are mindful, then God is truly All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","If they separate, God will enrich each from His abundance. God is All-Encompassing, All-Wise.","To God belongs what is in the heavens and what is on the earth. We certainly charged those who were given the Book before you, and you as well, to be mindful of God. If you disbelieve, then to God belongs what is in the heavens and what is on the earth. God is Self-Sufficient, All-Praiseworthy.","To God belongs what is in the heavens and what is on the earth. God suffices as a Guardian.","If He wills, He can remove you, O people, and bring others in your place. God is fully Capable of that.","Whoever desires the reward of this world — with God is the reward of this world and the Hereafter. God is All-Hearing, All-Seeing.","O you who believe, be steadfast upholders of justice, witnesses for God, even if against yourselves, your parents, or your relatives. Whether rich or poor, God has more right over both. So do not follow desire, lest you swerve from justice. If you distort or turn away, God is fully aware of what you do.","O you who believe, believe in God and His Messenger, and the Book He sent down upon His Messenger, and the Book He sent down before. Whoever disbelieves in God, His angels, His Books, His messengers, and the Last Day has strayed far astray.","Those who believed, then disbelieved, then believed, then disbelieved, then grew in disbelief—God will not forgive them, nor will He guide them to a way.","Give the hypocrites the news that a painful punishment awaits them.","Those who take the disbelievers as allies instead of the believers—do they seek power with them? Truly, all power belongs to God.","He has already sent down to you in the Book that when you hear God’s verses being denied and mocked, do not sit with them until they turn to another topic. Otherwise, you would be just like them. God will gather the hypocrites and the disbelievers in Hell, all together.","Those who lie in wait for you—if you gain a victory from God, they say, “Were we not with you?” But if the disbelievers have a share, they say, “Did we not have the upper hand over you and protect you from the believers?” God will judge between you on the Day of Resurrection, and God will never grant the disbelievers a way over the believers.","The hypocrites try to deceive God, but He is the one deceiving them. When they stand for prayer, they stand lazily, showing off before people, and they remember God only little.","Wavering between this and that—neither with these nor with those. Whoever God leads astray, you will never find a way for him.","O you who believe, do not take the disbelievers as allies instead of the believers. Do you want to give God a clear case against you?","The hypocrites will be in the lowest depth of the Fire, and you will never find a helper for them.","Except those who repent, reform, hold fast to God, and devote their religion sincerely to God—those are with the believers. And God will give the believers a great reward.","What would God gain by punishing you if you are grateful and believe? God is ever Appreciative, All-Knowing.","God does not love the public utterance of evil speech, except by one who has been wronged. God is All-Hearing, All-Knowing.","If you show goodness, or conceal it, or pardon an evil, then truly God is All-Pardoning, All-Powerful.","Those who deny God and His messengers and wish to separate between God and His messengers, saying, “We believe in some and deny others,” and wish to take a path in between.","Those are the true disbelievers. And We have prepared for the disbelievers a humiliating punishment.","But those who believe in God and His messengers and make no distinction between any of them—those He will give their rewards. God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","The People of the Book ask you to bring down upon them a book from the sky. They asked Moses for even greater than that, saying, “Show us God openly,” so the thunderbolt struck them for their wrongdoing. Then they took the calf after the clear proofs had come to them, yet We pardoned them for that. And We gave Moses clear authority.","And We raised the mountain over them for their covenant, and We said to them, “Enter the gate in prostration,” and We said to them, “Do not transgress on the Sabbath.” And We took from them a solemn covenant.","So for their breaking of their covenant, their denial of God’s verses, their killing of the prophets without right, and their saying, “Our hearts are sealed”—rather, God sealed them for their disbelief, so they believe not, except a few.","And for their disbelief and their uttering against Mary a monstrous slander.","And their saying, “We killed the Messiah, Jesus son of Mary, the messenger of God.” They did not kill him, nor did they crucify him, but it was made to appear so to them. Those who differed over him are truly in doubt about it. They have no knowledge of it, only the following of conjecture. They certainly did not kill him.","Rather, God raised him to Himself. God is All-Mighty, All-Wise.","There is none among the People of the Book but will surely believe in him before his death. And on the Day of Resurrection, he will be a witness against them.","So for the wrongdoing of those who are Jews, We forbade them good things that had been permitted to them, and for their frequent obstruction of God’s path.","And their taking of usury though they had been forbidden it, and their consuming of people’s wealth through falsehood. And We have prepared for the disbelievers among them a painful punishment.","But those among them who are firmly grounded in knowledge, and the believers—they believe in what has been sent down to you and what was sent down before you—and those who establish prayer, and those who give charity, and those who believe in God and the Last Day—those We will give a great reward.","We revealed to you just as We revealed to Noah and the prophets after him. We revealed to Abraham, Ishmael, Isaac, Jacob, the Tribes, Jesus, Job, Jonah, Aaron, and Solomon. And We gave David the Psalms.","Messengers We have told you about before, and messengers We have not told you about. And God spoke to Moses directly.","Messengers bearing good news and warning, so that people would have no argument against God after the messengers. God is All-Mighty, All-Wise.","But God bears witness to what He sent down to you — He sent it down with His knowledge — and the angels bear witness. God suffices as a Witness.","Truly, those who disbelieved and turned others from God’s path have strayed far astray.","Those who disbelieved and wronged — God would never forgive them or guide them to any path.","Except the path of Hell, dwelling in it forever. And that is easy for God.","O people, the Messenger has come to you with the truth from your Lord, so believe — it is better for you. But if you disbelieve, then to God belongs everything in the heavens and the earth. God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.","O People of the Book, do not go to excess in your religion, and do not say about God anything but the truth. The Messiah, Jesus son of Mary, was only a messenger of God and His word, which He cast to Mary, and a spirit from Him. So believe in God and His messengers, and do not say, “Three.” Stop — it is better for you. God is only one God. Glory be to Him that He should have a child. To Him belongs what is in the heavens and what is in the earth. God is sufficient as a Guardian.","The Messiah would never disdain to be a servant of God, nor would the angels nearest to Him. Whoever disdains His worship and grows arrogant — He will gather them all to Him.","As for those who believed and did righteous deeds, He will pay them their rewards in full and increase them from His grace. But as for those who disdained and grew arrogant, He will punish them with a painful punishment, and they will find for themselves no protector or helper besides God.","O humanity, a proof has come to you from your Lord, and We have sent down to you a clear light.","As for those who believed in God and held fast to Him, He will admit them into mercy from Him and grace, and He will guide them to Him on a straight path.","They ask you for a ruling. Say, “God gives you a ruling concerning the person with no parents or children. If a man dies leaving no child but has a sister, she receives half of what he left. And he inherits from her if she has no child. If there are two sisters, they receive two-thirds of what he left. And if they are siblings, men and women, then the male receives the share of two females.” God makes this clear to you so that you do not go astray. God is All-Knowing of all things.","O you who believe, fulfill your contracts. The grazing livestock have been made lawful for you, except what is recited to you, while you are not to hunt game when you are in a state of pilgrimage. God decrees what He wills.","O you who believe, do not violate God’s rites, nor the sacred month, nor the sacrificial offerings, nor the garlanded animals, nor those heading for the Sacred House seeking bounty and pleasure from their Lord. When you have left the state of pilgrimage, then hunt. And do not let the hatred of a people who once barred you from the Sacred Mosque drive you to transgress. Cooperate in righteousness and God-consciousness, and do not cooperate in sin and aggression. And be mindful of God. Truly, God is severe in punishment.","Forbidden to you are carrion, blood, the flesh of swine, what has been dedicated to other than God, the strangled, the beaten to death, the fallen, the gored, what predators have eaten—except what you slaughter before death—and what is sacrificed on stone altars, and that you seek decisions by divining arrows. That is wickedness. Today those who disbelieve have despaired of your religion, so do not fear them, but fear Me. Today I have perfected your religion for you, completed My favor upon you, and chosen Islam as your religion. But whoever is compelled by severe hunger with no inclination toward sin—then God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","They ask you what has been made lawful for them. Say, “The good things have been made lawful for you, and what you have trained of hunting animals, training them as God has taught you. So eat of what they catch for you, and mention God’s name over it. And be mindful of God. Surely, God is swift in reckoning.”","Today the good things have been made lawful for you. The food of those who were given the Scripture is lawful for you, and your food is lawful for them. And chaste women from among the believers and chaste women from among those who were given the Scripture before you—when you have given them their due compensation, being chaste yourselves, neither fornicating nor taking secret lovers. Whoever rejects faith, his deeds have been nullified, and in the Hereafter he will be among the losers.","O you who believe, when you rise for prayer, wash your faces and your hands up to the elbows, wipe your heads, and your feet up to the ankles. If you are in a state of major impurity, purify yourselves. If you are ill, or on a journey, or one of you has come from relieving himself, or you have touched women, and you find no water, then turn to clean earth and wipe your faces and your hands with it. God does not wish to place any hardship on you, but He wishes to purify you and to complete His blessing upon you, so that you may be grateful.","Remember God’s blessing upon you and His covenant by which He bound you, when you said, “We hear and we obey.” Be mindful of God. Truly, God is All-Knowing of what lies within hearts.","O you who believe, be steadfast for God, witnesses in justice. Let not the hatred of a people drive you to be unjust. Be just — that is closer to God-consciousness. Be mindful of God. Surely, God is All-Aware of what you do.","God has promised those who believe and do righteous deeds — for them is forgiveness and a great reward.","Those who disbelieve and deny Our signs — those are the companions of the Blaze.","O you who believe, remember God’s blessing upon you when a people intended to stretch their hands against you, and He restrained their hands from you. Be mindful of God, and in God let the believers place their trust.","God took the covenant of the Children of Israel, and We raised from among them twelve leaders. God said, “I am with you. If you establish the prayer, give the charity, believe in My messengers, support them, and lend God a good loan, I will surely erase your sins and admit you into gardens beneath which rivers flow. Whoever among you disbelieves after that has strayed from the right path.”","Because they broke their covenant, We cursed them and made their hearts hard. They distort words from their proper places and forgot a portion of what they were reminded of. You will never cease to discover treachery from them, except a few of them. So pardon them and overlook. Truly, God loves those who do good.","From those who said, “We are Christians,” We took their covenant, but they forgot a portion of what they were reminded of. So We stirred among them enmity and hatred until the Day of Resurrection. God will inform them of what they used to do.","O People of the Book, Our messenger has come to you, making clear to you much of what you used to conceal of the Book, and overlooking much. There has come to you from God a light and a clear Book.","Through it God guides whoever pursues His pleasure to the paths of peace, and He brings them out of darkness into light by His permission, and He guides them to a straight path.","Certainly those who said, “God is the Messiah, son of Mary,” have disbelieved. Say, “Who could prevent God in the least if He wished to destroy the Messiah, son of Mary, and his mother, and everyone on earth altogether?” To God belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth and everything between them. He creates what He wills. God is Capable of all things.","The Jews and the Christians said, “We are God’s children and His beloved.” Say, “Then why does He punish you for your sins?” Rather, you are human beings among those He created. He forgives whom He wills and punishes whom He wills. To God belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth and everything between them, and to Him is the final return.","O People of the Book, Our messenger has come to you, making things clear to you after a gap between messengers, lest you say, “No bearer of good news or warner came to us.” Now a bearer of good news and a warner has come to you. God is Capable of all things.","Remember when Moses said to his people, “O my people, remember God’s blessing upon you when He placed among you prophets, made you kings, and gave you what He had not given anyone in all the worlds.","O my people, enter the holy land that God has ordained for you, and do not turn back on your heels, or you will become losers.”","They said, “O Moses, in it is a tyrannical people, and we will never enter it until they leave. If they leave, then we will enter.”","Two men among those who feared, whom God had blessed, said, “Enter upon them through the gate — once you have entered it, you will surely prevail. And put your trust in God, if you are believers.”","They said, “O Moses, we will never enter it, ever, as long as they are in it. So go, you and your Lord, and fight. We are sitting right here.”","He said, “My Lord, I have no power over anyone but myself and my brother. So separate us from the defiantly disobedient people.”","He said, “Then it is forbidden to them for forty years — they will wander the earth. So do not grieve over the defiantly disobedient people.”","Recite to them the story of Adam’s two sons in truth: when they both offered a sacrifice, it was accepted from one of them but not accepted from the other. He said, “I will surely kill you.” He said, “God only accepts from the righteous.","If you stretch your hand toward me to kill me, I will not stretch my hand toward you to kill you. Truly, I fear God, Lord of the worlds.","I want you to bear my sin and your sin, and so become one of the companions of the Fire. That is the recompense of the wrongdoers.”","So his soul prompted him to kill his brother, and he killed him, and became one of the losers.","Then God sent a crow scratching in the ground to show him how to conceal his brother’s corpse. He said, “Woe to me! Am I too helpless to be like this crow and conceal my brother’s corpse?” And he became one of the regretful.","Because of that, We ordained for the Children of Israel that whoever kills a soul — not in retribution for a soul or for corruption in the land — it is as if he killed all of mankind, and whoever saves one, it is as if he saved all of mankind. Certainly Our messengers came to them with clear proofs, yet many of them after that were truly excessive in the land.","The only recompense for those who wage war against God and His Messenger and spread corruption in the land is that they be killed, or crucified, or have their hands and feet cut off on opposite sides, or be exiled from the land. That is disgrace for them in this world, and in the Hereafter they will have a tremendous punishment.","Except those who repent before you overpower them. Know that God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","O you who believe, be mindful of God and seek the means of nearness to Him, and strive in His cause, so that you may succeed.","Truly, those who disbelieved — even if they possessed everything on earth and its equal with it to ransom themselves from the punishment of the Day of Resurrection, it would not be accepted from them. For them is a painful punishment.","They will want to escape the Fire, but they will never escape it. For them is a lasting punishment.","As for the male thief and the female thief, cut off their hands as recompense for what they earned — a deterrent from God. God is Almighty, All-Wise.","Whoever repents after his wrongdoing and reforms, then God will turn to him in mercy. Surely God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","Do you not know that to God belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth? He punishes whom He wills and forgives whom He wills. God is Capable of all things.","O Messenger, do not be grieved by those who rush into disbelief—among those who say “We believe” with their mouths while their hearts do not believe, and among those who are Jews. They are avid listeners to falsehood, avid listeners on behalf of other people who have not come to you. They distort words from their proper places, saying, “If you are given this, take it, but if you are not given it, beware.” Whoever God wills to put to trial—you will never have any power to help him against God. Those are the ones whose hearts God did not will to purify. For them in this world is disgrace, and for them in the Hereafter is a tremendous punishment.","They are avid listeners to falsehood, devourers of unlawful gain. So if they come to you, judge between them or turn away from them. If you turn away from them, they will never harm you in the least. And if you judge, then judge between them with justice. Truly, God loves those who are just.","But how can they make you their judge when they have the Torah, in which is God’s judgment, and then they turn away after that? Those are not believers.","We sent down the Torah, in it guidance and light. The prophets who submitted judged by it for those who were Jewish, as did the rabbis and the scholars, according to what they were entrusted to preserve of God’s Book, and they were witnesses over it. So do not fear people — fear Me. And do not sell My verses for a small price. Whoever does not judge by what God sent down — those are the disbelievers.","We prescribed for them in it: a life for a life, an eye for an eye, a nose for a nose, an ear for an ear, a tooth for a tooth, and for wounds equal retaliation. But whoever forgoes it as charity, it will be an expiation for him. Whoever does not judge by what God sent down — those are the wrongdoers.","We sent Jesus son of Mary following in their footsteps, confirming what was before him of the Torah. And We gave him the Gospel, in it guidance and light, confirming what was before him of the Torah, and as guidance and admonition for the God-conscious.","Let the people of the Gospel judge by what God sent down in it. Whoever does not judge by what God sent down — those are the defiantly disobedient.","We sent down to you the Book in truth, confirming what was before it of the Scripture and as a guardian over it. So judge between them by what God sent down, and do not follow their desires away from the truth that has come to you. For each of you We appointed a law and a path. Had God willed, He would have made you one community, but He tests you through what He has given you. So race toward good deeds. To God is your return, all of you, and He will inform you of what you used to differ over.","Judge between them by what God sent down, and do not follow their desires, and beware of them lest they tempt you away from some of what God sent down to you. If they turn away, then know that God only intends to afflict them for some of their sins. Truly, many of the people are defiantly disobedient.","Is it the judgment of ignorance they seek? Who is better than God in judgment for a people who are certain?","O you who believe, do not take the Jews and the Christians as allies. They are allies of one another. Whoever among you allies with them is one of them. Truly, God does not guide the wrongdoing people.","You see those in whose hearts is a disease rushing toward them, saying, “We fear that a turn of fortune may strike us.” But perhaps God will bring victory or a command from Him, and they will come to regret what they concealed within themselves.","And those who believe will say, “Are these the ones who swore by God their most solemn oaths that they were with you?” Their deeds have come to nothing, and they have become losers.","O you who believe, whoever among you turns back from his religion, God will bring a people He loves and who love Him — humble toward the believers, mighty against the disbelievers, striving in God’s way, never fearing the blame of any critic. That is God’s grace; He gives it to whom He wills. God is All-Encompassing, All-Knowing.","Your ally is only God, His Messenger, and those who believe — those who establish prayer and give charity while they bow.","Whoever allies with God, His Messenger, and those who believe — then surely God’s party are the victors.","O you who believe, do not take as allies those who made your religion a mockery and a game — from among those given the Scripture before you and the disbelievers. Be mindful of God, if you are believers.","When you call to prayer, they take it as a mockery and a game. That is because they are a people who do not reason.","Say, “O People of the Scripture, do you resent us for anything other than that we believed in God and what was sent down to us and what was sent down before, and that most of you are defiantly disobedient?”","Say, “Shall I tell you of something worse than that in recompense with God? Those whom God cursed and with whom He was wrathful, and He made from among them apes and pigs and worshippers of false gods — those are worse in standing and further astray from the right path.”","When they come to you they say, “We believe,” yet they entered with disbelief and they left with it. God knows best what they were concealing.","You see many of them rushing into sin, aggression, and consuming what is unlawful. How wretched is what they were doing!","Why do the rabbis and scholars not forbid them from speaking sinfully and consuming what is unlawful? How wretched is what they were producing!","The Jews said, “God’s hand is chained.” Their hands are chained, and they are cursed for what they said. Rather, His hands are wide open — He spends however He wills. What has been sent down to you from your Lord will surely increase many of them in tyranny and disbelief. We have cast enmity and hatred among them until the Day of Resurrection. Every time they kindle a fire for war, God extinguishes it. They strive to spread corruption in the land, and God does not love the corrupters.","If the People of the Book had believed and been righteous, We would have erased their sins and admitted them into Gardens of Bliss.","Had they upheld the Torah and the Gospel and what was sent down to them from their Lord, they would have eaten from above them and from beneath their feet. Among them is a moderate community, but many of them — how evil is what they do.","O Messenger, convey what has been sent down to you from your Lord. If you do not, then you have not delivered His message. God will protect you from the people. Truly, God does not guide the disbelieving people.","Say, “O People of the Book, you stand on nothing until you uphold the Torah and the Gospel and what has been sent down to you from your Lord.” What has been sent down to you from your Lord will surely increase many of them in tyranny and disbelief. So do not grieve over the disbelieving people.","Surely those who believe, those who are Jewish, the Sabians, and the Christians — whoever believes in God and the Last Day and does good — no fear will be upon them, nor will they grieve.","We took the covenant of the Children of Israel and sent messengers to them. Every time a messenger came to them with what their souls did not desire, some they denied and some they killed.","They assumed there would be no trial, so they became blind and deaf. Then God turned to them in mercy, then many of them again became blind and deaf. God is All-Seeing of what they do.","Truly, those who said, “God is the Christ, son of Mary,” have disbelieved. Yet the Christ said, “O Children of Israel, worship God, my Lord and your Lord. Whoever associates partners with God, God has forbidden him Paradise, and his refuge is the Fire.” For the wrongdoers there are no helpers.","Truly, those who said, “God is the third of three,” have disbelieved. There is no god but One God. If they do not stop what they are saying, a painful punishment will surely strike those among them who disbelieved.","Will they not repent to God and seek His forgiveness? God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","The Christ, son of Mary, was only a messenger — messengers had passed before him — and his mother was a woman of truth. They both used to eat food. Look how We make the verses clear to them, then look how they are deluded.","Say, “Do you worship besides God what has no power to harm or benefit you?” God — He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.","Say, “O People of the Book, do not exceed the bounds in your religion beyond the truth, and do not follow the desires of a people who went astray before and led many astray and strayed from the right path.”","Those among the Children of Israel who disbelieved were cursed by the tongue of David and Jesus, son of Mary. That was because they disobeyed and used to transgress.","They would not forbid one another from the evil they committed. How wretched was what they used to do!","You see many of them allying with those who disbelieved. How wretched is what their souls sent ahead for them — that God’s wrath fell upon them, and in the punishment they will remain forever.","Had they believed in God and the Prophet and what was sent down to him, they would not have taken them as allies, but many of them are defiantly disobedient.","You will surely find the most hostile of people toward the believers to be the Jews and the polytheists. And you will surely find the nearest of them in affection toward the believers to be those who say, “We are Christians.” That is because among them are priests and monks, and because they are not arrogant.","When they hear what has been sent down to the Messenger, you see their eyes overflowing with tears because of the truth they recognize. They say, “Our Lord, we believe, so record us among the witnesses.","Why should we not believe in God and what has come to us of the truth, when we hope that our Lord will admit us among the righteous people?”","So God rewarded them for what they said with gardens beneath which rivers flow, dwelling therein forever. That is the recompense of those who do good.","But those who disbelieved and denied Our signs — those are the companions of the Blazing Fire.","O you who believe, do not forbid the good things God has made lawful for you, and do not transgress. Truly, God does not love the transgressors.","Eat of what God has provided you, lawful and good. And be mindful of God, in whom you believe.","God does not hold you accountable for idle talk in your oaths, but He holds you accountable for oaths you have bound yourselves to. Its expiation is feeding ten needy people from the average of what you feed your families, or clothing them, or freeing a slave. Whoever cannot find the means, then fasting for three days. That is the expiation for your oaths when you have sworn. Guard your oaths. Thus God makes His signs clear to you, so that you may be grateful.","O you who believe, intoxicants, gambling, stone altars, and divining arrows are nothing but filth from the work of Satan, so avoid them, that you may prosper.","Satan only wants to sow enmity and hatred among you through intoxicants and gambling, and to turn you away from the remembrance of God and from prayer. So will you stop?","Obey God and obey the Messenger, and beware. But if you turn away, then know that Our Messenger’s only duty is clear delivery.","There is no blame on those who believe and do good deeds for what they consumed, so long as they were mindful and believed and did good deeds, then were righteous and believed, then were God-conscious and did good. God loves those who do good.","O you who believe, God will surely test you with something of game within reach of your hands and your spears, so that God may know who fears Him in the unseen. Whoever transgresses after that — for him is a painful punishment.","O you who believe, do not kill game while you are in a state of consecration. Whoever among you kills it deliberately, the recompense is the equivalent of what he killed from livestock, as judged by two just men among you, an offering delivered to the Kaaba — or an expiation of feeding the needy, or its equivalent in fasting — so that he may taste the consequence of his deed. God has pardoned what is past, but whoever repeats it, God will take vengeance on him. God is Almighty, Possessor of Vengeance.","The catch of the sea and its food are made lawful for you, as provision for you and for travelers, but the game of the land is forbidden to you as long as you are in a state of consecration. Be mindful of God, to whom you will be gathered.","God has made the Kaaba, the Sacred House, a means of support for people, and the sacred month, and the offerings, and the garlanded animals. That is so you may know that God knows what is in the heavens and what is in the earth, and that God is All-Knowing of everything.","Know that God is severe in punishment and that God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","The Messenger’s only duty is to convey. God knows what you reveal and what you conceal.","Say, “The foul and the good are not equal, even if the abundance of the foul impresses you. So be mindful of God, O people of understanding, that you may succeed.”","O you who believe, do not ask about things that, if made clear to you, would distress you. But if you ask about them while the Quran is being sent down, they will be made clear to you. God has pardoned them. God is All-Forgiving, All-Forbearing.","A people before you asked such questions, then became disbelievers because of them.","God did not institute a bahirah, nor a sa’ibah, nor a wasilah, nor a ham. But those who disbelieve fabricate lies against God, and most of them do not reason.","When they are told, “Come to what God has sent down and to the Messenger,” they say, “Enough for us is what we found our fathers upon.” Even though their fathers knew nothing and were not guided?","O you who believe, guard yourselves. Those who stray cannot harm you if you are guided. To God is your return, all of you, and He will inform you of what you used to do.","O you who believe, when death approaches one of you, at the time of making a bequest, let testimony among you be by two just persons from among you, or two others from outside you if you are traveling through the land and the calamity of death strikes you. Detain them after the prayer, and if you have doubt, let them swear by God, “We will not sell it for any price, even if it concerns a relative, and we will not conceal God’s testimony — surely then we would be among the sinners.”","If it is discovered that those two deserved the charge of sin, then let two others stand in their place from among those whose rights were violated — the two nearest — and let them swear by God, “Our testimony is truer than their testimony, and we have not transgressed — surely then we would be among the wrongdoers.”","That makes it more likely that they will give testimony in its true form, or fear that oaths will be overturned after their oaths. Be mindful of God and listen. God does not guide the defiantly disobedient people.","The Day God gathers the messengers and says, “What response were you given?” They say, “We have no knowledge. Truly, You are the Knower of all that is unseen.”","When God said, “O Jesus, son of Mary, remember My favor upon you and upon your mother: when I strengthened you with the Holy Spirit, you spoke to people in the cradle and in maturity; when I taught you the Scripture, wisdom, the Torah, and the Gospel; when you fashioned from clay the shape of a bird by My leave, then breathed into it and it became a bird by My leave; and you healed the blind and the leper by My leave; and when you raised the dead by My leave; and when I restrained the Children of Israel from you when you came to them with clear proofs, and those among them who disbelieved said, ‘This is nothing but plain sorcery.’”","When I inspired the disciples, “Believe in Me and in My messenger,” they said, “We believe, and bear witness that we submit.”","When the disciples said, “O Jesus, son of Mary, can your Lord send down to us a table from the sky?” He said, “Be mindful of God, if you are believers.”","They said, “We wish to eat from it, and let our hearts be at ease, and know that you have told us the truth, and be among its witnesses.”","Jesus, son of Mary, said, “O God, our Lord, send down to us a table from the sky — it will be a feast for us, for the first of us and the last of us, and a miracle from You. Provide for us, and You are the best of providers.”","God said, “I will send it down to you. But whoever among you disbelieves after that, I will punish him with a punishment I have not punished anyone in all the worlds.”","When God said, “O Jesus, son of Mary, did you tell people, ‘Take me and my mother as two gods besides God’?” He said, “Glory be to You! It is not for me to say what I have no right to. If I had said it, You would have known it. You know what is within me, but I do not know what is within You. Truly, You are the Knower of all that is unseen.”","I said nothing to them except what You commanded me: “Worship God, my Lord and your Lord.” I was a witness over them as long as I was among them, but when You took me, You were the Watcher over them. You are Witness over all things.","If You punish them, they are Your servants. And if You forgive them, You are the Almighty, the All-Wise.","God said, “This is the Day when the truthful will benefit from their truthfulness.” For them are gardens beneath which rivers flow, dwelling therein forever. God is pleased with them and they are pleased with Him. That is the supreme triumph.","To God belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth and all that is within them. He is Capable of all things.","All praise belongs to God, who created the heavens and the earth and made darknesses and light. Yet those who disbelieve equate others with their Lord.","He is the One who created you from clay, then decreed a term — and a named term is with Him — yet still you doubt.","He is God in the heavens and on the earth. He knows your secret and your open speech, and He knows what you earn.","Not a sign comes to them from their Lord’s signs except that they turn away from it.","They denied the truth when it came to them, so the news of what they used to mock will come to them.","Have they not seen how many generations We destroyed before them? We had established them on the earth as We never established you, and We sent the sky upon them pouring rain, and We made rivers flow beneath them — then We destroyed them for their sins and raised after them another generation.","Even if We had sent down to you a book on parchment and they touched it with their own hands, those who disbelieve would have said, “This is nothing but clear sorcery.”","They said, “Why has no angel been sent down to him?” Had We sent down an angel, the matter would have been settled, and then they would not be given respite.","Had We made him an angel, We would have made him a man, and We would have confused for them what they already confuse.","Messengers before you were mocked, but what they mocked closed in on those who ridiculed them.","Say, “Travel through the earth, then see what became of the deniers.”","Say, “To whom belongs everything in the heavens and the earth?” Say, “To God. He has prescribed mercy upon Himself. He will surely gather you to the Day of Resurrection, about which there is no doubt.” Those who have lost their own souls — they do not believe.","To Him belongs whatever dwells in the night and the day. He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.","Say, “Should I take a protector other than God, the Originator of the heavens and the earth, when He feeds and is not fed?” Say, “I have been commanded to be the first to submit,” and do not be among those who associate partners with God.","Say, “I fear, if I disobey my Lord, the punishment of a tremendous Day.”","Whoever is spared it on that Day — He has shown him mercy. That is the clear triumph.","If God touches you with harm, none can remove it but Him. And if He touches you with good, He is Capable of all things.","He is the Vanquisher over His servants. He is the All-Wise, the All-Aware.","Say, “What is greatest in testimony?” Say, “God is witness between me and you. This Quran has been revealed to me so that I may warn you with it, and whoever it reaches. Do you truly testify that there are other gods besides God?” Say, “I do not testify to that.” Say, “He is only one God, and I am innocent of what you associate with Him.”","Those to whom We gave the Scripture recognize him as they recognize their own sons. Those who have lost their own souls — they do not believe.","Who is more unjust than one who fabricates a lie against God or denies His verses? Surely the unjust will never succeed.","On the Day We gather them all together, then We will say to those who associated partners with God, “Where are your partners that you used to claim?”","Then their only excuse will be to say, “By God, our Lord, we were never those who associated partners.”","Look how they lied against themselves, and what they used to fabricate has deserted them.","Among them are those who listen to you, but We have placed coverings over their hearts so they cannot understand it, and deafness in their ears. Even if they see every sign, they will not believe in it. Until, when they come to you arguing with you, those who disbelieve say, “This is nothing but tales of the ancients.”","They forbid others from it and distance themselves from it, yet they destroy none but themselves, and they do not realize.","If only you could see when they are made to stand before the Fire and say, “If only we could be sent back! We would not deny the verses of our Lord, and we would be among the believers.”","Rather, what they used to conceal before has become apparent to them. And even if they were sent back, they would return to what they were forbidden from. Truly, they are liars.","They said, “There is nothing but our worldly life, and we will not be resurrected.”","If only you could see when they are made to stand before their Lord. He says, “Is this not the truth?” They say, “Yes, by our Lord!” He says, “Then taste the punishment for what you used to deny.”","Certainly, those who denied the meeting with God have lost. Until, when the Hour comes upon them suddenly, they say, “O our grief for what we neglected regarding it!” And they carry their burdens on their backs. How wretched is what they carry!","The worldly life is nothing but play and amusement. Surely the home of the Hereafter is better for the God-conscious. Will you not reason?","We know that what they say grieves you. It is not you they deny, but it is God’s verses that the wrongdoers reject.","Messengers before you were denied, yet they endured patiently what they were denied and harmed by, until Our help came to them. None can alter God’s words. There has already come to you some news of the messengers.","If their turning away weighs heavily on you, then if you are able to seek a tunnel into the earth or a ladder into the sky to bring them a sign — had God willed, He would have gathered them all upon guidance. So do not be among the ignorant.","Only those who listen will respond. As for the dead, God will raise them, then to Him they will be returned.","They say, “Why has no sign been sent down to him from his Lord?” Say, “God is certainly Capable to send down a sign, but most of them do not know.”","There is no creature on earth, nor any bird flying with its wings, but they are communities like you. We have neglected nothing in the Book. Then to their Lord they will be gathered.","Those who denied Our verses are deaf and mute, in darkness. Whoever God wills, He leads astray, and whoever He wills, He places on a straight path.","Say, “Tell me: if God’s punishment came upon you or the Hour overtook you, would you call upon anyone other than God, if you are truthful?”","“No, it is Him alone you would call upon, and He would remove what you called upon Him for, if He willed, and you would forget what you associate with Him.”","We sent messengers to nations before you, and We seized them with hardship and adversity so that they might humble themselves.","If only they had humbled themselves when Our might came upon them! But their hearts hardened, and Satan made what they were doing seem appealing to them.","When they forgot what they had been reminded of, We opened upon them the gates of everything, until, just as they were rejoicing in what they had been given, We seized them suddenly — and at once they were in despair.","So the last remnant of the people who wronged was cut off. All praise belongs to God, Lord of all worlds.","Say, “Tell me: if God took away your hearing and your sight and sealed your hearts, what god other than God could restore them to you?” Look how We lay out the verses, yet they turn away.","Say, “Tell me: if God’s punishment came upon you suddenly or openly, would any be destroyed but the wrongdoing people?”","We send the messengers only as bearers of good news and as warners. So whoever believes and reforms — no fear will be upon them, nor will they grieve.","Those who deny Our signs — the punishment will touch them for their defiance.","Say, “I do not tell you that I possess God’s treasuries, nor do I know the unseen, nor do I tell you that I am an angel. I only follow what is revealed to me.” Say, “Are the blind and the seeing equal?” Will you not reflect?","Warn with it those who fear being gathered to their Lord — they have no protector or intercessor besides Him — so that they may be mindful.","Do not drive away those who call upon their Lord morning and evening, seeking His face. Nothing of their account falls on you, and nothing of your account falls on them. Were you to drive them away, you would be among the wrongdoers.","Thus We tested some of them through others, so they would say, “Are these the ones God has favored among us?” Is God not most knowing of the grateful?","When those who believe in Our verses come to you, say, “Peace be upon you. Your Lord has prescribed mercy upon Himself: whoever among you does evil out of ignorance, then repents after that and reforms — He is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.”","Thus We detail the verses, and so that the way of the criminals may become clear.","Say, “I have been forbidden to worship those you call upon besides God.” Say, “I will not follow your desires — I would then have gone astray and would not be among the guided.”","Say, “I stand on clear proof from my Lord, yet you have denied it. I do not possess what you seek to hasten. Judgment belongs to God alone. He declares the truth, and He is the best of judges.”","Say, “If I possessed what you seek to hasten, the matter would have been settled between me and you.” God is most knowing of the wrongdoers.","With Him are the keys of the unseen—none knows them but He. He knows what is on the land and in the sea. Not a leaf falls but He knows it, nor a grain in the darkness of the earth, nor anything moist or dry, but it is in a clear record.","He is the One who takes your souls by night and knows what you have committed by day, then raises you in it so that an appointed term may be fulfilled. Then to Him is your return, then He will inform you of what you used to do.","He is the Vanquisher over His servants. He sends guardians over you until, when death comes to one of you, Our messengers take his soul, and they never fail.","Then they are returned to God, their true Master. Truly, His is the judgment, and He is the swiftest of reckoners.","Say, “Who saves you from the darknesses of land and sea? You call upon Him in humility and in secret: ‘If He saves us from this, we will surely be among the grateful.’”","Say, “God saves you from it and from every distress, yet you associate others with Him.”","Say, “He is able to send upon you a punishment from above you or from beneath your feet, or to confuse you into factions and make some of you taste the violence of others.” Look how We turn the signs so that they may understand.","Your people have denied it, though it is the truth. Say, “I am not a guardian over you.”","Every prophecy has its appointed time, and you will come to know.","When you see those who engage in mockery of Our verses, turn away from them until they engage in another topic. And if Satan makes you forget, then after remembering, do not sit with the wrongdoing people.","Those who are God-conscious bear no responsibility for their account, but it is a reminder, so that they may be God-conscious.","Leave those who have taken their religion as play and amusement and whom the worldly life has deluded. Remind with it, lest a soul be ruined by what it has earned—it will have no protector or intercessor besides God. And if it offers every ransom, none will be accepted from it. Those are the ones who are ruined by what they earned. For them is a drink of scalding water and a painful punishment for what they used to deny.","Say, “Should we call upon, besides God, what neither benefits us nor harms us, and be turned back on our heels after God has guided us — like one the devils have lured away on earth, bewildered, while his companions call him to guidance: ‘Come to us!’?” Say, “Truly, God’s guidance is the guidance, and we have been commanded to submit to the Lord of all worlds.","And to establish the prayer and be mindful of Him. He is the One to whom you will be gathered.”","He is the One who created the heavens and the earth in truth. The Day He says “Be,” it is. His word is the truth. His is the dominion the Day the Horn is blown. Knower of the unseen and the seen, He is the All-Wise, the All-Aware.","And when Abraham said to his father Azar, “Do you take idols as gods? I see you and your people in clear misguidance.”","And so We showed Abraham the dominion of the heavens and the earth, that he might be among those with certainty.","When the night covered him, he saw a star. He said, “This is my Lord.” But when it set, he said, “I do not love those that set.”","When he saw the moon rising, he said, “This is my Lord.” But when it set, he said, “If my Lord does not guide me, I will surely be among the people who are lost.”","When he saw the sun rising, he said, “This is my Lord — this is greater!” But when it set, he said, “O my people, I am free of what you associate with God.","I have turned my face to the One who created the heavens and the earth, a monotheist, and I am not of those who associate others with God.”","His people argued with him. He said, “Do you argue with me about God when He has guided me? I do not fear what you associate with Him, unless my Lord wills something. My Lord encompasses all things in knowledge. Will you not then remember?","How should I fear what you have associated, while you do not fear that you have associated with God that for which He has sent down no authority to you? So which of the two groups has more right to security, if you know?”","Those who believe and do not taint their faith with wrongdoing — for them is security, and they are rightly guided.","That was Our argument We gave to Abraham against his people. We raise in degrees whoever We will. Your Lord is All-Wise, All-Knowing.","And We granted him Isaac and Jacob — each We guided. And Noah We guided before, and from his descendants: David, Solomon, Job, Joseph, Moses, and Aaron. Thus do We recompense those who do good.","And Zechariah, John, Jesus, and Elijah — each was among the righteous.","And Ishmael, Elisha, Jonah, and Lot — each We favored over all peoples.","And from their fathers, their descendants, and their brothers — We chose them and guided them to a straight path.","That is God’s guidance; He guides with it whoever He wills among His servants. Had they associated others with Him, all they did would have been lost.","Those are the ones We gave the Scripture, authority, and prophethood. If these people reject it, We have entrusted it to a people who will never reject it.","Those are the ones God guided, so follow their guidance. Say, “I ask you no payment for this. It is only a reminder for all peoples.”","They did not esteem God as He deserves to be esteemed when they said, “God has not sent down anything to any human.” Say, “Who sent down the Scripture that Moses brought as a light and guidance for people? You put it on scrolls, revealing some and concealing much. And you were taught what neither you nor your fathers knew.” Say, “God.” Then leave them in their idle talk, playing.","This is a blessed Scripture We have sent down, confirming what came before it, so that you may warn the Mother of Cities and those around it. Those who believe in the Hereafter believe in it, and they are diligent in their prayers.","Who is more unjust than one who fabricates a lie against God, or says, “I have received revelation,” when nothing was revealed to him, or one who says, “I will send down the like of what God has sent down”? If only you could see when the wrongdoers are in the throes of death and the angels stretch out their hands: “Give up your souls! Today you are repaid with the punishment of humiliation for what you used to say about God other than the truth, and for your arrogance toward His signs.”","You have come to Us alone, just as We created you the first time. You have left behind what We bestowed on you, and We do not see with you your intercessors whom you claimed were partners among you. The bond between you has been severed, and what you used to claim has forsaken you.","Truly, God is the splitter of seeds and date stones. He brings the living from the dead and brings the dead from the living. That is God — so how are you deluded?","The splitter of dawn, He made the night for rest and the sun and moon for reckoning. That is the decree of the All-Mighty, the All-Knowing.","He is the One who made the stars for you, so that you may find your way by them through the darkness of land and sea. We have made the signs clear for people who know.","He is the One who produced you from a single soul — then a place of settlement and a place of storage. We have made the signs clear for people who understand.","He is the One who sent down water from the sky, and with it We brought out the growth of every thing, and from it We brought out green shoots from which We produce clustered grain, and from the palm tree — from its sheaths — hanging clusters, and gardens of grapes, and olives, and pomegranates, alike and unlike. Look at its fruit when it bears fruit and its ripening. Surely in that are signs for people who believe.","They made the jinn partners with God, though He created them, and they fabricated for Him sons and daughters without knowledge. Glory be to Him! He is exalted above what they ascribe.","Originator of the heavens and the earth — how could He have a child when He has no companion, and He created all things, and He is All-Knowing of all things?","That is God, your Lord. There is no god but He, Creator of all things, so worship Him. He is Guardian over all things.","Vision cannot grasp Him, but He grasps all vision. He is the All-Subtle, the All-Aware.","Clear proofs have come to you from your Lord. Whoever sees, it is for his own benefit, and whoever is blind, it is to his own loss. I am not a keeper over you.","Thus We vary the verses — so that they may say, “You have studied,” and so that We may make it clear for people who know.","Follow what has been revealed to you from your Lord — there is no god but Him — and turn away from the polytheists.","Had God willed, they would not have associated partners with Him. We have not made you a guardian over them, and you are not a trustee over them.","Do not insult those they call upon besides God, lest they insult God out of hostility and ignorance. Thus We have made the deeds of every community seem appealing to them. Then to their Lord is their return, and He will inform them of what they used to do.","They swore by God their most solemn oaths that if a sign came to them, they would surely believe in it. Say, “The signs are only with God.” And what makes you realize that when they come, they will not believe?","We will turn their hearts and their eyes, just as they did not believe in it the first time, and We will leave them in their transgression, wandering blindly.","Even if We had sent down the angels to them, and the dead had spoken to them, and We had gathered everything before them face to face, they would not have believed unless God willed. But most of them are ignorant.","Thus We have made for every prophet an enemy — devils among humans and jinn — inspiring one another with gilded speech as a delusion. Had your Lord willed, they would not have done it. So leave them and what they fabricate.","So that the hearts of those who do not believe in the Hereafter may incline to it, and be pleased with it, and commit what they are committing.","Should I seek a judge other than God when it is He who sent down to you the Book, made clear? Those to whom We gave the Book know that it is sent down from your Lord in truth. So do not be among the doubters.","Your Lord’s word has been fulfilled in truth and justice. None can change His words. He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.","If you obey most of those on earth, they will lead you astray from God’s path. They follow nothing but conjecture, and they do nothing but guess.","Your Lord knows best who strays from His path, and He knows best the guided.","So eat of that over which God’s name has been mentioned, if you are believers in His verses.","Why would you not eat of that over which God’s name has been mentioned, when He has already detailed for you what He has forbidden to you — except what you are compelled to? Truly, many lead others astray by their desires without knowledge. Your Lord knows best the transgressors.","Abandon sin, both outward and inward. Truly, those who earn sin will be repaid for what they used to commit.","Do not eat of that over which God’s name has not been mentioned, for it is truly wickedness. The devils do inspire their allies to argue with you, and if you obey them, you are truly polytheists.","Is one who was dead and We gave him life and made for him a light by which he walks among people like one whose example is in the depths of darkness, never emerging from it? Thus what they used to do was made appealing to the disbelievers.","And so We placed in every town its greatest criminals to scheme therein. Yet they scheme only against themselves, and they do not realize it.","When a sign comes to them, they say, “We will never believe until we are given the like of what God’s messengers were given.” God knows best where to place His message. Humiliation before God and a severe punishment will strike those who committed crimes for what they used to scheme.","Whoever God wills to guide, He opens his chest to submission. And whoever He wills to lead astray, He makes his chest tight and constricted, as though he were climbing into the sky. Thus God places defilement upon those who do not believe.","This is your Lord’s path, made straight. We have detailed the verses for a people who take heed.","Theirs is the Abode of Peace with their Lord, and He is their Protector because of what they used to do.","On the Day He gathers them all together: “O assembly of jinn, you have exploited many of humankind.” Their allies among humankind will say, “Our Lord, we enjoyed one another, and we have reached the term You appointed for us.” He will say, “The Fire is your dwelling, abiding therein forever, except as God wills.” Your Lord is All-Wise, All-Knowing.","And so We make some of the wrongdoers allies of others because of what they used to earn.","“O assembly of jinn and humankind, did messengers not come to you from among you, relating to you My verses and warning you of the meeting of this Day of yours?” They will say, “We testify against ourselves.” The worldly life deluded them, and they will testify against themselves that they were disbelievers.","That is because your Lord would not destroy towns unjustly while their people were unaware.","For each there are ranks according to what they did, and your Lord is not unaware of what they do.","Your Lord is the Self-Sufficient, the Possessor of Mercy. If He wills, He can remove you and replace you with whatever He wills, just as He produced you from the descendants of another people.","Surely what you are promised is coming, and you cannot escape it.","Say, “O my people, act according to your position — I am acting. Soon you will know whose will be the final home. Truly, the wrongdoers do not succeed.”","They assigned to God a share of the crops and livestock He created, and they said, “This is for God” — so they claimed — “and this is for our partners.” But what was for their partners never reached God, while what was for God reached their partners. How wretched is their judgment!","Likewise, their partners made the killing of their children seem appealing to many of the polytheists, to ruin them and to confuse their religion for them. Had God willed, they would not have done it. So leave them and what they fabricate.","They said, “These livestock and crops are reserved — none may eat them except whom we please” — so they claimed — and livestock whose backs are forbidden, and livestock over which they do not mention God’s name, all as fabrication against Him. He will repay them for what they used to fabricate.","They said, “What is in the bellies of these livestock is exclusively for our males and forbidden to our wives, but if it is stillborn, they are partners in it.” He will repay them for their attribution. He is All-Wise, All-Knowing.","Lost are those who killed their children foolishly, without knowledge, and forbade what God had provided them, fabricating lies against God. They have gone astray and were never guided.","It is He who produced gardens, trellised and untrellised, and palm trees, and crops of diverse taste, and olives and pomegranates, alike and unlike. Eat of their fruit when they bear fruit, and give its due on the day of its harvest, and do not be excessive. He does not love the excessive.","And of the livestock, some for burden and some for slaughter. Eat of what God has provided you and do not follow Satan’s footsteps. He is a clear enemy to you.","Eight in pairs: two of sheep and two of goats. Say, “Is it the two males He has forbidden, or the two females, or what the wombs of the two females contain? Inform me with knowledge, if you are truthful.”","And two of camels and two of cattle. Say, “Is it the two males He has forbidden, or the two females, or what the wombs of the two females contain? Or were you witnesses when God charged you with this?” Who is more unjust than one who fabricates a lie against God to lead people astray without knowledge? Truly, God does not guide the wrongdoing people.","Say, “I find nothing in what has been revealed to me forbidden to one who would eat it, except that it be carrion, or blood poured out, or the flesh of swine — for it is filth — or a sinful offering invoked to other than God.” But whoever is compelled, neither craving nor transgressing, then your Lord is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","Upon the Jews We forbade every animal with claws, and of cattle and sheep We forbade them their fat, except what their backs carry, or the entrails, or what is mixed with bone. That is how We repaid them for their transgression, and We are truly truthful.","If they deny you, say, “Your Lord is of vast mercy, but His punishment will not be turned back from the criminal people.”","Those who associated partners with God will say, “Had God willed, we would not have associated anything, nor would our fathers, nor would we have forbidden anything.” Likewise did those before them deny until they tasted Our might. Say, “Do you have any knowledge you can produce for us? You follow nothing but assumption, and you do nothing but guess.”","Say, “To God belongs the conclusive argument. Had He willed, He would have guided you all.”","Say, “Bring your witnesses who testify that God forbade this.” If they testify, do not testify with them. Do not follow the desires of those who denied Our signs and those who do not believe in the Hereafter, and who set up equals to their Lord.","Say, “Come, let me recite what your Lord has forbidden you: that you associate nothing with Him, and be good to your parents, and do not kill your children out of poverty — We provide for you and for them — and do not approach indecencies, whether open or hidden, and do not kill the soul that God has made sacred except by right. This He has commanded you, so that you may reason.","Do not approach the orphan’s wealth except in the best manner until he reaches maturity. Give full measure and weight with justice — We do not burden a soul beyond its capacity. When you speak, be just, even if it concerns a relative. And fulfill God’s covenant. This He has commanded you, so that you may remember.","This is My path, straight, so follow it. Do not follow other ways, for they will scatter you from His path. This He has commanded you, so that you may be mindful.”","Then We gave Moses the Book, completing the favor upon the one who did good, and as a detailed explanation of all things, and as guidance and mercy, so that they might believe in the meeting with their Lord.","This is a Book We have sent down, blessed, so follow it and be mindful, so that you may be shown mercy.","Lest you say, “The Book was only sent down to two groups before us, and we were unaware of their studies.”","Or lest you say, “If only the Book had been sent down to us, we would have been better guided than them.” A clear proof has come to you from your Lord, and guidance and mercy. Who is more unjust than one who denies God’s verses and turns away from them? We will repay those who turn away from Our verses with the worst of punishment for their turning away.","Are they waiting for the angels to come to them, or for your Lord to come, or for some of your Lord’s signs to come? The day some of your Lord’s signs come, a soul’s faith will not benefit it if it had not believed before or earned good through its faith. Say, “Wait — We too are waiting.”","Those who divided their religion and became sects — you have nothing to do with them. Their affair rests with God; then He will inform them of what they used to do.","Whoever brings a good deed will have ten times its like, and whoever brings an evil deed will be repaid only its equal, and they will not be wronged.","Say, “My Lord has guided me to a straight path — an upright religion, the creed of Abraham, a monotheist. And he was not among the polytheists.”","Say, “My prayer, my worship, my life, and my death are for God, Lord of all worlds.","No partner has He. With this I have been commanded, and I am the first of those who submit.”","Say, “Should I seek a lord other than God, when He is the Lord of all things?” Every soul earns only against itself, and no bearer of burdens bears the burden of another. Then to your Lord is your return, and He will inform you of what you used to differ over.","It is He who made you successors on the earth and raised some of you above others in degrees, to test you through what He has given you. Truly your Lord is swift in punishment, yet He is surely All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","Alif Lam Mim Sad.","A Book sent down to you — so let there be no discomfort in your chest about it — that you may warn with it, and as a reminder for the believers.","Follow what has been sent down to you from your Lord, and do not follow protectors besides Him. How little you remember.","How many a town We destroyed — Our might came upon it by night or while they rested at midday.","Their only plea when Our might came upon them was to say, “We were wrongdoers.”","We will surely question those to whom messengers were sent, and We will surely question the messengers.","We will surely narrate to them with knowledge, for We were never absent.","The weighing on that Day is true. Those whose scales are heavy — they are the successful.","Those whose scales are light — they are the ones who lost their souls for the wrong they did to Our signs.","We established you on the earth and made for you livelihoods in it. How little you give thanks.","Truly We created you, then shaped you, then said to the angels, “Prostrate to Adam.” So they prostrated, except Iblis — he was not among those who prostrated.","He said, “What prevented you from prostrating when I commanded you?” He said, “I am better than him. You created me from fire and created him from clay.”","He said, “Then descend from it, for it is not for you to be arrogant in it. So get out — you are among the disgraced.”","He said, “Grant me respite until the Day they are resurrected.”","He said, “You are among those granted respite.”","He said, “Because You led me astray, I will surely sit in wait for them on Your straight path.","Then I will come at them from before them and from behind them, and from their right and from their left, and You will not find most of them grateful.”","He said, “Get out of it, despised and banished. Whoever among them follows you — I will surely fill Hell with all of you.”","“O Adam, dwell — you and your wife — in the Garden. Eat from wherever you wish, but do not approach this tree, or you will be among the wrongdoers.”","Then Satan whispered to them to expose what had been hidden from them of their nakedness, and he said, “Your Lord only forbade you this tree lest you become angels or become immortal.”","And he swore to them, “I am truly a sincere advisor to you both.”","So he lured them with deception. And when they tasted the tree, their nakedness became exposed to them, and they began covering themselves with leaves from the Garden. And their Lord called out to them, “Did I not forbid you from that tree and tell you that Satan is a clear enemy to you both?”","They said, “Our Lord, we have wronged ourselves, and if You do not forgive us and have mercy on us, we will surely be among the losers.”","He said, “Descend, some of you enemies to others. And on earth you will have a dwelling and provision for a time.”","He said, “In it you will live, and in it you will die, and from it you will be brought out.”","O Children of Adam, We have sent down to you clothing to cover your nakedness and as adornment. But the clothing of righteousness — that is better. That is one of God’s signs, so that they may remember.","O Children of Adam, do not let Satan tempt you as he drove your parents out of the Garden, stripping them of their clothing to expose their nakedness to them. He sees you — he and his tribe — from where you do not see them. We have made the devils allies of those who do not believe.","When they commit an indecency, they say, “We found our fathers doing it, and God commanded us to do it.” Say, “God does not command indecency. Do you say about God what you do not know?”","Say, “My Lord has commanded justice. Set your faces at every place of worship and call upon Him, devoting your faith sincerely to Him. As He originated you, so you will return.”","A group He guided, and upon a group misguidance was justly decreed. They took the devils as allies instead of God, and they think they are guided.","O Children of Adam, take your adornment at every place of worship, and eat and drink, but do not be excessive. He does not love the excessive.","Say, “Who has forbidden the adornment God has produced for His servants and the good things of provision?” Say, “They are for those who believe in the life of this world, and exclusively theirs on the Day of Resurrection.” Thus We detail the verses for people who know.","Say, “My Lord has only forbidden indecencies — what is apparent of them and what is hidden — and sin, and unjust aggression, and that you associate with God what He has sent down no authority for, and that you say about God what you do not know.”","For every nation is an appointed term. When their term arrives, they cannot delay it by a single hour, nor can they advance it.","O Children of Adam, if messengers from among you come to you recounting My verses to you — then whoever is God-conscious and does right, no fear will be upon them, nor will they grieve.","But those who denied Our verses and were arrogant toward them — those are the companions of the Fire; they will abide in it forever.","Who is more unjust than one who fabricates lies about God or denies His verses? Those will receive their share from the Book, until, when Our messengers come to take their souls, they say, “Where are those you used to call upon besides God?” They say, “They have abandoned us,” and they testify against themselves that they were disbelievers.","He says, “Enter the Fire among nations of jinn and humans that passed before you.” Every time a nation enters, it curses its sister, until, when they have all gathered together in it, the last of them says of the first, “Our Lord, these are the ones who led us astray, so give them a double punishment of the Fire.” He says, “For each is double, but you do not know.”","The first of them says to the last, “You had no advantage over us, so taste the punishment for what you used to earn.”","Truly, those who denied Our verses and were too arrogant for them — the gates of heaven will not be opened for them, nor will they enter Paradise until a camel passes through the eye of a needle. That is how We recompense the criminals.","For them is a bed of Hell, and above them are coverings. That is how We recompense the wrongdoers.","Those who believe and do righteous deeds — We do not burden any soul beyond its capacity — those are the people of Paradise; they will abide there forever.","We will have removed whatever resentment is in their hearts. Rivers flow beneath them, and they say, “Praise be to God, who guided us to this. We would never have been guided had God not guided us. Certainly, our Lord’s messengers came with the truth.” And they are called, “This is the Paradise you have been made to inherit for what you used to do.”","The people of Paradise call out to the people of the Fire, “We have found what our Lord promised us to be true. Have you found what your Lord promised to be true?” They say, “Yes.” Then a caller announces among them, “God’s curse is upon the wrongdoers.","Those who turn others from God’s path and seek to make it crooked, and who deny the Hereafter.”","Between them is a barrier, and on the Heights are men who recognize everyone by their marks. They call out to the people of Paradise, “Peace be upon you.” They have not yet entered it, though they long to.","When their eyes are turned toward the people of the Fire, they say, “Our Lord, do not place us among the wrongdoing people.”","The people of the Heights call out to men they recognize by their marks, saying, “Your accumulating has not availed you, nor has your arrogance.","Are these the ones you swore God would never reach with mercy? Enter Paradise — no fear upon you, nor will you grieve.”","The people of the Fire called out to the people of the Garden, “Pour some water on us, or some of what God has provided you.” They said, “God has forbidden both to the disbelievers.”","Those who took their religion as amusement and play, and whom the worldly life deluded. So today We forget them just as they forgot the meeting of this Day of theirs, and as they used to reject Our signs.","Certainly We brought them a Book that We detailed with knowledge — a guidance and a mercy for people who believe.","Are they waiting for anything but its fulfillment? The Day its fulfillment comes, those who had forgotten it before will say, “Our Lord’s messengers did come with the truth. Are there any intercessors for us to intercede on our behalf, or could we be sent back so we might act differently from what we used to do?” They have truly lost themselves, and what they used to fabricate has abandoned them.","Truly your Lord is God, who created the heavens and the earth in six days, then rose over the Throne. He covers the day with the night, chasing it relentlessly. And the sun, the moon, and the stars are subjected by His command. To Him belong creation and command. Blessed is God, Lord of all worlds.","Call upon your Lord humbly and in secret. He does not love the transgressors.","Do not spread corruption on the earth after it has been set right. Call upon Him in fear and hope. Surely God’s mercy is near to those who do good.","It is He who sends the winds as glad tidings before His mercy. When they carry heavy clouds, We drive them to a dead land, then We send down water through them, and We bring out every kind of fruit through it. Thus We bring out the dead, so that you may reflect.","The good land — its vegetation comes out by its Lord’s permission. But the bad produces nothing but scarcity. Thus We vary the verses for people who give thanks.","We sent Noah to his people, and he said, “O my people, worship God. You have no god other than Him. I fear for you the punishment of a tremendous Day.”","The chiefs of his people said, “We surely see you in clear error.”","He said, “O my people, there is no error in me, but I am a messenger from the Lord of all worlds.","I deliver to you the messages of my Lord and advise you, and I know from God what you do not know.","Are you astonished that a reminder has come to you from your Lord through a man from among you, to warn you and so that you may be mindful, and so that you may be shown mercy?”","But they denied him, so We saved him and those with him in the ark, and We drowned those who denied Our signs. They were truly a blind people.","And to Ad, their brother Hud. He said, “O my people, worship God. You have no god other than Him. Will you not be mindful?”","The chiefs who disbelieved among his people said, “We surely see you in foolishness, and we certainly think you are among the liars.”","He said, “O my people, there is no foolishness in me, but I am a messenger from the Lord of all worlds.","I deliver to you the messages of my Lord, and I am a trustworthy advisor to you.","Are you astonished that a reminder has come to you from your Lord through a man from among you, to warn you? And remember when He made you successors after the people of Noah and increased you in stature. So remember God’s blessings, that you may prosper.”","They said, “Have you come to us so that we worship God alone and abandon what our fathers used to worship? Then bring us what you threaten us with, if you are among the truthful.”","He said, “Defilement and wrath from your Lord have already fallen upon you. Do you argue with me over names that you and your fathers have coined, for which God has sent down no authority? Then wait; I am with you among those who wait.”","So We saved him and those with him by a mercy from Us, and We cut off the last remnant of those who denied Our verses. They were never believers.","To Thamud We sent their brother Salih. He said, “O my people, worship God. You have no god other than Him. A clear proof has come to you from your Lord. This is God’s she-camel, a sign for you. So leave her to graze in God’s land, and do not touch her with harm, or a painful punishment will seize you.","Remember when He made you successors after Ad and settled you in the land — you build palaces on its plains and carve houses from the mountains. So remember God’s blessings and do not spread corruption in the land.”","The arrogant chiefs of his people said to those who were oppressed — to those among them who believed, “Do you know that Salih is sent by his Lord?” They said, “We believe in what he has been sent with.”","Those who were arrogant said, “We reject what you believe in.”","So they hamstrung the she-camel and defied their Lord’s command and said, “O Salih, bring us what you threaten us with, if you are truly one of the messengers.”","So the earthquake seized them, and by morning they lay lifeless in their homes.","He turned away from them and said, “O my people, I delivered my Lord’s message to you and gave you sincere counsel, but you do not love those who give sincere counsel.”","And Lot, when he said to his people, “Do you commit an obscenity that no one in all the world has committed before you?","You approach men with desire instead of women. No, you are a people of excess.”","His people’s only response was to say, “Drive them out of your town. They are people who keep themselves pure!”","So We saved him and his family, except his wife — she was among those who stayed behind.","And We rained upon them a rain. So look at what became of the criminals.","To Midian We sent their brother Shuayb. He said, “O my people, worship God — you have no god other than Him. A clear proof has come to you from your Lord. So give full measure and weight, and do not shortchange people of their things, and do not spread corruption in the land after it has been set right. That is better for you, if you are believers.","Do not sit on every path, threatening and turning away from God’s path those who believe in Him, seeking to make it crooked. Remember when you were few and He multiplied you, and look at what became of the corrupters.","If a group among you believes in what I have been sent with and a group does not believe, then be patient until God judges between us. He is the best of judges.”","The arrogant chiefs among his people said, “We will surely drive you out, O Shuayb, you and those who believe with you, from our town, or you will return to our creed.” He said, “Even if we are unwilling?","We would be fabricating a lie against God if we returned to your creed after God has saved us from it. It is not for us to return to it unless God our Lord wills. Our Lord encompasses all things in knowledge. In God we place our trust. Our Lord, judge between us and our people in truth, for You are the best of judges.”","The disbelieving chiefs among his people said, “If you follow Shuayb, you will surely be losers.”","So the earthquake seized them, and by morning they lay lifeless in their homes.","Those who denied Shuayb — as though they had never lived there. Those who denied Shuayb — they were the losers.","He turned away from them and said, “O my people, I delivered to you my Lord’s messages and advised you sincerely. So how could I grieve for a disbelieving people?”","We never sent a prophet to any town without afflicting its people with hardship and adversity, so that they might humble themselves.","Then We replaced the bad with good, until they grew abundant and said, “Hardship and prosperity touched our fathers too.” So We seized them suddenly while they were unaware.","Had the people of those towns believed and been mindful, We would have opened upon them blessings from the sky and the earth. But they denied, so We seized them for what they used to earn.","Do the people of the towns feel secure that Our punishment will not come upon them at night while they sleep?","Or do the people of the towns feel secure that Our punishment will not come upon them in the morning while they play?","Do they feel secure from God’s plan? None feels secure from God’s plan except the losing people.","Has it not become clear to those who inherit the land after its people that, had We willed, We could have struck them for their sins? We seal their hearts, so they do not hear.","Those are the towns whose accounts We relate to you. Their messengers came to them with clear proofs, but they were never going to believe in what they had denied before. Thus does God seal the hearts of the disbelievers.","We found no commitment in most of them. We found most of them truly corrupt.","Then, after them, We sent Moses with Our miracles to Pharaoh and his chiefs, but they dealt unjustly with them. So see how the corrupters ended.","Moses said, “O Pharaoh, I am a messenger from the Lord of all worlds.","Duty-bound to say nothing about God but the truth. I have come to you with a clear proof from your Lord, so send the Children of Israel with me.”","He said, “If you have come with a miracle, then produce it, if you are truthful.”","So he cast his staff, and suddenly it was a serpent, plain for all to see.","And he drew out his hand, and suddenly it was white for the onlookers.","The chiefs of Pharaoh’s people said, “This is certainly a skilled sorcerer.","He wants to drive you out of your land. So what do you advise?”","They said, “Delay him and his brother, and send gatherers into the cities.","To bring you every skilled sorcerer.”","The sorcerers came to Pharaoh and said, “Surely there will be a reward for us if we are the victors?”","He said, “Yes, and you will be among those brought near.”","They said, “O Moses, either you throw, or we will be the ones to throw.”","He said, “Throw.” And when they threw, they bewitched the people’s eyes and terrified them, and they produced a great sorcery.","We revealed to Moses, “Throw your staff,” and at once it swallowed up what they were fabricating.","So the truth prevailed, and what they had been doing was nullified.","So they were defeated there and turned away humiliated.","The sorcerers fell down in prostration.","They said, “We believe in the Lord of all worlds.","The Lord of Moses and Aaron.”","Pharaoh said, “You believed in him before I gave you permission? This is a plot you have hatched in the city to drive its people out. Soon you will know.","I will cut off your hands and your feet on opposite sides, then I will crucify you all!”","They said, “To our Lord we are returning.","You only take revenge on us because we believed in the signs of our Lord when they came to us. Our Lord, pour patience upon us and take us in submission.”","The chiefs of Pharaoh’s people said, “Will you leave Moses and his people to spread corruption in the land and abandon you and your gods?” He said, “We will slaughter their sons and keep their women alive. We hold power over them.”","Moses said to his people, “Seek help from God and be patient. The earth belongs to God — He grants it to whomever He wills among His servants, and the outcome belongs to the God-conscious.”","They said, “We were harmed before you came to us and after you came to us.” He said, “Perhaps your Lord will destroy your enemy and make you successors in the land, then see how you act.”","Certainly We seized Pharaoh’s people with years of drought and shortage of fruits, so that they might take heed.","But when good came to them, they said, “This is ours.” And if misfortune struck them, they blamed it on Moses and those with him. Truly their ill omen lies only with God, but most of them do not know.","They said, “Whatever sign you bring us to bewitch us with, we will never believe in you.”","So We sent upon them the flood, the locusts, the lice, the frogs, and the blood—distinct signs—yet they were arrogant and were a criminal people.","And when the plague fell upon them, they said, “O Moses, call upon your Lord for us by what He has pledged with you. If you lift this plague from us, we will surely believe in you and send the Children of Israel with you.”","But when We lifted the plague from them for a term they were to reach, at once they broke their word.","So We took vengeance on them and drowned them in the sea, because they denied Our signs and were heedless of them.","And We made the people who had been oppressed inherit the eastern and western lands which We had blessed. And your Lord’s gracious word was fulfilled for the Children of Israel because they were patient. And We destroyed what Pharaoh and his people had built and what they used to erect.","And We brought the Children of Israel across the sea, and they came upon a people devoted to idols of theirs. They said, “O Moses, make for us a god just as they have gods.” He said, “You are truly a people acting in ignorance.","What these people are engaged in is doomed to destruction, and worthless is what they have been doing.”","He said, “Should I seek for you a god other than God, when He has favored you over all peoples?”","Remember when We saved you from Pharaoh’s people, who were inflicting on you the worst torment—slaughtering your sons and sparing your women. In that was a tremendous trial from your Lord.","We appointed for Moses thirty nights and completed them with ten, so his Lord’s appointed term was fulfilled at forty nights. Moses said to his brother Aaron, “Take my place among my people, set things right, and do not follow the way of the corrupters.”","When Moses came at Our appointed time and his Lord spoke to him, he said, “My Lord, show Yourself to me so I may look at You.” He said, “You will never see Me, but look at the mountain—if it remains firm in its place, then you will see Me.” When his Lord manifested Himself to the mountain, He leveled it, and Moses fell unconscious. When he recovered, he said, “Glory be to You! I repent to You, and I am the first of the believers.”","He said, “O Moses, I have chosen you above all people with My messages and My speech. So take what I have given you and be among the grateful.”","We inscribed for him on the Tablets instruction on all things and a detailed explanation of everything: “Hold on to them firmly and command your people to adopt the best of them. I will show you the home of the defiantly disobedient.”","I will turn away from My signs those who are arrogant on earth without right. Even if they see every sign, they will not believe in it. If they see the path of guidance, they will not take it as a path, but if they see the path of error, they will take it as a path. That is because they denied Our signs and were heedless of them.","Those who denied Our signs and the meeting of the Hereafter—their deeds have come to nothing. Will they be repaid for anything but what they used to do?","Moses’s people, after he left, made from their jewelry a calf—a body that lowed. Did they not see that it neither spoke to them nor guided them to any path? They took it up, and they were wrongdoers.","When remorse fell into their hands and they saw that they had gone astray, they said, “If our Lord does not have mercy on us and forgive us, we will surely be among the losers.”","When Moses returned to his people, angry and grieved, he said, “What a wretched way you succeeded me after I left! Did you rush your Lord’s command?” He threw down the tablets and seized his brother by the head, dragging him toward himself. He said, “Son of my mother, the people overpowered me and nearly killed me, so do not let the enemies gloat over me, and do not count me among the wrongdoing people.”","He said, “My Lord, forgive me and my brother, and admit us into Your mercy. You are the most merciful of the merciful.”","Those who took up the calf—wrath from their Lord will reach them, and humiliation in the life of this world. That is how We recompense the fabricators.","But those who committed evil deeds then repented after that and believed—truly your Lord, after that, is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","When the anger subsided from Moses, he picked up the tablets. In their text was guidance and mercy for those who stand in awe of their Lord.","Moses chose from his people seventy men for Our appointed time. When the quaking seized them, he said, “My Lord, had You willed, You could have destroyed them before, and me as well. Will You destroy us for what the fools among us have done? It is only Your trial—You lead astray by it whom You will and guide whom You will. You are our Protector, so forgive us and have mercy on us. You are the best of forgivers.","And decree for us good in this world and in the Hereafter. We have turned to You.” He said, “My punishment—I strike with it whom I will, but My mercy encompasses all things. I will decree it for the mindful who give charity, and who believe in Our verses.”","Those who follow the Messenger, the unlettered Prophet, whom they find written of in the Torah and the Gospel — he commands them to what is right and forbids them from what is wrong, makes lawful for them the good things and makes unlawful for them the foul things, and lifts from them their burden and the shackles that were upon them. So those who believe in him, honor him, support him, and follow the light that was sent down with him — those are the successful.","Say, “O people, I am God’s Messenger to you all — He to whom belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth. There is no god but He. He gives life and causes death. So believe in God and His Messenger, the unlettered Prophet, who believes in God and His words, and follow him, that you may be guided.”","Among Moses’s people is a community that guides by the truth and by it acts justly.","We divided them into twelve tribes as nations. And We revealed to Moses when his people asked him for water, “Strike the rock with your staff.” So twelve springs gushed from it. Each group knew its drinking place. And We shaded them with clouds and sent down upon them manna and quails. “Eat from the good things We have provided you.” They did not wrong Us, but they used to wrong themselves.","And they were told, “Settle in this town and eat from it wherever you wish, and say ‘Relieve us,’ and enter the gate in prostration — We will forgive you your sins. We will give more to those who do good.”","But those among them who did wrong substituted a word other than what they were told, so We sent upon them a plague from the sky for the wrong they used to do.","Ask them about the town that stood by the sea — when they transgressed on the Sabbath. Their fish would come to them surfacing on the day of their Sabbath, but on the day they did not observe the Sabbath, they would not come to them. Thus We tested them for their defiance.","When a group among them said, “Why do you admonish a people whom God will destroy or punish with a severe punishment?” They said, “As an excuse before your Lord, and perhaps they may become righteous.”","So when they forgot what they had been reminded of, We saved those who forbade evil and seized those who wronged with a wretched punishment for their defiance.","So when they persisted arrogantly in what they had been forbidden, We said to them, “Be despised apes!”","Your Lord declared that He would surely send against them, until the Day of Resurrection, those who would inflict on them the worst of punishment. Truly your Lord is swift in punishment, yet He is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","We scattered them across the earth as separate communities — among them the righteous, and among them those less than that. We tested them with good times and bad, so that they might return.","Then a generation succeeded them who inherited the Scripture, seizing the gains of this lowly world and saying, “We will be forgiven.” Yet if similar gains come their way, they seize them too. Was not the covenant of the Scripture taken from them that they would say nothing about God but the truth? And they have studied what is in it. The Home of the Hereafter is better for the God-conscious. Do you not reason?","Those who hold fast to the Scripture and establish prayer — We never waste the reward of those who set things right.","When We raised the mountain above them as though it were a canopy, and they thought it would fall upon them: “Hold firmly to what We have given you and remember what is in it, so that you may become righteous.”","When your Lord took from the children of Adam, from their loins, their descendants and made them testify against themselves: “Am I not your Lord?” They said, “Yes, we testify” — lest you say on the Day of Resurrection, “We were unaware of this.”","Or lest you say, “It was only our forefathers who associated partners before us, and we were merely descendants after them. Will You destroy us for what the falsifiers did?”","Thus We detail the verses, so that they may return.","Recite to them the story of the one to whom We gave Our verses, but he stripped himself of them, so Satan pursued him, and he became one of the deviant.","Had We willed, We would have elevated him through them, but he clung to the earth and followed his own desire. His example is like that of a dog: if you chase it, it pants, and if you leave it, it pants. That is the example of the people who denied Our verses. So relate the stories, that they may reflect.","Wretched is the example of the people who denied Our verses — it was themselves they were wronging.","Whoever God guides is truly guided, and whoever He leads astray — those are the losers.","Certainly We have destined for Hell many of the jinn and humans. They have hearts they do not understand with, they have eyes they do not see with, and they have ears they do not hear with. They are like cattle — rather, they are more astray. Those are the heedless.","To God belong the most beautiful names, so call upon Him by them. And leave those who deviate regarding His names. They will be repaid for what they used to do.","Among those We created is a community that guides by the truth and by it establishes justice.","Those who denied Our verses — We will gradually lead them to ruin from where they do not know.","I will give them time. Truly, My plan is firm.","Have they not reflected? There is no madness in their companion. He is nothing but a clear warner.","Have they not looked into the dominion of the heavens and the earth and everything God has created, and that perhaps their end has drawn near? So in what message after this will they believe?","Whoever God leads astray, there is no guide for him. He leaves them in their transgression, wandering blindly.","They ask you about the Hour — when will it arrive? Say, “Its knowledge is only with my Lord. None will reveal it at its time but He. It weighs heavy upon the heavens and the earth. It will not come upon you except suddenly.” They ask you as if you are well-informed about it. Say, “Its knowledge is only with God, but most people do not know.”","Say, “I have no power to bring benefit or harm to myself, except what God wills. If I knew the unseen, I would have gathered much good, and no harm would have touched me. I am nothing but a warner and a bearer of good news for people who believe.”","It is He who created you from a single soul and made from it its mate, so that he might find comfort in her. When he covered her, she carried a light burden and went about with it. Then when she grew heavy, they both called upon God, their Lord, “If You give us a healthy child, we will surely be among the grateful.”","But when He gave them a healthy child, they made partners for Him in what He had given them. Exalted is God above what they associate with Him.","Do they associate those who create nothing and are themselves created?","They cannot help them, nor can they help themselves.","If you call them to guidance, they will not follow you. It is the same for you whether you call upon them or you remain silent.","Truly, those you call upon besides God are servants like you. So call upon them and let them respond to you, if you are truthful.","Do they have feet to walk with? Or do they have hands to strike with? Or do they have eyes to see with? Or do they have ears to hear with? Say, “Call upon your partners, then plot against me and give me no respite.”","Surely my protector is God, who sent down the Book. He looks after the righteous.","Those you call upon besides Him cannot help you, nor can they help themselves.","If you call them to guidance, they do not hear. You see them looking at you, yet they do not see.","Hold to forgiveness, command what is right, and turn away from the ignorant.","If a provocation from Satan stirs you, seek refuge in God. Truly, He is All-Hearing, All-Knowing.","Those who are mindful, when a whisper from Satan touches them, they remember, and at once they see clearly.","But their brothers drag them deeper into error, then they never relent.","When you do not bring them a sign, they say, “Why have you not produced one?” Say, “I only follow what is revealed to me from my Lord. These are insights from your Lord, and guidance and mercy for a people who believe.”","When the Quran is recited, listen to it and be silent, so that you may be shown mercy.","Remember your Lord within yourself, humbly and in fear, in a voice below a shout, morning and evening, and do not be among the heedless.","Truly, those in the presence of your Lord are never too proud to worship Him. They glorify Him, and to Him they prostrate.","They ask you about the spoils of war. Say, “The spoils belong to God and the Messenger. So be mindful of God, mend what is between you, and obey God and His Messenger, if you are believers.”","The believers are only those whose hearts tremble when God is mentioned, and when His verses are recited to them, it increases them in faith, and they put their trust in their Lord.","Those who establish prayer and spend from what We have provided them.","Those are the true believers. For them are ranks with their Lord, and forgiveness, and a generous provision.","Just as your Lord brought you out of your home in truth, while a group of the believers were averse.","They argued with you about the truth after it had become clear, as though they were being driven to death while they looked on.","And when God promised you one of the two groups would be yours, you wished that the unarmed one would be yours. But God intended to establish the truth by His words and to cut off the last remnant of the disbelievers.","So that He would establish the truth and nullify falsehood, even if the criminals despised it.","When you cried out to your Lord for help, He answered you, “I will reinforce you with a thousand angels, following one another.”","God made it only as good news and so that your hearts would be reassured by it. Victory comes only from God. Truly, God is All-Mighty, All-Wise.","When He covered you with drowsiness as a security from Him, and sent down upon you water from the sky to purify you with it, to remove from you the filth of Satan, to strengthen your hearts, and to steady your feet.","When your Lord revealed to the angels, “I am with you, so strengthen those who believe. I will cast terror into the hearts of those who disbelieve, so strike above the necks and strike every fingertip of theirs.”","That is because they opposed God and His Messenger. And whoever opposes God and His Messenger — then surely God is severe in punishment.","That is yours, so taste it, and for the disbelievers is the punishment of the Fire.","O you who believe, when you meet those who disbelieve advancing in ranks, do not turn your backs to them.","Whoever turns his back to them on that day — unless maneuvering for battle or joining another group — has drawn upon himself wrath from God, and his refuge is Hell. What a wretched destination!","You did not kill them, but God killed them. You did not throw when you threw, but God threw — so that He might grant the believers a fine trial from Him. Truly, God is All-Hearing, All-Knowing.","That is so, and God weakens the scheming of the disbelievers.","If you sought a verdict, the verdict has come to you. If you desist, it is better for you. If you return, We will return, and your forces will avail you nothing, however numerous they may be — and God is with the believers.","O you who believe, obey God and His Messenger, and do not turn away from him while you hear.","Do not be like those who said, “We hear,” while they do not hear.","Surely the worst of creatures in God’s sight are the deaf and mute who do not reason.","Had God known any good in them, He would have made them hear. And even if He made them hear, they would have turned away in aversion.","O you who believe, respond to God and to the Messenger when he calls you to what gives you life. Know that God comes between a man and his heart, and that to Him you will be gathered.","Be mindful of a trial that will not strike only those among you who have wronged, and know that God is severe in punishment.","Remember when you were few and oppressed in the land, fearing that people would snatch you away. Then He sheltered you, strengthened you with His support, and provided you with good things, so that you might be grateful.","O you who believe, do not betray God and the Messenger, nor betray your trusts while you know.","Know that your wealth and your children are but a trial, and that with God is a tremendous reward.","O you who believe, if you are mindful of God, He will grant you a criterion, remove your misdeeds from you, and forgive you. God is the possessor of immense grace.","When the disbelievers plotted against you to imprison you, kill you, or expel you — they plotted and God plotted, and God is the best of plotters.","When Our verses are recited to them, they say, “We have heard. If we wished, we could say the like of this. This is nothing but tales of the ancients.”","When they said, “O God, if this is the truth from You, then rain down upon us stones from the sky or bring us a painful punishment.”","But God would not punish them while you were among them, and God would not punish them while they sought forgiveness.","Yet why should God not punish them when they bar others from the Sacred Mosque, and they were never its rightful guardians? Its rightful guardians are none but the God-conscious, but most of them do not know.","Their prayer at the House was nothing but whistling and clapping. So taste the punishment for your disbelief.","Those who disbelieve spend their wealth to bar others from God’s path. They will spend it, then it will become a source of anguish for them, then they will be defeated. And those who disbelieve will be gathered into Hell.","So that God may separate the wicked from the good, and heap the wicked one upon another, piling them all together, and cast them into Hell. Those are the losers.","Say to those who disbelieve, “If they cease, what has already passed will be forgiven them. But if they return, then the precedent of the ancients has already gone before.”","Fight them until there is no more persecution and religion belongs entirely to God. But if they cease, then surely God is All-Seeing of what they do.","But if they turn away, then know that God is your Protector. What an excellent Protector and what an excellent Helper.","Know that whatever you gain as spoils, a fifth of it belongs to God, the Messenger, the near relatives, the orphans, the needy, and the traveler — if you believe in God and what We sent down upon Our servant on the Day of Distinction, the day the two forces met. God is Capable of all things.","When you were on the near side of the valley and they were on the far side, and the caravan was below you. Had you made an appointment to meet, you would have disagreed over the timing. But it was so that God might carry out a matter already destined — so that whoever perished would perish upon clear proof, and whoever lived would live upon clear proof. Truly God is All-Hearing, All-Knowing.","When God showed them to you in your dream as few — had He shown them to you as many, you would have lost heart and disputed over the matter. But God kept you safe. He is All-Knowing of what lies within the hearts.","When He made them appear few in your eyes as you met, and made you appear few in their eyes — so that God might carry out a matter already destined. To God all matters return.","O you who believe, when you meet a force, stand firm and remember God often, so that you may succeed.","Obey God and His Messenger, and do not dispute with one another lest you lose heart and your strength departs. Be patient — surely God is with the patient.","Do not be like those who left their homes boastfully, showing off before people, and barring others from God’s path. God encompasses all that they do.","When Satan made their deeds appealing to them and said, “No one among people can overcome you today, and I am your protector.” But when the two forces came within sight of each other, he turned on his heels and said, “I disown you. I see what you do not see. I fear God.” God is severe in punishment.","When the hypocrites and those with disease in their hearts said, “Their religion has deluded these people.” But whoever puts his trust in God — surely God is All-Mighty, All-Wise.","If you could see when the angels take the souls of those who disbelieved, striking their faces and their backs: “Taste the punishment of the Blaze!”","That is for what your hands sent ahead, and God is never unjust to His servants.","Like the way of Pharaoh’s people and those before them — they denied God’s signs, so God seized them for their sins. Surely God is All-Strong, severe in punishment.","That is because God would never change a blessing He had bestowed upon a people until they change what is within themselves, and because God is All-Hearing, All-Knowing.","Like the way of Pharaoh’s people and those before them — they rejected the signs of their Lord, so We destroyed them for their sins and drowned Pharaoh’s people. All of them were wrongdoers.","Truly, the worst of creatures in God’s sight are those who disbelieve — they will not believe.","Those of them with whom you made a treaty, then they break their pledge every time, and they are not righteous.","So if you encounter them in war, make a harsh example of them for those behind them, so that they may take heed.","And if you fear treachery from a people, cast their treaty back to them on equal terms. Truly, God does not love the treacherous.","Let not those who disbelieve think they have escaped. They cannot escape.","And prepare against them whatever force you can and cavalry at the ready, to strike terror into God’s enemy and your enemy, and others beyond them you do not know — God knows them. Whatever you spend in God’s cause will be repaid to you in full, and you will not be wronged.","And if they incline toward peace, then incline toward it, and put your trust in God. He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.","And if they intend to deceive you, then God is enough for you. It is He who strengthened you with His support and with the believers.","And He united their hearts. Had you spent all that is on earth, you could not have united their hearts, but God united them. He is All-Mighty, All-Wise.","O Prophet, God is sufficient for you and for whoever follows you among the believers.","O Prophet, urge the believers to fight. If there are twenty steadfast among you, they will overcome two hundred. And if there are a hundred of you, they will overcome a thousand of those who disbelieve, because they are a people who do not understand.","Now God has lightened your burden, for He knows there is weakness among you. So if there are a hundred steadfast among you, they will overcome two hundred. And if there are a thousand of you, they will overcome two thousand, by God’s permission. God is with the steadfast.","It is not for a prophet to have captives until he has thoroughly subdued in the land. You desire the gains of this world, but God desires the Hereafter. God is All-Mighty, All-Wise.","Were it not for a decree from God that had already gone before, a tremendous punishment would have touched you for what you took.","So eat of what you have gained, lawful and good, and be mindful of God. Truly, God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","O Prophet, say to the captives in your hands, “If God finds any good in your hearts, He will give you something better than what was taken from you and will forgive you. God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.”","But if they intend to betray you, they already betrayed God before, and He gave power over them. God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.","Those who believed, emigrated, and strove with their wealth and their lives in God’s cause, and those who gave shelter and support — they are allies of one another. As for those who believed but did not emigrate, you owe them no allegiance whatsoever until they emigrate. Yet if they seek your help in religion, you must help them, except against a people with whom you have a treaty. God is All-Seeing of what you do.","Those who disbelieve are allies of one another. Unless you do this, there will be strife in the land and great corruption.","Those who believed, emigrated, and strove in God’s cause, and those who gave shelter and support — they are the true believers. For them is forgiveness and a generous provision.","And those who believed afterward, emigrated, and strove alongside you — they are of you. But blood relatives are closer to one another in God’s Book. Truly, God is All-Knowing of all things.","A declaration of disavowal from God and His Messenger to those polytheists with whom you made treaties.","So travel freely through the land for four months, and know that you cannot escape God, and that God will disgrace the disbelievers.","And a proclamation from God and His Messenger to the people on the day of the greater pilgrimage: God is free of the polytheists, and so is His Messenger. If you repent, that is better for you, but if you turn away, then know that you cannot escape God. And give the disbelievers tidings of a painful punishment.","Except those polytheists with whom you made a treaty and who then did not fall short with you in anything and did not support anyone against you — fulfill their treaty to its full term. Truly, God loves the righteous.","When the sacred months have passed, kill the polytheists wherever you find them, seize them, besiege them, and lie in wait for them at every ambush point. But if they repent, establish prayer, and give charity, then let them go their way. Surely, God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","If any of the polytheists seeks your protection, grant him protection so that he may hear God’s word, then escort him to his place of safety. That is because they are a people who do not know.","How can the polytheists have a treaty with God and with His Messenger? Except those with whom you made a treaty at the Sacred Mosque — so long as they are true to you, be true to them. Truly, God loves the righteous.","How? If they gain the upper hand over you, they respect neither kinship nor covenant with you. They please you with their mouths while their hearts refuse, and most of them are defiantly disobedient.","They sold God’s verses for a petty price and barred others from His path. Evil is what they used to do.","They respect neither kinship nor covenant with a believer. Those are the transgressors.","But if they repent, establish prayer, and give charity, then they are your brothers in faith. We detail the verses for people who know.","But if they break their oaths after their treaty and attack your religion, then fight the leaders of disbelief — they have no binding oaths — so that they may desist.","Will you not fight a people who broke their oaths, plotted to expel the Messenger, and were the ones who started against you first? Do you fear them? God is more deserving of your fear, if you are believers.","Fight them—God will punish them by your hands, disgrace them, grant you victory over them, and heal the chests of a believing people.","And remove the rage from their hearts. God turns in mercy to whom He wills. God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.","Or did you think you would be left alone without God has made evident those among you who strove and took no intimate ally besides God, His Messenger, and the believers? God is fully aware of what you do.","It is not for the polytheists to maintain God’s mosques while bearing witness against themselves of disbelief. Those—their deeds have come to nothing, and in the Fire they will remain forever.","Only those who believe in God and the Last Day, establish prayer, give charity, and fear none but God maintain God’s mosques. It is they who may be among the guided.","Do you equate giving water to pilgrims and maintaining the Sacred Mosque with one who believes in God and the Last Day and strives in God’s cause? They are not equal before God. God does not guide the wrongdoing people.","Those who believed, emigrated, and strove in God’s cause with their wealth and their lives hold a greater rank with God. It is they who are the triumphant.","Their Lord gives them glad tidings of mercy from Him, and approval, and gardens where lasting bliss awaits them.","They will dwell there forever. Truly, with God is a tremendous reward.","O you who believe, do not take your fathers and your brothers as allies if they prefer disbelief over faith. Whoever among you allies with them—it is they who are the wrongdoers.","Say, “If your fathers, your sons, your brothers, your spouses, your clan, wealth you have acquired, trade you fear will decline, and homes you cherish are dearer to you than God, His Messenger, and striving in His cause, then wait until God brings His command.” God does not guide the corrupt people.","God has granted you victory in many battlefields, and on the day of Hunayn, when your great numbers impressed you, but they availed you nothing, and the earth, vast as it is, closed in on you, then you turned back in retreat.","Then God sent down His tranquility upon His messenger and upon the believers, and sent down forces you did not see, and punished those who disbelieved. That is the recompense of the disbelievers.","Then after that, God turns in mercy to whom He wills. And God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","O you who believe, the polytheists are impure, so let them not approach the Sacred Mosque after this year of theirs. And if you fear poverty, God will enrich you from His bounty if He wills. Truly God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.","Fight those among the People of the Scripture who do not believe in God or the Last Day, who do not forbid what God and His messenger have forbidden, and who do not follow the religion of truth—until they pay the tribute out of hand while they are humbled.","The Jews said, “Ezra is the son of God,” and the Christians said, “The Messiah is the son of God.” That is what they say with their mouths, echoing the words of those who disbelieved before them. May God destroy them! How deluded they are!","They took their rabbis and their monks as lords besides God, and the Messiah son of Mary, though they were commanded only to worship one God. There is no god but Him. Glory be to Him, far above what they associate with Him.","They want to extinguish God’s light with their mouths, but God refuses anything except to perfect His light, even if the disbelievers despise it.","It is He who sent His messenger with guidance and the religion of truth to make it prevail over all religion, even if the polytheists despise it.","O you who believe, many of the rabbis and monks devour people’s wealth falsely and turn others from God’s path. Those who hoard gold and silver and do not spend it in God’s path—give them news of a painful punishment.","On the Day it will be heated in the fire of Hell and their foreheads, sides, and backs will be branded with it: “This is what you hoarded for yourselves, so taste what you used to hoard.”","The number of months with God is twelve months in God’s decree, since the day He created the heavens and the earth. Of these, four are sacred. That is the upright religion, so do not wrong yourselves during them. And fight the polytheists collectively as they fight you collectively. And know that God is with the God-conscious.","Postponing sacred months is only an increase in disbelief. Those who disbelieve are led astray by it—they permit it one year and forbid it another year to match the number God has made sacred, thus permitting what God has forbidden. The evil of their deeds has been made appealing to them. And God does not guide the disbelieving people.","O you who believe, what is wrong with you that when you are told, “March out in God’s cause,” you cling heavily to the earth? Are you content with the life of this world over the Hereafter? The enjoyment of this worldly life compared to the Hereafter is nothing but little.","If you do not march out, He will punish you with a painful punishment and replace you with another people, and you will not harm Him in the least. God is Capable of all things.","If you do not help him, God already helped him when those who disbelieved drove him out, the second of two, when they were in the cave, when he said to his companion, “Do not grieve; surely God is with us.” So God sent down His tranquility upon him and supported him with forces you did not see, and He made the word of those who disbelieved the lowest. And God’s word is the highest. God is All-Mighty, All-Wise.","March out, light or heavy, and strive with your wealth and your lives in God’s cause. That is better for you, if only you knew.","Had it been a near gain and an easy journey, they would have followed you, but the distance was too far for them. They will swear by God, “Had we been able, we would have gone out with you.” They destroy themselves, and God knows that they are truly liars.","God has pardoned you — why did you give them permission before it became clear to you who was truthful and you knew the liars?","Those who believe in God and the Last Day do not ask your permission to strive with their wealth and their lives. God is All-Knowing of the God-conscious.","Only those who do not believe in God and the Last Day ask your permission, and whose hearts are filled with doubt, so they waver in their doubt.","Had they intended to go out, they would have prepared for it. But God detested their departure, so He held them back, and they were told, “Stay behind with those who stay behind.”","Had they gone out among you, they would have added nothing to you but confusion, and they would have rushed about in your midst seeking to sow discord among you — and among you are those who would listen to them. God is All-Knowing of the wrongdoers.","They certainly sought discord before and turned matters over against you, until the truth came and God’s command prevailed, while they were averse.","Among them is he who says, “Give me leave and do not put me to trial.” Unquestionably, into trial they have already fallen! Surely Hell surrounds the disbelievers.","If good befalls you, it grieves them, and if calamity strikes you, they say, “We took our precaution beforehand,” and they turn away rejoicing.","Say, “Nothing will befall us except what God has decreed for us. He is our Protector.” And in God let the believers put their trust.","Say, “Are you waiting for anything to befall us except one of the two best outcomes? While we are waiting for God to strike you with punishment from Him or at our hands. So wait — we are waiting with you.”","Say, “Spend willingly or unwillingly — it will never be accepted from you. You have been a defiantly disobedient people.”","Nothing prevented their contributions from being accepted except that they disbelieved in God and His Messenger, they do not come to prayer except lazily, and they do not spend except reluctantly.","So let not their wealth or their children impress you. God only intends to punish them through these in the life of this world, and that their souls depart while they are disbelievers.","They swear by God that they are truly of you, but they are not of you — they are a people who are afraid.","If they could find a refuge, or caves, or any place to enter, they would turn to it, rushing headlong.","Among them are those who criticize you regarding the charitable donations. If they are given from them, they are pleased, but if they are not given from them, they are suddenly enraged.","If only they had been content with what God and His Messenger gave them and said, “God is enough for us. God will give us from His bounty, and so will His Messenger. To God we turn in hope.”","Charitable donations are only for the poor, the needy, those who administer them, those whose hearts are to be reconciled, for freeing slaves, for debtors, in God’s cause, and for the traveler — an obligation from God. God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.","Among them are those who hurt the Prophet and say, “He is all ears.” Say, “An ear of good for you — he believes in God and trusts the believers and is a mercy to those of you who believe.” Those who hurt God’s Messenger will have a painful punishment.","They swear by God to you to please you, but God and His Messenger are more deserving that they should please Him, if they are believers.","Do they not know that whoever opposes God and His Messenger — for him is the fire of Hell, abiding in it forever? That is the supreme disgrace.","The hypocrites fear that a chapter will be sent down against them, exposing what is in their hearts. Say, “Mock on — God will bring out what you fear.”","And if you ask them, they will surely say, “We were only chatting and playing.” Say, “Was it God and His verses and His Messenger you were mocking?”","Make no excuses — you have disbelieved after your belief. If We pardon a group among you, We will punish another group because they were criminals.","The hypocrite men and hypocrite women are all the same. They enjoin what is wrong and forbid what is right and clench their fists tight. They forgot God, so He forgot them. Truly, the hypocrites are the defiantly disobedient.","God has promised the hypocrite men and hypocrite women and the disbelievers the Fire of Hell, dwelling in it forever. It is enough for them. God has cursed them, and for them is a lasting punishment.","Like those before you — they were mightier than you in strength and more abundant in wealth and children. They enjoyed their share, and you have enjoyed your share just as those before you enjoyed theirs, and you indulged as they indulged. Those — their deeds have come to nothing in this world and the Hereafter, and those are the losers.","Has the news not reached them of those before them — the people of Noah, Ad, Thamud, the people of Abraham, the inhabitants of Midian, and the overturned cities? Their messengers came to them with clear proofs. God would never wrong them, but they wronged themselves.","The believing men and believing women are allies of one another. They enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong, establish prayer, give charity, and obey God and His Messenger. Those — God will have mercy on them. Surely God is All-Mighty, All-Wise.","God has promised the believing men and believing women gardens beneath which rivers flow, dwelling in them forever, and fine dwellings in the Gardens of Eden. But pleasure from God is greater. That is the supreme triumph.","O Prophet, strive against the disbelievers and the hypocrites and be harsh with them. Their refuge is Hell — what a wretched destination!","They swear by God they said nothing, yet they certainly uttered the word of disbelief and disbelieved after their submission, and they plotted what they could not attain. They resented nothing except that God and His Messenger had enriched them from His bounty. If they repent, it will be better for them, but if they turn away, God will punish them with a painful punishment in this world and the Hereafter, and they will have no ally or helper on earth.","Among them are those who made a covenant with God: “If He gives us from His bounty, we will surely give in charity and we will surely be among the righteous.”","But when He gave them from His bounty, they hoarded it and turned away in aversion.","So He made hypocrisy settle in their hearts until the Day they meet Him, because they broke their promise to God and because they used to lie.","Did they not know that God knows their secrets and their private conversations, and that God is the All-Knower of the unseen?","Those who mock the believers who give freely in charity and those who find nothing to give but their meager effort — they ridicule them. God ridicules them, and for them is a painful punishment.","Ask forgiveness for them or do not ask forgiveness for them — even if you ask forgiveness for them seventy times, God will never forgive them. That is because they disbelieved in God and His Messenger. God does not guide the defiantly disobedient people.","Those left behind rejoiced at staying back behind God’s Messenger, and they hated to strive with their wealth and their lives in God’s cause. They said, “Do not march out in the heat.” Say, “The fire of Hell is far more intense in heat.” If only they could understand.","Let them laugh a little and weep much — a recompense for what they used to earn.","If God returns you to a group of them and they ask your permission to go out, say, “You will never go out with me, and you will never fight an enemy alongside me. You were content to sit back the first time, so sit with those who stay behind.”","Never pray over any of them who dies, and never stand at his grave. They disbelieved in God and His Messenger and died as defiantly disobedient.","Let not their wealth and their children impress you. God only intends to punish them through these in this world, and that their souls depart while they are disbelievers.","When a chapter is sent down saying, “Believe in God and strive alongside His Messenger,” the affluent among them ask your leave and say, “Let us stay with those who sit behind.”","They were content to be with those who stay behind, and their hearts were sealed, so they do not understand.","But the Messenger and those who believed with him strove with their wealth and their lives. For them are all good things, and it is they who are the successful.","God has prepared for them gardens beneath which rivers flow, dwelling therein forever. That is the supreme triumph.","The excuse-makers among the desert Arabs came seeking permission to stay behind, and those who lied to God and His Messenger sat idle. A painful punishment will strike those among them who disbelieved.","No blame falls on the weak, the sick, or those who find nothing to spend, so long as they are sincere to God and His Messenger. There are no grounds against those who do good. God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","Nor on those who, when they came to you so you might provide them mounts, you said, “I have nothing to carry you on,” and they turned away with their eyes overflowing with tears out of grief that they could find nothing to spend.","The grounds are only against those who ask your permission while they are wealthy. They were content to be with those who stay behind, and God has sealed their hearts, so they do not know.","They will make excuses to you when you return to them. Say, “Do not make excuses. We will never believe you. God has already informed us about your affairs.” God will see your deeds, and so will His Messenger. Then you will be returned to the Knower of the unseen and the seen, and He will inform you of what you used to do.","They will swear by God to you when you return to them, so that you may turn away from them. So turn away from them — they are filth, and their refuge is Hell, a recompense for what they used to earn.","They swear to you so that you may be pleased with them. But even if you are pleased with them, God is never pleased with the defiantly disobedient people.","The desert Arabs are more severe in disbelief and hypocrisy, and more likely not to know the limits of what God has sent down to His Messenger. God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.","Among the desert Arabs are those who regard what they spend as a penalty and await misfortune to befall you. Upon them is the turn of misfortune. God is All-Hearing, All-Knowing.","Among the desert Arabs are those who believe in God and the Last Day and regard what they spend as means of nearness to God and the Messenger’s prayers. It is truly a means of nearness for them. God will admit them into His mercy. Truly, God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","The forerunners, the first among the emigrants and the helpers, and those who followed them in goodness — God is pleased with them and they are pleased with Him. He has prepared for them gardens beneath which rivers flow, dwelling therein forever. That is the supreme triumph.","Among the desert Arabs around you are hypocrites, and among the people of Medina — they have persisted in hypocrisy. You do not know them; We know them. We will punish them twice, then they will be returned to a tremendous punishment.","Others have confessed their sins — they mixed righteous deeds with bad ones. Perhaps God will turn to them in mercy. Truly, God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","Take from their wealth a charity to purify them and cleanse them with it, and pray for them — your prayer is a comfort to them. God is All-Hearing, All-Knowing.","Do they not know that it is God who accepts repentance from His servants and receives charities, and that God is the Ever-Accepting of repentance, the Most Merciful?","Say, “Work, and God will see your work, and His Messenger, and the believers. You will be returned to the Knower of the unseen and the seen, and He will inform you of what you used to do.”","Others are deferred to God’s command — either He will punish them or He will turn to them in mercy. God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.","Those who built a mosque to cause harm, disbelief, and division among the believers, and as an outpost for whoever waged war against God and His Messenger before — they will surely swear, “We intended nothing but good.” God bears witness that they are liars.","Never stand in it. A mosque founded on righteousness from the first day is more worthy for you to stand in. In it are men who love to purify themselves. God loves those who purify themselves.","Is one who founded his structure on mindfulness of God and His pleasure better, or one who founded his structure on the edge of a crumbling cliff, so it collapsed with him into the fire of Hell? God does not guide the wrongdoing people.","The structure they built will never cease to be a source of doubt in their hearts, unless their hearts are cut to pieces. God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.","God has purchased from the believers their lives and their wealth in exchange for Paradise. They fight in God’s cause — they kill and are killed. A true promise binding upon Him in the Torah, the Gospel, and the Quran. And who fulfills his covenant better than God? So rejoice in the bargain you have made. That is the supreme triumph.","The repentant, the worshippers, the praisers, the journeyers, the bowing, the prostrating, the enjoiners of good and the forbidders of evil, and the keepers of God’s limits — give glad tidings to the believers.","It was not for the Prophet and those who believed to seek forgiveness for the polytheists, even if they were relatives, after it became clear to them that they are companions of the Blaze.","Abraham’s seeking forgiveness for his father was only because of a promise he had made to him. But when it became clear to him that he was an enemy of God, he disowned him. Truly, Abraham was tender-hearted, forbearing.","God would never lead a people astray after He had guided them until He makes clear to them what they should be mindful of. Surely God is All-Knowing of all things.","Truly, to God belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth. He gives life and causes death. You have no protector or helper besides God.","God has turned in mercy to the Prophet, the Emigrants, and the Helpers who followed him in the hour of hardship, after the hearts of a group of them had nearly swerved. Then He turned to them in mercy. He is truly Compassionate, Merciful to them.","And to the three who were left behind — until the earth, vast as it is, closed in on them, and their own souls closed in on them, and they realized there was no refuge from God except in Him — then He turned to them in mercy so they might repent. Truly, God is the Ever-Relenting, the Most Merciful.","O you who believe, be mindful of God and be with the truthful.","It was not for the people of Medina and the surrounding Bedouins to stay behind from God’s Messenger, nor to prefer their own lives over his. That is because no thirst, no fatigue, no hunger strikes them in God’s cause, and they tread no ground that enrages the disbelievers, and they inflict no blow upon an enemy, except that a righteous deed is recorded for them thereby. Surely God does not waste the reward of those who do good.","They spend no expenditure, small or large, and they cross no valley, except that it is recorded for them, so that God may repay them the best of what they used to do.","It was not for the believers to march out all together. Why not have a group from every division among them go to gain deep understanding of the religion and warn their people when they return to them, so that they may be on guard?","O you who believe, fight those of the disbelievers nearest to you, and let them find harshness in you. Know that God is with the reverent.","Whenever a chapter is sent down, some of them say, “Which of you did this increase in faith?” As for those who believe, it increased them in faith, and they rejoice.","But as for those in whose hearts is a disease, it added filth to their filth, and they died as disbelievers.","Do they not see that they are tested every year once or twice, yet they do not repent, nor do they take heed?","Whenever a chapter is sent down, they glance at one another: “Does anyone see you?” Then they slip away. God has turned their hearts away, because they are a people who do not understand.","Truly a messenger has come to you from among yourselves. What you suffer grieves him. He is deeply concerned for you, and to the believers he is compassionate, merciful.","So if they turn away, say, “God is enough for me. There is no god but Him. In Him I place my trust, and He is the Lord of the Mighty Throne.”","Alif Lam Ra. These are the verses of the Wise Book.","Is it a wonder to people that We revealed to a man from among them: “Warn the people and give glad tidings to those who believe that they have a sure footing of truth with their Lord”? The disbelievers said, “This is clearly a sorcerer.”","Truly your Lord is God, who created the heavens and the earth in six days, then rose over the Throne, directing all affairs. No intercessor exists except after His permission. That is God, your Lord, so worship Him. Will you not reflect?","To Him is your return, all of you — God’s promise in truth. He originates creation, then restores it, so that He may recompense those who believed and did righteous deeds with justice. As for those who disbelieved, for them is a drink of scalding water and a painful punishment for what they used to deny.","It is He who made the sun a radiance and the moon a light, and determined for it phases, so that you may know the number of years and the reckoning. God did not create that except in truth. He details the signs for people who know.","Surely in the alternation of night and day and what God created in the heavens and the earth are signs for people who are mindful.","Those who do not expect to meet Us, and are pleased with the life of this world, and feel secure in it, and those who are heedless of Our signs.","Their refuge is the Fire, for what they used to earn.","Those who believed and did righteous deeds — their Lord guides them through their faith. Rivers flow beneath them in Gardens of Bliss.","Their call therein is, “Glory be to You, O God,” and their greeting therein is, “Peace.” The last of their call is, “All praise belongs to God, Lord of all worlds.”","If God were to hasten evil for people as they hasten for good, their term would already have been decreed for them. So We leave those who do not expect to meet Us, wandering blindly in their transgression.","When hardship touches a person, he calls upon Us — lying on his side, sitting, or standing. But when We remove his hardship from him, he passes on as though he never called upon Us for any hardship that touched him. Thus what the transgressors used to do was made appealing to them.","We destroyed the generations before you when they did wrong, and their messengers came to them with clear proofs, but they would never believe. Thus We recompense the criminal people.","Then We made you successors in the earth after them, to see how you would act.","When Our verses are recited to them as clear proofs, those who do not expect to meet Us say, “Bring a Quran other than this, or change it.” Say, “It is not for me to change it on my own. I only follow what is revealed to me. I fear, if I disobey my Lord, the punishment of a tremendous Day.”","Say, “Had God willed, I would not have recited it to you, nor would He have made it known to you. I lived among you a lifetime before it — do you not reason?”","Who is more unjust than one who fabricates a lie against God or denies His verses? Surely the criminals will never succeed.","They worship besides God what neither harms them nor benefits them, and they say, “These are our intercessors with God.” Say, “Are you informing God of something He does not know in the heavens or on the earth?” Glory be to Him, and exalted is He above what they associate with Him.","Humanity was but one community, then they differed. Were it not for a word that had preceded from your Lord, their disputes would have been settled between them.","They say, “Why has no miracle been sent down to him from his Lord?” Say, “The unseen belongs only to God. So wait — I am waiting with you.”","When We let people taste mercy after hardship has touched them, at once they scheme against Our signs. Say, “God is swifter in scheming.” Surely Our messengers record what you scheme.","It is He who conveys you through land and sea. Until, when you are on ships and they sail with them with a pleasant wind and they rejoice in it, a violent wind comes upon them and waves surge at them from every side, and they think they are engulfed — they call upon God, devoting their faith sincerely to Him: “If You save us from this, we will truly be among the grateful.”","But when He saves them, at once they transgress in the land without right. O people, your transgression is only against yourselves — a fleeting enjoyment of this worldly life. Then to Us is your return, and We will inform you of what you used to do.","The example of this worldly life is like water We sent down from the sky, and the plants of the earth absorbed it — what people and livestock eat — until, when the earth took on its full adornment and was beautified, and its people thought they had mastery over it, Our command came upon it by night or by day, and We made it as if mown down, as though it had not flourished the day before. Thus We make the verses clear for people who reflect.","God calls to the Abode of Peace and guides whom He wills to a straight path.","For those who did good is the best reward and more. No dust will cover their faces, nor humiliation. Those are the companions of Paradise—they will remain there forever.","But those who earned evil deeds—the recompense of an evil deed is its like, and humiliation will cover them. They have no protector from God. It is as though their faces were draped with pieces of the darkest night. Those are the companions of the Fire—they will remain there forever.","On the Day We gather them all together, then We will say to those who associated partners, “Stay in your place—you and your partners.” We will separate them, and their partners will say, “It was not us you were worshiping.","God is sufficient as a witness between us and you. We were truly unaware of your worship.”","There every soul will face what it sent ahead. They will be returned to God, their true Master, and what they used to fabricate will vanish from them.","Say, “Who provides for you from the sky and the earth? Or who controls hearing and sight? And who brings the living from the dead and brings the dead from the living? And who governs all affairs?” They will say, “God.” Say, “Will you not then be mindful?”","That is God, your true Lord. What is there after truth but error? How then are you turned away?","Thus your Lord’s word has been proven true against those who defiantly disobeyed—that they will not believe.","Say, “Is there among your partners any who originates creation and then repeats it?” Say, “God originates creation and then repeats it. How then are you deluded?”","Say, “Is there among your partners any who guides to the truth?” Say, “God guides to the truth. Is the one who guides to the truth more worthy of being followed, or the one who cannot find guidance unless he is guided? What is wrong with you? How do you judge?”","Most of them follow nothing but assumption. Surely assumption avails nothing against the truth. God is All-Knowing of what they do.","This Quran could not have been fabricated by anyone other than God. Rather, it is a confirmation of what came before it and a detailed explanation of the Scripture—there is no doubt in it—from the Lord of all worlds.","Or do they say, “He fabricated it”? Say, “Then produce a chapter like it and call upon whoever you can besides God, if you are truthful.”","Rather, they denied what they could not encompass in knowledge, and its interpretation has not yet come to them. Likewise those before them denied. So look how the wrongdoers ended up.","Among them are those who believe in it, and among them are those who do not believe in it. Your Lord knows best the corrupters.","If they deny you, say, “To me my deeds, and to you your deeds. You are free of what I do, and I am free of what you do.”","Among them are those who listen to you. Can you make the deaf hear, even though they do not understand?","Among them are those who look at you. Can you guide the blind, even though they do not see?","Truly, God does not wrong people in the least, but people wrong themselves.","On the Day He gathers them, it will be as though they had lingered only an hour of a day, recognizing one another. Lost are those who denied the meeting with God and were never guided.","Whether We show you some of what We promise them, or We take you in death, to Us is their return. Then God is witness over what they do.","Every nation has a messenger. When their messenger comes, judgment is passed between them in justice, and they are not wronged.","They say, “When will this promise come to pass, if you are truthful?”","Say, “I have no power to harm or benefit myself, except as God wills. Every nation has an appointed term. When their term comes, they cannot delay it by a single hour, nor can they advance it.”","Say, “Have you considered: if His punishment came to you by night or by day, what part of it would the guilty wish to hasten?”","Then, when it has struck, will you believe in it? Now? When you used to hasten it?","Then those who wronged are told, “Taste the punishment of eternity. Are you repaid for anything but what you used to earn?”","They ask you to tell them, “Is it true?” Say, “Yes, by my Lord, it is certainly true, and you cannot escape it.”","If every soul that wronged possessed everything on earth, it would offer it as ransom. They will conceal their regret when they see the punishment, and judgment is passed between them in justice, and they are not wronged.","Surely, to God belongs whatever is in the heavens and the earth. Surely, God’s promise is true, but most of them do not know.","He gives life and causes death, and to Him you will be returned.","O people, there has come to you an instruction from your Lord, a healing for what is in the hearts, a guidance, and a mercy for the believers.","Say, “In God’s grace and in His mercy—in that let them rejoice. It is better than what they accumulate.”","Say, “Have you considered what God has sent down to you of provision, and you have made some of it forbidden and some lawful?” Say, “Did God give you permission, or do you fabricate lies against God?”","What do those who fabricate lies against God think about the Day of Resurrection? Truly, God is full of grace toward people, but most of them are not grateful.","You are not engaged in any matter, nor do you recite any of the Quran, nor do you do any deed, except that We are witnesses over you when you undertake it. Not even the weight of an atom on earth or in the sky escapes your Lord, nor anything smaller than that or larger, except that it is in a clear record.","Surely, God’s allies—no fear will be upon them, nor will they grieve.","Those who believed and were mindful.","For them is good news in the life of this world and in the Hereafter. There is no changing God’s words. That is the supreme triumph.","Let their words not grieve you. All power belongs to God. He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.","Surely, to God belongs everyone in the heavens and everyone on earth. And those who invoke others besides God do not follow any partners—they follow nothing but assumption, and they do nothing but guess.","It is He who made the night for you to find rest in, and the day bright. In that are signs for people who listen.","They say, “God has taken a son.” Glory be to Him! He is the Self-Sufficient. To Him belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on earth. You have no authority for this. Do you say about God what you do not know?","Say, “Those who fabricate lies against God will never succeed.”","A brief enjoyment in this world, then to Us is their return, then We will make them taste the severe punishment for their disbelief.","Recite to them the story of Noah, when he said to his people, “O my people, if my presence and my reminding you of God’s signs have become unbearable to you, then in God I place my trust. So gather your resolve and your partners, then let your plan not be obscure to you. Then carry it out against me and give me no respite.","But if you turn away, I have not asked you for any payment. My payment is only from God, and I have been commanded to be among those who submit.”","They denied him, so We saved him and those with him in the ark and made them successors, and We drowned those who denied Our signs. So look at how the fate of those who were warned turned out.","Then after him We sent messengers to their peoples, and they came to them with clear proofs, but they would not believe in what they had denied before. That is how We seal the hearts of the transgressors.","Then after them We sent Moses and Aaron to Pharaoh and his chiefs with Our miracles, but they were arrogant and were a criminal people.","When the truth came to them from Us, they said, “This is clearly sorcery.”","Moses said, “Is this what you say about the truth when it has come to you? Is this sorcery? Sorcerers never succeed.”","They said, “Have you come to turn us away from what we found our fathers upon, so that greatness in the land may belong to the two of you? We will never believe in you.”","Pharaoh said, “Bring me every skilled sorcerer.”","When the sorcerers came, Moses said to them, “Cast whatever you will cast.”","When they cast, Moses said, “What you have brought is sorcery. God will surely nullify it. God does not set right the work of corrupters.”","And God establishes the truth by His words, even if the criminals despise it.","None believed in Moses except some youth from among his people, out of fear that Pharaoh and their chiefs would persecute them. Pharaoh was truly a tyrant in the land, and he was truly among the transgressors.","Moses said, “O my people, if you have believed in God, then place your trust in Him, if you are truly submitters.”","They said, “In God we place our trust. Our Lord, do not make us a trial for the wrongdoing people.","And save us by Your mercy from the disbelieving people.”","We revealed to Moses and his brother, “Settle your people in Egypt in houses, and make your houses places of worship, and establish prayer.” And give glad tidings to the believers.","Moses said, “Our Lord, You have given Pharaoh and his chiefs splendor and wealth in the life of this world. Our Lord, that they may lead others astray from Your path. Our Lord, obliterate their wealth and harden their hearts so that they do not believe until they see the painful punishment.”","He said, “Your prayer has been answered. So stay on the straight course, and do not follow the path of those who do not know.”","We brought the Children of Israel across the sea, and Pharaoh and his soldiers pursued them in aggression and hostility until, when drowning overtook him, he said, “I believe that there is no god except the One in whom the Children of Israel believe, and I am among the submitters.”","“Now? When you had disobeyed before and were among the corrupters?","So today We will preserve your body, that you may be a sign for those after you.” Yet surely many people are heedless of Our signs.","We settled the Children of Israel in a noble dwelling and provided them with good things. They did not differ until knowledge came to them. Your Lord will judge between them on the Day of Resurrection concerning what they used to differ over.","If you are in doubt about what We have sent down to you, then ask those who have been reading the Scripture before you. The truth has come to you from your Lord, so never be among the doubters.","And never be among those who denied God’s verses, or you will be among the losers.","Truly, those against whom your Lord’s word has been justified will not believe.","Even if every sign came to them, until they see the painful punishment.","If only there had been a town that believed and its faith benefited it — except the people of Jonah. When they believed, We removed from them the punishment of disgrace in the life of this world and granted them enjoyment for a time.","Had your Lord willed, everyone on earth would have believed, all of them together. Will you then compel people until they become believers?","No soul can believe except by God’s permission. He places filth upon those who do not reason.","Say, “Look at what is in the heavens and the earth.” But signs and warnings are of no use to a people who will not believe.","So are they waiting for anything but the like of the days of those who passed before them? Say, “Then wait; I am with you among those waiting.”","Then We save Our messengers and those who believed. Thus it is binding upon Us — We save the believers.","Say, “O people, if you are in doubt about my religion, then I do not worship those you worship besides God, but I worship God, who takes your souls. And I have been commanded to be among the believers.","And: ‘Direct your face toward the religion, a monotheist, and never be among those who associate others with God.","And do not call upon, besides God, what neither benefits you nor harms you. If you do, then you will be among the wrongdoers.’","If God touches you with harm, none can remove it but Him. And if He intends good for you, none can repel His grace. He bestows it upon whomever He wills of His servants. And He is the All-Forgiving, the Most Merciful.”","Say, “O people, the truth has come to you from your Lord. Whoever is guided is guided only for his own soul, and whoever goes astray goes astray only against it. And I am not a guardian over you.”","Follow what is revealed to you and be patient until God judges. He is the best of judges.","Alif Lam Ra. A Book whose verses have been perfected, then made clear, from One All-Wise, All-Aware.","That you worship none but God. I am truly a warner and a bearer of good news to you from Him.","And seek your Lord’s forgiveness, then turn to Him in repentance. He will grant you good provision until an appointed term and will give every person of merit his due. But if you turn away, I fear for you the punishment of a great Day.","To God is your return, and He is Capable of all things.","They fold up their chests to hide from Him. Even when they cover themselves with their garments, He knows what they conceal and what they reveal. He is All-Knowing of what lies within the chests.","There is no creature on earth but its provision rests with God. He knows its dwelling place and its place of deposit. All is in a clear record.","He is the One who created the heavens and the earth in six days — and His throne was upon the water — to test you: which of you is best in deed. Yet if you say, “You will be raised after death,” those who disbelieve will surely say, “This is nothing but plain sorcery.”","If We delay the punishment for a limited time, they will surely say, “What holds it back?” On the Day it comes upon them, it will not be turned away from them, and what they used to mock will close in on them.","If We let man taste mercy from Us, then strip it away from him, he is utterly despairing, ungrateful.","And if We let him taste comfort after hardship has touched him, he will surely say, “The troubles have left me!” He is jubilant, boastful.","Except those who are patient and do righteous deeds. For them is forgiveness and a great reward.","Perhaps you would leave out some of what is revealed to you, and your chest tightens over it, because they say, “Why has no treasure been sent down upon him, or why has no angel come with him?” You are only a warner, and God is Guardian over all things.","Or do they say, “He fabricated it”? Say, “Then produce ten fabricated chapters like it, and call upon whoever you can besides God, if you are truthful.”","If they do not respond to you, then know that it was sent down with God’s knowledge, and that there is no god but He. Will you then submit?","Whoever desires the life of this world and its adornment, We will pay them in full for their deeds therein, and they will not be shortchanged therein.","Those are the ones who have nothing in the Hereafter but the Fire. What they crafted therein has come to nothing, and worthless is what they used to do.","Is one who stands on clear proof from his Lord, followed by a witness from Him, and before it the Book of Moses as a guide and a mercy — those believe in it. But whoever among the factions disbelieves in it, the Fire is his appointed place. So do not be in doubt about it. It is the truth from your Lord, but most people do not believe.","Who is more unjust than one who fabricates a lie against God? Those will be brought before their Lord, and the witnesses will say, “These are the ones who lied against their Lord.” Truly, God’s curse is upon the wrongdoers.","Those who turn others from God’s path and seek to make it crooked, and they — in the Hereafter — are disbelievers.","Those could never escape on earth, and they had no protectors besides God. The punishment will be multiplied for them. They could not bear to hear, and they could not see.","Those are the ones who lost their own souls, and what they used to fabricate has abandoned them.","Without doubt, in the Hereafter they are the greatest losers.","Truly, those who believed and did righteous deeds and humbled themselves before their Lord — those are the companions of Paradise. They will abide therein forever.","The example of the two groups is like the blind and the deaf, and the seeing and the hearing. Are they equal in comparison? Will you not then reflect?","We sent Noah to his people: “I am a clear warner to you.","That you worship none but God. I fear for you the punishment of a painful Day.”","The chiefs of his people who disbelieved said, “We see you as nothing but a human like us, and we see that none have followed you except the lowest among us, at first impression. We see no superiority for you over us. Rather, we think you are liars.”","He said, “O my people, have you considered — if I stand on clear proof from my Lord and He has given me a mercy from Himself, but it has been made obscure to you, can we force it on you when you are averse to it?","O my people, I ask you no wealth for it. My reward is only from God. And I will not drive away those who believe — they will meet their Lord. But I see that you are a people acting in ignorance.","O my people, who would protect me from God if I drove them away? Will you not reflect?","I do not say to you that I possess God’s treasures, nor do I know the unseen, nor do I say that I am an angel. And I do not say of those whom your eyes despise that God will never grant them any good — God knows best what is in their souls. Truly, I would then be among the wrongdoers.”","They said, “O Noah, you have argued with us and argued at great length. So bring us what you threaten us with, if you are among the truthful.”","He said, “Only God will bring it upon you, if He wills, and you cannot escape.","My counsel will not benefit you, even if I wished to counsel you, if God intends to lead you astray. He is your Lord, and to Him you will be returned.”","Or do they say, “He fabricated it”? Say, “If I fabricated it, then upon me is my guilt, and I am innocent of what you commit.”","It was revealed to Noah, “None of your people will believe except those who have already believed, so do not grieve over what they have been doing.","Build the ark under Our eyes and Our revelation, and do not plead with Me concerning those who have wronged. They will be drowned.”","He was building the ark, and whenever the leaders of his people passed by him, they mocked him. He said, “If you mock us, we will mock you just as you mock.","Soon you will know who will be visited by a punishment that disgraces him, and upon whom a lasting punishment will descend.”","Until, when Our command came and the oven burst with water, We said, “Carry in it two of every kind, a pair, and your family — except those against whom the word has already been passed — and whoever has believed.” And none believed with him except a few.","He said, “Board it. In God’s name is its sailing and its anchoring. Truly my Lord is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.”","It sailed with them through waves like mountains, and Noah called out to his son, who stood apart, “O my son, board with us and do not be with the disbelievers.”","He said, “I will take refuge on a mountain that will protect me from the water.” He said, “There is no protector today from God’s command, except him on whom He has mercy.” And the waves came between them, and he was among the drowned.","It was said, “O earth, swallow your water! O sky, cease!” The water subsided, the matter was settled, and it rested upon al-Judi. And it was said, “Away with the wrongdoing people!”","Noah called out to his Lord and said, “My Lord, my son is of my family, and Your promise is true, and You are the most just of judges.”","He said, “O Noah, he is not of your family. He is of unrighteous conduct. So do not ask Me about what you have no knowledge of. I warn you against being among the ignorant.”","He said, “My Lord, I seek refuge in You from asking You what I have no knowledge of. And unless You forgive me and have mercy on me, I will be among the losers.”","It was said, “O Noah, disembark with peace from Us and blessings upon you and upon nations from those with you. But there are nations We will grant enjoyment, then a painful punishment from Us will touch them.”","These are accounts of the unseen that We reveal to you. Neither you nor your people knew them before this. So be patient. Surely the outcome belongs to the God-conscious.","And to Ad, their brother Hud. He said, “O my people, worship God. You have no god other than Him. You are nothing but fabricators.","O my people, I ask you no payment for this. My payment is only from Him who created me. Will you not reason?","O my people, seek your Lord’s forgiveness, then turn to Him in repentance. He will send the sky upon you in torrents and add strength to your strength. Do not turn away as criminals.”","They said, “O Hud, you have brought us no clear proof. We will not abandon our gods on your word, and we do not believe you.","All we can say is that some of our gods have afflicted you with madness.” He said, “I call God as my witness, and you bear witness, that I am free of what you associate.","Besides Him. So plot against me, all of you, then give me no respite.","I have placed my trust in God, my Lord and your Lord. There is no creature but He grasps it by its forelock. Truly, my Lord is on a straight path.","So if you turn away, I have already delivered to you what I was sent with. My Lord will replace you with another people, and you will not harm Him in the least. My Lord is Guardian over all things.”","When Our command came, We saved Hud and those who believed with him by a mercy from Us, and We saved them from a harsh punishment.","That was Ad. They rejected their Lord’s signs, disobeyed His messengers, and followed the command of every stubborn tyrant.","They were pursued by a curse in this world and on the Day of Resurrection. Truly, Ad denied their Lord. Away with Ad, the people of Hud!","And to Thamud, their brother Salih. He said, “O my people, worship God. You have no god other than Him. He produced you from the earth and settled you in it, so seek His forgiveness, then turn to Him in repentance. Truly my Lord is Near, Responsive.”","They said, “O Salih, you were among us a source of hope before this. Do you forbid us from worshiping what our fathers worshiped? We are in grave doubt about what you call us to.”","He said, “O my people, consider: if I stand on clear proof from my Lord and He has given me mercy from Himself, then who would protect me from God if I disobeyed Him? You would only increase me in loss.","O my people, this is God’s she-camel, a sign for you. So let her graze in God’s earth and do not touch her with harm, or a near punishment will seize you.”","But they hamstrung her. So he said, “Enjoy yourselves in your homes for three days. That is a promise not to be belied.”","When Our command came, We saved Salih and those who believed with him by mercy from Us, and from the disgrace of that day. Your Lord is the All-Strong, the All-Mighty.","The blast seized those who wronged, and they lay fallen in their homes.","As though they had never lived there. Surely Thamud denied their Lord. Away with Thamud!","Certainly Our messengers came to Abraham with glad tidings. They said, “Peace.” He said, “Peace,” and before long he brought a roasted calf.","But when he saw their hands not reaching for it, he found them strange and felt a fear of them. They said, “Do not be afraid. We have been sent to the people of Lot.”","And his wife was standing by, and she laughed. So We gave her glad tidings of Isaac, and after Isaac, Jacob.","She said, “Woe to me! Am I to give birth when I am an old woman and this husband of mine is an old man? This is truly a strange thing!”","They said, “Do you marvel at God’s command? God’s mercy and His blessings be upon you, O people of this house. Surely He is Praiseworthy, Glorious.”","When the alarm had left Abraham and the glad tidings had reached him, he began to argue with Us concerning the people of Lot.","Truly Abraham was forbearing, tender-hearted, ever turning back to God.","“O Abraham, turn away from this. Your Lord’s command has already come, and there is coming upon them a punishment that cannot be turned back.”","And when Our messengers came to Lot, he was distressed by them and felt helpless over them, and he said, “This is a dreadful day.”","And his people came rushing toward him — and before this they had been committing evil deeds. He said, “O my people, here are my daughters; they are purer for you. So be mindful of God and do not disgrace me before my guests. Is there not a single right-minded man among you?”","They said, “You know well we have no right to your daughters, and you certainly know what we want.”","He said, “If only I had strength against you or could take refuge in a mighty support!”","They said, “O Lot, we are your Lord’s messengers. They will never reach you. So travel with your family during a portion of the night, and let none of you look back — except your wife. What strikes them will strike her. Their appointed time is the morning. Is the morning not near?”","So when Our command came, We turned it upside down and rained upon it stones of baked clay, layer upon layer.","Marked by your Lord. And it is never far from the wrongdoers.","To Midian, We sent their brother Shuayb. He said, “O my people, worship God — you have no god other than Him. And do not short the measure and the scale. I see you in prosperity, but I fear for you the punishment of an all-encompassing Day.","O my people, give full measure and full weight with justice. Do not cheat people of their goods, and do not spread corruption in the land.","What God leaves for you is better for you, if you are believers. And I am not a guardian over you.”","They said, “O Shuayb, does your prayer command you that we abandon what our fathers worshiped, or that we stop doing with our wealth as we please? Surely you are the forbearing, the right-minded!”","He said, “O my people, consider — what if I stand on clear proof from my Lord, and He has provided me good provision from Himself? I do not want to go against you by doing what I forbid you from. I only want to set things right as much as I can. My success comes only through God. In Him I place my trust, and to Him I turn.","O my people, let not your opposition to me lead you to be struck by the like of what struck the people of Noah, or the people of Hud, or the people of Salih. And the people of Lot are not far from you.","Seek your Lord’s forgiveness, then turn to Him in repentance. Truly my Lord is Most Merciful, Most Loving.”","They said, “O Shuayb, we do not understand much of what you say, and we see you as weak among us. Were it not for your clan, we would have stoned you. You hold no power over us.”","He said, “O my people, is my clan mightier to you than God? You have cast Him behind your backs. Surely my Lord encompasses all that you do.","O my people, do as you will — I will do as I will. You will come to know who will receive a humiliating punishment and who is a liar. So watch — I too am watching with you.”","When Our command came, We saved Shuayb and those who believed with him by a mercy from Us. The blast seized those who wronged, and they lay fallen in their homes.","As though they had never lived there. Away with Midian, just as Thamud was done away with!","Certainly We sent Moses with Our miracles and a clear authority.","To Pharaoh and his chiefs. But they followed Pharaoh’s command, and Pharaoh’s command was not rightly guided.","He will lead his people on the Day of Resurrection and bring them down to the Fire. Wretched is the watering place they are led to!","They were pursued by a curse in this life and on the Day of Resurrection. Wretched is the gift they are given!","That is from the news of the towns We relate to you — some still standing and some mown down.","We did not wrong them, but they wronged themselves. Their gods that they called upon besides God availed them nothing when your Lord’s command came, and they only increased them in ruin.","Such is your Lord’s grip when He seizes the towns while they are wrongdoing. Truly His grip is painful, severe.","In that is a sign for whoever fears the punishment of the Hereafter. That is a Day for which all people will be gathered, and that is a Day that will be witnessed.","We only delay it for a fixed term.","The Day it comes, no soul will speak except by His permission. Among them will be the wretched and the blessed.","As for those who are wretched, they will be in the Fire, where they will have wailing and gasping.","They will remain in it as long as the heavens and the earth endure, except what your Lord wills. Your Lord does whatever He wills.","As for those who are blessed, they will be in Paradise, remaining in it as long as the heavens and the earth endure, except what your Lord wills — a gift unending.","So do not be in doubt about what these people worship. They only worship as their forefathers worshiped before. We will pay them their share in full, undiminished.","Truly We gave Moses the Book, but they differed over it. Were it not for a word that had already gone out from your Lord, it would have been decided between them. They are certainly in troubling doubt about it.","Your Lord will surely repay each of them in full for their deeds. He is All-Aware of what they do.","So stand firm as you have been commanded, along with those who have turned back with you, and do not transgress. He is All-Seeing of what you do.","Do not lean toward those who have done wrong, lest the Fire touch you. You have no protectors besides God, and then you will not be helped.","Establish prayer at both ends of the day and in the early hours of the night. Surely good deeds wipe away bad deeds. That is a reminder for those who remember.","Be patient, for God never wastes the reward of those who do good.","If only there had been among the generations before you people of virtue who forbade corruption in the land — except the few among them whom We saved. Those who did wrong pursued the luxury they were given, and they were criminals.","Your Lord would never destroy towns unjustly while their people were doing right.","Had your Lord willed, He would have made humanity one community, but they continue to differ.","Except those your Lord has shown mercy. For that He created them. And your Lord’s word has been fulfilled: “I will surely fill Hell with jinn and humans altogether.”","All that We relate to you of the accounts of the messengers is to steady your heart. In this has come to you the truth, and a lesson and a reminder for the believers.","Say to those who do not believe, “Do what you can in your position — we are doing ours.”","“Wait — we too are waiting.”","To God belongs the unseen of the heavens and the earth, and to Him all matters return. So worship Him and place your trust in Him. Your Lord is never unaware of what you do.","Alif Lam Ra. These are the verses of the clear Book.","We sent it down as an Arabic Quran so that you may understand.","We relate to you the best of stories through what We have revealed to you of this Quran, though before it you were among the unaware.","When Joseph said to his father, “O my father, I saw eleven stars and the sun and the moon — I saw them prostrating to me.”","He said, “O my son, do not tell your brothers of your dream, lest they plot a scheme against you. Surely Satan is a clear enemy to man.","And so your Lord will choose you and teach you the interpretation of dreams and complete His favor upon you and upon the family of Jacob, just as He completed it upon your forefathers before — Abraham and Isaac. Your Lord is All-Knowing, All-Wise.”","Certainly in Joseph and his brothers there are lessons for those who ask.","When they said, “Joseph and his brother are dearer to our father than we are, though we are a strong band. Our father is clearly misguided.","Kill Joseph or cast him to some distant land, and your father’s attention will be yours alone. After that, you can be righteous people.”","One of them said, “Do not kill Joseph. Throw him into the bottom of the well — some travelers will pick him up — if you must do something.”","They said, “O our father, why do you not trust us with Joseph? We truly wish him well.","Send him with us tomorrow to enjoy himself and play. We will surely watch over him.”","He said, “It grieves me that you should take him, and I fear the wolf may eat him while you are heedless of him.”","They said, “If the wolf eats him while we are a strong band, then we are truly losers.”","When they took him away and agreed to throw him into the depths of the well, We revealed to him, “You will surely inform them of this deed of theirs while they do not perceive.”","They came to their father at nightfall, weeping.","They said, “O our father, we went racing one another and left Joseph with our belongings, and the wolf devoured him. But you will not believe us, even if we are truthful.”","And they brought false blood on his shirt. He said, “Rather, your souls have enticed you into something. So beautiful patience. And God is the One sought for help against what you describe.”","A caravan came and sent their water-drawer, and he let down his bucket. He said, “What good news! Here is a boy!” And they concealed him as merchandise. And God is All-Knowing of what they do.","They sold him for a paltry price — a few coins — and they had no interest in him.","The one who bought him in Egypt said to his wife, “Make his stay honorable. Perhaps he will benefit us, or we will adopt him as a son.” And so We established Joseph in the land, and so that We might teach him the interpretation of dreams. God is Prevailing over His affair, but most people do not know.","When he reached his full maturity, We gave him judgment and knowledge. And so We recompense those who do good.","The woman in whose house he lived tried to seduce him. She locked the doors and said, “Come to me.” He said, “God forbid! Truly, he is my master who has made my stay honorable. The wrongdoers never succeed.”","She desired him, and he would have desired her had he not seen the proof of his Lord. So it was, that We might turn evil and indecency away from him. He was truly one of Our devoted servants.","They both raced to the door, and she tore his shirt from behind, and they found her husband at the door. She said, “What is the recompense of one who intended evil toward your wife except imprisonment or a painful punishment?”","He said, “It was she who tried to seduce me.” And a witness from her household testified, “If his shirt is torn from the front, then she has told the truth and he is a liar.","But if his shirt is torn from behind, then she has lied and he is truthful.”","So when he saw his shirt torn from behind, he said, “This is of your scheming. Truly, your scheming is great.","Joseph, turn away from this. And you — seek forgiveness for your sin. You were truly among the sinners.”","Women in the city said, “The governor’s wife is trying to seduce her slave-boy. Love has pierced her heart. We see her in clear error.”","When she heard of their scheming, she sent for them and prepared a banquet for them, and she gave each of them a knife. Then she said, “Come out before them.” When they saw him, they were stunned by him and cut their hands, and said, “God preserve us! This is no human being — this is none but a noble angel!”","She said, “So this is the one you blamed me for. I did try to seduce him, but he held firm. And if he does not do what I command him, he will surely be imprisoned and will surely be among the humiliated.”","He said, “My Lord, prison is dearer to me than what they are calling me to. And unless You turn their scheming away from me, I will incline toward them and be among the ignorant.”","So his Lord answered him and turned their scheming away from him. Truly He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.","Then it occurred to them, after they had seen the signs, that they should imprison him for a time.","Two young men entered the prison with him. One of them said, “I saw myself pressing wine.” The other said, “I saw myself carrying bread on my head, and birds were eating from it. Tell us its interpretation — we see that you are among the good-doers.”","He said, “No food that you are provided will come to you but I will have told you its interpretation before it reaches you. That is from what my Lord has taught me. I have abandoned the way of a people who do not believe in God and who deny the Hereafter.","I have followed the way of my fathers — Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob. It was never for us to associate anything with God. That is from God’s grace upon us and upon mankind, but most people are not grateful.","O my two fellow prisoners, are many different lords better, or God, the One, the Vanquisher?","What you worship besides Him are nothing but names you and your fathers have invented. God has sent down no authority for them. Judgment belongs to none but God. He has commanded that you worship none but Him. That is the right religion, but most people do not know.","O my two fellow prisoners, as for one of you, he will pour wine for his master. As for the other, he will be crucified, and birds will eat from his head. The matter about which you inquire has been decided.”","He said to the one he thought would be saved of the two, “Mention me to your master.” But Satan made him forget to mention him to his master, so he remained in prison for several years.","The king said, “I see seven fat cows being devoured by seven lean ones, and seven green ears of grain and others dry. O notables, explain my vision to me, if you can interpret visions.”","They said, “Confused dreams, and we have no knowledge of interpreting dreams.”","The one of the two who was saved said, remembering after a long time, “I will inform you of its interpretation, so send me.”","“Joseph, O truthful one, explain to us seven fat cows being devoured by seven lean ones, and seven green ears of grain and others dry, so that I may return to the people, so that they may know.”","He said, “You will sow for seven years steadily. Whatever you harvest, leave it in its ear, except a little from which you eat.","Then after that will come seven harsh years that will consume what you stored up for them, except a little of what you preserve.","Then after that will come a year in which people will be given rain and in which they will press.”","The king said, “Bring him to me.” But when the messenger came to him, he said, “Go back to your master and ask him about the women who cut their hands. My Lord is well aware of their scheming.”","He said, “What was your intent when you tried to seduce Joseph?” They said, “God forbid! We knew of no evil in him.” The wife of the chief said, “Now the truth has come to light. I tried to seduce him, and he is truly one of the truthful.”","“That is so he may know that I did not betray him in his absence, and that God does not guide the scheming of the treacherous.","Yet I do not absolve myself. Surely the soul is ever inciting to evil, except those on whom my Lord has mercy. My Lord is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.”","The king said, “Bring him to me; I will reserve him for myself.” And when he spoke with him, he said, “Today you are established and trusted in our presence.”","He said, “Put me in charge of the storehouses of the land. I am a careful guardian, well-informed.”","And so We established Joseph in the land, settling wherever he wished. We bestow Our mercy on whoever We will, and We do not let the reward of those who do good go to waste.","And the reward of the Hereafter is better for those who believed and were God-conscious.","Joseph’s brothers came and entered upon him. He recognized them, but they did not recognize him.","And when he had furnished them with their provisions, he said, “Bring me a brother of yours from your father. Do you not see that I give full measure and that I am the best of hosts?","But if you do not bring him to me, there will be no measure for you with me, and do not come near me.”","They said, “We will try to persuade his father to part with him, and we will certainly do it.”","And he told his servants, “Place their merchandise in their saddlebags, so that they may recognize it when they return to their family, so that they may come back.”","When they returned to their father, they said, “O our father, the measure has been denied to us, so send our brother with us and we will obtain our measure. We will surely guard him.”","He said, “Can I trust you with him any more than I trusted you with his brother before? God is the best Guardian, and He is the Most Merciful of the merciful.”","And when they opened their baggage, they found their merchandise returned to them. They said, “O our father, what more could we ask for? Here is our merchandise returned to us. We will provide for our family, protect our brother, and gain an extra camel-load. That is an easy measure.”","He said, “I will never send him with you until you give me a solemn pledge before God that you will bring him back to me, unless you are completely overwhelmed.” And when they gave him their pledge, he said, “God is Guardian over what we say.”","And he said, “O my sons, do not enter through one gate, but enter through different gates. I cannot avail you anything against God. Judgment belongs to none but God. In Him I place my trust, and in Him let all who trust place their trust.”","And when they entered as their father had commanded them, it availed them nothing against God — it was only a need in Jacob’s soul that he fulfilled. He was truly possessed of knowledge because of what We had taught him, but most people do not know.","When they entered upon Joseph, he drew his brother close to him and said, “I am your brother, so do not grieve over what they used to do.”","When he had furnished them with their provisions, he placed the drinking cup in his brother’s bag. Then a crier called out, “O caravan, you are thieves!”","They said, turning toward them, “What are you missing?”","They said, “We are missing the king’s measuring cup, and whoever brings it will receive a camel’s load, and I guarantee it.”","They said, “By God, you know well that we did not come to cause corruption in the land, and we were never thieves.”","They said, “Then what is its recompense if you are liars?”","They said, “Its recompense is that whoever it is found in his bag — he himself is its recompense. That is how we repay the wrongdoers.”","So he began with their bags before his brother’s bag, then he extracted it from his brother’s bag. Thus did We scheme for Joseph. He could not have taken his brother under the king’s law unless God willed it. We raise in degrees whomever We will. And above every possessor of knowledge is one more knowing.","They said, “If he steals, a brother of his stole before.” Joseph kept it to himself and did not reveal it to them. He said, “You are in a worse position, and God knows best what you describe.”","They said, “O Chief, he has a father who is very old, so take one of us in his place. We see that you are a man of goodness.”","He said, “God forbid that we take anyone other than the one with whom we found our property. We would then truly be wrongdoers.”","When they despaired of him, they withdrew in private counsel. Their eldest said, “Do you not know that your father took a solemn pledge from you before God, and before that you failed regarding Joseph? I will never leave this land until my father permits me or God decides for me, and He is the best of judges.”","“Return to your father and say, ‘O our father, your son stole, and we testified only to what we knew, and we could not guard against the unseen.","And ask the town where we were and the caravan we traveled with. We are truly telling the truth.’”","He said, “Rather, your souls have enticed you into something. So patience is beautiful. Perhaps God will bring them all back to me. He is the All-Knowing, the All-Wise.”","And he turned away from them and said, “O my grief over Joseph!” And his eyes turned white from sorrow, and he was suppressing his anguish.","They said, “By God, you will not stop remembering Joseph until you waste away or perish!”","He said, “I only complain of my anguish and grief to God, and I know from God what you do not know.”","“O my sons, go and search for Joseph and his brother, and do not despair of God’s relief. Truly, none despair of God’s relief except the disbelieving people.”","So when they entered upon him, they said, “O Chief, hardship has struck us and our family, and we have brought meager goods. So give us full measure and be charitable to us. Surely God rewards the charitable.”","He said, “Do you know what you did to Joseph and his brother when you were ignorant?”","They said, “Is it really you who are Joseph?” He said, “I am Joseph, and this is my brother. God has been gracious to us. Whoever is mindful and patient — God never wastes the reward of those who do good.”","They said, “By God, God has truly favored you over us, and we were certainly in the wrong.”","He said, “No blame upon you today. May God forgive you, and He is the Most Merciful of the merciful.","Take this shirt of mine and cast it over my father’s face — he will regain his sight. And bring me your family, all of them.”","And when the caravan set out, their father said, “I truly sense the scent of Joseph — if only you would not think me senile.”","They said, “By God, you are still in your old delusion.”","But when the bearer of good news arrived, he cast it over his face, and he regained his sight. He said, “Did I not tell you that I know from God what you do not know?”","They said, “O our father, ask forgiveness for us of our sins. We were truly in the wrong.”","He said, “I will ask my Lord to forgive you. He is the All-Forgiving, the Most Merciful.”","So when they entered upon Joseph, he drew his parents close to him and said, “Enter Egypt, God willing, in safety.”","And he raised his parents upon the throne, and they fell before him in prostration. He said, “O my father, this is the fulfillment of my dream from before. My Lord has made it come true. He was good to me when He brought me out of prison and brought you from the desert after Satan had sown discord between me and my brothers. My Lord is Subtle in what He wills. He is the All-Knowing, the All-Wise.”","“My Lord, You have granted me some authority and taught me the interpretation of events. Originator of the heavens and the earth, You are my Protector in this world and the Hereafter. Take my soul in submission and join me with the righteous.”","That is from the news of the unseen which We reveal to you. You were not with them when they agreed on their plan while they were scheming.","Most people will not believe, no matter how eager you are.","You ask them no payment for it. It is only a reminder for all the worlds.","How many a sign in the heavens and the earth they pass by, turning away from it.","Most of them do not believe in God without associating others with Him.","Do they feel secure that an overwhelming punishment from God will not come upon them, or that the Hour will not come upon them suddenly while they are unaware?","Say, “This is my path: I call to God with clear insight — I and whoever follows me. Glory be to God, and I am not among those who associate others with Him.”","We sent before you none but men from the people of the towns, to whom We revealed. Have they not traveled through the land and seen what was the fate of those before them? Surely the home of the Hereafter is better for the God-conscious. Will you not reason?","Until, when the messengers despaired and thought they had been denied, Our help came to them, and We saved whoever We willed. Our punishment is never turned back from the guilty people.","Certainly in their stories is a lesson for people of understanding. It was not a fabricated tale, but a confirmation of what came before it, a detailed explanation of all things, a guidance, and a mercy for people who believe.","Alif Lam Mim Ra. These are the verses of the Book. What has been sent down to you from your Lord is the truth, but most people do not believe.","God is the One who raised the heavens without pillars that you can see, then established Himself over the Throne. He subjected the sun and the moon, each running for an appointed term. He directs all affairs and makes the signs clear, so that you may be certain of the meeting with your Lord.","He is the One who spread the earth and placed in it firm mountains and rivers, and of every fruit He made in it two pairs. He covers the day with the night. Surely in that are signs for people who reflect.","In the earth are neighboring tracts, and gardens of grapevines, and crops, and palm trees—clustered and unclustered—watered with the same water, yet We make some of them surpass others in taste. Surely in that are signs for people who reason.","If you are amazed, then truly amazing is their saying, “When we have become dust, will we really be in a new creation?” Those are the ones who have disbelieved in their Lord. Those will have shackles around their necks. Those are the companions of the Fire—they will remain in it forever.","They urge you to hasten the bad before the good, though exemplary punishments have already passed before them. Your Lord is truly full of forgiveness toward people despite their wrongdoing, and your Lord is truly severe in punishment.","Those who disbelieve say, “Why has no sign been sent down to him from his Lord?” You are only a warner, and every people have a guide.","God knows what every female carries, and what the wombs shrink and what they grow. Everything with Him is by precise measure.","Knower of the unseen and the seen, the Grand, the Most Exalted.","It is the same among you—whoever conceals his speech and whoever declares it openly, and whoever hides by night and goes about freely by day.","He has successive angels before him and behind him, guarding him by God’s command. God does not change the condition of a people until they change what is within themselves. And when God wills misfortune for a people, there is no repelling it, and they have no protector apart from Him.","It is He who shows you lightning, inspiring fear and hope, and He produces the heavy clouds.","The thunder glorifies His praise, and the angels too, out of awe of Him. He sends the thunderbolts and strikes with them whoever He wills, yet they dispute about God—and He is fierce in might.","To Him belongs the call of truth. And those they call upon besides Him do not respond to them at all—they are like one stretching his palms toward water so it may reach his mouth, but it never reaches it. The prayer of the disbelievers is nothing but futility.","To God prostrates whoever is in the heavens and the earth, willingly and unwillingly, and so do their shadows, morning and evening.","Say, “Who is the Lord of the heavens and the earth?” Say, “God.” Say, “Have you then taken protectors besides Him who have no power to benefit or harm even themselves?” Say, “Are the blind and the seeing equal? Or are darkness and light equal?” Or have they assigned partners to God who created as He creates, so that the creation seemed alike to them? Say, “God is the Creator of all things, and He is the One, the Vanquisher.”","He sent down water from the sky, and valleys flowed according to their measure, and the torrent carried a rising foam. And from what they heat in the fire, seeking ornaments or goods, comes a foam like it. Thus God strikes the comparison of truth and falsehood. As for the foam, it vanishes as waste, but what benefits people remains in the earth. Thus God strikes comparisons.","For those who answered their Lord is the best reward. And those who did not answer Him—even if they possessed everything on earth and its equal with it, they would offer it all as ransom. Those will have the worst reckoning, and their refuge is Hell—what a wretched resting place!","Is one who knows that what was sent down to you from your Lord is the truth like one who is blind? Only those of understanding take heed.","Those who fulfill God’s covenant and do not break the pact.","And those who join what God has commanded to be joined, and fear their Lord, and dread the worst reckoning.","And those who endured patiently seeking their Lord’s face, and established prayer, and spent from what We provided them secretly and openly, and repel evil with good—those will have the ultimate home.","Gardens of eternity, which they will enter along with whoever was righteous among their fathers, their spouses, and their descendants. And the angels will enter upon them from every gate.","“Peace be upon you for your patience.” How excellent is the ultimate home!","But those who break God’s covenant after it was affirmed, and sever what God has commanded to be joined, and spread corruption in the earth—those will have the curse, and theirs is the worst home.","God extends provision to whom He wills and restricts it. They rejoiced in the life of this world, yet the life of this world compared to the Hereafter is nothing but a fleeting enjoyment.","Those who disbelieve say, “Why has no sign been sent down to him from his Lord?” Say, “Truly, God leads astray whoever He wills and guides to Himself whoever turns back to Him.”","Those who believe, whose hearts find peace in the remembrance of God — surely, in the remembrance of God hearts find peace.","Those who believe and do righteous deeds — blessed are they, and beautiful is their return.","Thus We have sent you among a nation before which other nations have passed away, so that you may recite to them what We have revealed to you, yet they disbelieve in the Most Merciful. Say, “He is my Lord. There is no god but Him. In Him I place my trust, and to Him is my return.”","Even if there were a Quran by which mountains were moved, or the earth were split apart, or the dead were spoken to — rather, to God belongs the command entirely. Have those who believe not yet realized that had God willed, He would have guided all people? Disaster will not cease to strike those who disbelieve for what they have done, or to settle close to their homes, until God’s promise comes. Truly, God does not break His promise.","Messengers before you were mocked, and I gave the disbelievers respite, then I seized them — so how was My punishment?","Is He who stands over every soul for what it has earned? Yet they have assigned partners to God. Say, “Name them. Or would you inform Him of something He does not know on earth? Or is it just empty words?” Rather, their scheming has been made appealing to those who disbelieve, and they have been barred from the path. Whoever God leads astray has no guide.","For them is punishment in the life of this world, and the punishment of the Hereafter is far harder — and they have no protector against God.","The likeness of the Garden promised to the righteous: rivers flow beneath it, its fruit is everlasting and so is its shade. That is the end for the righteous, and the end for the disbelievers is the Fire.","Those to whom We gave the Book rejoice in what has been sent down to you, but among the factions are those who reject part of it. Say, “I have only been commanded to worship God and not associate anything with Him. To Him I call, and to Him is my return.”","Thus We sent it down as an authority in Arabic. If you follow their desires after the knowledge that has come to you, you will have no protector or shield against God.","We sent messengers before you and gave them wives and offspring. No messenger could bring a sign except by God’s permission. For every term there is a decree.","God erases what He wills and confirms, and with Him is the Mother of the Book.","Whether We show you some of what We promise them or take your life, your duty is only to convey, and Ours is the reckoning.","Do they not see that We come upon the land, diminishing it from its edges? God judges — none can reverse His judgment — and He is swift in reckoning.","Those before them plotted, but all plotting belongs to God. He knows what every soul earns, and the disbelievers will come to know whose is the final home.","Those who disbelieve say, “You are not a messenger.” Say, “God is sufficient as a witness between me and you, and whoever has knowledge of the Book.”","Alif Lam Ra. A Book We sent down to you so that you may bring people out of darkness into light, by their Lord’s permission, to the path of the Almighty, the Praiseworthy.","God—to whom belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth. Woe to the disbelievers from a severe punishment.","Those who prefer the life of this world over the Hereafter, and turn others from God’s path, and seek to make it crooked—they are in deep error.","We never sent a messenger except in the language of his people, so he could make things clear to them. Then God leads astray whom He wills and guides whom He wills. He is the Almighty, the All-Wise.","Truly We sent Moses with Our miracles: “Bring your people out of darkness into light, and remind them of the days of God.” In that are miracles for everyone who is patient and grateful.","When Moses said to his people, “Remember God’s blessing upon you when He saved you from Pharaoh’s people, who were inflicting the worst torment on you, slaughtering your sons and sparing your women. In that was a tremendous trial from your Lord.”","When your Lord proclaimed, “If you are grateful, I will surely give you more, but if you are ungrateful, My punishment is truly severe.”","Moses said, “If you disbelieve—you and everyone on earth altogether—God is truly Self-Sufficient, Praiseworthy.”","Has the news not reached you of those before you—the people of Noah, Ad, and Thamud, and those after them? None knows them but God. Their messengers came to them with clear proofs, but they thrust their hands into their mouths and said, “We reject what you have been sent with, and we are in deep, troubling doubt about what you call us to.”","Their messengers said, “Is there doubt about God, Originator of the heavens and the earth? He calls you to forgive you some of your sins and grant you respite until an appointed time.” They said, “You are nothing but humans like us. You want to turn us away from what our fathers used to worship. So bring us a clear authority.”","Their messengers said to them, “We are nothing but humans like you, but God bestows His favor on whomever He wills of His servants. It is not for us to bring you any authority except by God’s permission. And in God let the believers place their trust.","Why should we not place our trust in God when He has guided us to our paths? We will surely endure whatever harm you cause us. And in God let those who trust place their trust.”","Those who disbelieved said to their messengers, “We will surely drive you out of our land, or you will return to our creed.” So their Lord revealed to them, “We will surely destroy the wrongdoers.","And We will surely settle you in the land after them. That is for whoever fears My station and fears My threat.”","They sought victory, and every stubborn tyrant was brought to ruin.","Beyond him lies Hell, and he is given festering water to drink.","He gulps it but can barely swallow it. Death comes at him from every direction, yet he does not die, and beyond him lies a harsh punishment.","The example of those who disbelieve in their Lord: their deeds are like ashes lashed by wind on a stormy day. They have no power over anything they earned. That is the far-gone straying.","Do you not see that God created the heavens and the earth in truth? If He wills, He can remove you and bring a new creation.","And that is not difficult for God.","They all appear before God, and the weak say to those who were arrogant, “We were your followers — can you shield us from any of God’s punishment?” They say, “Had God guided us, we would have guided you. It is the same for us whether we panic or endure — there is no escape for us.”","And Satan says when the matter is settled, “Truly, God promised you the promise of truth, and I promised you but betrayed you. I had no authority over you — I merely called you and you answered me. So do not blame me; blame yourselves. I cannot rescue you, and you cannot rescue me. I reject what you associated me with before.” Surely the wrongdoers will have a painful punishment.","And those who believed and did righteous deeds are admitted into gardens beneath which rivers flow, dwelling there forever by their Lord’s permission. Their greeting therein is “Peace.”","Do you not see how God strikes an example? A good word is like a good tree — its roots firm and its branches in the sky.","Yielding its fruit every season by its Lord’s permission. God strikes examples for people so that they may reflect.","And the example of a foul word is like a foul tree, uprooted from the surface of the earth, having no stability.","God makes firm those who believe with the firm word in the life of this world and in the Hereafter. And God leads the wrongdoers astray. And God does what He wills.","Have you not seen those who exchanged God’s blessing for ingratitude and led their people to the abode of ruin?","Hell — they will burn in it. What a wretched settlement!","They set up rivals to God to lead others astray from His path. Say, “Enjoy yourselves, for your destination is the Fire.”","Tell My servants who believe to establish prayer and spend from what We have provided them, secretly and openly, before a Day comes in which there is no bargaining and no friendship.","God is the One who created the heavens and the earth, sent down water from the sky, and brought out with it fruits as provision for you. He subjected the ships to you, sailing through the sea by His command, and He subjected the rivers to you.","He subjected the sun and the moon to you, both in constant motion, and He subjected the night and the day to you.","He gave you of everything you asked Him for. If you tried to count God’s blessings, you could never enumerate them. Truly, man is deeply unjust, deeply ungrateful.","And when Abraham said, “My Lord, make this city secure, and keep me and my sons from worshiping idols.","My Lord, they have led so many people astray. So whoever follows me is of me, and whoever disobeys me — You are truly All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","Our Lord, I have settled some of my descendants in a barren valley by Your Sacred House. Our Lord, so that they may establish prayer, make the hearts of people incline toward them, and provide them with fruits, so that they may be grateful.","Our Lord, You know what we conceal and what we reveal. Nothing on earth or in the sky is hidden from God.","Praise be to God, who granted me Ishmael and Isaac in my old age. Surely my Lord is the Hearer of supplication.","My Lord, make me one who establishes prayer, and from my descendants as well. Our Lord, accept my supplication.","Our Lord, forgive me, my parents, and the believers on the Day the reckoning is established.”","Do not think God is unaware of what the wrongdoers do. He only delays them until a Day when eyes will stare in horror.","Racing forward, heads craned upward, their gaze not returning to them, and their hearts hollow.","Warn the people of the Day when the punishment comes upon them, and those who wronged will say, “Our Lord, grant us a brief reprieve so we may answer Your call and follow the messengers.” Did you not swear before that there would be no end for you?","You dwelt in the homes of those who wronged themselves, and it was made clear to you how We dealt with them, and We set examples for you.","They schemed their schemes, but with God is their scheming — even if their scheming was such that mountains would crumble from it.","So do not think God will break His promise to His messengers. Truly God is All-Mighty, Possessor of retribution.","On the Day the earth is replaced by another earth, and the heavens too, and they emerge before God, the One, the Vanquisher.","You will see the criminals that Day bound together in chains.","Their garments of tar, and fire covering their faces.","So that God may recompense every soul for what it earned. Truly God is swift in reckoning.","This is a message for the people — so that they may be warned by it, and so that they may know that He is One God, and so that those of understanding may take heed.","Alif Lam Ra. These are the verses of the Book and a clear Quran.","Perhaps those who disbelieved will wish they had been Muslims.","Leave them to eat and enjoy themselves, and let hope distract them — they will come to know.","We never destroyed a town except that it had a known decree.","No nation can advance its appointed time, nor can they delay it.","They said, “O you upon whom the Reminder was sent down, you are truly mad.","Why do you not bring us the angels, if you are among the truthful?”","We do not send down the angels except with the truth, and then they would not be given respite.","It is We who sent down the Reminder, and it is We who will preserve it.","We sent messengers before you among the factions of old.","And no messenger came to them except that they mocked him.","Thus We drive it into the hearts of the criminals.","They do not believe in it, though the precedent of the ancients has already passed.","Even if We opened for them a gate in the sky and they kept ascending through it.","They would say, “Our eyes have been dazzled — rather, we are a bewitched people.”","We placed constellations in the sky and adorned it for the beholders.","And We guarded it from every accursed devil.","Except one who steals a hearing, and a clear flame pursues him.","And the earth — We spread it out, cast upon it firm mountains, and grew in it everything in due measure.","And We made in it livelihoods for you, and for those you do not provide for.","There is nothing whose treasuries are not with Us, and We do not send it down except in a known measure.","We sent the winds as pollinators, then sent down water from the sky and gave it to you to drink — and you are not its keepers.","Truly it is We who give life and cause death, and We are the Inheritors.","We have known those among you who came before, and We have known those who came after.","Your Lord — it is He who will gather them. He is All-Wise, All-Knowing.","Certainly We created man from dried clay, from molded dark mud.","And the jinn We created before him from the fire of scorching wind.","And when your Lord said to the angels, “I am creating a human being from dried clay, from molded dark mud.","So when I have fashioned him and breathed into him of My spirit, fall down before him in prostration.”","So the angels prostrated, all of them together.","Except Iblis — he refused to be among those who prostrated.","He said, “O Iblis, what is the matter with you that you are not among those who prostrated?”","He said, “I would never prostrate to a human being You created from dried clay, from molded dark mud.”","He said, “Then get out of here, for you are accursed.","And upon you is the curse until the Day of Judgment.”","He said, “My Lord, then grant me respite until the Day they are resurrected.”","He said, “You are among those granted respite.","Until the Day of the appointed time.”","He said, “My Lord, because You have led me astray, I will surely make things alluring for them on earth, and I will surely lead them all astray.","Except Your devoted servants among them.”","He said, “This is a straight path binding upon Me.","Over My servants you have no authority, except those who follow you from among the deviant.","And Hell is surely the promised place for all of them.","It has seven gates; to each gate is an assigned portion of them.”","Truly the reverent will be in gardens and springs.","“Enter them in peace, secure.”","And We will strip from their hearts whatever rancor there was — as brothers, on couches, facing one another.","No weariness will touch them there, nor will they ever be expelled from it.","Inform My servants that I am the All-Forgiving, the Most Merciful.","And that My punishment — it is the painful punishment.","Tell them about Abraham’s guests.","When they entered upon him and said, “Peace,” he said, “We are afraid of you.”","They said, “Do not be afraid. We bring you good news of a knowledgeable boy.”","He said, “Do you bring me good news when old age has touched me? What good news do you bring?”","They said, “We bring you good news in truth, so do not be among those who despair.”","He said, “Who despairs of his Lord’s mercy except those who are astray?”","He said, “So what is your mission, O messengers?”","They said, “We have been sent to a criminal people.","Except Lot’s family — we will save them all.","Except his wife — we have decreed that she will be among those who remain behind.”","So when the messengers came to Lot’s family.","He said, “You are people unknown to me.”","They said, “Rather, we have come to you with what they used to doubt.","We have come to you with the truth, and we are truthful.","So travel with your family during a portion of the night, and follow behind them, and let none of you turn around, and go where you are commanded.”","We conveyed to him that decree: that the last remnant of those people would be cut off by morning.","The people of the city came rejoicing.","He said, “These are my guests, so do not disgrace me.","Be mindful of God and do not humiliate me.”","They said, “Did we not forbid you from all people?”","He said, “Here are my daughters, if you must act.”","By your life, they were wandering blindly in their intoxication.","So the blast seized them at sunrise.","We turned it upside down and rained upon them stones of baked clay.","Surely in that are signs for those who read the signs.","It lies along an established road.","Surely in that is a sign for the believers.","The people of the Thicket were truly wrongdoers.","So We took vengeance on them, and both are along a clear highway.","Certainly the people of the Stone Valley denied the messengers.","We gave them Our signs, but they turned away from them.","They used to carve houses from the mountains, feeling secure.","So the blast seized them at morning.","Nothing they had earned availed them.","We did not create the heavens and the earth and what is between them except in truth. The Hour is surely coming, so forgive with a gracious forgiveness.","Your Lord is the Supreme Creator, the All-Knowing.","We have given you seven of the oft-repeated verses and the great Quran.","Do not extend your eyes toward what We have given some pairs among them to enjoy, and do not grieve over them, and lower your wing to the believers.","Say, “I am the clear warner.”","Just as We sent down upon the dividers.","Those who made the Quran into fragments.","By your Lord, We will question them all.","About what they used to do.","So proclaim what you are commanded and turn away from the polytheists.","We are enough for you against the mockers.","Those who set up another god alongside God — they will come to know.","We certainly know that your chest tightens at what they say.","So glorify your Lord with praise and be among those who prostrate.","Worship your Lord until the certainty comes to you.","God’s command has come, so do not seek to hasten it. Glory be to Him, and exalted is He above what they associate with Him.","He sends down the angels with the spirit of His command upon whomever He wills of His servants: “Warn that there is no god but Me, so fear Me.”","He created the heavens and the earth in truth. Exalted is He above what they associate with Him.","He created man from a drop of fluid, and at once he is an open adversary.","And livestock He created for you — in them is warmth and benefits, and from them you eat.","In them is beauty for you when you bring them home at evening and when you drive them out to pasture.","They carry your heavy loads to lands you could not have reached except with great hardship. Truly your Lord is Most Compassionate, Most Merciful.","And horses, mules, and donkeys for you to ride and as adornment. And He creates what you do not know.","Upon God lies the direction of the path, and some paths veer away. Had He willed, He would have guided you all.","It is He who sent down water from the sky. From it you have drink, and from it come plants on which you graze your herds.","With it He grows for you crops, olives, palms, grapevines, and every kind of fruit. Surely in that is a sign for people who reflect.","He subjected the night and the day to your service, and the sun and the moon. And the stars are subjected by His command. Surely in that are signs for people who reason.","And what He has spread across the earth for you in varying colors — surely in that is a sign for people who take heed.","It is He who subjected the sea so that you may eat fresh meat from it and extract from it ornaments you wear. You see the ships plowing through it, so that you may seek His bounty, and so that you may be grateful.","He cast firm mountains into the earth lest it sway with you, and rivers and pathways, so that you may find your way.","And landmarks. And by the stars they are guided.","Is the One who creates like those who do not create? Will you not reflect?","If you tried to count God’s blessings, you could never exhaust them. Truly, God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","God knows what you conceal and what you reveal.","Those they invoke besides God create nothing — they themselves are created.","Dead, not alive, and they do not perceive when they will be raised.","Your God is one God. As for those who do not believe in the Hereafter, their hearts are in denial, and they are arrogant.","Without doubt, God knows what they conceal and what they reveal. He does not love the arrogant.","When they are told, “What has your Lord sent down?” they say, “Legends of the ancients.”","So that they bear their burdens in full on the Day of Resurrection, and some of the burdens of those they led astray without knowledge. How wretched is what they bear!","Those before them plotted, but God came at their structure from the foundations, and the roof collapsed upon them from above, and the punishment came to them from where they did not perceive.","Then on the Day of Resurrection He will disgrace them and say, “Where are My partners over whom you used to dispute?” Those given knowledge will say, “Surely disgrace and misery today are upon the disbelievers.”","Those whom the angels take in death while they are wronging themselves — they will offer submission: “We were not doing any evil.” But yes! God is All-Knowing of what you used to do.","So enter the gates of Hell, dwelling therein forever. How wretched is the abode of the arrogant!","And it is said to the God-conscious, “What has your Lord sent down?” They say, “Good.” For those who do good in this world is good, and the home of the Hereafter is better. How excellent is the home of the righteous.","Gardens of eternity which they enter, beneath which rivers flow. In them they have whatever they wish. Thus does God recompense the reverent.","Those whom the angels take in death while they are pure — they say to them, “Peace be upon you. Enter Paradise for what you used to do.”","Are they waiting for anything but the angels to come to them or your Lord’s command to come? So did those before them. God did not wrong them, but they used to wrong themselves.","So the evils of what they did struck them, and what they used to mock closed in around them.","Those who associated partners with God said, “Had God willed, we would not have worshiped anything besides Him — neither we nor our fathers — nor would we have forbidden anything besides Him.” So did those before them. Is there upon the messengers anything but clear delivery?","Certainly We sent to every nation a messenger: “Worship God and shun false gods.” Among them were those whom God guided, and among them were those upon whom misguidance was justified. So travel through the earth and see how the deniers met their end.","Even if you are eager for their guidance, God does not guide those He leaves astray, and they will have no helpers.","They swore by God their most solemn oaths that God will not resurrect those who die. But yes — a binding promise upon Him — yet most people do not know.","So that He may make clear to them what they differed over, and so that those who disbelieved may know that they were liars.","Our word to a thing, when We will it, is only that We say to it, “Be,” and it is.","Those who emigrated for God’s sake after they were wronged — We will surely settle them well in this world, and the reward of the Hereafter is greater, if only they knew.","Those who were patient and place their trust in their Lord.","We sent before you none but men to whom We revealed. So ask the people of knowledge if you do not know.","With clear proofs and scriptures. And We sent down to you the Reminder so that you may make clear to people what was sent down to them, and so that they may reflect.","Do those who plot evil deeds feel secure that God will not cause the earth to swallow them, or that the punishment will not come upon them from where they do not perceive?","Or that He will not seize them during their movements? They cannot escape.","Or that He will not seize them through gradual decline? Truly your Lord is Most Compassionate, Most Merciful.","Have they not seen how the shadows of everything God has created shift from the right and the left, prostrating to God, utterly humbled?","To God prostrates every creature in the heavens and on the earth, and the angels — and they are not arrogant.","They fear their Lord above them and do what they are commanded.","God has said, “Do not take two gods. He is only one God. So fear Me alone.”","To Him belongs whatever is in the heavens and the earth, and to Him is devotion perpetually due. Will you then be mindful of other than God?","Whatever blessing you have is from God. Then when hardship touches you, it is to Him you cry out.","Then when He lifts the hardship from you, suddenly a group among you associates partners with their Lord.","So that they may deny what We have given them. So enjoy yourselves — you will soon come to know.","They assign to what they have no knowledge of a share of what We have provided them. By God, you will surely be questioned about what you used to fabricate.","They assign daughters to God — glory be to Him — while they have what they desire.","When one of them is given news of a female, his face darkens and he is filled with suppressed rage.","He hides from the people because of the evil of what he was given news of. Should he keep it in humiliation, or bury it in the dust? How wretched is their judgment!","For those who do not believe in the Hereafter is the worst description, and for God is the highest description. He is the All-Mighty, the All-Wise.","If God were to hold people accountable for their wrongdoing, He would not leave upon it a single creature. But He defers them to an appointed time. When their time comes, they cannot delay it by a single hour, nor can they advance it.","They assign to God what they themselves detest, and their tongues utter the lie that the best reward is theirs. Without doubt, the Fire is theirs, and they will be abandoned.","By God, We sent messengers to nations before you, but Satan made their deeds appealing to them. So he is their patron today, and for them is a painful punishment.","We have not sent down the Book to you except so that you may make clear to them what they differed over, and as guidance and mercy for a people who believe.","God sent down water from the sky and brought the earth to life after its death. Surely in that is a sign for a people who listen.","Truly, in livestock there is a lesson for you. We give you to drink from what is in their bellies—from between dung and blood—pure milk, pleasant for those who drink it.","From the fruits of date palms and grapevines you derive intoxicants and wholesome provision. Surely in that is a sign for people who reason.","Your Lord inspired the bee: “Make your homes in the mountains, in the trees, and in what they construct.","Then eat from every kind of fruit and follow the paths your Lord has made easy for you.” From their bellies comes a drink of varying colors, in which there is healing for people. Surely in that is a sign for people who reflect.","God created you, then He takes you in death. Among you are those who are returned to the most feeble age, so that after having known, they know nothing at all. Truly, God is All-Knowing, All-Powerful.","God has favored some of you over others in provision. Yet those who were favored would not hand their provision to those whom their right hands possess so that they become equal in it. Do they then deny God’s blessings?","God has made for you spouses from among yourselves and made for you from your spouses children and grandchildren, and provided you with good things. Do they then believe in falsehood and deny God’s blessings?","They worship besides God what possesses no power to provide them anything from the heavens and the earth, nor are they able to.","So do not make comparisons for God. Truly, God knows and you do not know.","God strikes a parable: a slave who is owned, powerless over anything, and one whom We have provided with good provision from Us, and he spends from it secretly and openly. Are they equal? All praise belongs to God. But most of them do not know.","God strikes a parable of two men: one of them mute, powerless over anything, a burden on his master—wherever he directs him, he brings no good. Is he equal to one who commands justice and is on a straight path?","To God belongs the unseen of the heavens and the earth. The matter of the Hour is nothing but the blink of an eye, or even nearer. Truly, God is Capable of all things.","God brought you out of your mothers’ wombs knowing nothing, and gave you hearing, sight, and hearts, so that you might be grateful.","Have they not seen the birds held in flight in the open sky? None holds them but God. Surely in that are signs for people who believe.","God made your homes a place of rest for you, and made for you from the hides of livestock tents you find light on the day you travel and the day you settle, and from their wool, fur, and hair — furnishings and provision for a time.","God made for you shade from what He created, and made for you shelters in the mountains, and made for you garments that protect you from the heat and garments that protect you in battle. Thus He completes His favor upon you, so that you might submit.","If they turn away, your only duty is clear delivery of the message.","They recognize God’s favor, then deny it, and most of them are ungrateful.","On the Day We raise from every nation a witness, then those who disbelieved will not be permitted to make excuses, nor will they be allowed to make amends.","When those who wronged see the punishment, it will not be lightened for them, nor will they be given respite.","When those who associated partners see their partners, they will say, “Our Lord, these are our partners whom we used to call upon besides You.” But they will hurl back at them the words, “You are surely liars!”","They will offer submission to God on that Day, and all they used to fabricate will forsake them.","Those who disbelieved and turned others from God’s path — We will increase them in punishment upon punishment for the corruption they used to spread.","On the Day We raise in every nation a witness against them from among themselves, and We bring you as a witness against these — We have sent down to you the Book as a clarification of all things, and as guidance, mercy, and glad tidings for those who submit.","Truly, God commands justice, excellence, and giving to relatives, and He forbids indecency, wrongdoing, and transgression. He admonishes you so that you may take heed.","Fulfill God’s covenant when you have made it, and do not break your oaths after confirming them, for you have made God your guarantor. God knows what you do.","Do not be like the woman who unraveled her yarn after spinning it strong, using your oaths as a means of deceit among yourselves because one community is more numerous than another. God only tests you through this, and He will certainly make clear to you on the Day of Resurrection what you used to differ over.","Had God willed, He would have made you one community, but He leads astray whom He wills and guides whom He wills. And you will surely be questioned about what you used to do.","Do not use your oaths as a means of deceit among yourselves, lest a foot slip after being firmly planted, and you taste misery for having turned others from God’s path, and yours be a tremendous punishment.","Do not sell God’s covenant for a paltry price. What is with God is far better for you, if only you knew.","What you have runs out, but what God has endures. And We will surely recompense those who were patient their reward according to the best of what they used to do.","Whoever does good, whether male or female, while being a believer, We will surely grant them a good life, and We will surely recompense them their reward according to the best of what they used to do.","So when you recite the Quran, seek refuge in God from Satan, the accursed.","He has no authority over those who believe and place their trust in their Lord.","His authority is only over those who take him as an ally and those who, through him, associate partners with God.","When We replace a verse in place of another verse — and God knows best what He sends down — they say, “You are only a fabricator.” Rather, most of them do not know.","Say, “The Holy Spirit brought it down from your Lord in truth, to strengthen those who believe, and as guidance and glad tidings for those who submit.”","We certainly know that they say, “It is only a human who teaches him.” The tongue of the one they point to is foreign, while this is a clear Arabic tongue.","Truly, those who do not believe in God’s verses — God will not guide them, and for them is a painful punishment.","It is only those who do not believe in God’s verses who fabricate lies, and it is they who are the liars.","Whoever disbelieves in God after having believed — except one who is compelled while his heart remains at peace with faith — but whoever opens his chest to disbelief, upon them is wrath from God, and for them is a terrible punishment.","That is because they preferred the life of this world over the Hereafter, and because God does not guide the disbelieving people.","Those are the ones whose hearts, hearing, and sight God has sealed, and those are the heedless.","Without doubt, in the Hereafter they will be the losers.","Then surely your Lord, to those who emigrated after they were persecuted, then strived and endured — surely your Lord, after all that, is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","On the Day every soul comes pleading for itself, and every soul is paid in full for what it did, and they will not be wronged.","God strikes a parable: a town that was secure and at peace, its provision coming to it abundantly from every place. Then it denied God’s blessings, so God made it taste the garment of hunger and fear for what they used to do.","A messenger from among them had come to them, but they denied him, so the punishment seized them while they were wrongdoers.","So eat from what God has provided you, lawful and good, and be grateful for God’s blessing, if it is Him you worship.","He has only forbidden you carrion, blood, the flesh of swine, and what has been slaughtered in the name of other than God. But whoever is compelled, neither craving nor transgressing, then God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","Do not say, based on the lies your tongues utter, “This is lawful and this is forbidden,” fabricating lies against God. Truly those who fabricate lies against God will not succeed.","A brief enjoyment, and for them is a painful punishment.","Upon those who became Jews, We forbade what We related to you before. We did not wrong them, but they used to wrong themselves.","Then surely your Lord, to those who did evil in ignorance and then repented after that and made amends—truly your Lord, after all that, is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","Abraham was a nation unto himself, devoutly obedient to God, a monotheist, and he was never among those who associated others with God.","Grateful for His blessings. He chose him and guided him to a straight path.","And We gave him good in this world, and in the Hereafter he is surely among the righteous.","Then We revealed to you, “Follow the way of Abraham, a monotheist, and he was never among those who associated others with God.”","The Sabbath was imposed only upon those who differed over it. Your Lord will surely judge between them on the Day of Resurrection concerning what they used to differ over.","Call to the way of your Lord with wisdom and good counsel, and debate with them in the best manner. Your Lord knows best who has strayed from His path, and He knows best who are guided.","If you retaliate, then retaliate with the like of what was inflicted upon you. But if you are patient, that is surely better for the patient.","Be patient—and your patience is only through God. Do not grieve over them, and do not be distressed by what they scheme.","Truly God is with the mindful and those who do good.","Glory to Him who took His servant on a night journey from the Sacred Mosque to the Farthest Mosque, whose surroundings We have blessed, to show him some of Our signs. He is the All-Hearing, the All-Seeing.","We gave Moses the Scripture and made it a guidance for the Children of Israel: “Take no guardian besides Me.","O descendants of those We carried with Noah.” He was truly a grateful servant.","We decreed to the Children of Israel in the Scripture: “You will surely spread corruption in the land twice, and you will surely rise to great arrogance.”","When the first of the two promises came, We sent against you servants of Ours of great might, and they ravaged through the homes. It was a promise fulfilled.","Then We gave you back your turn against them and reinforced you with wealth and sons and made you greater in number.","If you do good, you do good for yourselves, and if you do evil, it is against yourselves. So when the last promise came, to disgrace your faces and to enter the mosque as they entered it the first time, and to utterly destroy whatever they overran.","Perhaps your Lord will have mercy on you. But if you return, We will return. And We have made Hell a prison for the disbelievers.","Truly this Quran guides to what is most upright and gives good news to the believers who do righteous deeds that they will have a great reward.","And that those who do not believe in the Hereafter — We have prepared for them a painful punishment.","Man prays for evil as he prays for good. Man is ever hasty.","We made the night and the day two signs. We darkened the sign of the night and made the sign of the day bright, so that you may seek bounty from your Lord and so that you may know the number of years and the reckoning. Everything We have explained in detail.","Every person’s fate We have fastened to his neck, and on the Day of Resurrection We will bring out for him a record that he will find spread open.","“Read your record. Your own soul suffices today as a reckoner against you.”","Whoever is guided is guided only for his own soul, and whoever goes astray goes astray only against it. No bearer of burdens bears the burden of another. And We never punish until We send a messenger.","When We intend to destroy a town, We command its affluent ones, and they defiantly disobey in it, so the decree is justified against it, and We destroy it utterly.","How many generations We have destroyed after Noah. Your Lord suffices as All-Aware, All-Seeing of His servants’ sins.","Whoever desires the immediate life, We hasten for him in it whatever We will, for whomever We choose. Then We assign him Hell, where he will burn, condemned and cast out.","Whoever desires the Hereafter and strives for it with the striving it deserves, while he is a believer — those are the ones whose striving is appreciated.","To each — these and those — We extend from your Lord’s giving. And your Lord’s giving is never restricted.","Look how We have favored some of them over others. Yet the Hereafter is greater in ranks and greater in distinction.","Do not set up another god alongside God, or you will sit condemned and forsaken.","Your Lord has decreed that you worship none but Him, and that you show kindness to your parents. If one or both of them reach old age with you, do not say to them so much as “Uff,” and do not rebuke them, but speak to them with gracious words.","And lower to them the wing of humility out of mercy, and say, “My Lord, have mercy on them as they raised me when I was small.”","Your Lord knows best what is in your souls. If you are righteous, He is truly Forgiving to those who turn back to Him.","Give the relative his due, and the needy, and the traveler, and do not squander wastefully.","Surely the squanderers are brothers of the devils, and Satan is ever ungrateful to his Lord.","If you must turn away from them, seeking a mercy from your Lord that you hope for, then speak to them a gentle word.","Do not keep your hand chained to your neck, and do not stretch it open completely, or you will sit blamed and depleted.","Truly your Lord extends provision to whomever He wills and restricts it. He is ever All-Aware, All-Seeing of His servants.","Do not kill your children for fear of poverty. We provide for them and for you. Surely killing them is a grave sin.","Do not go near adultery. It is an obscenity and a wretched path.","Do not kill the soul that God has made sacred, except by right. Whoever is killed unjustly — We have given his heir authority, but let him not exceed in killing. He will be aided.","Do not approach the orphan’s wealth except in the way that is best, until he reaches maturity. And fulfill your covenants — surely the covenant will be questioned about.","Give full measure when you measure, and weigh with an even balance. That is better and fairer in outcome.","Do not pursue what you have no knowledge of. Surely the hearing, the sight, and the heart — each of those will be questioned about.","Do not walk on the earth with arrogance. You will never tear through the earth, and you will never reach the mountains in height.","The evil of all that is detestable in the sight of your Lord.","That is from the wisdom your Lord has revealed to you. Do not set up another god alongside God, or you will be cast into Hell, blamed and rejected.","Has your Lord favored you with sons and taken for Himself females from the angels? Surely you say a monstrous thing.","We have varied the teachings in this Quran so they may take heed, yet it only increases their aversion.","Say, “If there were gods with Him as they claim, then they would have sought a way to the Lord of the Throne.”","Glory be to Him, and exalted is He far above what they say — immeasurably exalted.","The seven heavens and the earth and all who are in them glorify Him. There is nothing that does not glorify His praise, but you do not comprehend their glorification. Truly He is Ever-Forbearing, All-Forgiving.","When you recite the Quran, We place between you and those who do not believe in the Hereafter an invisible barrier.","We have placed coverings over their hearts so they cannot comprehend it, and deafness in their ears. And when you mention your Lord alone in the Quran, they turn their backs in aversion.","We know best what they listen with when they listen to you, and when they confer privately, when the wrongdoers say, “You follow nothing but a bewitched man.”","See how they coin comparisons for you — they have gone astray and cannot find a way.","They say, “When we are bones and crumbled dust, will we really be raised as a new creation?”","Say, “Be stones or iron.","Or any creation that looms great in your minds.” They will say, “Who will bring us back?” Say, “The One who created you the first time.” They will shake their heads at you and say, “When will that be?” Say, “Perhaps it is near.”","The Day He calls you, you will respond with His praise and think you lingered only a little while.","Tell My servants to speak in the best manner. Surely Satan stirs discord between them. Surely Satan has always been a clear enemy to man.","Your Lord knows you best. If He wills, He will have mercy on you, or if He wills, He will punish you. We have not sent you as a guardian over them.","Your Lord knows best who is in the heavens and the earth. We have favored some prophets over others, and We gave David the Psalms.","Say, “Call upon those you claimed besides Him — they have no power to remove harm from you or to shift it.”","Those they call upon themselves seek means of nearness to their Lord, vying which of them is closest, and they hope for His mercy and fear His punishment. Truly your Lord’s punishment is something to be dreaded.","There is no town but We will destroy it before the Day of Resurrection or punish it with a severe punishment. That has been written in the Record.","Nothing prevented Us from sending miracles except that the earlier peoples denied them. We gave Thamud the she-camel as a clear miracle, yet they were unjust with it. We only send miracles as a warning.","And when We told you, “Your Lord has encompassed the people.” We made the vision We showed you only a trial for the people, and likewise the cursed tree in the Quran. We warn them, yet it only increases them in great defiance.","And when We said to the angels, “Prostrate to Adam,” they prostrated — except Iblis. He said, “Am I to prostrate to one You created from clay?”","He said, “Do You see this one You have honored above me? If You grant me respite until the Day of Resurrection, I will surely seize his descendants, all but a few.”","He said, “Go! Whoever among them follows you — Hell is your recompense, a full recompense.","Lure whoever you can among them with your voice, rally against them your cavalry and infantry, share with them in wealth and children, and make them promises.” But Satan promises them nothing but delusion.","“Over My servants you have no authority.” Your Lord suffices as a Guardian.","Your Lord is the One who drives ships for you through the sea so that you may seek His bounty. Truly He is ever Merciful to you.","When harm touches you at sea, all those you call upon vanish — except Him. Yet when He delivers you to land, you turn away. Man has always been ungrateful.","Do you feel secure that He will not cause the shore to swallow you, or send a storm of stones upon you, and then you find no guardian for yourselves?","Or do you feel secure that He will not send you back into it another time and unleash upon you a shattering wind and drown you for your disbelief, and then you find no one to pursue Us on your behalf?","We have honored the children of Adam and carried them over land and sea, provided them with good things, and favored them, with clear favor, over much of what We created.","On the Day We call every people by their leader — whoever is given his book in his right hand, those will read their book, and they will not be wronged by so much as a thread.","Whoever was blind in this life will be blind in the Hereafter, and further astray in path.","They nearly tempted you away from what We revealed to you, so that you would fabricate something else against Us — and then they would have taken you as a close friend.","Had We not made you firm, you would have almost inclined toward them a little.","Then We would have made you taste double the punishment in life and double in death, and you would have found no helper against Us.","They nearly provoked you to drive you out of the land, to expel you from it — and then they would not have remained after you except briefly.","That has been the way with those We sent before you of Our messengers, and you will find no change in Our way.","Establish the prayer from the decline of the sun until the darkness of night, and the recitation at dawn — truly the recitation at dawn is witnessed.","And in part of the night, rise with it as an extra devotion for you. Perhaps your Lord will raise you to a praised station.","Say, “My Lord, admit me a truthful entry and bring me out a truthful exit, and grant me from You a supporting authority.”","Say, “The truth has come and falsehood has perished. Surely falsehood is ever bound to perish.”","We send down of the Quran what is a healing and a mercy for the believers, but it only increases the wrongdoers in loss.","When We bestow favor upon man, he turns away and distances himself, and when hardship touches him, he falls into despair.","Say, “Everyone acts according to his own disposition, and your Lord knows best who is more guided in path.”","They ask you about the spirit. Say, “The spirit is from my Lord’s command, and you have been given of knowledge only a little.”","If We willed, We could take away what We revealed to you — then you would find no advocate against Us for it.","Except as a mercy from your Lord. Truly His grace upon you has been great.","Say, “If all of humankind and the jinn gathered together to produce the like of this Quran, they could not produce its like, even if they backed one another.”","Certainly We have set out for people in this Quran every kind of example, yet most people refuse anything but denial.","They said, “We will never believe you until you cause a spring to gush from the earth for us.","Or you have a garden of palms and grapevines and cause rivers to burst through it in full force.","Or you make the sky fall upon us in fragments as you have claimed, or you bring God and the angels before us face to face.","Or you have a house of gold, or you ascend into the sky — and we will never believe in your ascension until you send down to us a book we can read.” Say, “Glory be to my Lord! Am I anything but a human messenger?”","Nothing prevented people from believing when guidance came to them except that they said, “Has God sent a human as a messenger?”","Say, “If there were angels walking settled on the earth, We would have sent down to them from the sky an angel as a messenger.”","Say, “God suffices as a witness between me and you. Truly He is, of His servants, All-Aware, All-Seeing.”","Whoever God guides is truly guided, and whoever He leads astray — you will find no protectors for them besides Him. We will gather them on the Day of Resurrection on their faces, blind, mute, and deaf. Their refuge is Hell — every time it dies down, We increase its blaze for them.","That is their recompense because they rejected Our verses and said, “When we are bones and dust, will we really be raised as a new creation?”","Have they not seen that God, who created the heavens and the earth, is able to create the likes of them? He has set for them an appointed time about which there is no doubt, yet the wrongdoers refuse anything but denial.","Say, “If you possessed the treasuries of my Lord’s mercy, you would withhold them for fear of spending. Man has always been stingy.”","Truly We gave Moses nine clear miracles — so ask the Children of Israel — when he came to them, and Pharaoh said to him, “I surely think you are bewitched, O Moses.”","He said, “You know well that none sent these down as eye-openers except the Lord of the heavens and the earth, and I surely think you are doomed, O Pharaoh.”","So he wanted to drive them from the land, but We drowned him and all who were with him.","And We said to the Children of Israel after him, “Dwell in the land, and when the promise of the Hereafter comes, We will bring you all together.”","With truth We sent it down, and with truth it descended. And We have not sent you except as a bearer of good news and a warner.","A Quran We divided into parts so that you may recite it to people at intervals, and We sent it down in successive stages.","Say, “Believe in it or do not believe. Those who were given knowledge before it, when it is recited to them, fall on their faces in prostration.”","And they say, “Glory be to our Lord! Our Lord’s promise is truly fulfilled.”","And they fall on their faces weeping, and it increases them in humility.","Say, “Call upon God or call upon the Most Merciful — whichever you call upon, to Him belong the most beautiful names.” And do not raise your voice in your prayer nor whisper it, but seek a way between that.","And say, “Praise be to God, who has not taken a son, and who has no partner in sovereignty, and who has no protector out of weakness.” And exalt Him with great exaltation.","All praise belongs to God, who sent down the Book upon His servant and made in it no crookedness.","Upright, to warn of a severe punishment from Him and to give good news to the believers who do righteous deeds that theirs is a good reward.","Remaining in it forever.","And to warn those who said, “God has taken a son.”","They have no knowledge of it, nor did their fathers. Monstrous is the word that comes out of their mouths. They say nothing but a lie.","Perhaps you will destroy yourself with grief over them if they do not believe in this message.","We made what is on the earth an adornment for it, to test which of them is best in deed.","And We will surely make what is on it a barren, leveled ground.","Did you think that the companions of the Cave and the Inscription were a wonder among Our signs?","When the young men took refuge in the cave and said, “Our Lord, grant us mercy from Yourself and prepare for us right guidance in our affair.”","So We sealed their ears in the cave for a number of years.","Then We raised them up to know which of the two groups was better at counting the time they had stayed.","We relate to you their story in truth. They were youths who believed in their Lord, and We increased them in guidance.","We strengthened their hearts when they stood up and said, “Our Lord is the Lord of the heavens and the earth. We will never call upon any god besides Him — we would then have spoken an outrageous lie.","These people of ours have taken gods besides Him. Why do they not bring clear authority for them? Who is more unjust than one who fabricates a lie against God?","And now that you have withdrawn from them and what they worship other than God, take refuge in the cave. Your Lord will spread His mercy over you and prepare for you ease in your affair.”","You would see the sun, when it rose, inclining away from their cave to the right, and when it set, passing them by on the left, while they lay in an open space within it. That is one of God’s signs. Whoever God guides is truly guided, and whoever He leads astray — you will never find for him a guiding protector.","You would think them awake, yet they were asleep. We turned them to the right and to the left, and their dog lay with its forelegs stretched out at the entrance. Had you looked upon them, you would have turned from them in flight and been filled with terror of them.","And so We raised them up that they might question one another. One of them said, “How long have you stayed?” They said, “We have stayed a day, or part of a day.” They said, “Your Lord knows best how long you have stayed. Send one of you with this silver coin of yours to the city, and let him see which food is purest, and let him bring you provision from it. Let him be discreet, and let no one become aware of you.","If they discover you, they will stone you or force you back into their creed, and then you will never succeed.”","And so We made them known, so that they would know that God’s promise is true and that the Hour is beyond doubt. When they disputed among themselves over their affair, they said, “Build a structure over them — their Lord knows them best.” Those who prevailed in the matter said, “We will surely build a place of worship over them.”","They will say, “Three, their dog being the fourth.” And they will say, “Five, their dog being the sixth” — guessing at the unseen. And they will say, “Seven, and their dog being the eighth.” Say, “My Lord knows best their number. None knows them but a few.” So do not argue about them except with an obvious argument, and do not consult any of them about them.","Never say of anything, “I will do that tomorrow.”","Except by adding, “If God wills.” And remember your Lord when you forget, and say, “Perhaps my Lord will guide me to something nearer than this in right direction.”","They remained in their cave three hundred years, and added nine.","Say, “God knows best how long they stayed.” To Him belongs the unseen of the heavens and the earth. How perfectly He sees and hears! They have no protector besides Him, and He shares His authority with no one.","Recite what has been revealed to you from your Lord’s Book. None can alter His words, and you will never find any refuge apart from Him.","Keep yourself patient with those who call upon their Lord morning and evening, seeking His face. Do not let your eyes pass beyond them, desiring the adornment of this worldly life. Do not obey one whose heart We have made heedless of Our remembrance, who follows his own desires, and whose affair has gone to excess.","Say, “The truth is from your Lord. So whoever wills, let him believe, and whoever wills, let him disbelieve.” We have prepared for the wrongdoers a Fire whose walls will surround them. If they cry for relief, they will be relieved with water like molten metal that scalds the faces. Wretched is the drink, and evil is the resting place!","Truly, those who believe and do righteous deeds — We never waste the reward of anyone who does good work.","Those will have Gardens of Eternity, rivers flowing beneath them. They will be adorned there with bracelets of gold and will wear green garments of fine silk and brocade, reclining there on couches. Excellent is the reward, and beautiful is the resting place!","Set for them the parable of two men: We gave one of them two gardens of grapevines, surrounded them with palm trees, and placed crops between them.","Both gardens yielded their produce and fell short in nothing. And We made a river flow through them.","He had abundant fruit. So he said to his companion while conversing with him, “I have more wealth than you and a mightier following.”","He entered his garden, wronging himself. He said, “I do not think this will ever perish.","And I do not think the Hour is coming. And even if I am returned to my Lord, I will surely find something better than this in return.”","His companion said to him while conversing with him, “Do you deny the One who created you from dust, then from a drop of fluid, then shaped you into a man?","But as for me, He is God, my Lord, and I associate no one with my Lord.","If only, when you entered your garden, you had said: ‘What God wills! There is no power except through God.’ Though you see me as less than you in wealth and children.","Then perhaps my Lord will give me something better than your garden and send upon it a calamity from the sky, so that it becomes barren, slippery ground.","Or its water sinks deep, so that you will never be able to reach it.”","And his fruit was destroyed. So he began wringing his hands over what he had spent on it, while it lay collapsed on its trellises, and he said, “If only I had not associated anyone with my Lord!”","He had no group to help him besides God, nor could he help himself.","There, authority belongs to God alone, the True. He is best in reward and best in outcome.","Set for them the parable of the life of this world: it is like water We sent down from the sky, and the plants of the earth absorbed it, then turned to dry stubble scattered by the winds. God is over all things All-Powerful.","Wealth and children are the adornment of the life of this world, but lasting good deeds are better with your Lord in reward and better in hope.","On the Day We set the mountains in motion and you see the earth laid bare, and We gather them all, leaving not one of them behind.","They are lined up before your Lord: “You have come to Us just as We created you the first time. Yet you claimed We would never set an appointed time for you.”","The record is laid open, and you see the criminals terrified of what is in it, saying, “Woe to us! What is with this record? It leaves out nothing, small or great, without counting it!” They found everything they did present before them. Your Lord wrongs no one.","When We said to the angels, “Prostrate to Adam,” they prostrated, except Iblis. He was of the jinn, and he defied his Lord’s command. Will you then take him and his offspring as allies instead of Me, when they are your enemy? What a wretched exchange for the wrongdoers!","I did not make them witnesses to the creation of the heavens and the earth, nor to the creation of themselves, and I would never take those who lead astray as helpers.","On the Day He says, “Call upon those partners of Mine you claimed,” they will call upon them, but they will not respond to them, and We will place between them a gulf of destruction.","The criminals will see the Fire and realize they are falling into it, finding no escape from it.","Certainly We have varied in this Quran every kind of parable for people, but man is the most argumentative of all things.","Nothing prevented people from believing when guidance came to them and seeking their Lord’s forgiveness, except that the fate of earlier peoples should come upon them or that the punishment should confront them face to face.","We send the messengers only as bearers of good news and warners. Yet those who disbelieve argue with falsehood to refute the truth, and they have taken My signs and what they were warned of as mockery.","Who is more unjust than one who is reminded of his Lord’s verses, then turns away from them and forgets what his own hands have sent ahead? We have placed coverings over their hearts so they cannot comprehend it, and deafness in their ears. Even if you call them to guidance, they will never be guided.","Your Lord is the All-Forgiving, Full of Mercy. If He were to hold them accountable for what they have earned, He would have hastened the punishment for them. But they have an appointed time from which they will find no refuge.","Those are the towns We destroyed when they did wrong, and We set an appointed time for their destruction.","When Moses said to his young companion, “I will not stop until I reach the junction of the two seas, even if I travel for ages.”","But when they reached the junction between them, they forgot their fish, and it made its way into the sea, slipping away.","When they had passed beyond, he said to his companion, “Bring us our meal. We have certainly met with exhaustion on this journey of ours.”","He said, “Did you see — when we took shelter by the rock, I forgot the fish, and nothing made me forget to mention it except Satan, and it made its way into the sea in a wondrous manner.”","He said, “That is what we were seeking.” So they retraced their steps, following their tracks.","They found a servant of Ours whom We had granted mercy from Us and taught knowledge from Our presence.","Moses said to him, “May I follow you so that you teach me some of the right guidance you have been taught?”","He said, “You will never be able to have patience with me.","And how can you be patient with what you have no knowledge of?”","He said, “You will find me patient, God willing, and I will not disobey you in any matter.”","He said, “If you follow me, then do not ask me about anything until I bring it up to you myself.”","So they set out, until when they boarded a ship, he made a hole in it. He said, “Did you make a hole in it to drown its people? You have certainly done a dreadful thing!”","He said, “Did I not tell you that you would never be able to have patience with me?”","He said, “Do not hold me accountable for what I forgot, and do not burden me with hardship in my affair.”","So they set out, until when they met a boy, he killed him. He said, “Did you kill a pure soul for no soul? You have certainly done a horrible thing!”","He said, “Did I not tell you that you would never be able to have patience with me?”","He said, “If I ask you about anything after this, then do not keep my company. You have received enough excuse from me.”","So they set out, until when they came to the people of a town, they asked its people for food, but they refused to host them. Then they found in it a wall about to collapse, so he restored it. He said, “If you wished, you could have taken payment for it.”","He said, “This is the parting between me and you. I will inform you of the interpretation of what you could not bear with patience.","As for the ship, it belonged to poor people working at sea. I intended to damage it, for behind them was a king who seized every ship by force.","As for the boy, his parents were believers, and we feared he would overwhelm them with transgression and disbelief.","So we intended that their Lord replace him for them with one better in purity and closer in compassion.","As for the wall, it belonged to two orphan boys in the city, and beneath it was a treasure belonging to them, and their father had been righteous. So your Lord intended that they reach their maturity and extract their treasure — a mercy from your Lord. I did not do any of it by my own command. That is the interpretation of what you could not bear with patience.”","They ask you about Dhul-Qarnayn. Say, “I will recite to you a mention of him.”","We established him in the earth and gave him a means to everything.","So he followed a means.","Until, when he reached the setting of the sun, he found it setting in a murky spring, and he found near it a people. We said, “O Dhul-Qarnayn, either you punish them or you treat them with kindness.”","He said, “As for whoever wrongs, we will punish him, then he will be returned to his Lord, and He will punish him with a terrible punishment.","But as for whoever believes and does good, he will have the finest recompense, and we will speak to him ease from our command.”","Then he followed a means.","Until, when he reached the rising of the sun, he found it rising upon a people for whom We had made no shelter from it.","So it was. And We had encompassed all that he possessed in knowledge.","Then he followed a means.","Until, when he reached the point between the two barriers, he found beside them a people who could barely understand speech.","They said, “O Dhul-Qarnayn, Gog and Magog are spreading corruption in the land. May we pay you a tribute on the condition that you build a barrier between us and them?”","He said, “What my Lord has established me in is better. So assist me with strength, and I will build a rampart between you and them.","Bring me blocks of iron.” Until, when he had leveled the gap between the two cliffs, he said, “Blow.” Until, when he had made it a fire, he said, “Bring me molten copper to pour over it.”","So they could not scale it, nor could they tunnel through it.","He said, “This is a mercy from my Lord. But when my Lord’s promise comes, He will level it to the ground. And my Lord’s promise is true.”","And on that Day We will leave them surging over one another, and the Horn will be blown, and We will gather them all together.","And on that Day We will lay Hell bare before the disbelievers.","Those whose eyes were veiled from My remembrance, and who could not bear to hear.","Do those who disbelieve think they can take My servants as protectors instead of Me? We have prepared Hell as a welcome for the disbelievers.","Say, “Shall we tell you who are the greatest losers in their deeds?","Those whose effort went astray in the life of this world while they thought they were doing good.","Those are the ones who denied their Lord’s verses and His meeting, so their deeds came to nothing, and We will assign them no weight on the Day of Resurrection.","That is their recompense — Hell — for having disbelieved and taken My verses and My messengers in mockery.”","Truly, those who believed and did righteous deeds — the Gardens of Paradise are their welcome.","Dwelling there forever, never wishing to leave.","Say, “If the sea were ink for the words of my Lord, the sea would run dry before my Lord’s words ran out, even if we brought the like of it to replenish it.”","Say, “I am only a human being like you. It is revealed to me that your God is one God. So whoever hopes to meet his Lord, let him do righteous work and never associate anyone in the worship of his Lord.”","Kaf Ha Ya Ain Sad.","A mention of your Lord’s mercy to His servant Zechariah.","When he called upon his Lord with a quiet call.","He said, “My Lord, my bones have grown feeble, and my head blazes with white hair, and never have I been, in calling upon You, my Lord, unblessed.","I fear my kinsmen after me, and my wife is barren, so grant me from Yourself an heir.","Who will inherit from me and inherit from the family of Jacob. And make him, my Lord, pleasing.”","“O Zechariah, We give you glad tidings of a boy whose name is John — We have not given this name to anyone before him.”","He said, “My Lord, how can I have a boy when my wife is barren and I have reached extreme old age?”","He said, “So it will be. Your Lord says, ‘It is easy for Me, and I created you before when you were nothing.’”","He said, “My Lord, give me a sign.” He said, “Your sign is that you will not speak to people for three nights, though sound in body.”","So he came out to his people from the sanctuary and signaled to them: “Glorify morning and evening.”","“O John, hold the Scripture with strength.” And We gave him wisdom as a child.","And tenderness from Us and purity, and he was God-conscious.","And dutiful to his parents, and he was not tyrannical or disobedient.","Peace be upon him the day he was born, the day he dies, and the day he is raised alive.","And mention in the Book Mary, when she withdrew from her family to an eastern place.","She placed a screen between herself and them. Then We sent to her Our Spirit, and he appeared to her as a well-formed man.","She said, “I seek refuge in the Most Merciful from you, if you are God-conscious.”","He said, “I am only your Lord’s messenger, to grant you a pure boy.”","She said, “How can I have a boy when no man has touched me and I have not been unchaste?”","He said, “So it will be. Your Lord says, ‘It is easy for Me, and so that We may make him a sign for people and a mercy from Us.’ It is a matter already decreed.”","So she conceived him and withdrew with him to a distant place.","The labor pains drove her to the trunk of a palm tree. She said, “O if only I had died before this and been a thing forgotten, utterly forgotten!”","He called out to her from beneath her, “Do not grieve. Your Lord has placed beneath you a stream.","And shake the trunk of the palm tree toward you — it will drop fresh, ripe dates upon you.","So eat and drink and let your eye be comforted. And if you see any human, say, ‘I have vowed a fast to the Most Merciful, so I will not speak to anyone today.’”","Then she brought him to her people, carrying him. They said, “O Mary, you have done something monstrous!","O sister of Aaron, your father was not a man of evil, nor was your mother unchaste.”","She pointed to him. They said, “How can we speak to one who is a child in the cradle?”","He said, “I am God’s servant. He has given me the Scripture and made me a prophet.","He has made me blessed wherever I am, and He has charged me with prayer and charity as long as I live.","And dutiful to my mother — He has not made me overbearing or wretched.","Peace is upon me the day I was born, the day I die, and the day I am raised alive.”","That is Jesus, son of Mary — the word of truth about which they dispute.","It is not for God to take a son. Glory be to Him! When He decrees a matter, He only says to it, “Be,” and it is.","“Truly God is my Lord and your Lord, so worship Him. This is a straight path.”","But the factions differed among themselves. So woe to those who disbelieved from the witnessing of a tremendous Day.","How well they will hear and see on the Day they come to Us! But today the wrongdoers are in clear error.","Warn them of the Day of Regret, when the matter is decided — while they are in heedlessness and do not believe.","It is We who will inherit the earth and all who are upon it, and to Us they will be returned.","Mention in the Book Abraham. He was a man of truth, a prophet.","When he said to his father, “O my father, why do you worship what cannot hear, cannot see, and cannot benefit you at all?","O my father, there has come to me knowledge that did not come to you, so follow me and I will guide you to a straight path.","O my father, do not worship Satan. Truly Satan has been disobedient to the Most Merciful.","O my father, I fear that a punishment from the Most Merciful will touch you, and you will become an ally of Satan.”","He said, “Do you turn away from my gods, O Abraham? If you do not stop, I will surely stone you. Now leave me for a long time.”","He said, “Peace be upon you. I will ask my Lord to forgive you. He has been ever gracious to me.","I will withdraw from you and from what you call upon besides God, and I will call upon my Lord. Perhaps in calling upon my Lord I will not be unblessed.”","So when he withdrew from them and from what they worshiped besides God, We granted him Isaac and Jacob, and each We made a prophet.","We granted them of Our mercy, and We gave them a lofty tongue of truth.","Mention in the Book Moses. He was chosen, and he was a messenger, a prophet.","We called him from the right side of the Mount, and We drew him near in intimate conversation.","We granted him, out of Our mercy, his brother Aaron as a prophet.","Mention in the Book Ishmael. He was true to his promise, and he was a messenger, a prophet.","He used to command his family to pray and give charity, and he was pleasing to his Lord.","Mention in the Book Idris. He was a man of truth, a prophet.","We raised him to a lofty station.","Those are the ones God blessed among the prophets — from the descendants of Adam, from those We carried with Noah, from the descendants of Abraham and Israel, and from those We guided and chose. When the verses of the Most Merciful were recited to them, they fell down in prostration, weeping.","Then successors came after them who neglected prayer and followed their desires. They will soon meet ruin.","Except those who repented, believed, and did good — those will enter Paradise and will not be wronged in the least.","Gardens of Eden that the Most Merciful has promised His servants in the unseen. His promise will surely be fulfilled.","They will hear no idle talk there — only peace. And they will have their provision there, morning and evening.","That is the Paradise We give as inheritance to those of Our servants who were righteous.","“We do not descend except by your Lord’s command. To Him belongs what is before us, what is behind us, and what is between. Your Lord is never forgetful.”","Lord of the heavens and the earth and all that is between them — so worship Him and be steadfast in His worship. Do you know anyone equal to Him?","Man says, “When I have died, will I really be brought out alive?”","Does man not remember that We created him before, when he was nothing?","By your Lord, We will gather them and the devils, then We will bring them around Hell on their knees.","Then We will drag out from every sect the one most defiant toward the Most Merciful.","Then We know best who most deserves to burn in it.","There is none among you but will pass over it. That is upon your Lord a decree firmly decided.","Then We will save the righteous and leave the wrongdoers in it on their knees.","When Our verses are recited to them as clear proofs, those who disbelieved say to those who believed, “Which of the two groups is better in standing and finer in company?”","How many a generation We destroyed before them who were better in possessions and appearance!","Say, “Whoever is in misguidance, let the Most Merciful extend his time. Until, when they see what they are promised — whether the punishment or the Hour — they will know who is worse in position and weaker in forces.”","God increases in guidance those who are guided. And lasting good deeds are better with your Lord in reward and better in outcome.","Have you seen the one who disbelieved in Our verses and said, “I will surely be given wealth and children”?","Has he penetrated the unseen, or has he taken a covenant with the Most Merciful?","No! We will record what he says and extend for him the punishment extensively.","We will inherit from him what he speaks of, and he will come to Us alone.","They have taken gods besides God so that they might be a source of strength for them.","No! They will deny their worship and turn against them as adversaries.","Do you not see that We have sent the devils upon the disbelievers, inciting them relentlessly?","So do not be hasty against them. We are only counting for them a countdown.","The Day We gather the reverent to the Most Merciful as a delegation.","And We drive the criminals to Hell as a herd to water.","They will have no power of intercession — except whoever has taken a covenant with the Most Merciful.","They say, “The Most Merciful has taken a son.”","You have brought something monstrous!","The heavens nearly tear apart from it, and the earth splits open, and the mountains collapse in ruins.","That they attribute to the Most Merciful a son.","It is not befitting for the Most Merciful to take a son.","There is no one in the heavens and the earth but comes to the Most Merciful as a servant.","He has counted them and numbered them precisely.","And every one of them will come to Him on the Day of Resurrection alone.","Truly, those who believed and did righteous deeds — the Most Merciful will grant them love.","We have made it easy in your tongue only so that you may give glad tidings with it to the righteous and warn with it a fiercely contentious people.","How many a generation We destroyed before them! Do you perceive any one of them, or hear from them even a whisper?","Ta Ha.","We did not send down the Quran upon you to make you suffer.","Only as a reminder for whoever fears.","A revelation from Him who created the earth and the high heavens.","The Most Merciful, established over the Throne.","To Him belongs what is in the heavens and what is on the earth and what is between them and what is beneath the soil.","If you speak aloud, He knows the secret and what is even more hidden.","God — there is no god but Him. To Him belong the most beautiful names.","Has the story of Moses reached you?","When he saw a fire, he said to his family, “Stay here. I have spotted a fire. Perhaps I can bring you a torch from it, or find guidance at the fire.”","When he came to it, he was called, “O Moses!","It is I — I am your Lord. So remove your sandals; you are in the sacred valley of Tuwa.","And I have chosen you, so listen to what is revealed.","It is I — I am God. There is no god but Me. So worship Me and establish the prayer for My remembrance.","The Hour is coming — I nearly conceal it — so that every soul may be repaid for what it strives for.","So let not whoever disbelieves in it and follows his desire divert you from it, lest you perish.","And what is that in your right hand, O Moses?”","He said, “It is my staff. I lean on it, and I beat down leaves with it for my sheep, and I have other uses for it.”","He said, “Throw it down, O Moses.”","So he threw it down, and suddenly it was a serpent, slithering.","He said, “Pick it up and do not fear. We will return it to its former state.","And press your hand to your side — it will come out white, without blemish — another sign.","That We may show you some of Our greatest signs.","Go to Pharaoh; he has truly transgressed.”","He said, “My Lord, expand my chest for me.","And ease my task for me.","And untie the knot from my tongue.","So they may understand my speech.","And appoint for me a minister from my family.","Aaron, my brother.","Strengthen my back through him.","And let him share in my task.","So that we may glorify You abundantly.","And remember You abundantly.","Truly, You have always been Seeing of us.”","He said, “You have been granted your request, O Moses.","And We had already favored you another time.","When We inspired your mother with what was inspired.","‘Place him in the chest and cast it into the river, and the river will deliver him to the shore. An enemy of Mine and an enemy of his will take him.’ And I cast upon you love from Me, and so that you would be reared under My eye.","When your sister walked along and said, ‘Shall I direct you to someone who will nurse him?’ So We returned you to your mother, that her eyes might be cooled and she would not grieve. And you killed a soul, but We saved you from distress and tried you with trials. Then you stayed years among the people of Midian, and then you came at the appointed time, O Moses.","And I fashioned you for Myself.","Go, you and your brother, with My signs, and do not slacken in My remembrance.","Go, both of you, to Pharaoh—he has truly transgressed.","Speak to him gently, so that perhaps he may be reminded or fear.”","They said, “Our Lord, we fear that he may act rashly against us or that he may transgress.”","He said, “Do not fear. I am with you both, Hearing and Seeing.","So go to him and say, ‘We are the messengers of your Lord, so send the Children of Israel with us and do not torment them. We have come to you with a sign from your Lord, and peace be upon whoever follows the guidance.","It has been revealed to us that the punishment is upon whoever denies and turns away.’”","He said, “Then who is your Lord, O Moses?”","He said, “Our Lord is the One who gave everything its creation, then guided it.”","He said, “Then what about the former generations?”","He said, “Knowledge of them is with my Lord in a record. My Lord neither errs nor forgets.”","He who made the earth a cradle for you and traced pathways through it for you and sent down water from the sky—and with it We brought out diverse pairs of plants.","Eat and graze your livestock. Surely in that are signs for those of understanding.","From it We created you, to it We will return you, and from it We will bring you out once more.","Certainly We showed him Our signs, all of them, but he denied and refused.","He said, “Have you come to drive us out of our land with your sorcery, O Moses?","We will surely bring you sorcery like it. So set between us and you an appointment that neither we nor you will fail to keep, at a fair place.”","He said, “Your appointment is the Day of Adornment, and let the people be gathered mid-morning.”","So Pharaoh turned away, gathered his schemes, then came.","Moses said to them, “Woe to you! Do not fabricate lies against God, lest He destroy you with a punishment. Whoever fabricates has already failed.”","They disputed their affair among themselves and conferred in secret.","They said, “These two are surely sorcerers who want to drive you out of your land with their sorcery and do away with your exemplary way of life.","So muster your schemes, then come in a row. Whoever prevails today has truly succeeded.”","They said, “O Moses, either you throw or we will be the first to throw.”","He said, “Rather, you throw.” And suddenly their ropes and staffs appeared to him, by their sorcery, to be slithering.","So Moses felt a fear within himself.","We said, “Do not be afraid. You are the one who will prevail.","Throw what is in your right hand — it will swallow what they have crafted. What they have crafted is only a sorcerer’s trick, and the sorcerer never succeeds wherever he goes.”","So the sorcerers fell down in prostration. They said, “We believe in the Lord of Aaron and Moses.”","He said, “You believed in him before I gave you permission? He is surely your chief who taught you sorcery. I will cut off your hands and feet on opposite sides, and I will crucify you on the trunks of palm trees, and you will surely know which of us is more severe in punishment and more lasting.”","They said, “We will never prefer you over the clear proofs that have come to us, nor over Him who created us. So decree whatever you will decree — you only decree for this worldly life.","We have believed in our Lord so that He may forgive us our sins and the sorcery you compelled us to practice. God is better and more lasting.”","Whoever comes to his Lord as a criminal — for him is Hell, where he neither dies nor lives.","But whoever comes to Him as a believer, having done righteous deeds — for those are the highest ranks.","Gardens of Eternity beneath which rivers flow, dwelling therein forever. That is the recompense of whoever purifies himself.","Certainly We revealed to Moses, “Travel by night with My servants and strike for them a dry path through the sea — fearing no pursuit and having no dread.”","Pharaoh pursued them with his armies, and the sea overwhelmed them with what overwhelmed them.","Pharaoh led his people astray and did not guide them.","“O Children of Israel, We saved you from your enemy, appointed for you the right side of the Mount, and sent down upon you manna and quails.","Eat from the good things We have provided you, and do not transgress in it lest My wrath descend upon you — and whoever My wrath descends upon has truly fallen.","Truly I am ever-Forgiving to whoever repents, believes, does good, and then stays guided.”","“What made you hasten ahead of your people, O Moses?”","He said, “They are close behind me, and I hastened to You, my Lord, that You might be pleased.”","He said, “We have tested your people after you left, and the Samaritan has led them astray.”","So Moses returned to his people, angry and grieved. He said, “O my people, did your Lord not make you a good promise? Was the time too long for you, or did you want wrath from your Lord to descend upon you, so you broke your promise to me?”","They said, “We did not break our promise to you of our own will, but we were made to carry loads of the people’s ornaments, and we threw them in — and so did the Samaritan.”","Then he produced for them a calf — a body that lowed — and they said, “This is your god and the god of Moses, but he forgot.”","Do they not see that it returns no word to them and possesses for them neither harm nor benefit?","Aaron had told them before, “O my people, you are only being tested by it. Your Lord is the Most Merciful, so follow me and obey my command.”","They said, “We will not stop devoting ourselves to it until Moses returns to us.”","He said, “O Aaron, what prevented you, when you saw them go astray.","From following me? Have you disobeyed my command?”","He said, “O son of my mother, do not seize me by my beard or by my head. I feared you would say, ‘You divided the Children of Israel and did not heed my word.’”","He said, “What is your case, O Samaritan?”","He said, “I saw what they did not see. I seized a handful from the messenger’s trace and cast it in. Thus my soul enticed me.”","He said, “Go! In this life it is yours to say, ‘No contact!’ And you have an appointment you will not escape. Now look at your god to which you remained devoted — we will surely burn it, then scatter it completely into the sea.”","Your only god is God, there is no god but Him. He encompasses all things in knowledge.","Thus We relate to you from the tidings of what has already passed, and We have given you from Us a reminder.","Whoever turns away from it will carry on the Day of Resurrection a heavy burden.","Abiding in it — and wretched for them is the burden on the Day of Resurrection.","The Day the horn is blown, and We gather the criminals that Day, blue-eyed.","They whisper among themselves, “You stayed no more than ten.”","We know best what they say, when the most upright of them in way says, “You stayed no more than a day.”","They ask you about the mountains. Say, “My Lord will scatter them utterly.","He will leave them a flat, barren plain.","You will see in it no crookedness and no curve.”","That Day they will follow the caller with no deviation from him. Voices will be hushed before the Most Merciful, and you will hear nothing but a faint murmur.","That Day intercession will not avail except for one whom the Most Merciful has permitted and whose word He has approved.","He knows what is before them and what is behind them, and they cannot encompass Him in knowledge.","Faces will be humbled before the Living, the Self-Sustaining, and whoever carried wrongdoing will have utterly failed.","But whoever does righteous deeds while he is a believer will fear neither injustice nor deprivation.","Thus We sent it down as an Arabic Quran and varied within it warnings, so that they might become righteous or it might bring about remembrance in them.","Exalted is God, the True King. Do not hasten with the Quran before its revelation to you is completed, and say, “My Lord, increase me in knowledge.”","We made a covenant with Adam before, but he forgot, and We found in him no firm resolve.","When We said to the angels, “Prostrate to Adam,” they prostrated, except Iblis — he refused.","So We said, “O Adam, this is an enemy to you and to your wife. Do not let him drive you both out of the Garden, lest you suffer.","You are guaranteed not to go hungry in it, nor to be naked.","And you will not go thirsty in it, nor be scorched by the sun.”","But Satan whispered to him. He said, “O Adam, shall I lead you to the Tree of Eternity and a kingdom that never decays?”","So they both ate from it, and their nakedness became exposed to them, and they began covering themselves with leaves from the Garden. Adam disobeyed his Lord and went astray.","Then his Lord chose him, turned to him in mercy, and guided him.","He said, “Descend from it, both of you, altogether — some of you enemies to others. But whenever guidance comes to you from Me, whoever follows My guidance will neither go astray nor suffer.","And whoever turns away from My remembrance will have a miserable life, and We will raise him blind on the Day of Resurrection.”","He will say, “My Lord, why have You raised me blind when I used to see?”","He will say, “Just so — Our verses came to you and you forgot them, and just so today you are forgotten.”","And that is how We recompense whoever was excessive and did not believe in the verses of his Lord. And the punishment of the Hereafter is more severe and more lasting.","Has it not become clear to them how many generations We destroyed before them, in whose dwellings they now walk? Surely in that are signs for people of reason.","Were it not for a word that had already gone out from your Lord — and an appointed term — it would have been inescapable.","So be patient with what they say, and glorify your Lord with praise before sunrise and before sunset, and during the hours of the night glorify Him, and at the edges of the day, so that you may be content.","Do not extend your eyes toward what We have given some pairs among them to enjoy — the splendor of this worldly life — by which We test them. Your Lord’s provision is better and more lasting.","Command your family to pray and be steadfast in it. We do not ask you for provision — We provide for you. And the best outcome belongs to righteousness.","They say, “Why does he not bring us a sign from his Lord?” Has the clear proof of what is in the former scriptures not come to them?","Had We destroyed them with a punishment before him, they would have said, “Our Lord, if only You had sent us a messenger so we could have followed Your signs before we were humiliated and disgraced.”","Say, “Everyone is waiting, so wait. You will come to know who the people of the straight path are, and who is guided.”","The reckoning for mankind has drawn near, yet they turn away in heedlessness.","No new reminder comes to them from their Lord but they listen to it while they play.","Their hearts distracted. Those who wronged whispered among themselves, “Is this anything but a mortal like you? Will you fall for sorcery with your eyes wide open?”","He said, “My Lord knows every word spoken in the heaven and the earth, and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.”","Rather, they said, “Jumbled dreams!” Rather, “He fabricated it!” Rather, “He is a poet! Let him bring us a miracle as the earlier ones were sent with.”","Not one town that We destroyed before them believed — will these then believe?","We sent before you only men to whom We revealed — so ask the people of knowledge if you do not know.","We did not make them bodies that did not eat food, nor were they immortal.","Then We fulfilled the promise to them, and We saved them and whomever We willed, and We destroyed the transgressors.","Certainly We have sent down to you a Book in which is your remembrance — will you not reason?","How many a wrongdoing town We shattered and raised after it another people.","When they sensed Our might, they fled from it.","“Do not flee! Return to the luxury you were given and to your dwellings, so that you may be questioned.”","They said, “O woe to us! We were wrongdoers!”","That remained their cry until We made them a harvest, still and lifeless.","We did not create the heaven and the earth and what is between them in play.","Had We wished to take a pastime, We would have taken it from Ourselves, if We were to do so at all.","Rather, We hurl the truth against falsehood and it crushes its skull, and at once it perishes. And woe to you for what you ascribe.","To Him belongs whoever is in the heavens and the earth. And those in His presence are never too proud to worship Him, nor do they tire.","They glorify Him night and day, never flagging.","Or have they taken gods from the earth who can raise the dead?","Had there been gods in them besides God, both would have been ruined. So glory be to God, Lord of the Throne, far above what they ascribe.","He is not questioned about what He does, but they will be questioned.","Or have they taken gods besides Him? Say, “Bring your proof. This is the reminder of those with me and the reminder of those before me.” But most of them do not know the truth, so they turn away.","We sent no messenger before you except that We revealed to him: “There is no god but Me, so worship Me.”","They say, “The Most Merciful has taken a son.” Glory be to Him! Rather, they are honored servants.","They do not precede Him in speech, and they act by His command.","He knows what is before them and what is behind them, and they do not intercede except for one He approves, and they tremble in awe of Him.","Whoever among them says, “I am a god besides Him” — that one We will repay with Hell. That is how We repay the wrongdoers.","Have those who disbelieved not seen that the heavens and the earth were a joined mass, then We split them apart? And We made from water every living thing. Will they not then believe?","We placed firm mountains in the earth so it would not sway with them, and We made in it wide pathways so they might find their way.","We made the sky a protected canopy, yet they turn away from its signs.","He is the One who created the night and the day, the sun and the moon — each gliding in an orbit.","We never granted immortality to any human before you. If you die, will they live forever?","Every soul will taste death. We test you with evil and good as a trial, and to Us you will be returned.","When those who disbelieve see you, they only take you in mockery: “Is this the one who speaks against your gods?” Yet they themselves deny the mention of the Most Merciful.","Man was created from haste. I will show you My signs, so do not rush Me.","They say, “When will this promise come, if you are truthful?”","If only those who disbelieve knew the time when they will not be able to ward off the Fire from their faces or from their backs, nor will they be helped.","Rather, it will come upon them suddenly and stun them, and they will not be able to repel it, nor will they be given respite.","Messengers before you were mocked, but what they mocked closed in on those who ridiculed them.","Say, “Who guards you by night and by day from the Most Merciful?” Yet they turn away from the remembrance of their Lord.","Or do they have gods that protect them apart from Us? They cannot help themselves, nor will they be protected from Us.","Rather, We gave these people and their fathers enjoyment until life grew long for them. Do they not see that We come upon the land, shrinking it from its edges? Are they then the victors?","Say, “I only warn you through revelation.” But the deaf do not hear the call when they are warned.","If even a whiff of your Lord’s punishment touched them, they would surely say, “Woe to us! We were truly wrongdoers!”","We will set up the scales of justice for the Day of Resurrection, and no soul will be wronged in the least. Even if it is the weight of a mustard seed, We will bring it. And We are sufficient as reckoners.","Truly We gave Moses and Aaron the Criterion, and a light, and a reminder for the God-conscious.","Those who fear their Lord in the unseen, and who dread the Hour.","And this is a blessed reminder We have sent down. Will you then deny it?","We had already given Abraham his right guidance before, and We were Knowing of him.","When he said to his father and his people, “What are these statues to which you are devoted?”","They said, “We found our fathers worshiping them.”","He said, “Certainly you and your fathers have been in clear error.”","They said, “Have you brought us the truth, or are you jesting?”","He said, “Rather, your Lord is the Lord of the heavens and the earth, He who originated them, and I am to that a witness.","By God, I will surely plot against your idols after you turn your backs.”","So he smashed them to pieces, all except the largest of them, so that they might turn to it.","They said, “Who did this to our gods? He is surely among the wrongdoers.”","They said, “We heard a young man mentioning them; he is called Abraham.”","They said, “Bring him before the people’s eyes so they may witness.”","They said, “Was it you who did this to our gods, O Abraham?”","He said, “Rather, this largest of them did it. So ask them, if they can speak.”","So they turned to themselves and said, “Truly, you yourselves are the wrongdoers.”","Then they were turned back on their heads: “You well know these do not speak.”","He said, “Do you then worship, instead of God, what does not benefit you at all nor harm you?","Shame on you and on what you worship instead of God! Will you not reason?”","They said, “Burn him and support your gods, if you are going to act.”","We said, “O fire, be coolness and safety for Abraham.”","They intended a plot against him, but We made them the greatest losers.","And We delivered him and Lot to the land We had blessed for all peoples.","And We granted him Isaac, and Jacob as an extra gift, and each of them We made righteous.","And We made them leaders guiding by Our command, and We inspired them to do good deeds, to establish prayer, and to give charity. And they were worshipers of Us.","And Lot—We gave him judgment and knowledge, and We delivered him from the town that practiced abominations. They were truly an evil, defiantly sinful people.","And We admitted him into Our mercy. He was truly among the righteous.","And Noah, when he called out before that—We answered him and delivered him and his family from the great distress.","And We defended him against the people who denied Our signs. They were truly an evil people, so We drowned them all.","And David and Solomon, when they judged concerning the field when the people’s sheep had strayed into it by night — We were witness to their judgment.","So We gave Solomon understanding of it, and to each We granted judgment and knowledge. We made the mountains glorify along with David, and the birds. We were the doers of this.","And We taught him the craft of armor-making for you, to protect you from your own violence. Will you then be grateful?","And to Solomon We subjected the raging wind, running by his command toward the land We had blessed. We were Knowing of all things.","And among the devils were those who dived for him and did other work besides. We were their keepers.","And Job, when he called out to his Lord, “Affliction has touched me, and You are the Most Merciful of the merciful.”","So We answered him and removed the affliction that was upon him, and We gave him back his family and the like of them with them — a mercy from Us and a reminder for the worshippers.","And Ishmael, and Enoch, and Dhul-Kifl — each was of the patient.","And We admitted them into Our mercy. They were truly among the righteous.","And the man of the whale, when he departed in anger and thought We would never constrain him. Then he cried out in the depths of darkness, “There is no god but You! Glory be to You! I was truly among the wrongdoers.”","So We answered him and saved him from the anguish. Thus do We save the believers.","And Zechariah, when he called out to his Lord, “My Lord, do not leave me alone, and You are the best of inheritors.”","So We answered him and granted him John, and We made his wife fit for him. They used to hasten in good deeds and call upon Us in hope and fear, and they were humble before Us.","And she who guarded her chastity — We breathed into her of Our spirit and made her and her son a sign for all peoples.","Truly this community of yours is one community, and I am your Lord, so worship Me.","But they tore their affair apart among themselves. All will return to Us.","So whoever does righteous deeds while he is a believer — his effort will not be denied, and We are recording it for him.","It is forbidden for any town We have destroyed that they should ever return.","Until when Gog and Magog are opened and they pour down from every elevation.","And the true promise draws near — then suddenly the eyes of those who disbelieved will stare in horror: “Woe to us! We were heedless of this — no, we were wrongdoers!”","You and what you worship besides God are the fuel of Hell. You will enter it.","Had these been gods, they would not have entered it. But all will abide in it forever.","In it they will have groaning, and in it they will hear nothing.","Surely those for whom the finest reward has preceded from Us — they are kept far from it.","They will not hear its slightest sound, and they will abide forever in what their souls desire.","The Great Terror will not grieve them, and the angels will receive them: “This is your Day that you were promised.”","The Day We roll up the sky as a scroll rolls up writings. Just as We originated the first creation, We will bring it back—a promise binding upon Us. We will certainly do it.","We wrote in the Psalms, after the Reminder, that the earth will be inherited by My righteous servants.","Surely in this is a message for a people devoted to worship.","We sent you only as a mercy to all the worlds.","Say, “What is revealed to me is that your God is one God. So will you submit?”","If they turn away, say, “I have warned you all equally. And I do not know whether what you are promised is near or far.”","He knows what is spoken aloud, and He knows what you conceal.","And I do not know—perhaps it is a trial for you and an enjoyment for a time.","He said, “My Lord, judge in truth.” And our Lord is the Most Merciful, the One whose help is sought against what you claim.","O people, be mindful of your Lord. Truly the quaking of the Hour is a tremendous thing.","The Day you see it, every nursing mother will forget what she nursed, and every pregnant woman will drop her load, and you will see people drunk, though they are not drunk — but God’s punishment is severe.","Among people is he who argues about God without knowledge, following every rebellious devil.","It is decreed against him that whoever befriends him, he will lead astray and guide to the punishment of the Blaze.","O people, if you are in doubt about the resurrection — We created you from dust, then from a drop, then from a clinging clot, then from a lump of flesh, formed and unformed, so that We may make it clear to you. We settle in the wombs whatever We will for an appointed term, then We bring you out as infants, then so that you may reach your full strength. Among you is he who is taken in death, and among you is he who is returned to the most feeble old age, so that he knows nothing after having known. And you see the earth lifeless, but when We send down water upon it, it stirs and swells and sprouts every delightful kind.","That is because God is the Truth, and He gives life to the dead, and He is Capable of all things.","And the Hour is coming — no doubt about it — and God will raise those in the graves.","Among people is he who argues about God without knowledge, without guidance, and without an illuminating Book.","Turning his side in arrogance to lead others astray from God’s path. For him in this world is disgrace, and on the Day of Resurrection We will make him taste the punishment of burning.","“That is for what your hands have sent ahead, and God is never unjust to His servants.”","Among people is he who worships God on an edge — if good comes to him, he is content with it, but if a trial strikes him, he turns on his face. He has lost this world and the Hereafter. That is the clear loss.","He calls upon, besides God, what neither harms him nor benefits him. That is the extreme misguidance.","He calls upon one whose harm is closer than his benefit. What a wretched protector, and what a wretched companion!","God will admit those who believe and do righteous deeds into gardens beneath which rivers flow. God does what He wills.","Whoever thinks that God will never help him in this world and the Hereafter, let him stretch a rope to the sky, then cut it off, and let him see — will his scheme remove what enrages him?","Thus We sent it down as clear verses, and God guides whom He wills.","Those who believe, those who are Jewish, the Sabians, the Christians, the Magians, and those who associate partners with God — God will judge between them on the Day of Resurrection. God is Witness over all things.","Do you not see that to God prostrate whoever is in the heavens and whoever is on the earth, and the sun, the moon, the stars, the mountains, the trees, the creatures, and many among people? Yet many have deserved the punishment. And whoever God humiliates, none can honor him. God does what He wills.","These are two adversaries who disputed about their Lord. As for those who disbelieved, garments of fire have been cut for them, and scalding water will be poured over their heads.","By it, what is in their bellies and their skins will be melted.","And for them are maces of iron.","Every time they try to escape from it out of anguish, they are driven back into it: “Taste the punishment of the Blaze!”","God will admit those who believe and do righteous deeds into gardens beneath which rivers flow. They will be adorned there with bracelets of gold and pearls, and their clothing there will be silk.","They were guided to the purest of speech, and they were guided to the path of the Praiseworthy.","Those who disbelieve and bar others from God’s path and from the Sacred Mosque — which We made equal for all people, the resident there and the visitor — and whoever intends therein deviation through wrongdoing, We will make him taste a painful punishment.","And when We established for Abraham the site of the House: “Do not associate anything with Me, and purify My House for those who circle it, those who stand in prayer, and those who bow and prostrate.","And proclaim the pilgrimage to the people. They will come to you on foot and on every lean mount, coming from every distant pass.","That they may witness benefits for themselves and mention God’s name on appointed days over the livestock He has provided them. So eat from them and feed the miserable poor.","Then let them complete their rites, fulfill their vows, and circle the Ancient House.”","That is so. And whoever honors God’s sacred rites, it is better for him with his Lord. Livestock has been made lawful for you except what is recited to you. So shun the filth of idols and shun false speech.","Being monotheists before God, not associating anything with Him. And whoever associates partners with God — it is as though he has fallen from the sky, and the birds snatch him away, or the wind hurls him to a distant place.","That is so. And whoever honors God’s rites — that truly comes from the righteousness of hearts.","In them are benefits for you until an appointed time, then their place of sacrifice is at the Ancient House.","For every nation We appointed a rite of sacrifice, so that they may mention God’s name over the livestock He provided them. Your God is one God, so submit to Him. And give good news to the humble.","Those whose hearts tremble when God is mentioned, those who endure what befalls them, those who establish prayer, and those who spend from what We have provided them.","And the sacrificial camels — We made them among God’s rites for you. In them is good for you. So mention God’s name over them as they stand in rows. Then when they collapse on their sides, eat from them and feed the contented and the needy. Thus We subjected them to you, so that you may be grateful.","Neither their meat nor their blood reaches God, but your righteousness reaches Him. Thus He subjected them to you so that you may glorify God for guiding you. And give good news to those who do good.","Truly God defends those who believe. God does not love any treacherous ingrate.","Permission is granted to those who are fought because they were wronged. And surely God is Capable of granting them victory.","Those who were driven from their homes without right, only because they said, “Our Lord is God.” Were it not that God repels people by means of one another, monasteries, churches, synagogues, and mosques — in which God’s name is mentioned abundantly — would have been demolished. And God will surely help those who help Him. Truly God is All-Strong, All-Mighty.","Those who, if We establish them in the land, establish prayer, give charity, enjoin what is right, and forbid what is wrong. And to God belongs the outcome of all matters.","If they deny you, before them the people of Noah denied, and Ad and Thamud.","And the people of Abraham and the people of Lot.","And the people of Midian. And Moses was denied. So I gave the disbelievers respite, then I seized them — and how was My reproach?","How many a town We destroyed while it was wrongdoing, and now it lies fallen on its roofs, and how many an abandoned well and lofty palace.","Have they not traveled through the land so that they might have hearts to reason with or ears to hear with? It is not the eyes that go blind, but it is the hearts within the chests that go blind.","They urge you to hasten the punishment, but God will never break His promise. A single day with your Lord is like a thousand years by your counting.","How many a town I gave respite to while it was steeped in wrongdoing, then I seized it. And to Me is the final return.","Say, “O people, I am only a clear warner to you.”","So those who believe and do righteous deeds — for them is forgiveness and a generous provision.","But those who strive against Our verses, seeking to undermine them — those are the companions of the Blaze.","We never sent before you any messenger or prophet but that when he recited, Satan cast into his recitation. Then God abolishes what Satan casts, and God makes His verses precise. God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.","So that He may make what Satan casts a trial for those in whose hearts is disease and those whose hearts are hardened. Truly the wrongdoers are in extreme discord.","And so that those given knowledge may know that it is the truth from your Lord and believe in it, and their hearts may humbly submit to it. Surely God guides those who believe to a straight path.","Those who disbelieve will remain in doubt of it until the Hour comes upon them suddenly, or the punishment of a barren Day strikes them.","Sovereignty on that Day belongs to God. He will judge between them. So those who believed and did righteous deeds will be in Gardens of Bliss.","But those who disbelieved and denied Our verses — for them is a humiliating punishment.","Those who emigrated in God’s cause, then were killed or died — God will surely provide them a good provision. Truly God is the Best of Providers.","He will surely admit them to an entrance that pleases them. God is All-Knowing, All-Forbearing.","So it is. Whoever retaliates with the like of what was inflicted on him, then is wronged again — God will surely help him. Surely God is All-Pardoning, All-Forgiving.","That is because God merges the night into the day and merges the day into the night, and because God is All-Hearing, All-Seeing.","That is because God is the Truth, and what they invoke besides Him is falsehood, and because God is the Most High, the Most Great.","Do you not see that God sends down water from the sky, and the earth becomes green? Truly God is Subtle, All-Aware.","To Him belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth. Surely God is the Self-Sufficient, the Praiseworthy.","Do you not see that God has subjected to you all that is on the earth, and the ships sailing through the sea by His command, and He holds back the sky from falling upon the earth except by His permission? Truly, God is Compassionate to people, Merciful.","He is the One who gave you life, then causes you to die, then gives you life again. Surely the human being is ungrateful.","For every community We appointed a rite they observe. So let them not dispute with you over this matter. Call to your Lord — you are surely upon straight guidance.","If they argue with you, say, “God knows best what you do.”","God will judge between you on the Day of Resurrection concerning what you used to differ over.","Do you not know that God knows all that is in the heaven and the earth? That is in a Record. That is easy for God.","They worship besides God that for which He has sent down no authority and of which they have no knowledge. The wrongdoers will have no helper.","When Our verses are recited to them as clear proofs, you see revulsion on the faces of those who disbelieve — they nearly assault those who recite Our verses to them. Say, “Shall I tell you of something worse than that? The Fire — God has promised it to those who disbelieve. What a wretched destination!”","O people, a parable is struck, so listen to it: those you call upon besides God will never create a fly, even if they all gathered together for it. And if a fly snatches something from them, they cannot retrieve it from it. How feeble is the seeker and the sought!","They have not valued God as He deserves to be valued. Surely God is All-Strong, All-Mighty.","God chooses messengers from the angels and from people. Truly, God is All-Hearing, All-Seeing.","He knows what is before them and what is behind them. To God all matters are returned.","O you who believe, bow down and prostrate, worship your Lord, and do good, so that you may succeed.","Strive in God’s cause as He deserves to be striven for. He has chosen you and placed no hardship on you in religion — the faith of your father Abraham. He named you Muslims before and in this, so that the Messenger may be a witness over you and you may be witnesses over people. So establish the prayer, give the charity, and hold fast to God. He is your Protector — what an excellent Protector and what an excellent Helper!","Truly the believers have succeeded.","Those who are humble in their prayer.","And those who turn away from idle talk.","And those who give their charity.","And those who guard their private parts.","Except with their wives or what their right hands possess, for then they are not blamed.","But whoever seeks beyond that—those are the transgressors.","And those who are faithful to their trusts and their covenants.","And those who are constant in their prayers.","Those are the inheritors.","Who will inherit Paradise, dwelling in it forever.","Certainly We created man from an extract of clay.","Then We placed him as a drop in a secure resting place.","Then We created the drop into a clinging clot, then We created the clot into a lump of flesh, then We created the lump into bones, then We clothed the bones with flesh, then We brought him into being as another creation. So blessed is God, the best of creators.","Then after that, you will surely die.","Then on the Day of Resurrection, you will be raised.","We created above you seven pathways, and We were never heedless of creation.","We sent down water from the sky in measured amount and lodged it in the earth—and We are surely able to take it away.","With it We produced for you gardens of palms and grapevines, in which you have abundant fruits, and from which you eat.","And a tree that grows from Mount Sinai, producing oil and a condiment for those who eat.","Truly in livestock there is a lesson for you. We give you drink from what is in their bellies, and in them you have many benefits, and from them you eat.","And on them and on ships you are carried.","We sent Noah to his people, and he said, “O my people, worship God. You have no god other than Him. Will you not be mindful?”","But the chiefs of his people who disbelieved said, “This is nothing but a man like you who wants to elevate himself above you. Had God willed, He would have sent down angels. We never heard of this among our earliest forefathers.","He is nothing but a man possessed by madness, so wait on him for a while.”","He said, “My Lord, help me, for they have denied me.”","So We revealed to him, “Build the ark under Our watchful eyes and Our revelation. When Our command comes and the oven bursts with water, load into it two of every kind, a pair, and your family — except those among them against whom the word has already been passed. And do not plead with Me concerning those who have wronged. They will be drowned.","And when you have settled, you and those with you, upon the ark, say, ‘Praise be to God, who saved us from the wrongdoing people.’","And say, ‘My Lord, land me at a blessed landing, for You are the best of those who bring to land.’”","Surely in that are signs, and surely We were testing.","Then We raised after them another generation.","So We sent among them a messenger from themselves: “Worship God. You have no god other than Him. Will you not be mindful?”","And the chiefs of his people — those who disbelieved and denied the meeting of the Hereafter, and whom We had given luxury in the life of this world — said, “This is nothing but a man like you. He eats from what you eat and drinks from what you drink.","And if you obey a man like yourselves, you will surely be losers.","Does he promise you that when you have died and become dust and bones, you will be brought out?","Far-fetched, far-fetched is what you are promised!","There is nothing but our life of this world — we die and we live — and we will never be resurrected.","He is nothing but a man who has fabricated a lie against God, and we will never believe him.”","He said, “My Lord, help me, for they have denied me.”","He said, “In a short while, they will surely be filled with regret.”","So the blast seized them in justice, and We made them debris. So away with the wrongdoing people!","Then We raised after them other generations.","No nation can advance its appointed time, nor can they delay it.","Then We sent Our messengers in succession. Every time a nation’s messenger came to them, they denied him. So We made them follow one another and made them cautionary tales. So away with a people who do not believe!","Then We sent Moses and his brother Aaron with Our miracles and a clear authority.","To Pharaoh and his chiefs, but they were arrogant, and they were a haughty people.","They said, “Should we believe two men like ourselves while their people are servants to us?”","So they denied them both and were among those destroyed.","And We gave Moses the Scripture, so that they might be guided.","And We made the son of Mary and his mother a sign, and We sheltered them on a high ground with a resting place and flowing water.","O messengers, eat of the good things and do righteous deeds. Truly, I am All-Knowing of what you do.","This community of yours is one community, and I am your Lord, so be mindful of Me.","But they tore their affair among themselves into factions, each party rejoicing in what they have.","So leave them in their flood of ignorance until a time.","Do they think that the wealth and children We provide them with.","We are hastening for them in good things? No, they do not perceive.","Surely those who are, out of awe of their Lord, apprehensive.","And those who believe in the verses of their Lord.","And those who do not associate partners with their Lord.","And those who give what they give while their hearts tremble that they are returning to their Lord.","It is they who hasten in good deeds, and they are foremost in them.","We do not burden any soul beyond its capacity. With Us is a record that speaks the truth, and they will not be wronged.","But their hearts are in a flood of heedlessness toward this, and they have deeds besides that which they continue to do.","Until, when We seize their affluent ones with punishment, at once they cry out.","Do not cry out today. You will not be helped against Us.","My verses were recited to you, but you used to turn back on your heels.","Arrogant toward it, babbling by night, talking nonsense.","Have they not reflected on the Word, or has there come to them what did not come to their forefathers?","Or do they not recognize their messenger, so they reject him?","Or do they say, “He is possessed”? No, he brought them the truth, but most of them despise the truth.","If the truth had followed their desires, the heavens and the earth and everyone in them would have been ruined. Rather, We brought them their reminder, yet they turn away from their reminder.","Or do you ask them for a payment? Your Lord’s provision is better, and He is the Best of Providers.","You are surely calling them to a straight path.","But those who do not believe in the Hereafter are truly deviating from the path.","Even if We had mercy on them and removed the hardship upon them, they would persist in their transgression, wandering blindly.","We had already seized them with punishment, yet they did not humble themselves before their Lord, nor did they plead.","Until, when We open upon them a gate of severe punishment, at once they are in utter despair within it.","He is the One who produced for you hearing, sight, and hearts. How little you give thanks.","He is the One who spread you across the earth, and to Him you will be gathered.","He is the One who gives life and causes death, and to Him belongs the alternation of night and day. Will you not reason?","Rather, they said the same as the ancients said.","They said, “When we have died and become dust and bones, will we truly be resurrected?","We were promised this, we and our fathers, before. This is nothing but tales of the ancients.”","Say, “To whom belongs the earth and everyone in it, if you know?”","They will say, “To God.” Say, “Will you not then remember?”","Say, “Who is the Lord of the seven heavens and the Lord of the Great Throne?”","They will say, “To God.” Say, “Will you not then be mindful?”","Say, “In whose hand is the dominion of all things, and He grants protection while none can be protected against Him, if you know?”","They will say, “To God.” Say, “Then how are you deluded?”","Rather, We brought them the truth, and they are surely liars.","God has not taken any offspring, nor has there been any god alongside Him. Otherwise, each god would have taken away what he created, and some of them would have overpowered others. Glory be to God, far above what they describe.","Knower of the unseen and the seen, exalted is He above what they associate with Him.","Say, “My Lord, if You show me what they are promised.","My Lord, then do not place me among the wrongdoing people.”","And We are certainly able to show you what We promise them.","Repel evil with what is best. We know best what they describe.","And say, “My Lord, I seek refuge in You from the promptings of the devils.","And I seek refuge in You, my Lord, from their presence.”","Until, when death comes to one of them, he says, “My Lord, send me back.","So that I may do good in what I left behind.” No! It is merely a word he utters. And behind them is a barrier until the Day they are resurrected.","When the Horn is blown, there will be no kinship between them that Day, nor will they ask about one another.","Those whose scales are heavy—they are the successful.","And those whose scales are light—they are the ones who lost themselves, in Hell abiding forever.","The Fire will scorch their faces, and they will be grimacing in it.","“Were My verses not recited to you, and you kept denying them?”","They will say, “Our Lord, our wretchedness overcame us, and we were a people astray.","Our Lord, bring us out of it. If we return, then truly we are wrongdoers.”","He will say, “Be despised in it, and do not speak to Me.","There was a group of My servants who used to say, ‘Our Lord, we have believed, so forgive us and have mercy on us, and You are the Best of the Merciful.’","But you took them in mockery until they made you forget My remembrance, and you used to laugh at them.","Today I have recompensed them for their patience—they are the triumphant.”","He will say, “How many years did you remain on earth?”","They will say, “We remained a day or part of a day, so ask those who keep count.”","He will say, “You remained only a little, if only you had known.","Did you think that We created you in vain and that you would not be returned to Us?”","Exalted is God, the True King. There is no god but Him, Lord of the Noble Throne.","Whoever calls upon another god alongside God—he has no proof of it—his reckoning is only with his Lord. Surely the disbelievers will not succeed.","And say, “My Lord, forgive and have mercy, and You are the Best of the Merciful.”","A chapter We have sent down and made obligatory, and in it We have sent down clear verses, so that you may take heed.","The adulteress and the adulterer — lash each one of them a hundred lashes, and let no pity for them overtake you in God’s religion, if you believe in God and the Last Day. And let a group of the believers witness their punishment.","The adulterer does not marry except an adulteress or a polytheist woman, and the adulteress — none marries her except an adulterer or a polytheist man. That has been forbidden to the believers.","Those who accuse chaste women and then do not produce four witnesses — lash them eighty lashes and never accept their testimony. Those are the defiantly disobedient.","Except those who repent after that and reform, for God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","Those who accuse their wives and have no witnesses except themselves — the testimony of one of them is four oaths by God that he is among the truthful.","And the fifth, that God’s curse be upon him if he is among the liars.","But it wards off the punishment from her if she testifies four oaths by God that he is among the liars.","And the fifth, that God’s wrath be upon her if he is among the truthful.","Were it not for God’s grace upon you and His mercy, and that God is Accepting of repentance, All-Wise.","Those who brought the slander are a group among you. Do not consider it bad for you; rather, it is good for you. Each one of them will have what he earned of sin, and the one among them who took the lead in it — for him is a tremendous punishment.","Why, when you heard it, did the believing men and believing women not think well of themselves and say, “This is an obvious slander”?","Why did they not produce four witnesses to it? Since they did not produce the witnesses, it is they who, in God’s sight, are the liars.","Were it not for God’s grace upon you and His mercy in this world and the Hereafter, a tremendous punishment would have touched you for what you plunged into.","You passed it along with your tongues and spoke with your mouths what you had no knowledge of, thinking it trivial — while in God’s sight it was enormous.","Why, when you heard it, did you not say, “It is not for us to speak of this. Glory be to You! This is a monstrous slander”?","God admonishes you never to repeat the like of it, if you are believers.","God makes the verses clear to you, and God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.","Truly, those who love for indecency to spread among the believers — for them is a painful punishment in this world and the Hereafter. God knows, and you do not know.","Were it not for God’s grace upon you and His mercy, and that God is Compassionate, Merciful.","O you who believe, do not follow the footsteps of Satan. Whoever follows the footsteps of Satan—he commands indecency and wrong. Were it not for God’s grace upon you and His mercy, not one of you would ever have been purified. But God purifies whom He wills. God is All-Hearing, All-Knowing.","Let not those of grace and means among you swear against giving to relatives, the needy, and those who emigrated in God’s cause. Let them pardon and overlook. Do you not love that God should forgive you? God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","Truly, those who slander chaste, unsuspecting, believing women are cursed in this world and the Hereafter, and for them is a tremendous punishment.","On the Day their tongues, their hands, and their feet will testify against them about what they used to do.","On that Day, God will pay them their true recompense in full, and they will know that God is the Manifest Truth.","Vile women are for vile men, and vile men are for vile women. Good women are for good men, and good men are for good women. These are innocent of what they say. For them is forgiveness and a generous provision.","O you who believe, do not enter houses other than your own until you have asked permission and greeted their inhabitants. That is better for you, so that you may be mindful.","If you find no one in them, do not enter until you are given permission. And if you are told, “Go back,” then go back. That is purer for you. God is All-Knowing of what you do.","There is no blame on you for entering uninhabited houses in which there is something of use for you. God knows what you reveal and what you conceal.","Tell the believing men to lower their gaze and guard their private parts. That is purer for them. Surely God is Well-Aware of what they do.","And tell the believing women to lower their gaze and guard their private parts and not display their adornment except what is apparent of it, and let them draw their head-coverings over their chests. Let them not display their adornment except to their husbands, or their fathers, or their husbands’ fathers, or their sons, or their husbands’ sons, or their brothers, or their brothers’ sons, or their sisters’ sons, or their women, or what their right hands possess, or male attendants having no desire, or children who are not yet aware of women’s nakedness. Let them not stamp their feet to make known what they conceal of their adornment. Turn to God in repentance, all of you, O believers, so that you may succeed.","Marry off the unmarried among you and the righteous among your male and female slaves. If they are poor, God will enrich them from His bounty. God is All-Encompassing, All-Knowing.","Let those who cannot find marriage be chaste until God enriches them from His bounty. As for those among your slaves who seek a contract of emancipation, grant it to them if you find goodness in them, and give them from God’s wealth that He has given you. Do not force your slave-girls into prostitution, if they desire chastity, so that you may seek the fleeting gains of this worldly life. Whoever forces them — then surely God, after their being forced, is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","We have sent down to you clear verses and an example from those who passed before you and a lesson for the righteous.","God is the Light of the heavens and the earth. The likeness of His light is that of a niche in which is a lamp. The lamp is in a glass. The glass is as if it were a radiant star, lit from a blessed tree — an olive, neither eastern nor western — whose oil nearly glows even if no fire touches it. Light upon light. God guides to His light whoever He wills. God strikes parables for people. God is All-Knowing of all things.","In houses that God has permitted to be raised and His name to be remembered in them, glorifying Him therein morning and evening.","Men whom neither trade nor commerce distracts from the remembrance of God, the keeping of prayer, and the giving of charity. They fear a Day when hearts and eyes will be overturned.","So that God may recompense them for the best of what they did and increase them from His bounty. God provides for whoever He wills without limit.","As for those who disbelieved, their deeds are like a mirage in a desert plain — the thirsty man thinks it is water, until when he reaches it he finds it nothing, and he finds God there, Who pays him his account in full. God is swift in reckoning.","Or like layers of darkness in a deep sea, covered by waves, above which are waves, above which are clouds — layers of darkness, one above another. When he holds out his hand, he can barely see it. Whoever God grants no light — he has no light.","Do you not see that everyone in the heavens and the earth glorifies God, and the birds with wings spread? Each knows its prayer and its glorification. And God is All-Knowing of what they do.","To God belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth, and to God is the final return.","Do you not see that God drives clouds, then joins them together, then piles them into masses, and you see the rain emerging from within them? And He sends down from the sky, from mountains therein, hail, striking with it whoever He wills and diverting it from whoever He wills. The flash of its lightning nearly takes away the sight.","God alternates the night and the day. Surely in that is a lesson for those with insight.","God created every creature from water. Among them are those that crawl on their bellies, among them are those that walk on two legs, and among them are those that walk on four. God creates whatever He wills. Truly God is Capable of all things.","We have sent down clear verses. And God guides whoever He wills to a straight path.","They say, “We believe in God and in the Messenger, and we obey,” then a group of them turns away after that. Those are not believers.","When they are called to God and His Messenger so that he may judge between them, a group of them turns away.","But if the right is on their side, they come to him in full compliance.","Is there a disease in their hearts, or do they doubt, or do they fear that God and His Messenger will deal with them unjustly? Rather, it is they who are the wrongdoers.","The only response of the believers, when they are called to God and His Messenger so that he may judge between them, is to say, “We hear and we obey.” It is they who are the successful.","Whoever obeys God and His Messenger, fears God, and is mindful of Him—it is they who are the triumphant.","They swore by God their most solemn oaths that if you commanded them, they would go out. Say, “Do not swear. Obedience is expected.” Surely God is All-Aware of what you do.","Say, “Obey God and obey the Messenger.” But if you turn away, then he is only responsible for what he was charged with, and you are responsible for what you were charged with. If you obey him, you will be guided. The Messenger’s only duty is clear delivery.","God has promised those among you who believe and do righteous deeds that He will surely make them successors on the earth, just as He made those before them successors, and that He will surely establish for them their religion which He has chosen for them, and that He will surely replace their fear with security. They worship Me, associating nothing with Me. Whoever disbelieves after that—it is they who are the defiantly disobedient.","Establish the prayer, give the charity, and obey the Messenger, so that you may be shown mercy.","Do not think that those who disbelieve can escape on earth. Their refuge is the Fire—and what a wretched destination!","O you who believe, let those whom your right hands possess and those among you who have not reached puberty ask your permission three times: before the dawn prayer, when you remove your garments at noon, and after the night prayer. Three times of privacy for you. There is no blame on you or on them beyond these — they move freely among you, some of you attending to others. Thus God makes clear to you the verses. God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.","When the children among you reach puberty, let them ask permission as those before them asked permission. Thus God makes clear to you His verses. God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.","Women past childbearing who have no hope of marriage — there is no blame on them if they set aside their outer garments, so long as they do not display their adornment. But to be modest is better for them. God is All-Hearing, All-Knowing.","There is no blame on the blind, no blame on the lame, no blame on the sick, nor on yourselves for eating from your own houses, or the houses of your fathers, or the houses of your mothers, or the houses of your brothers, or the houses of your sisters, or the houses of your paternal uncles, or the houses of your paternal aunts, or the houses of your maternal uncles, or the houses of your maternal aunts, or those whose keys you possess, or your friends’. There is no blame on you whether you eat together or separately. So when you enter houses, greet one another with a greeting from God, blessed and good. Thus God makes clear to you the verses, so that you may understand.","The believers are only those who believe in God and His Messenger, and when they are with him on a matter of collective concern, they do not leave until they have asked his permission. Truly, those who ask your permission — those are the ones who believe in God and His Messenger. So when they ask your permission for some affair of theirs, give leave to whom you will among them, and ask God’s forgiveness for them. God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","Do not treat the Messenger’s summons among you like your summoning of one another. God knows well those of you who slip away under cover. Let those who defy his command beware that a trial may strike them or a painful punishment may strike them.","Surely, to God belongs whatever is in the heavens and the earth. He knows well what you are upon. On the Day they are returned to Him, He will inform them of what they did. God is All-Knowing of everything.","Blessed is He who sent down the Criterion upon His servant, that he may be a warner to all peoples.","He to whom belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth, who has not taken a child, who has no partner in dominion, who created everything and measured it precisely.","Yet they have taken gods besides Him that create nothing and are themselves created, that have no power over harm or benefit for themselves, and have no power over death, life, or resurrection.","Those who disbelieve say, “This is nothing but a lie he fabricated, and other people helped him with it.” They have committed injustice and falsehood.","They say, “Legends of the ancients that he had written down, dictated to him morning and evening.”","Say, “It was sent down by Him who knows every secret in the heavens and the earth. Truly, He is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.”","They say, “What is with this messenger? He eats food and walks through the markets! Why was an angel not sent down to him to be a warner alongside him?","Or a treasure cast down to him, or a garden given to him from which he eats?” The wrongdoers say, “You follow nothing but a bewitched man.”","Look how they coin comparisons for you—they have gone astray and cannot find a way.","Blessed is He who, if He willed, could give you better than that—gardens beneath which rivers flow—and give you palaces.","But they deny the Hour, and We have prepared a Blaze for whoever denies the Hour.","When it sees them from a distant place, they hear its raging and roaring.","When they are thrown into a tight space within it, shackled together, they cry out for destruction.","Do not cry for one destruction today—cry for many destructions!","Say, “Is that better, or the Garden of Eternity promised to the righteous?” It is their reward and destination.","In it they have whatever they wish, dwelling forever. It is a promise binding upon your Lord.","On the Day He gathers them and what they worship besides God, He will say, “Was it you who led these servants of Mine astray, or did they stray from the path on their own?”","They will say, “Glory be to You! It was not for us to take any protectors besides You, but You gave them and their fathers comfort until they forgot the Reminder and became a ruined people.”","So they have denied you in what you say, and you can neither avert nor help yourselves. Whoever among you does wrong, We will make him taste a terrible punishment.","We never sent any messengers before you except that they ate food and walked through the markets. We have made some of you a trial for others—will you be patient? Your Lord is All-Seeing.","Those who do not expect to meet Us said, “Why are angels not sent down to us, or why do we not see our Lord?” They have grown arrogant within themselves and exceeded in great insolence.","The Day they see the angels — no good news that Day for the criminals — and they will say, “Forbidden, utterly forbidden!”","We will turn to whatever deeds they did and make them scattered dust.","The people of Paradise that Day will have the best abode and the finest resting place.","The Day the sky splits open with clouds and the angels are sent down in successive descent.","True sovereignty that Day belongs to the Most Merciful. And it will be a Day grievous for the disbelievers.","The Day the wrongdoer bites his hands, saying, “If only I had taken a path with the Messenger!","O woe to me! If only I had not taken so-and-so as a close friend!","He truly led me astray from the Reminder after it had come to me.” And Satan has always been a foresaker  of man.","The Messenger said, “O my Lord, truly my people have abandoned this Quran.”","And so We made for every prophet an enemy from among the criminals. But your Lord is sufficient as a Guide and a Helper.","Those who disbelieved said, “Why was the Quran not sent down to him all at once?” It was so, that We might strengthen your heart with it, and We revealed it in stages.","They never bring you an argument except that We bring you the truth and a better explanation.","Those who will be dragged on their faces to Hell — they are worst in position and most astray in path.","We gave Moses the Scripture and appointed his brother Aaron with him as a minister.","We said, “Go, both of you, to the people who denied Our signs.” Then We destroyed them utterly.","And the people of Noah — when they denied the messengers, We drowned them and made them a sign for mankind. And We have prepared for the wrongdoers a painful punishment.","And Ad and Thamud and the people of the Well and many generations in between.","To each We set examples, and each We destroyed completely.","They have surely passed by the town that was rained upon with a rain of evil. Did they not see it? No — they did not expect resurrection.","When they see you, they only take you in mockery: “Is this the one God sent as a messenger?","He nearly would have led us astray from our gods, had we not held firmly to them.” They will know, when they see the punishment, who is most astray in path.","Have you seen the one who takes his own desire as his god? Will you then be a guardian over him?","Or do you think that most of them hear or understand? They are nothing but like cattle — rather, they are more astray in path.","Have you not seen how your Lord extended the shade? Had He willed, He could have made it still. Then We made the sun a guide over it.","Then We drew it back to Us gradually.","He is the One who made the night a garment for you, and sleep a rest, and made the day a resurrection.","He is the One who sent the winds as glad tidings before His mercy. And We sent down from the sky purifying water.","To revive with it a dead land and to give drink to what We created — livestock and many people.","Certainly We have distributed it among them so they might reflect, yet most people refuse anything but ingratitude.","Had We willed, We could have sent a warner to every town.","So do not obey the disbelievers, and strive against them with it a great striving.","He is the One who released the two seas — this one sweet and fresh, that one salty and bitter — and placed between them a barrier and an impassable boundary.","He is the One who created from water a human being, then made him of lineage and marriage. Your Lord is All-Powerful.","Yet they worship besides God what neither benefits them nor harms them. The disbeliever is ever a supporter against his Lord.","We have not sent you except as a bearer of good news and a warner.","Say, “I ask you no payment for this — only that whoever wills may take a path to his Lord.”","Put your trust in the Ever-Living who never dies, and glorify Him with praise. He is sufficient as All-Aware of His servants’ sins.","He who created the heavens and the earth and everything between them in six days, then rose over the Throne — the Most Merciful. So ask about Him one who is well-informed.","When they are told, “Prostrate to the Most Merciful,” they say, “And what is the Most Merciful? Should we prostrate to whatever you command us?” And it only increases their aversion.","Blessed is He who placed constellations in the sky and placed in it a lamp and a luminous moon.","He is the One who made the night and the day follow each other, for whoever wishes to reflect or wishes to be grateful.","The servants of the Most Merciful are those who walk upon the earth humbly, and when the ignorant address them, they say, “Peace.”","And those who spend the night before their Lord, prostrating and standing.","And those who say, “Our Lord, turn away from us the punishment of Hell — truly its punishment is relentless.","It is terrible as a resting place and a residence.”","And those who, when they spend, are neither extravagant nor stingy, but keep a balance between the two.","And those who do not invoke another god alongside God, and do not kill the soul that God has forbidden except by right, and do not commit adultery. Whoever does that will meet a penalty.","The punishment will be multiplied for him on the Day of Resurrection, and he will remain in it, humiliated.","Except whoever repents, believes, and does righteous deeds — for those, God will replace their evil deeds with good ones. And God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","And whoever repents and does righteous deeds truly turns to God in sincere repentance.","And those who do not bear false witness, and when they pass by idle talk, they pass with dignity.","And those who, when reminded of their Lord’s verses, do not fall upon them deaf and blind.","And those who say, “Our Lord, grant us from our spouses and offspring the delight of our eyes, and make us a model for the righteous.”","Those will be rewarded with the highest chambers for their patience, and will be met there with greetings and peace.","Abiding there forever — how excellent a resting place and a residence.","Say, “My Lord would not care about you were it not for your supplication. But you have denied, so it will be inescapable.”","Ta Sin Mim.","These are the verses of the clear Book.","Perhaps you will destroy yourself with grief because they will not believe.","If We willed, We could send down upon them a sign from the sky, and their necks would remain bowed before it in submission.","No new reminder comes to them from the Most Merciful except that they turn away from it.","They have already denied, so the news of what they used to mock will come to them.","Have they not looked at the earth—how many of every noble kind We have caused to grow in it?","Surely in that is a sign, yet most of them were not believers.","And your Lord—He is truly the All-Mighty, the Most Merciful.","And when your Lord called Moses, “Go to the wrongdoing people.","The people of Pharaoh. Will they not be mindful?”","He said, “My Lord, I fear they will deny me.","My chest tightens and my tongue does not flow freely, so send for Aaron.","And they hold a charge against me, so I fear they will kill me.”","He said, “No! Go, both of you, with Our signs. We are with you, listening.","Go to Pharaoh and say, ‘We are the messenger of the Lord of all worlds.","That you send the Children of Israel with us.’”","He said, “Did we not raise you among us as a child, and you stayed among us for years of your life?","And you committed that deed of yours—and you were among the ungrateful.”","He said, “I did it then while I was among the misguided.","So I fled from you when I feared you, and my Lord granted me wisdom and made me one of the messengers.","And is that a favor you remind me of—that you enslaved the Children of Israel?”","Pharaoh said, “What is the Lord of the worlds?”","He said, “The Lord of the heavens and the earth and everything between them, if you would be certain.”","He said to those around him, “Do you not hear?”","He said, “Your Lord and the Lord of your earliest forefathers.”","He said, “This messenger of yours who has been sent to you is truly mad!”","He said, “The Lord of the east and the west and everything between them, if you would reason.”","He said, “If you take any god other than me, I will surely make you one of the imprisoned!”","He said, “Even if I brought you something clear?”","He said, “Then bring it, if you are truthful.”","So he cast his staff, and suddenly it was a serpent, plain for all to see.","And he drew out his hand, and suddenly it was white to the onlookers.","He said to the chiefs around him, “This is truly a skilled sorcerer.","He wants to drive you out of your land with his sorcery. So what do you advise?”","They said, “Delay him and his brother, and send gatherers through the cities.","To bring you every skilled sorcerer.”","So the sorcerers were assembled at the appointed time on a designated day.","And the people were told, “Will you gather together.","So that we may follow the sorcerers if they are the victors?”","When the sorcerers came, they said to Pharaoh, “Will there truly be a reward for us if we are the victors?”","He said, “Yes, and you will then be among those brought near.”","Moses said to them, “Cast whatever you will cast.”","So they cast their ropes and their staffs and said, “By Pharaoh’s might, we will surely be the victors!”","Then Moses cast his staff, and suddenly it swallowed up what they had fabricated.","So the sorcerers fell down prostrating.","They said, “We believe in the Lord of the worlds.","The Lord of Moses and Aaron!”","He said, “You believed in him before I gave you permission? He is surely your chief who taught you sorcery. Soon you will know. I will cut off your hands and feet on opposite sides, and I will crucify you all!”","They said, “No harm. To our Lord we are returning.","We hope that our Lord will forgive us our sins, since we are the first of the believers.”","We revealed to Moses, “Travel by night with My servants — you will be pursued.”","So Pharaoh sent gatherers through the cities.","“These are but a small band.","And they have enraged us.","And we are all on alert.”","So We drove them out of gardens and springs.","And treasures and noble dwellings.","So it was, and We made the Children of Israel inherit them.","So they pursued them at sunrise.","When the two groups saw each other, Moses’ companions said, “We are overtaken!”","He said, “No! My Lord is with me — He will guide me.”","So We revealed to Moses, “Strike the sea with your staff.” It split apart, and each part was like a towering mountain.","And We brought the others near to that place.","And We saved Moses and all who were with him.","Then We drowned the others.","Surely in that is a sign, yet most of them were not believers.","And truly your Lord — He is the All-Mighty, the Most Merciful.","And recite to them the story of Abraham.","When he said to his father and his people, “What do you worship?”","They said, “We worship idols, and we remain devoted to them.”","He said, “Do they hear you when you call?","Or do they benefit you, or harm you?”","They said, “Rather, we found our fathers doing the same.”","He said, “Have you considered what you have been worshiping.","You and your ancient forefathers?","They are all enemies to me, except the Lord of all worlds.","He who created me, and He guides me.","And He who feeds me and gives me drink.","And when I fall ill, He heals me.","And He who will cause me to die, then bring me back to life.","And He whom I hope will forgive my sin on the Day of Judgment.","My Lord, grant me wisdom and join me with the righteous.","And grant me a reputation of truth among later generations.","And make me among the inheritors of the Garden of Bliss.","And forgive my father — he was truly among the misguided.","And do not disgrace me on the Day they are resurrected.","The Day when neither wealth nor children will be of any use.","Except for whoever comes to God with a sound heart.”","And Paradise was brought near for the righteous.","And Hellfire was laid bare for the deviants.","And they were told, “Where is what you used to worship.","Besides God? Can they help you, or help themselves?”","So they were hurled into it — they and the deviants.","And the soldiers of Iblis, all together.","They said, quarreling within it.","“By God, we were clearly in error.","When we made you equal to the Lord of all worlds.","And none led us astray but the criminals.","So we have no intercessors.","Nor any close friend.","If only we could have another chance, so we could be among the believers.”","Surely in that is a sign, yet most of them were not believers.","And truly your Lord — He is the All-Mighty, the Most Merciful.","The people of Noah denied the messengers.","When their brother Noah said to them, “Will you not be righteous?","I am a trustworthy messenger to you.","So be mindful of God and obey me.","I ask you no payment for it. My payment is only from the Lord of all worlds.","So be mindful of God and obey me.”","They said, “Should we believe in you when the lowest of people have followed you?”","He said, “What knowledge do I have of what they used to do?","Their account is only with my Lord, if you could perceive.","I will not drive away the believers.","I am only a clear warner.”","They said, “If you do not stop, O Noah, you will surely be among those stoned.”","He said, “My Lord, my people have denied me.","So judge between me and them decisively, and save me and those with me of the believers.”","So We saved him and those with him in the laden ship.","Then We drowned the rest.","Surely in that is a sign, yet most of them were not believers.","And your Lord is truly the All-Mighty, the Most Merciful.","Ad denied the messengers.","When their brother Hud said to them, “Will you not be righteous?","I am a trustworthy messenger to you.","So be mindful of God and obey me.","I ask you no payment for it. My payment is only from the Lord of all worlds.","Do you build a monument on every hilltop to amuse yourselves?","And take up fortresses as though you will live forever?","And when you strike, you strike as tyrants?","So be mindful of God and obey me.","Be mindful of the One who provided you with what you know.","Provided you with livestock and sons.","And gardens and springs.","I fear for you the punishment of a tremendous Day.”","They said, “It is the same to us whether you preach or are not among the preachers.","This is nothing but the custom of the ancients.","And we will not be punished.”","So they denied him, and We destroyed them. Surely in that is a sign, yet most of them were not believers.","And your Lord is truly the All-Mighty, the Most Merciful.","Thamud denied the messengers.","When their brother Salih said to them, “Will you not be righteous?","I am a trustworthy messenger to you.","So be mindful of God and obey me.","I ask you no payment for it. My payment rests only with the Lord of all worlds.","Do you think you will be left secure in what is here?","In gardens and springs.","And crops and palm trees with tender fruit-sheaths.","And you carve homes from the mountains with great skill?","So be mindful of God and obey me.","And do not obey the command of the excessive.","Who spread corruption in the land and do not reform.”","They said, “You are nothing but one of the bewitched.","You are only a human like us. So bring a sign, if you are truthful.”","He said, “This is a she-camel. She has her turn to drink, and you have your turn to drink on an appointed day.","Do not touch her with harm, or the punishment of a terrible day will seize you.”","But they hamstrung her, and by morning they were full of regret.","So the punishment seized them. Surely in that is a sign, yet most of them were not believers.","And truly your Lord is the All-Mighty, the Most Merciful.","The people of Lot denied the messengers.","When their brother Lot said to them, “Will you not be righteous?","I am a trustworthy messenger to you.","So be mindful of God and obey me.","I ask you no payment for it. My payment rests only with the Lord of all worlds.","Do you approach males from among all beings?","And leave what your Lord created for you of your wives? No, you are a transgressing people.”","They said, “If you do not stop, O Lot, you will surely be among those expelled.”","He said, “I am truly one who detests your deed.","My Lord, save me and my family from what they do.”","So We saved him and his family, all of them.","Except an old woman among those who stayed behind.","Then We destroyed the others.","And We rained upon them a rain — how wretched was the rain of those who had been warned.","Surely in that is a sign, yet most of them were not believers.","And truly your Lord is the All-Mighty, the Most Merciful.","The companions of the woodland denied the messengers.","When Shuayb said to them, “Will you not be righteous?","I am a trustworthy messenger to you.","So be mindful of God and obey me.","I ask you no payment for it. My payment rests only with the Lord of all worlds.","Give full measure and do not be among those who cause loss.","And weigh with an even balance.","And do not cheat people of their things, and do not go about spreading corruption in the land.","And be mindful of Him who created you and the earlier generations.”","They said, “You are nothing but one of the bewitched.","You are only a human like us, and we think you are among the liars.","So bring down upon us fragments of the sky, if you are truthful.”","He said, “My Lord knows best what you do.”","So they denied him, and the punishment of the day of the shadow seized them. It was truly the punishment of a terrible day.","Surely in that is a sign, yet most of them were not believers.","And truly your Lord is the All-Mighty, the Most Merciful.","Truly, it is a revelation from the Lord of all worlds.","The Trustworthy Spirit brought it down.","Upon your heart, so that you may be among the warners.","In a clear Arabic tongue.","And it is in the scriptures of the ancients.","Is it not a sign for them that the scholars of the Children of Israel recognize it?","Had We sent it down upon some non-Arab.","And he had recited it to them, they would not have believed in it.","Thus We have driven it into the hearts of the criminals.","They will not believe in it until they see the painful punishment.","It will come upon them suddenly while they are unaware.","Then they will say, “Will we be given respite?”","Do they seek to hasten Our punishment?","Have you considered: if We let them enjoy themselves for years.","Then what they were promised came to them.","What good would their years of enjoyment do them?","We never destroyed a town without it having warners.","As a reminder. And We were never unjust.","The devils did not bring it down.","It does not befit them, nor could they.","They are barred from even hearing it.","So do not invoke another god alongside God, lest you be among those punished.","And warn your closest kin.","And lower your wing to those who follow you among the believers.","If they disobey you, say, “I am innocent of what you do.”","And put your trust in the Almighty, the Most Merciful.","Who sees you when you stand.","And your movements among those who prostrate.","He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.","Shall I tell you upon whom the devils descend?","They descend upon every sinful liar.","They lend an ear, and most of them are liars.","As for the poets—the misguided follow them.","Do you not see that they wander in every valley.","And that they say what they do not do?","Except those who believe, do righteous deeds, remember God often, and defend themselves after they have been wronged. And those who have done wrong will come to know what fate they will be turned to.","Ta Sin. These are the verses of the Quran and a clear Book.","A guidance and glad tidings for the believers.","Those who establish prayer, give charity, and in the Hereafter they are certain.","Truly, those who do not believe in the Hereafter — We have made their deeds appealing to them, so they wander blindly.","Those are the ones for whom is the worst punishment, and in the Hereafter they are the greatest losers.","You are surely receiving the Quran from One All-Wise, All-Knowing.","When Moses said to his family, “I have spotted a fire. I will bring you news from it, or bring you a burning brand so that you may warm yourselves.”","When he came to it, he was called: “Blessed is whoever is in the fire and whoever is around it. Glory be to God, Lord of all worlds.","O Moses, it is I — God, the All-Mighty, the All-Wise.","Throw down your staff.” When he saw it writhing as if it were a serpent, he turned fleeing and did not look back. “O Moses, do not be afraid. The messengers do not fear in My presence.","But whoever has done wrong then replaced evil with good — I am truly All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","Put your hand into your collar and it will come out white, without blemish — among nine miracles to Pharaoh and his people. They were truly a defiantly sinful people.”","When Our signs came to them, plain to see, they said, “This is obvious sorcery.”","They rejected them, though their souls were convinced of them, out of wrongdoing and arrogance. So look how the corrupters ended up.","We gave David and Solomon knowledge, and they said, “Praise be to God, who has favored us over many of His believing servants.”","Solomon inherited David and said, “O people, we have been taught the language of birds and have been given of everything. This is truly the clear bounty.”","Solomon’s forces of jinn, humans, and birds were assembled before him, marshaled in order.","Until, when they came upon the Valley of the Ants, an ant said, “O ants, enter your dwellings so that Solomon and his forces do not crush you without even realizing it.”","He smiled, laughing at her words, and said, “My Lord, inspire me to be grateful for Your blessing that You have bestowed upon me and upon my parents, and to do righteous deeds that please You, and admit me by Your mercy among Your righteous servants.”","He inspected the birds and said, “Why do I not see the hoopoe? Or is he among the absent?","I will surely punish him with a severe punishment, or I will surely slaughter him, unless he brings me a clear authority.”","But he stayed not long and said, “I have encompassed what you have not encompassed, and I have come to you from Sheba with certain news.","I found a woman ruling over them, and she has been given of everything, and she has a magnificent throne.","I found her and her people prostrating to the sun instead of God. Satan has made their deeds appealing to them and turned them from the path, so they are not guided.”","So that they do not prostrate to God, who brings out what is hidden in the heavens and the earth and knows what you conceal and what you reveal.","God — there is no god but He, Lord of the Mighty Throne.","He said, “We will see whether you have spoken the truth or are among the liars.","Go with this letter of mine and deliver it to them, then turn away from them and see what they respond.”","She said, “O chiefs, a noble letter has been delivered to me.","It is from Solomon, and it reads: ‘In the name of God, the Most Compassionate, the Most Merciful.","Do not be arrogant toward me, and come to me in submission.’”","She said, “O chiefs, advise me in my affair. I have never decided a matter without you present.”","They said, “We possess strength and fierce might, but the decision is yours, so consider what you will command.”","She said, “Truly, when kings enter a town, they ruin it and reduce its most honored people to the lowest. And so they do.","But I will send them a gift and see what the envoys bring back.”","So when he came to Solomon, he said, “Do you offer me wealth? What God has given me is better than what He has given you. Rather, it is you who rejoice in your gift.","Go back to them — we will certainly come at them with forces they cannot withstand, and we will drive them out of it humiliated and debased.”","He said, “O chiefs, which of you can bring me her throne before they come to me in submission?”","A powerful one among the jinn said, “I will bring it to you before you rise from your seat, and I am strong enough for it and trustworthy.”","The one who had knowledge of the Scripture said, “I will bring it to you before your glance returns to you.” And when he saw it settled before him, he said, “This is from my Lord’s grace, to test me — whether I give thanks or am ungrateful. Whoever gives thanks only gives thanks for his own benefit, and whoever is ungrateful — my Lord is Self-Sufficient, Most Generous.”","He said, “Disguise her throne for her, and we will see whether she is guided or is among those who are not guided.”","So when she arrived, she was asked, “Is your throne like this?” She said, “It looks like it.” And we were given knowledge before her, and we were in submission.","But what she used to worship besides God had barred her. She was from a disbelieving people.","She was told, “Enter the hall.” And when she saw it, she thought it was a deep pool of water and uncovered her legs. He said, “It is a hall paved smooth with crystal.” She said, “My Lord, I have wronged myself, and I submit, along with Solomon, to God, Lord of all worlds.”","Certainly We sent to Thamud their brother Salih: “Worship God.” But at once they split into two factions quarreling.","He said, “O my people, why do you hasten toward evil before good? Why do you not seek God’s forgiveness, so that you may be shown mercy?”","They said, “We see you and those with you as a bad omen.” He said, “Your omen is with God. Rather, you are a people being tested.”","In the city there were nine men who spread corruption in the land and did no good.","They said, “Swear to one another by God: ‘We will ambush him and his family by night, then tell his guardian: we did not witness the destruction of his family, and we are telling the truth.’”","They plotted a plot, and We plotted a plot, while they were unaware.","So look at how their plotting ended — We destroyed them and their people, all of them.","There are their houses, desolate because of their wrongdoing. Surely in that is a sign for people who know.","And We saved those who believed and were righteous.","And Lot, when he said to his people, “Do you commit this obscenity while you can see?","Do you really approach men with desire instead of women? Rather, you are a people steeped in ignorance.”","The only response of his people was to say, “Drive Lot’s family out of your town — they are people who keep themselves pure!”","So We saved him and his family, except his wife — We decreed her to be among those who stayed behind.","And We rained upon them a rain — how wretched was the rain of those who had been warned!","Say, “Praise be to God, and peace upon His servants whom He chose.” Is God better, or what they associate with Him?","Or is it He who created the heavens and the earth and sent down rain from the sky for you, and We grew with it gardens of delight whose trees you could never have grown? Is there a god beside God? No, they are a people who equate others with Him.","Or is it He who made the earth a stable ground and set rivers through it and placed firm mountains upon it and set a barrier between the two seas? Is there a god beside God? No, most of them do not know.","Or is it He who answers the desperate when he calls upon Him and removes affliction and makes you successors on the earth? Is there a god beside God? Little do you reflect.","Or is it He who guides you through the darknesses of land and sea, and who sends the winds as glad tidings ahead of His mercy? Is there a god beside God? Exalted is God above what they associate with Him.","Or is it He who originates creation then repeats it, and who provides for you from the sky and the earth? Is there a god beside God? Say, “Bring your proof, if you are truthful.”","Say, “No one in the heavens and the earth knows the unseen except God.” And they do not perceive when they will be resurrected.","Rather, their knowledge has failed them regarding the Hereafter. No, they are in doubt about it. No, they are blind to it.","Those who disbelieved said, “When we have become dust — we and our fathers — will we really be brought out?","We were promised this before, we and our fathers. This is nothing but tales of the ancients.”","Say, “Travel through the earth and see how the criminals met their end.”","Do not grieve over them, and do not be distressed by what they scheme.","They say, “When will this promise come, if you are truthful?”","Say, “Perhaps some of what you seek to hasten is already close behind you.”","Truly your Lord is full of grace toward people, but most of them are not grateful.","Your Lord certainly knows what their chests conceal and what they declare.","There is no hidden thing in the heaven and the earth that is not in a clear record.","This Quran relates to the Children of Israel most of what they differ over.","It is surely a guidance and a mercy for the believers.","Your Lord will judge between them by His decree. He is the All-Mighty, the All-Knowing.","So put your trust in God. You are upon the clear truth.","You cannot make the dead hear, nor can you make the deaf hear the call when they turn away retreating.","You cannot guide the blind out of their error. You can only make hear those who believe in Our verses, for they are ones who submit.","When the decree falls upon them, We will bring out for them a creature from the earth that speaks to them: that people had no certainty in Our signs.","On the Day We gather from every nation a throng of those who denied Our verses, and they will be held in ranks.","Until, when they arrive, He will say, “Did you deny My verses without encompassing them in knowledge? Or what was it you were doing?”","The decree will fall upon them for the wrong they did, and they will not speak.","Do they not see that We made the night for them to rest in and the day giving sight? Surely in that are signs for people who believe.","On the Day the Horn is blown, everyone in the heavens and everyone on the earth will be struck with terror, except whom God wills. And all will come to Him humbled.","You see the mountains and think them fixed, yet they drift like clouds. The handiwork of God, Who perfected everything. He is fully Aware of what you do.","Whoever brings a good deed will have something better than it, and they will be safe from the terror of that Day.","And whoever brings an evil deed — their faces will be thrust into the Fire. “Are you repaid for anything but what you used to do?”","“I have only been commanded to worship the Lord of this city, who made it sacred — and to Him belongs everything — and I have been commanded to be among those who submit.","And to recite the Quran.” Whoever is guided is guided only for his own sake. And whoever goes astray — say, “I am only one of the warners.”","And say, “All praise belongs to God. He will show you His signs and you will recognize them.” Your Lord is not unaware of what you do.","Ta Sin Mim.","These are the verses of the clear Book.","We recite to you from the account of Moses and Pharaoh in truth, for a people who believe.","Truly, Pharaoh exalted himself in the land and divided its people into factions, oppressing a group among them—slaughtering their sons and sparing their women. He was among the corrupters.","And We wished to favor those who were oppressed in the land, and to make them leaders, and to make them the inheritors.","And to establish them in the land, and to show Pharaoh and Haman and their soldiers through them the very thing they feared.","We inspired Moses’s mother: “Nurse him, and when you fear for him, cast him into the river. Do not be afraid and do not grieve. We will return him to you and make him one of the messengers.”","So Pharaoh’s household picked him up, only for him to become an enemy and a source of grief to them. Surely Pharaoh and Haman and their soldiers were sinners.","Pharaoh’s wife said, “A delight to my eye and yours—do not kill him. Perhaps he will benefit us, or we may adopt him as a son.” And they did not perceive.","And the heart of Moses’s mother became empty. She nearly disclosed him, had We not strengthened her heart so that she would be among the believers.","She said to his sister, “Follow him.” So she watched him from a distance while they did not perceive.","And We had forbidden wet-nurses for him before, so she said, “Shall I direct you to a household who will care for him for you and be sincere to him?”","So We returned him to his mother, that her eye might be cooled and she would not grieve, and that she would know that God’s promise is true—but most of them do not know.","When he reached his full strength and maturity, We gave him judgment and knowledge. Thus do We recompense those who do good.","He entered the city at a time when its people were unaware, and he found in it two men fighting — one from his own faction and the other from his enemy. The one from his faction called on him for help against the one from his enemy, so Moses struck him and killed him. He said, “This is the work of Satan. He is truly a misleading, open enemy.”","He said, “My Lord, I have wronged myself, so forgive me.” So He forgave him. He is the All-Forgiving, the Most Merciful.","He said, “My Lord, for the favor You have bestowed on me, I will never be a supporter of the guilty.”","So he became in the city, fearful and watchful, when suddenly the one who had sought his help the day before was crying out to him again. Moses said to him, “You are clearly a troublemaker.”","But when he was about to seize the one who was an enemy to them both, the man said, “O Moses, do you want to kill me as you killed a man yesterday? You only want to be a tyrant in the land, and you do not want to be among those who set things right.”","A man came running from the farthest end of the city. He said, “O Moses, the chiefs are conspiring against you to kill you, so leave! I am truly one who advises you sincerely.”","So he left it, fearful and watchful. He said, “My Lord, save me from the wrongdoing people.”","When he set out toward Midian, he said, “Perhaps my Lord will guide me to the right path.”","When he arrived at the waters of Midian, he found a crowd of people watering their flocks, and he found apart from them two women holding back their flock. He said, “What is the matter with you two?” They said, “We cannot water until the shepherds move away, and our father is a very old man.”","So he watered their flock for them, then withdrew to the shade and said, “My Lord, I am truly in need of whatever good You send down to me.”","Then one of the two women came to him, walking shyly. She said, “My father invites you so he may reward you for watering our flock for us.” When he came to him and told him his story, he said, “Do not be afraid. You have escaped from the wrongdoing people.”","One of the two women said, “O my father, hire him. The best man you can hire is the strong and trustworthy.”","He said, “I wish to marry one of these two daughters of mine to you, on the condition that you serve me for eight years. If you complete ten, that is from you, and I do not wish to make it hard for you. You will find me, God willing, among the righteous.”","He said, “That is settled between me and you. Whichever of the two terms I fulfill, there will be no grievance against me. And God is trustee over what we say.”","When Moses had fulfilled the term and set out with his family, he spotted a fire on the side of the mountain. He said to his family, “Stay here. I have spotted a fire. Perhaps I can bring you back some news from it, or a burning brand, so that you may warm yourselves.”","When he came to it, he was called from the right bank of the valley, in the blessed spot, from the tree, “O Moses, truly I am God, Lord of all worlds.”","“Cast down your staff.” But when he saw it writhing as if it were a serpent, he turned fleeing and did not look back. “O Moses, come forward and do not be afraid. You are among the safe.”","“Slip your hand into your garment—it will come out white, without blemish. And draw your arm close to yourself against fear. These two are proofs from your Lord to Pharaoh and his chiefs. They were a defiantly sinful people.”","He said, “My Lord, I killed a man among them, and I fear they will kill me.","And my brother Aaron is more eloquent than me in speech, so send him with me as a supporter to confirm me. I fear they will deny me.”","He said, “We will strengthen your arm through your brother and grant you both authority, so they will not reach you. Through Our signs, you and whoever follows you will be the victors.”","But when Moses came to them with Our clear miracles, they said, “This is nothing but fabricated sorcery. We never heard of this among our forefathers.”","Moses said, “My Lord knows best who has brought guidance from Him and who will have the ultimate home. Surely the wrongdoers will not succeed.”","Pharaoh said, “O chiefs, I know of no god for you other than myself. So kindle for me, O Haman, upon the clay, and build me a tower, that I may look upon Moses’s god. I certainly think he is one of the liars.”","He and his soldiers grew arrogant in the land without right, and they thought they would never be returned to Us.","So We seized him and his soldiers and hurled them into the sea. See how the wrongdoers met their end!","We made them leaders calling to the Fire, and on the Day of Resurrection they will not be helped.","We made a curse follow them in this world, and on the Day of Resurrection they will be among the despised.","Truly We gave Moses the Book after We had destroyed the earlier generations—insights for people, and guidance, and mercy, so that they might remember.","You were not on the western side when We decreed the matter to Moses, nor were you among the witnesses.","But We raised generations, and long ages passed over them. You were not dwelling among the people of Midian, reciting Our verses to them, but it is We who were sending messengers.","You were not at the side of the Mount when We called out, but it is a mercy from your Lord so that you may warn a people to whom no warner came before you, so that they might remember.","Were it not that a disaster might strike them for what their hands have sent ahead, and they would say, “Our Lord, if only You had sent us a messenger so we could follow Your verses and be among the believers.”","Yet when the truth came to them from Us, they said, “Why was he not given the like of what Moses was given?” Did they not reject what Moses was given before? They said, “Two works of sorcery supporting each other,” and they said, “We reject them all.”","Say, “Then bring a book from God that is better in guidance than these two, and I will follow it—if you are truthful.”","If they do not respond to you, then know that they only follow their desires. And who is more astray than one who follows his desire without guidance from God? Truly God does not guide the wrongdoing people.","Certainly We have conveyed the Word to them in succession, so that they might remember.","Those to whom We gave the Book before it—they believe in it.","When it is recited to them, they say, “We believe in it. It is the truth from our Lord. Even before it, we were submitters.”","Those will be given their reward twice for their patience, and they repel evil with good, and they spend from what We have provided them.","When they hear idle talk, they turn away from it and say, “To us our deeds, and to you your deeds. Peace be upon you. We do not seek the ignorant.”","You do not guide whom you love, but God guides whom He wills. He knows best the rightly guided.","They said, “If we follow the guidance with you, we will be snatched from our land.” Have We not established for them a secure sanctuary to which the fruits of all things are brought as provision from Us? But most of them do not know.","How many a town We destroyed that was insolent in its livelihood! There are their dwellings, barely inhabited after them. It is We who were the inheritors.","Your Lord would never destroy the towns until He had sent to their capital a messenger reciting Our verses to them. And We would never destroy the towns unless their people were wrongdoers.","Whatever you have been given is only the enjoyment of worldly life and its adornment. What is with God is better and more lasting. Will you not reason?","Is the one We promised a good promise, which he will meet, like the one We gave the enjoyment of this worldly life, then on the Day of Resurrection he will be among those brought forward?","On the Day He calls to them and says, “Where are My partners that you used to claim?”","Those against whom the word has come due will say, “Our Lord, these are the ones we led astray. We led them astray as we ourselves went astray. We disown them before You. It was not us they worshipped.”","They will be told, “Call upon your partners.” So they will call upon them, but they will not answer them, and they will see the punishment. If only they had been guided.","On the Day He calls to them and says, “What did you answer the messengers?”","All answers will be obscured from them that Day, and they will not question one another.","But as for the one who repented, believed, and did good, he may well be among the successful.","Your Lord creates what He wills and chooses. They have no choice. Glory be to God, and exalted is He above what they associate with Him.","Your Lord knows what their hearts conceal and what they reveal.","He is God—there is no god but Him. To Him belongs all praise in the first life and the last. His is the judgment, and to Him you will be returned.","Say, “Have you considered: if God made the night perpetual over you until the Day of Resurrection, what god other than God could bring you light? Will you not listen?”","Say, “Have you considered: if God made the day perpetual over you until the Day of Resurrection, what god other than God could bring you a night in which to rest? Will you not see?”","Out of His mercy He made for you the night and the day, so that you may rest in it and seek of His bounty, and so that you may be grateful.","On the Day He calls to them and says, “Where are My partners that you used to claim?”","We will draw from every nation a witness and say, “Produce your proof.” Then they will know that the truth belongs to God, and all they used to fabricate will vanish from them.","Korah was from Moses’s people, but he oppressed them. We gave him such treasures that their very keys would weigh down a band of strong men. When his people said to him, “Do not gloat. Surely God does not love those who gloat.","Seek, through what God has given you, the Home of the Hereafter, and do not forget your share of this world. Do good as God has done good to you, and do not seek corruption in the land. Truly God does not love the corrupters.”","He said, “I was only given this because of knowledge I possess.” Did he not know that God had destroyed before him generations who were mightier than him in strength and greater in accumulation? The guilty are not even asked about their sins.","So he came out before his people in his splendor. Those who desired the life of this world said, “If only we had the like of what Korah has been given! He truly is a man of great fortune.”","But those who had been given knowledge said, “Woe to you! God’s reward is better for whoever believes and does good, and none receive it except the patient.”","So We caused the earth to swallow him and his home. He had no group to help him against God, nor could he help himself.","Those who had wished for his position the day before began saying, “Ah! God extends provision to whomever He wills among His servants and restricts it. Had God not been gracious to us, He would have caused the earth to swallow us. Ah! The disbelievers never succeed.”","That Home of the Hereafter — We assign it to those who desire neither dominance in the land nor corruption. The outcome belongs to the righteous.","Whoever brings a good deed will have something better than it, and whoever brings an evil deed — those who did evil will only be repaid for what they used to do.","Certainly He who ordained the Quran upon you will return you to a place of return. Say, “My Lord knows best who has brought guidance and who is in clear error.”","You never expected the Book to be cast upon you — it was only a mercy from your Lord. So never be a supporter of the disbelievers.","Let them not turn you away from God’s verses after they have been sent down to you. Call to your Lord, and never be among those who associate partners with God.","Do not call upon another god alongside God. There is no god but Him. Everything will perish except His face. His is the judgment, and to Him you will be returned.","Alif Lam Mim.","Do people think they will be left alone because they say, “We believe,” and not be tested?","We tested those before them, and God will surely know those who are truthful and will surely know the liars.","Or do those who commit evil deeds think they can outrun Us? How wretched is their judgment!","Whoever hopes to meet God — God’s appointed time is certainly coming. He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.","Whoever strives, strives only for himself. Truly God is Self-Sufficient, beyond need of all creation.","Those who believe and do righteous deeds — We will surely erase their sins and will surely reward them the best of what they used to do.","We have enjoined upon man kindness to his parents. But if they press you to associate with Me what you have no knowledge of, do not obey them. To Me is your return, and I will inform you of what you used to do.","Those who believe and do righteous deeds — We will surely admit them among the righteous.","Among people is he who says, “We believe in God,” but when he is harmed for God’s sake, he treats the persecution of people as though it were God’s punishment. Yet if help comes from your Lord, they will surely say, “We were with you.” Does God not know best what is in the hearts of all creation?","God will surely know those who believe and will surely know the hypocrites.","Those who disbelieve say to those who believe, “Follow our path, and let us bear your sins.” They will not bear any of their sins. They are surely liars.","They will carry their own burdens and burdens along with their burdens, and they will surely be questioned on the Day of Resurrection about what they used to fabricate.","We sent Noah to his people, and he remained among them a thousand years less fifty. Then the flood seized them while they were wrongdoers.","So We saved him and the companions of the ship, and We made it a sign for all peoples.","And Abraham, when he said to his people, “Worship God and be mindful of Him. That is better for you, if only you knew.","You worship nothing but idols besides God, and you fabricate lies. Those you worship besides God have no power to provide for you. So seek provision from God, worship Him, and give thanks to Him. To Him you will be returned.”","If you deny, nations before you have already denied. The Messenger’s only duty is clear delivery.","Have they not seen how God originates creation, then repeats it? Truly, that is easy for God.","Say, “Travel through the earth and observe how He originated creation. Then God will bring about the final creation. God is Capable of all things.","He punishes whom He wills and shows mercy to whom He wills, and to Him you will be turned back.","You cannot escape Him on earth or in heaven, and you have no protector or helper besides God.”","Those who disbelieve in God’s signs and in meeting Him — they have despaired of My mercy, and for them is a painful punishment.","But his people’s only response was to say, “Kill him or burn him!” So God saved him from the fire. Surely in that are signs for people who believe.","And he said, “You have taken idols besides God only out of mutual affection between you in the life of this world. Then on the Day of Resurrection, you will disown one another and curse one another, and your refuge will be the Fire, and you will have no helpers.”","So Lot believed in him. And he said, “I am emigrating to my Lord. He is the All-Mighty, the All-Wise.”","And We granted him Isaac and Jacob, and We placed prophethood and the Scripture among his descendants. We gave him his reward in this world, and in the Hereafter he is surely among the righteous.","And Lot, when he said to his people, “You commit the obscenity that no one in all the world has preceded you in.","Do you truly approach men, cut off the road, and commit evil in your gatherings?” But his people’s only response was to say, “Bring us God’s punishment, if you are truthful!”","He said, “My Lord, help me against the corrupting people.”","When Our messengers came to Abraham with the good news, they said, “We are going to destroy the people of this town. Truly, its people have been wrongdoers.”","He said, “Lot is there.” They said, “We know well who is there. We will surely save him and his family, except his wife — she is among those who remain behind.”","When Our messengers came to Lot, he was distressed by them and felt helpless about them. They said, “Do not fear and do not grieve. We will save you and your family, except your wife — she is among those who remain behind.","We are bringing down upon the people of this town a punishment from the sky for their defiance.”","And We certainly left from it a clear sign for people who reason.","To Midian, their brother Shuayb. He said, “O my people, worship God and hope for the Last Day, and do not spread corruption in the land.”","But they denied him, so the earthquake seized them, and they lay lifeless in their homes.","And Aad and Thamud — it has become clear to you from their dwellings. Satan made their deeds appealing to them and turned them away from the path, though they were capable of seeing.","And Korah, Pharaoh, and Haman — Moses certainly came to them with clear proofs, but they were arrogant in the land, and they could not outrun Us.","So each We seized for his sin. Among them were those upon whom We sent a storm of stones, among them were those seized by the blast, among them were those We caused the earth to swallow, and among them were those We drowned. God would never wrong them, but it was themselves they were wronging.","The example of those who take protectors other than God is like the spider that builds a house. Surely the flimsiest of houses is the spider’s house — if only they knew.","God knows whatever they call upon besides Him. He is the All-Mighty, the All-Wise.","These are the examples We set for people, but none grasp them except those who have knowledge.","God created the heavens and the earth in truth. Truly in that is a sign for the believers.","Recite what has been revealed to you of the Book and establish prayer. Truly, prayer restrains from indecency and wrongdoing. And the remembrance of God is greater. God knows what you do.","Do not argue with the People of the Book except in the best manner — except those among them who have done wrong — and say, “We believe in what has been sent down to us and what has been sent down to you. Our God and your God is one, and to Him we submit.”","And so We sent down the Book to you. Those to whom We gave the Book believe in it, and among these are some who believe in it. None deny Our verses except the disbelievers.","You did not recite any book before it, nor did you write one with your right hand — otherwise the falsifiers would have had cause to doubt.","Rather, it is clear signs in the hearts of those given knowledge. None deny Our signs except the wrongdoers.","They say, “Why have signs not been sent down upon him from his Lord?” Say, “The signs are only with God, and I am only a clear warner.”","Is it not enough for them that We sent down upon you the Book, recited to them? Surely in that is a mercy and a reminder for a people who believe.","Say, “God suffices as a witness between me and you. He knows what is in the heavens and the earth.” Those who believe in falsehood and disbelieve in God — it is they who are the losers.","They urge you to hasten the punishment. Were it not for an appointed term, the punishment would have come to them. It will surely come upon them suddenly while they are unaware.","They urge you to hasten the punishment, yet Hell is certainly encompassing the disbelievers.","On the Day the punishment covers them from above them and from beneath their feet, and He says, “Taste what you used to do.”","O My servants who believe, My earth is vast, so worship Me alone.","Every soul will taste death. Then to Us you will be returned.","Those who believe and do righteous deeds — We will surely settle them in lofty chambers of Paradise beneath which rivers flow, dwelling therein forever. Excellent is the reward of those who act.","Those who are patient and place their trust in their Lord.","How many a creature does not carry its own provision—God provides for it and for you. He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.","If you asked them, “Who created the heavens and the earth and subjected the sun and the moon?” they would surely say, “God.” So how are they deluded?","God expands provision for whoever He wills among His servants and restricts it for him. Truly, God is All-Knowing of all things.","If you asked them, “Who sent down water from the sky and revived the earth after its death?” they would surely say, “God.” Say, “Praise be to God.” But most of them do not reason.","This worldly life is nothing but diversion and play. The home of the Hereafter—that is truly the life. If only they knew.","When they board a ship, they call upon God, devoting their faith sincerely to Him. But when He delivers them to land, at once they associate others with Him.","So that they deny what We have given them and so that they enjoy themselves. They will come to know.","Have they not seen that We made a secure sanctuary while people are snatched away all around them? Is it in falsehood they believe and God’s blessing they deny?","Who is more unjust than one who fabricates a lie against God or denies the truth when it comes to him? Is there not in Hell a dwelling for the disbelievers?","Those who strive in Our cause—We will surely guide them to Our ways. God is certainly with those who do good.","Alif Lam Mim.","The Romans have been defeated.","In the nearest land, yet after their defeat they will prevail.","Within a few years. To God belongs the command before and after. On that day the believers will rejoice.","At God’s victory. He grants victory to whom He wills, and He is the All-Mighty, the Most Merciful.","God’s promise. God never breaks His promise, but most people do not know.","They know the outward of this worldly life, but of the Hereafter they are heedless.","Have they not reflected within themselves? God did not create the heavens and the earth and what is between them except in truth and for an appointed term. Yet truly many people deny the meeting with their Lord.","Have they not traveled through the earth and seen what was the end of those before them? They were mightier than them in strength, and they tilled the earth and developed it more than they have developed it. Their messengers came to them with clear proofs. God would never wrong them, but they wronged themselves.","Then the end of those who did evil was the worst, because they denied God’s signs and used to mock them.","God originates creation, then repeats it, then to Him you will be returned.","On the Day the Hour arrives, the criminals will be struck with despair.","They will have no intercessors among their partners, and they will disown their partners.","On the Day the Hour arrives, that Day they will be separated.","As for those who believed and did righteous deeds, they will be delighted in a garden.","But as for those who disbelieved and denied Our signs and the meeting of the Hereafter, those will be brought into the punishment.","So glory be to God when you reach the evening and when you reach the morning.","And to Him belongs all praise in the heavens and the earth, and in the late afternoon and when you reach midday.","He brings the living from the dead and brings the dead from the living, and He gives life to the earth after its death. And likewise you will be brought out.","Among His signs is that He created you from dust, then suddenly you were human beings spreading across the earth.","Among His signs is that He created for you from yourselves mates so that you may find tranquility in them, and He placed between you love and mercy. Surely in that are signs for people who reflect.","Among His signs is the creation of the heavens and the earth and the diversity of your languages and your colors. Surely in that are signs for those of knowledge.","Among His signs is your sleep by night and by day and your seeking of His bounty. Surely in that are signs for people who listen.","Among His signs is that He shows you lightning, inspiring fear and hope, and He sends down water from the sky and revives the earth after its death. Surely in that are signs for people who reason.","Among His signs is that the sky and the earth stand by His command. Then when He calls you with a single call from the earth, at once you will emerge.","To Him belongs everyone in the heavens and the earth. All are devoutly obedient to Him.","He is the One who originates creation then repeats it, and that is even easier for Him. His is the highest attribute in the heavens and the earth, and He is the All-Mighty, the All-Wise.","He sets for you an example from yourselves: do you have among those your right hands possess any partners in what We have provided you, so that you are equal in it, fearing them as you fear one another? This is how We make the verses clear for people who reason.","But those who wronged followed their own desires without knowledge. So who can guide the one God has led astray? They have no helpers.","So set your face toward the religion, a monotheist — the natural disposition of God upon which He created people. There is no altering God’s creation. That is the upright religion, but most people do not know.","Turning to Him in repentance, and be mindful of Him, and establish the prayer, and do not be among those who associate partners with God.","Among those who divided their religion and became sects, each faction rejoicing in what they have.","When hardship touches people, they call upon their Lord, turning to Him in repentance. Then when He gives them a taste of mercy from Him, at once a group of them associate partners with their Lord.","So as to deny what We have given them. So enjoy yourselves — you will soon know.","Or have We sent down upon them any authority that speaks of what they associate with Him?","When We give people a taste of mercy, they rejoice in it. But if misfortune strikes them because of what their own hands have sent ahead, at once they despair.","Have they not seen that God extends provision to whom He wills and restricts it? Surely in that are signs for people who believe.","So give the relative his right, and the needy, and the traveler. That is best for those who seek God’s face, and it is they who are the successful.","Whatever you give in usury to increase through people’s wealth does not increase with God. But whatever you give in charity, seeking God’s face — it is they who will receive manifold.","God is the One who created you, then provided for you, then causes you to die, then brings you to life. Can any of your partners do any of that? Glory be to Him, and exalted is He above what they associate with Him.","Corruption has appeared on land and sea because of what people’s hands have earned, so He may let them taste some of what they have done — that they might turn back.","Say, “Travel through the earth and see what was the end of those before. Most of them were idolaters.”","So set your face toward the upright religion before a Day comes from God that cannot be turned back. On that Day, they will be split apart.","Whoever disbelieves, his disbelief is upon him. And whoever does good, they are preparing for themselves.","So that He may recompense those who believed and did good deeds out of His grace. Truly, He does not love the disbelievers.","Among His signs is that He sends the winds bearing good news, and to let you taste of His mercy, and so that ships may sail by His command, and so that you may seek of His bounty — and that you may be grateful.","We sent before you messengers to their peoples, and they came to them with clear proofs. Then We took vengeance on those who committed crimes, and it was a duty upon Us to aid the believers.","God is the One who sends the winds, and they stir up clouds, and He spreads them across the sky however He wills and breaks them into fragments — then you see the rain emerging from within them. And when He strikes with it whomever He wills of His servants, at once they rejoice.","Even though before it was sent down upon them — just before it — they were in utter despair.","So look at the traces of God’s mercy: how He gives life to the earth after its death. Surely, that same One gives life to the dead, and He is Capable of all things.","Yet if We sent a wind and they saw it turned yellow, they would persist in disbelief after it.","You cannot make the dead hear, nor can you make the deaf hear the call when they turn away retreating.","You cannot guide the blind out of their error. You can only make hear those who believe in Our signs, for they are ones who submit.","God is the One who created you from weakness, then made after weakness strength, then made after strength weakness and gray hair. He creates what He wills, and He is the All-Knowing, the All-Powerful.","On the Day the Hour arrives, the criminals will swear they remained no more than an hour. That is how they were deluded.","But those given knowledge and faith will say, “You remained, by God’s decree, until the Day of Resurrection. This is the Day of Resurrection, but you did not know.”","On that Day, the excuses of those who wronged will not benefit them, nor will they be asked to make amends.","Truly We have set out for people in this Quran every kind of parable. Yet if you bring them a sign, those who disbelieve will surely say, “You are nothing but followers of falsehood.”","Thus does God seal the hearts of those who do not know.","So be patient. Surely God’s promise is true. And do not let those who lack certainty unsettle you.","Alif Lam Mim.","These are the verses of the Wise Book.","A guidance and a mercy for those who do good.","Those who establish prayer, give charity, and are certain of the Hereafter.","Those are upon guidance from their Lord, and those are the successful.","Among people is he who buys idle talk to lead astray from God’s path without knowledge, and takes it in mockery. For those is a humiliating punishment.","When Our verses are recited to him, he turns away in arrogance as though he never heard them, as though in his ears is deafness. So give him tidings of a painful punishment.","Truly, those who believe and do righteous deeds — for them are Gardens of Bliss.","Abiding in them forever. God’s promise is true. He is the All-Mighty, the All-Wise.","He created the heavens without pillars you can see, and cast into the earth firm mountains lest it sway with you, and spread throughout it every kind of creature. And We sent down water from the sky and caused every noble pair to grow in it.","This is God’s creation. So show me what those besides Him have created. Rather, the wrongdoers are in clear misguidance.","We gave Luqman wisdom: “Be grateful to God.” Whoever is grateful is only grateful for his own sake, and whoever is ungrateful — God is Self-Sufficient, Praiseworthy.","And when Luqman said to his son, advising him, “O my son, do not associate anything with God. Surely, associating others with God is a tremendous wrong.”","We enjoined upon man concerning his parents — his mother carried him in weakness upon weakness, and his weaning is in two years — “Be grateful to Me and to your parents. To Me is the destination.","But if they strive to make you associate with Me what you have no knowledge of, do not obey them. Yet keep their company in this world with kindness, and follow the path of whoever turns to Me. Then to Me is your return, and I will inform you of what you used to do.”","“O my son, even if it be the weight of a mustard seed, within a rock or in the heavens or in the earth, God will bring it. Surely God is the Subtle, the All-Aware.","O my son, establish the prayer, enjoin what is right, forbid what is wrong, and bear patiently whatever befalls you. Truly, that is among the most resolute of matters.","Do not turn your cheek away from people, and do not walk upon the earth in arrogance. God does not love any conceited boaster.","Be moderate in your stride and lower your voice. Surely the most detestable of voices is the braying of donkeys.”","Do you not see that God has subjected to you whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth, and has lavished upon you His blessings, outward and inward? Yet among people are those who argue about God without knowledge, without guidance, and without an illuminating scripture.","When they are told, “Follow what God has sent down,” they say, “Rather, we follow what we found our fathers upon.” Even if Satan were calling them to the punishment of the Blaze?","Whoever submits his face to God while being a doer of good has grasped the firmest handhold. To God belongs the outcome of all matters.","Whoever disbelieves, let his disbelief not grieve you. To Us is their return, and We will inform them of what they did. God is All-Knowing of what lies within the hearts.","We let them enjoy for a little while, then We drive them to a harsh punishment.","If you asked them, “Who created the heavens and the earth?” they would surely say, “God.” Say, “All praise belongs to God.” But most of them do not know.","To God belongs whatever is in the heavens and the earth. God is the Self-Sufficient, the Praiseworthy.","If every tree on earth were pens and the sea, replenished by seven more seas after it, were ink, God’s words would not be exhausted. Truly God is All-Mighty, All-Wise.","Your creation and your resurrection are but like that of a single soul. Truly God is All-Hearing, All-Seeing.","Do you not see that God merges the night into the day and merges the day into the night, and has subjected the sun and the moon, each running to an appointed term, and that God is fully Aware of what you do?","That is because God is the Truth, and what they invoke besides Him is falsehood, and because God is the Most High, the Most Great.","Do you not see that ships sail through the sea by God’s grace, to show you some of His signs? In that are signs for everyone patient and grateful.","When waves cover them like canopies, they call upon God, devoting their faith sincerely to Him. But when He delivers them to shore, some of them are moderate. No one rejects Our verses except every treacherous ingrate.","O people, be mindful of your Lord and fear a Day when no parent will avail their child, nor will any child avail their parent in the least. Surely God’s promise is true, so do not let the life of this world deceive you, and do not let the Deceiver deceive you about God.","Truly God alone has knowledge of the Hour. He sends down the rain and knows what is in the wombs. No soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in what land it will die. Truly God is All-Knowing, All-Aware.","Alif Lam Mim.","The revelation of the Book, in which there is no doubt, is from the Lord of all worlds.","Or do they say, “He fabricated it”? Rather, it is the truth from your Lord, so that you may warn a people to whom no warner came before you, that they may be guided.","God is the One who created the heavens and the earth and everything between them in six days, then rose over the Throne. You have no protector and no intercessor apart from Him. Will you not then remember?","He directs every matter from the heaven to the earth; then it ascends to Him in a day whose measure is a thousand years by your counting.","That is the Knower of the unseen and the seen, the All-Mighty, the Most Merciful.","He who perfected everything He created, and began the creation of man from clay.","Then He made his offspring from an extract of worthless fluid.","Then He shaped him and breathed into him of His spirit, and made for you hearing, sight, and hearts. Little do you give thanks.","They say, “When we have dissolved into the earth, will we truly be in a new creation?” Rather, they are deniers of the meeting with their Lord.","Say, “The Angel of Death, who has been assigned to you, will take your souls in full. Then to your Lord you will be returned.”","If only you could see when the criminals hang their heads before their Lord: “Our Lord, we have seen and we have heard, so send us back and we will do good. We are now certain.”","Had We willed, We could have given every soul its guidance, but the word from Me has come due: “I will surely fill Hell with jinn and humans altogether.”","So taste, because you forgot the meeting of this Day of yours. We have forgotten you. Taste the punishment of eternity for what you used to do.","Only those believe in Our verses who, when reminded by them, fall down in prostration and glorify their Lord with praise, and they are not arrogant.","Their sides forsake their beds, calling upon their Lord in fear and hope, and from what We have provided them they spend.","No soul knows what has been hidden for them of delight of the eyes, as recompense for what they used to do.","Is one who believed like one who was defiantly disobedient? They are not equal.","As for those who believed and did righteous deeds, for them are the Gardens of Refuge as hospitality for what they used to do.","But as for those who defiantly disobeyed, their refuge is the Fire. Every time they try to escape it, they are thrown back in, and they are told, “Taste the punishment of the Fire that you used to deny.”","We will make them taste the lesser punishment before the greater punishment, so that perhaps they will return.","Who is more unjust than one who is reminded of his Lord’s verses and then turns away from them? Truly, We will take vengeance on the criminals.","We gave Moses the Book, so do not be in doubt about meeting Him, and We made it a guidance for the Children of Israel.","We appointed from among them leaders who guided by Our command when they were patient, and they were certain of Our signs.","Surely your Lord — it is He who will judge between them on the Day of Resurrection concerning what they used to differ over.","Has it not become clear to them how many generations We destroyed before them, in whose dwellings they now walk? Surely in that are signs. Will they not listen?","Have they not seen that We drive water to the barren land and bring out crops from which their livestock and they themselves eat? Will they not see?","They say, “When is this verdict, if you are truthful?”","Say, “On the Day of the Verdict, the faith of those who disbelieved will not benefit them, nor will they be given respite.”","So turn away from them and wait. They too are waiting.","O Prophet, be mindful of God and do not obey the disbelievers and the hypocrites. Truly, God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.","Follow what is revealed to you from your Lord. God is fully Aware of what you do.","Put your trust in God. God is sufficient as a Guardian.","God has not placed two hearts inside any man’s chest. He has not made your wives whom you declare unlawful to yourselves your mothers. And He has not made your adopted sons your true sons. That is merely your talk from your mouths, but God speaks the truth, and He guides to the way.","Call them by their fathers — that is more just in God’s sight. If you do not know their fathers, then they are your brothers in faith and your allies. There is no blame on you for what you did by mistake, but only for what your hearts deliberately intended. God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","The Prophet has a greater claim on the believers than they have on themselves, and his wives are their mothers. And blood relatives have a greater claim on one another in God’s Book than the believers and the emigrants, though you may still show kindness to your allies. That has been written in the Book.","And when We took from the prophets their covenant — and from you, and from Noah, Abraham, Moses, and Jesus son of Mary — We took from them a solemn covenant.","So that He may question the truthful about their truthfulness. And He has prepared for the disbelievers a painful punishment.","O you who believe, remember God’s favor upon you when armies came against you, and We sent upon them a wind and forces you did not see. And God was All-Seeing of what you do.","When they came at you from above you and from below you, and when eyes shifted wildly and hearts reached the throats, and you harbored doubts about God.","There the believers were tested and shaken with a violent shaking.","And when the hypocrites and those in whose hearts is disease said, “God and His Messenger promised us nothing but delusion.”","And when a group of them said, “O people of Yathrib, there is no stand for you, so turn back.” And a party of them asked the Prophet’s leave, saying, “Our homes are exposed,” when they were not exposed. They wanted nothing but to flee.","Had it been entered upon them from all its sides and they were asked to turn to treachery, they would have done so, and they would have hesitated only briefly.","They had already pledged to God before that they would not turn their backs. And a pledge to God will be questioned.","Say, “Flight will not benefit you if you flee from death or killing, and even then you would enjoy only a little.”","Say, “Who is it that can shield you from God if He intends harm for you, or intends mercy for you?” They will find for themselves no protector or helper besides God.","God already knows those among you who hold others back and those who say to their brothers, “Come to us,” and they hardly come to battle at all.","Grudging toward you. When fear comes, you see them looking at you, their eyes rolling like one overtaken by death. But when the fear passes, they lash you with sharp tongues, grudging toward any good. Those have not believed, so God rendered their deeds worthless. And that is easy for God.","They think the confederates have not gone. And if the confederates were to come, they would wish they were out in the desert among the nomads, asking for news of you. And had they been among you, they would have fought only a little.","Certainly in God’s Messenger you have had a fine example—for whoever hopes in God and the Last Day and remembers God often.","When the believers saw the confederates, they said, “This is what God and His Messenger promised us, and God and His Messenger spoke the truth.” It only increased them in faith and submission.","Among the believers are men who have been true to what they pledged to God. Some of them have fulfilled their vow, and some are still waiting, and they have not changed in the least.","So that God may recompense the truthful for their truthfulness and punish the hypocrites if He wills, or turn to them in mercy. Truly God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","God drove back those who disbelieved in their rage, having gained nothing. God spared the believers the fighting. God is All-Powerful, All-Mighty.","He brought down from their fortresses those of the People of the Book who had supported them and cast terror into their hearts—a group you killed and a group you took captive.","He made you inherit their land, their homes, their wealth, and a land you had never set foot on. God is Capable of all things.","O Prophet, say to your wives, “If you desire the life of this world and its adornment, then come, I will provide for you and release you with a gracious release.","But if you desire God and His Messenger and the Home of the Hereafter, then truly God has prepared for those of you who do good a magnificent reward.”","O wives of the Prophet, whoever among you commits a clear indecency, the punishment will be doubled for her twofold. And that is easy for God.","And whoever among you is devoutly obedient to God and His Messenger and does righteous deeds, We will give her her reward twice over, and We have prepared for her a generous provision.","O wives of the Prophet, you are not like any other women. If you are mindful, then do not be soft in speech, lest he in whose heart is disease should covet, and speak fitting words.","Settle in your homes and do not display yourselves as in the former time of ignorance. Establish prayer and give charity and obey God and His Messenger. God only wishes to remove defilement from you, O People of the Household, and to purify you completely.","And remember what is recited in your homes of God’s verses and wisdom. Truly God is the Subtle, the All-Aware.","Truly, the submitting men and submitting women, the believing men and believing women, the devout men and devout women, the truthful men and truthful women, the patient men and patient women, the humble men and humble women, the charitable men and charitable women, the fasting men and fasting women, the men who guard their chastity and the women who guard it, and the men who remember God often and the women who remember Him — God has prepared for them forgiveness and a great reward.","It is not for a believing man or a believing woman, when God and His Messenger have decided a matter, to have any choice in their affair. Whoever disobeys God and His Messenger has clearly gone astray.","When you said to the one whom God had blessed and whom you had blessed, “Keep your wife and be mindful of God,” you were concealing within yourself what God was going to reveal, and you feared the people, though God is more deserving of your fear. So when Zayd had no further need of her, We married her to you, so that there would be no difficulty for the believers regarding the wives of their adopted sons once they have no further need of them. And God’s command is always fulfilled.","There is no blame on the Prophet for what God has ordained for him — the way of God with those who passed before. And God’s command is a decree determined.","Those who deliver God’s messages and fear Him and fear no one but God. And God is sufficient as a Reckoner.","Muhammad is not the father of any of your men, but the Messenger of God and the seal of the prophets. And God is All-Knowing of all things.","O you who believe, remember God with much remembrance.","And glorify Him morning and evening.","It is He who blesses you, and His angels, to bring you out of darkness into light. And He is ever Merciful to the believers.","Their greeting on the Day they meet Him will be, “Peace.” And He has prepared for them a generous reward.","O Prophet, We have sent you as a witness, a bearer of good news, and a warner.","And a caller to God by His permission, and a radiant lamp.","And give the believers good news that they will have a great bounty from God.","And do not obey the disbelievers and the hypocrites, disregard their harm, and put your trust in God. And God is sufficient as a Guardian.","O you who believe, when you marry believing women and then divorce them before you have touched them, you have no waiting period to count against them. So provide for them and release them with a gracious release.","O Prophet, We have made lawful for you your wives whose dowries you have paid, and what your right hand possesses from what God has granted you, and the daughters of your paternal uncles and the daughters of your paternal aunts and the daughters of your maternal uncles and the daughters of your maternal aunts who emigrated with you, and a believing woman if she gives herself to the Prophet if the Prophet wishes to marry her — exclusively for you, not for the believers. We know what We have ordained for them regarding their wives and what their right hands possess, so that there be no difficulty upon you. God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","You may defer any of them you wish and take to yourself any of them you wish, and whoever you desire of those you had set aside, there is no blame on you. That is more likely to cool their eyes and that they not grieve and that they all be content with what you give them. God knows what is in your hearts. God is All-Knowing, All-Forbearing.","Women are not lawful for you after this, nor that you exchange them for other wives, even if their beauty pleases you — except what your right hand possesses. God is ever Watchful over all things.","O you who believe, do not enter the Prophet’s homes unless you are given permission for a meal, without waiting for its preparation. But when you are invited, enter, and when you have eaten, disperse and do not linger for conversation. That used to hurt the Prophet, and he would be shy of you, but God is not shy of the truth. When you ask his wives for something, ask them from behind a screen. That is purer for your hearts and their hearts. It is not for you to hurt God’s Messenger, nor to ever marry his wives after him. Truly, that would be enormous in God’s sight.","Whether you reveal something or conceal it, God is ever All-Knowing of all things.","There is no blame on them regarding their fathers, their sons, their brothers, their brothers’ sons, their sisters’ sons, their women, or what their right hands possess. And be mindful of God. God is ever Witness over all things.","God and His angels send blessings upon the Prophet. O you who believe, send blessings upon him and greet him with peace.","Those who hurt God and His Messenger — God has cursed them in this world and the Hereafter and has prepared for them a humiliating punishment.","Those who hurt believing men and believing women for what they have not earned have burdened themselves with slander and clear sin.","O Prophet, tell your wives, your daughters, and the women of the believers to draw their outer garments over themselves. That is more likely that they will be recognized and not harassed. And God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","If the hypocrites, those with sickness in their hearts, and the rumor-mongers in the city do not cease, We will surely incite you against them, and then they will not remain your neighbors there except briefly.","Cursed, wherever they are found they will be seized and killed outright.","God’s way with those who passed before, and you will never find any change in God’s way.","People ask you about the Hour. Say, “Its knowledge is only with God.” And what would make you know? Perhaps the Hour is near.","Truly God has cursed the disbelievers and prepared for them a Blaze.","Dwelling in it forever. They will find no protector and no helper.","The Day their faces are turned over in the Fire, they will say, “If only we had obeyed God and obeyed the Messenger!”","And they will say, “Our Lord, we obeyed our masters and our elders, and they led us astray from the path.","Our Lord, give them double the punishment and curse them with a mighty curse.”","O you who believe, do not be like those who harassed Moses—God cleared him of what they said, and he was honored in God’s sight.","O you who believe, be mindful of God and speak words that are upright.","He will set right your deeds for you and forgive your sins. Whoever obeys God and His Messenger has truly achieved a great triumph.","We offered the trust to the heavens, the earth, and the mountains, but they refused to bear it and shrank from it—yet the human being bore it. He was truly most wrongdoing, most ignorant.","So that God may punish the hypocrite men and hypocrite women, and the polytheist men and polytheist women, and so that God may turn in mercy to the believing men and believing women. And God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","All praise belongs to God, to whom belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth, and to Him belongs all praise in the Hereafter. He is the All-Wise, the All-Aware.","He knows what penetrates into the earth and what comes out of it, what descends from the sky and what ascends into it. He is the Most Merciful, the All-Forgiving.","Those who disbelieved said, “The Hour will not come upon us.” Say, “Yes, by my Lord, it will surely come upon you — the Knower of the unseen. Not an atom’s weight in the heavens or on the earth escapes Him, nor anything smaller than that or greater, except that it is in a clear record.”","So that He may reward those who believed and did righteous deeds. For them is forgiveness and a generous provision.","But those who strove against Our verses, seeking to undermine them — for them is a punishment of painful torment.","Those given knowledge see that what has been sent down to you from your Lord is the truth, and it guides to the path of the Almighty, the Praiseworthy.","Those who disbelieved said, “Shall we point you to a man who tells you that when you have been utterly torn to pieces, you will be in a new creation?","Has he fabricated a lie against God, or is there madness in him?” Rather, those who do not believe in the Hereafter are in the punishment and the far-gone error.","Have they not looked at what is before them and behind them of the sky and the earth? If We willed, We could cause the earth to swallow them or drop fragments of the sky upon them. Surely in that is a sign for every servant who turns back to God.","We certainly granted David favor from Us: “O mountains, echo praises with him, and the birds as well.” And We made iron soft for him.","“Fashion full coats of armor and measure the links precisely.” And do righteous deeds. Truly I am All-Seeing of what you do.","And to Solomon We subjected the wind — its morning course was a month’s journey and its evening course was a month’s journey. We made a spring of molten copper flow for him. And among the jinn were those who worked before him by his Lord’s permission, and whoever of them deviated from Our command, We made him taste the punishment of the Blaze.","They made for him whatever he wished of sanctuaries, statues, basins like reservoirs, and firmly set cauldrons. “Work in gratitude, O family of David.” Yet few of My servants are truly grateful.","When We decreed death upon him, nothing alerted them to his death except a creature of the earth eating away at his staff. So when he collapsed, the jinn realized that had they known the unseen, they would not have remained in the humiliating punishment.","Truly, there was a sign for Sheba in their homeland: two gardens, one to the right and one to the left. “Eat from your Lord’s provision and give thanks to Him. A good land and a Forgiving Lord.”","But they turned away, so We sent against them the flood of the dam and replaced their two gardens with two gardens bearing bitter fruit, tamarisk, and a few lote trees.","That is how We repaid them for their ingratitude. Do We ever repay anyone but the ungrateful?","We placed between them and the towns We had blessed visible towns, and We measured out the journey between them. “Travel through them by night and day in safety.”","But they said, “Our Lord, lengthen the distances between our journeys.” They wronged themselves, so We made them tales and tore them to utter shreds. Surely in that are signs for everyone who is patient and grateful.","Iblis certainly proved his assumption about them true, and they followed him—all except a group of the believers.","Yet he had no authority over them, except that We might distinguish those who believe in the Hereafter from those who are in doubt about it. Your Lord is Guardian over all things.","Say, “Call upon those you claimed besides God. They do not possess an atom’s weight in the heavens or on earth, nor do they have any share in either, nor does He have any supporter among them.”","Intercession does not benefit before Him except for those He permits. Until, when terror is lifted from their hearts, they say, “What did your Lord say?” They say, “The truth.” He is the Most High, the Most Great.","Say, “Who provides for you from the heavens and the earth?” Say, “God. And surely either we or you are upon guidance or in clear misguidance.”","Say, “You will not be asked about our sins, nor will we be asked about what you do.”","Say, “Our Lord will gather us together, then He will judge between us in truth. He is the Judge, the All-Knowing.”","Say, “Show me those you have attached to Him as partners.” No! Rather, He is God, the All-Mighty, the All-Wise.","We have not sent you except to all of humanity as a bearer of good news and a warner, but most people do not know.","They say, “When will this promise come to pass, if you are truthful?”","Say, “You have an appointment on a Day you cannot delay by a single hour, nor advance.”","Those who disbelieved said, “We will never believe in this Quran, nor in what came before it.” If only you could see when the wrongdoers are made to stand before their Lord, hurling words back at one another. Those who were oppressed say to those who were arrogant, “Had it not been for you, we would have been believers.”","Those who were arrogant say to those who were oppressed, “Did we turn you away from guidance after it came to you? No, you were criminals.”","Those who were oppressed say to those who were arrogant, “Rather, it was your scheming by night and day, when you commanded us to disbelieve in God and set up rivals to Him.” They conceal their regret when they see the punishment. We place shackles around the necks of those who disbelieved. Are they repaid for anything but what they used to do?","Never did We send a warner to any town without its affluent ones saying, “We disbelieve in what you have been sent with.”","They said, “We have more wealth and children, and we will not be punished.”","Say, “Truly, my Lord extends provision to whom He wills and restricts it, but most people do not know.”","It is not your wealth or your children that bring you closer to Us, but whoever believes and does good — for them is a multiplied recompense for what they did, and they will be secure in the lofty chambers.","Those who strive against Our verses, seeking to undermine them — they will be brought into the punishment.","Say, “Truly, my Lord extends provision to whom He wills of His servants and restricts it for him. Whatever you spend, He will replace it. He is the Best of Providers.”","On the Day He gathers them all together, then says to the angels, “Was it you these people used to worship?”","They say, “Glory be to You! You are our Protector, not them. Rather, they used to worship the jinn — most of them believed in them.”","So today none of you holds any power to benefit or harm another. We say to those who wronged, “Taste the punishment of the Fire that you used to deny.”","When Our clear verses are recited to them, they say, “This is nothing but a man who wants to turn you away from what your fathers used to worship.” They say, “This is nothing but a fabricated lie.” And those who disbelieved say of the truth when it comes to them, “This is nothing but plain sorcery.”","We gave them no scriptures to study, and We sent them no warner before you.","Those before them denied, and these have not reached a tenth of what We gave them. They denied My messengers — so how was My reproach?","Say, “I advise you of one thing only: that you stand before God, in pairs and alone, then reflect. Your companion has no madness in him. He is only a warner to you before a severe punishment.”","Say, “Whatever payment I may have asked of you, it is yours. My payment comes only from God, and He is Witness over all things.”","Say, “Truly, my Lord hurls the truth — the Knower of all that is unseen.”","Say, “The truth has come, and falsehood can neither originate nor restore.”","Say, “If I stray, I stray only against my own soul. And if I am guided, it is by what my Lord reveals to me. He is All-Hearing, Ever Near.”","If you could see when they are stricken with terror — no escape — and they are seized from a place nearby!","They will say, “We believe in it!” But how can they reach it from so far away?","They had already rejected it before, casting at the unseen from a distant place.","A barrier is placed between them and what they desire, just as was done with their kind before them. They were in grave doubt.","All praise belongs to God, Originator of the heavens and the earth, who made the angels messengers with wings in pairs, threes, and fours. He adds to creation whatever He wills. Truly, God is Capable of all things.","Whatever mercy God opens for people, none can withhold it, and whatever He withholds, none can release it after Him. He is the All-Mighty, the All-Wise.","O people, remember God’s blessing upon you. Is there any creator other than God who provides for you from the sky and the earth? There is no god but Him. So how are you deluded?","If they deny you, messengers before you were denied. And to God all matters are returned.","O people, God’s promise is true. So do not let the life of this world deceive you, and do not let the Deceiver deceive you about God.","Satan is an enemy to you, so treat him as an enemy. He only invites his followers to become companions of the Blaze.","Those who disbelieve will have a severe punishment, and those who believe and do righteous deeds will have forgiveness and a great reward.","Is the one whose evil deeds are made appealing to him so that he sees them as good? For God leads astray whoever He wills and guides whoever He wills. So do not let your soul perish over them in grief. Surely God is All-Knowing of what they do.","God is the One who sends the winds, and they stir up clouds, and We drive them to a dead land and revive the earth with it after its death. Such is the resurrection.","Whoever seeks glory — all glory belongs to God. To Him good words ascend, and righteous deeds elevate it. Those who plot evil will have a severe punishment, and the plotting of those will come to nothing.","God created you from dust, then from a drop, then made you pairs. No female conceives or delivers except with His knowledge. No one granted long life has years added, nor has any taken from his life, except that it is in a record. Truly, that is easy for God.","The two seas are not alike: this one is fresh, sweet, pleasant to drink, and that one is salty, bitter. Yet from each you eat fresh meat and extract ornaments you wear. And you see ships plowing through it, so that you may seek His bounty, and so that you may be grateful.","He merges the night into the day and merges the day into the night, and He subjected the sun and the moon, each running for an appointed term. That is God, your Lord — to Him belongs the dominion. And those you call upon besides Him do not possess even the membrane of a date seed.","If you call upon them, they do not hear your call, and even if they heard, they would not respond to you. On the Day of Resurrection they will deny your association of them. And none can inform you like One who is All-Aware.","O people, you are the ones in need of God, and God — He is the Self-Sufficient, the Praiseworthy.","If He wills, He can do away with you and bring a new creation.","That is not difficult for God.","No bearer of burdens bears the burden of another. And if a heavily laden soul calls for help with its load, none of it will be carried, even by a close relative. You can only warn those who fear their Lord in the unseen and establish prayer. Whoever purifies himself purifies himself for his own self. To God is the final return.","The blind and the seeing are not equal.","Nor are darkness and light.","Nor are shade and scorching heat.","The living and the dead are not equal. God makes whoever He wills hear, and you cannot make those in the graves hear.","You are only a warner.","We have sent you with the truth as a bearer of good news and a warner. There is no community but a warner has passed among it.","If they deny you, those before them also denied. Their messengers came to them with clear proofs, with scriptures, and with the illuminating Book.","Then I seized those who disbelieved — so how was My rejection?","Do you not see that God sent down water from the sky, and We brought out with it fruits of varying colors? And among the mountains are streaks of white and red, of varying colors, and pitch-black.","And among people, creatures, and livestock are likewise varying colors. Only those with knowledge among His servants truly fear God. Surely God is All-Mighty, All-Forgiving.","Those who recite God’s Book, establish prayer, and spend from what We have provided them, secretly and openly, hope for a trade that will never fail.","So that He may pay them their rewards in full and increase them from His grace. Truly He is All-Forgiving, Most Appreciative.","What We have revealed to you of the Book is the truth, confirming what came before it. Surely God is All-Aware, All-Seeing of His servants.","Then We passed the Book on to those We chose from Our servants. Among them is one who wrongs himself, among them is one who is moderate, and among them is one who races ahead in good deeds by God’s permission. That is the great grace.","Gardens of eternity they will enter, adorned there with bracelets of gold and pearls, and their clothing there is silk.","They will say, “All praise is for God, who has removed grief from us. Truly our Lord is All-Forgiving, Most Appreciative.","He who has settled us in the Abode of Permanence out of His grace. No weariness touches us there, and no fatigue touches us there.”","As for those who disbelieve, for them is the fire of Hell. They are not sentenced to death so they could die, nor is its torment lightened for them. Thus We recompense every ungrateful denier.","They will cry out there, “Our Lord, take us out! We will do good, other than what we used to do.” Did We not give you lives long enough for whoever would reflect to reflect? And the warner came to you. So taste, for the wrongdoers have no helper.","Truly, God is the Knower of the unseen of the heavens and the earth. He is All-Knowing of what is within the hearts.","It is He who made you successors on the earth. So whoever disbelieves, his disbelief is upon him. And their disbelief only increases the disbelievers in loathing before their Lord. And their disbelief only increases the disbelievers in loss.","Say, “Have you considered your partners whom you call upon besides God? Show me what they have created of the earth. Or do they have a share in the heavens? Or have We given them a book so they stand on clear proof from it? No, the wrongdoers promise one another nothing but delusion.”","Surely, God holds the heavens and the earth lest they slip away. And if they were to slip away, no one could hold them after Him. He is ever Forbearing, All-Forgiving.","They swore by God their most solemn oaths that if a warner came to them, they would be more guided than any other nation. But when a warner came to them, it only increased them in aversion.","Arrogance in the land and evil scheming. But evil scheming engulfs none but its own people. So do they await anything but the way of the ancients? You will never find any change in God’s way, and you will never find any alteration in God’s way.","Have they not traveled through the land and seen how the end was for those before them, though they were mightier than them in strength? Nothing in the heavens or the earth can escape God. He is ever All-Knowing, All-Powerful.","If God were to hold people accountable for what they have earned, He would not leave a single creature on its surface. But He defers them to an appointed term. And when their term comes, then truly God is ever All-Seeing of His servants.","Ya Sin.","By the Wise Quran.","You are truly among the messengers.","On a straight path.","A revelation from the Almighty, the Most Merciful.","To warn a people whose fathers were not warned, so they are heedless.","Certainly the word has proved true against most of them, so they do not believe.","We have placed shackles on their necks, reaching up to their chins, so their heads are forced up.","And We have placed a barrier before them and a barrier behind them and covered them, so they cannot see.","It is the same to them whether you warn them or do not warn them — they will not believe.","You can only warn one who follows the Reminder and fears the Most Merciful in the unseen. So give him glad tidings of forgiveness and a generous reward.","It is We who give life to the dead and record what they have sent ahead and their traces. And everything We have counted in a clear record.","Set before them the example of the people of the town, when the messengers came to it.","When We sent two to them and they rejected them both, so We reinforced them with a third, and they said, “We are messengers sent to you.”","They said, “You are nothing but humans like us, and the Most Merciful has not sent down anything. You are only lying.”","They said, “Our Lord knows that we are truly messengers sent to you.","And our duty is only the clear delivery.”","They said, “We see an evil omen in you. If you do not stop, we will surely stone you, and a painful punishment from us will surely touch you.”","They said, “Your evil omen is with you. Is it because you were reminded? Rather, you are a transgressing people.”","And a man came running from the farthest end of the city. He said, “O my people, follow the messengers.","Follow those who ask no payment of you, and they are rightly guided.”","“Why would I not worship Him who created me, and to Him you will be returned?","Should I take gods besides Him? If the Most Merciful intends me harm, their intercession will avail me nothing, nor will they rescue me.","Truly, I would then be in clear error.","I believe in your Lord, so hear me!”","He was told, “Enter Paradise.” He said, “If only my people knew.","How my Lord has forgiven me and placed me among the honored!”","We did not send down upon his people after him any army from the sky, nor would We ever send one down.","It was only a single blast, and at once they were extinguished.","O what grief over these servants! No messenger ever came to them but they mocked him.","Have they not seen how many generations We destroyed before them, that none of them will return to them?","Yet all of them, gathered together, will be brought before Us.","A sign for them is the dead earth — We gave it life and brought grain from it, and from it they eat.","We placed in it gardens of palms and grapevines, and We caused springs to gush from it.","So they may eat of its fruit — and their hands did not make it. Will they not then be grateful?","Glory be to Him who created all pairs — from what the earth grows, from themselves, and from what they do not know.","A sign for them is the night: We strip the daylight from it, and suddenly they are in darkness.","The sun runs to a resting place appointed for it. That is the decree of the All-Mighty, the All-Knowing.","The moon — We determined for it phases, until it returns like an old date-stalk.","The sun may not overtake the moon, nor may the night outpace the day. Each floats in an orbit.","A sign for them is that We carried their offspring in the laden ship.","And We created for them the like of it, which they ride.","And if We will, We drown them — then there is no one to cry to for help, nor are they rescued.","Except by mercy from Us and as provision for a time.","When they are told, “Be mindful of what is before you and what is behind you, so that you may be shown mercy.”","Not a single sign of their Lord’s signs comes to them but they turn away from it.","When they are told, “Spend from what God has provided you,” those who disbelieve say to those who believe, “Should we feed someone whom, if God willed, He would have fed? You are clearly astray.”","They say, “When will this promise come, if you are truthful?”","They await nothing but a single blast that will seize them while they are still disputing.","They will not be able to leave a will, nor will they return to their families.","The horn will be blown, and at once they will rush from the graves to their Lord.","They will say, “Woe to us! Who has raised us from our resting place?” “This is what the Most Merciful promised, and the messengers spoke the truth.”","It will be but a single blast, and at once they will all be brought before Us.","So today no soul will be wronged in the least, and you will only be repaid for what you used to do.","Truly the people of Paradise are busy today in joyful delight.","They and their spouses, reclining on couches in shaded groves.","They have fruit therein, and they have whatever they desire.","“Peace” — a word from a Merciful Lord.","“Stand apart today, O criminals!”","“Did I not command you, O Children of Adam, not to worship Satan? He is a clear enemy to you.","And worship Me — this is a straight path.","He has led astray vast multitudes of you. Did you not reason?","This is Hell, which you were promised.","Burn in it today for what you used to deny.”","Today We seal their mouths, and their hands speak to Us, and their feet bear witness to what they used to earn.","If We willed, We could have blotted out their eyes, and they would race toward the path — but how would they see?","If We willed, We could have paralyzed them in their place, and they could neither move forward nor turn back.","Whoever We grant long life, We reverse him in creation. Do they not reason?","We did not teach him poetry, nor would it befit him. It is only a reminder and a clear Quran.","To warn whoever is alive, and that the word may be justified against the disbelievers.","Do they not see that We created for them, from what Our hands have made, livestock, and they are their owners?","And We tamed them for them — some they ride, and some they eat.","And in them they have benefits and drinks. Will they not be grateful?","Yet they have taken gods besides God, hoping they might be helped.","They cannot help them, though they stand as soldiers marshaled before them.","So let their words not grieve you. Truly We know what they conceal and what they declare.","Does man not see that We created him from a drop of fluid? Yet there he is — an open adversary!","He strikes a likeness for Us and forgets his own creation. He says, “Who will give life to bones when they are decayed?”","Say, “He who produced them the first time will give them life. He is All-Knowing of every creation.","He who made for you fire from the green tree, and from it you kindle.","Is not He who created the heavens and the earth Capable of creating the likes of them? Yes indeed, and He is the Supreme Creator, the All-Knowing.","His command, when He wills a thing, is only to say to it ‘Be,’ and it is.”","So glory be to Him in whose hand is the dominion of all things, and to Him you will be returned.","By those lined up in rows.","And those who drive with force.","And those who recite a reminder.","Truly your God is One.","Lord of the heavens and the earth and all between them, and Lord of the easts.","We adorned the nearest heaven with the beauty of the stars.","And as a guard against every rebellious devil.","They cannot listen to the highest assembly and are pelted from every side.","Driven away—and for them is a lasting punishment.","Except one who snatches by stealth, and a piercing flame pursues him.","So ask them: are they harder to create, or those We have created? We created them from sticky clay.","Rather, you are amazed while they mock.","When they are reminded, they do not remember.","When they see a sign, they ridicule it.","And they say, “This is nothing but plain sorcery.","When we have died and become dust and bones, will we really be resurrected?","And our forefathers too?”","Say, “Yes, and you will be humiliated.”","It will be but a single blast, and at once they will be looking on.","And they will say, “Woe to us! This is the Day of Recompense.”","“This is the Day of Separation that you used to deny.","Gather those who wronged, and their kinds, and what they used to worship.","Besides God, and guide them to the path of the Blaze.”","“But stop them—they are to be questioned.”","“What is wrong with you that you do not help one another?”","No, today they are in full surrender.","They turned to one another, questioning each other.","They said, “You used to come at us from the right.”","They replied, “Rather, you yourselves were not believers.","We had no authority over you. Rather, you were a transgressing people.","So our Lord’s word has come due upon us. We will surely taste it.","We led you astray because we ourselves were astray.”","So on that Day they will all share in the punishment.","That is how We deal with the criminals.","Whenever they were told, “There is no god but God,” they grew arrogant.","And they would say, “Are we to abandon our gods for a mad poet?”","Rather, he came with the truth and confirmed the messengers.","You will surely taste the painful punishment.","You are only repaid for what you used to do.","Except God’s devoted servants.","For them there is a known provision.","Fruits—and they will be honored.","In Gardens of Bliss.","On couches, facing one another.","A cup from a flowing spring will be passed around to them.","White, delicious to the drinkers.","No headache from it, nor will they be intoxicated by it.","And with them will be women of modest gaze, with large eyes.","As if they were sheltered eggs.","They will turn to one another, questioning each other.","One of them said, “I had a companion.","Who used to say, ‘Are you really among those who believe?","When we have died and become dust and bones, will we truly be judged?’”","He said, “Will you look down?”","So he looked down and saw him in the midst of the Blazing Fire.","He said, “By God, you nearly ruined me!","Had it not been for my Lord’s grace, I would have been among those brought there.","Are we then not to die.","Except our first death, and we will not be punished?”","Truly, this is the supreme triumph.","For the like of this, let the workers work.","Is that a better welcome, or the tree of Zaqqum?","We made it a trial for the wrongdoers.","It is a tree that grows from the bottom of the Blazing Fire.","Its fruit-clusters are like the heads of devils.","They will eat from it and fill their bellies with it.","Then on top of it they will have a brew of scalding water.","Then their return is surely to the Blazing Fire.","They found their fathers astray.","So they rushed in their footsteps.","And before them, most of the ancients went astray.","And We had sent warners among them.","So look how those who were warned ended up.","Except God’s devoted servants.","Noah called out to Us, and how excellent are We in answering!","We saved him and his family from the great distress.","We made his descendants the survivors.","And We left for him among later generations.","“Peace be upon Noah among all peoples.”","Thus do We recompense those who do good.","He was among Our believing servants.","Then We drowned the others.","And among his followers was Abraham.","When he came to his Lord with a sound heart.","When he said to his father and his people, “What are you worshiping?","Is it false gods besides God that you desire?","So what do you think of the Lord of all peoples?”","Then he cast a glance at the stars.","And said, “I am feeling ill.”","So they turned away from him, departing.","Then he crept toward their gods and said, “Will you not eat?","What is wrong with you that you do not speak?”","Then he turned on them, striking with his right hand.","So they came rushing toward him.","He said, “Do you worship what you carve.","When God created you and what you make?”","They said, “Build him a structure and cast him into the fire!”","They plotted against him, but We made them the lowest.","And he said, “I am going to my Lord; He will guide me.","My Lord, grant me a righteous child.”","So We gave him glad tidings of a forbearing boy.","When he was old enough to work alongside him, he said, “O my son, I see in a dream that I am slaughtering you, so consider what you think.” He said, “O my father, do what you are commanded. You will find me, if God wills, among the patient.”","When they had both submitted and he laid him down on his forehead.","We called out to him, “O Abraham.","You have fulfilled the vision.” Truly, this is how We recompense the doers of good.","This was certainly the clear trial.","And We ransomed him with a great sacrifice.","And We left for him among later generations.","“Peace be upon Abraham.”","This is how We recompense the doers of good.","He was truly one of Our believing servants.","And We gave him glad tidings of Isaac, a prophet among the righteous.","And We blessed him and Isaac. Among their descendants are doers of good and those clearly wronging themselves.","And We certainly bestowed favor upon Moses and Aaron.","And We saved them both and their people from the great affliction.","And We helped them, so they were the victors.","And We gave them both the clarifying Scripture.","And We guided them both to the straight path.","And We left for them among later generations.","“Peace be upon Moses and Aaron.”","Truly, this is how We recompense the doers of good.","They were both among Our believing servants.","And Elias was certainly one of the messengers.","When he said to his people, “Will you not be mindful?","Do you call upon Baal and abandon the Best of Creators?","God, your Lord and the Lord of your earliest forefathers?”","But they denied him, so they will surely be brought to judgment.","Except God’s devoted servants.","And We left for him among later generations.","“Peace be upon the family of Elias.”","Truly, this is how We recompense the doers of good.","He was one of Our believing servants.","And Lot was certainly one of the messengers.","When We saved him and his family, all of them.","Except an old woman among those who stayed behind.","Then We destroyed the others.","You pass by them in the morning.","And at night. Will you not reason?","And Jonah was certainly one of the messengers.","When he fled to the laden ship.","He drew lots and was among the losers.","So the whale swallowed him, and he was blameworthy.","Had he not been among those who glorified God.","He would have remained in its belly until the Day they are resurrected.","So We cast him onto the barren shore, and he was ill.","And We grew over him a gourd plant.","And We sent him to a hundred thousand or more.","They believed, so We let them enjoy life for a time.","So ask them: does your Lord have daughters while they have sons?","Or did We create the angels female while they witnessed?","Surely it is out of their own fabrication that they say.","“God has begotten,” and they are certainly liars.","Did He choose daughters over sons?","What is wrong with you? How do you judge?","Will you not reflect?","Or do you have a clear authority?","Then bring your scripture, if you are truthful.","They have claimed a kinship between Him and the jinn, yet the jinn know well that they will be brought forth.","Glory be to God, far above what they ascribe to Him.","But not God’s devoted servants.","So you and what you worship.","You cannot lure anyone away from Him.","Except one who is bound for the Blaze.","“There is not one among us except that he has an appointed station.","And we are truly those lined up in ranks.","And we are truly those who glorify.”","They used to say.","“If only we had a reminder from the ancients.","We would surely have been God’s devoted servants.”","Yet they disbelieved in it, and soon they will know.","Our word has already gone to Our servants, the messengers.","They will certainly be aided.","And Our forces will certainly be the victors.","So turn away from them for a time.","And watch them, for they will soon see.","Is it Our punishment they seek to hasten?","When it descends upon their courtyard, how wretched will be the morning of those who were warned.","And turn away from them for a time.","And watch, for they will soon see.","Glory be to your Lord, the Lord of Might, far above what they ascribe.","And peace be upon the messengers.","And all praise belongs to God, Lord of all worlds.","Sad. By the Quran, full of remembrance.","But those who disbelieve are steeped in arrogance and opposition.","How many a generation We destroyed before them! They cried out, but it was too late to escape.","They were astonished that a warner came to them from among themselves, and the disbelievers said, “This is a sorcerer, a liar.","Has he made the gods into one God? Truly, this is an astonishing thing!”","The chiefs among them went off saying, “Walk away and hold firm to your gods. This is certainly something intended.","We never heard of this in the last religion. This is nothing but a fabrication.","Was the reminder sent down to him alone out of all of us?” Rather, they are in doubt about My reminder. Rather, they have not yet tasted My punishment.","Or do they possess the treasuries of your Lord’s mercy, the Almighty, the Ever-Giving?","Or do they have the dominion of the heavens and the earth and everything between them? Then let them climb the pathways.","A defeated host they are there, among the factions.","Before them, the people of Noah denied, and Aad, and Pharaoh of the stakes.","And Thamud, and the people of Lot, and the companions of the Thicket. Those were the factions.","Every one of them denied the messengers, so My punishment was justified.","These await nothing but a single blast with no pause.","They said, “Our Lord, hasten for us our share before the Day of Reckoning.”","Be patient over what they say, and remember Our servant David, the one of strength. Truly, he was ever turning back.","We subjected the mountains to glorify with him at evening and sunrise.","And the birds, gathered — all turning back to him.","We strengthened his kingdom and gave him wisdom and decisive speech.","Has the account of the disputants reached you, when they scaled the sanctuary?","When they entered upon David and he was alarmed by them, they said, “Do not fear. We are two disputants — one of us has wronged the other. So judge between us in truth and do not be unjust, and guide us to the right path.”","“This is my brother. He has ninety-nine ewes, and I have one ewe. He said, ‘Entrust her to me,’ and he overpowered me in argument.”","He said, “He has certainly wronged you by asking for your ewe to add to his ewes. Surely many partners wrong one another — except those who believe and do righteous deeds, and how few they are.” And David realized that We had tested him, so he asked his Lord for forgiveness and fell down bowing and turned back in repentance.","So We forgave him that. Certainly, he has nearness to Us and a beautiful return.","O David, We have made you a successor on the earth, so judge between people in truth and do not follow desire, lest it lead you astray from God’s path. Those who stray from God’s path — for them is a severe punishment because they forgot the Day of Reckoning.","We did not create the heaven and the earth and what is between them in vain. That is the assumption of those who disbelieve. So woe to those who disbelieve from the Fire.","Or should We treat those who believe and do righteous deeds like the corrupters on earth? Or should We treat the God-conscious like the wicked?","A blessed Book We have sent down to you, so that they may reflect upon its verses and so that people of understanding may be reminded.","We granted David Solomon. What an excellent servant — he was ever turning back to God.","When the fine, standing steeds were paraded before him in the evening.","He said, “I have loved the love of good things over the remembrance of my Lord, until it disappeared behind the veil.","Bring them back to me.” Then he began stroking their legs and necks.","Certainly We tested Solomon and cast upon his throne a lifeless body, then he turned back.","He said, “My Lord, forgive me and grant me a kingdom that will not belong to anyone after me. Truly, You are the Bestower.”","So We subjected the wind to him, blowing gently by his command wherever he directed.","And the devils — every builder and diver.","And others bound together in chains.","“This is Our gift, so give freely or withhold, without account.”","Truly, he has nearness to Us and a beautiful return.","And remember Our servant Job, when he called out to his Lord, “Satan has afflicted me with hardship and suffering.”","“Strike the ground with your foot — here is a cool wash and a drink.”","We restored his family to him, and the like of them with them, as a mercy from Us and a reminder for people of understanding.","“Take in your hand a bundle of grass and strike with it, and do not break your oath.” We found him patient. What an excellent servant — he was ever turning back to God.","And remember Our servants Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob — possessors of strength and vision.","We purified them with a pure quality: remembrance of the Hereafter.","They are, in Our sight, truly among the chosen, the finest.","And remember Ishmael, Elisha, and Dhul-Kifl — each was among the finest.","This is a reminder. And surely the reverent will have a beautiful return.","Gardens of eternity, their gates flung open to them.","Reclining therein, calling for abundant fruit and drink.","And beside them, companions of modest gaze, all of equal age.","This is what you are promised for the Day of Reckoning.","Surely this is Our provision, never to be exhausted.","So it is. But the transgressors will have the worst return.","Hell, where they will burn. What a wretched resting place!","This — let them taste it: scalding water and foul discharge.","And other torments of its kind, in pairs.","“Here is a crowd plunging in with you. No welcome for them — they will burn in the Fire.”","They said, “No, it is you who deserve no welcome. You brought this upon us. What a wretched abode!”","They said, “Our Lord, whoever brought this upon us — double his punishment in the Fire.”","And they said, “Why do we not see men we used to count among the wicked?","Did we take them in mockery, or have our eyes missed them?”","Surely that is true — the quarreling of the people of the Fire.","Say, “I am only a warner, and there is no god but God, the One, the Vanquisher.","Lord of the heavens and the earth and all that is between them, the All-Mighty, the Ever-Forgiving.”","Say, “It is a mighty tiding.","From which you turn away.","I had no knowledge of the highest assembly when they disputed.","It is only revealed to me that I am a clear warner.”","When your Lord said to the angels, “I am creating a human being from clay.","So when I have shaped him and breathed into him of My spirit, fall down before him in prostration.”","So the angels prostrated, all of them together.","Except Iblis. He was arrogant and was among the disbelievers.","He said, “O Iblis, what prevented you from prostrating to what I created with My own hands? Were you arrogant, or are you among the exalted?”","He said, “I am better than him. You created me from fire and created him from clay.”","He said, “Then get out of it, for you are accursed.","And upon you is My curse until the Day of Judgment.”","He said, “My Lord, then grant me respite until the Day they are resurrected.”","He said, “You are among those granted respite.","Until the Day of the appointed time.”","He said, “Then by Your might, I will surely lead them all astray.","Except Your servants among them, the sincere ones.”","He said, “The truth it is, and the truth I speak.","I will surely fill Hell with you and with whoever follows you among them, all together.”","Say, “I ask you no payment for it, and I am not one of the pretenders.","It is nothing but a reminder to all the worlds.","And you will surely know its tiding after a time.”","The revelation of the Book is from God, the All-Mighty, the All-Wise.","Truly, We have sent down the Book to you in truth, so worship God, devoting your religion sincerely to Him.","Surely, to God belongs sincere religion. And those who take protectors besides Him say, “We only worship them so they may bring us closer to God.” God will judge between them regarding what they differ over. God does not guide one who is a liar, an ingrate.","Had God wished to take a son, He would have chosen whatever He willed from what He creates. Glory be to Him! He is God, the One, the Vanquisher.","He created the heavens and the earth in truth. He wraps the night over the day and wraps the day over the night. He subjected the sun and the moon, each running for an appointed term. Surely, He is the All-Mighty, the All-Forgiving.","He created you from a single soul, then made from it its mate, and sent down for you eight pairs of livestock. He creates you in your mothers’ bellies, creation after creation, in three darknesses. That is God, your Lord — to Him belongs the dominion. There is no god but Him. So how are you turned away?","If you disbelieve, God is truly free of need of you, yet He is not pleased with disbelief for His servants. And if you give thanks, He is pleased with it for you. No bearer of burdens bears the burden of another. Then to your Lord is your return, and He will inform you of what you used to do. He is All-Knowing of what is within the chests.","When hardship touches a person, he calls upon his Lord, turning to Him. Then when He grants him a blessing from Himself, he forgets what he used to call upon before and sets up rivals to God to lead others astray from His path. Say, “Enjoy your disbelief for a little while — you are among the companions of the Fire.”","Is one who is devoutly obedient during the hours of the night, prostrating and standing, fearing the Hereafter and hoping for his Lord’s mercy? Say, “Are those who know equal to those who do not know?” Only people of understanding take heed.","Say, “O My servants who believe, be mindful of your Lord. For those who do good in this world is good. And God’s earth is vast. The patient will be paid their reward without limit.”","Say, “I have been commanded to worship God, devoting my religion sincerely to Him.","And I have been commanded to be the first of those who submit.”","Say, “I fear, if I disobey my Lord, the punishment of a tremendous Day.”","Say, “It is God I worship, devoting my religion sincerely to Him.”","So worship whatever you wish besides Him. Say, “The losers are those who lose themselves and their families on the Day of Resurrection.” Surely, that is the clear loss.","Above them are canopies of Fire, and beneath them canopies. That is what God uses to frighten His servants. O My servants, be mindful of Me.","Those who shunned false gods and refused to worship them and turned back to God — for them is glad tidings. So give glad tidings to My servants.","Those who listen to what is said and follow the best of it. Those are the ones God has guided, and those are the people of understanding.","Is the one upon whom the word of punishment has been justified — can you rescue the one in the Fire?","But those who were mindful of their Lord will have lofty chambers, above which are lofty chambers built high, beneath which rivers flow. God’s promise — God never breaks His promise.","Do you not see that God sent down water from the sky and channeled it into springs in the earth, then brings out with it crops of varying colors, then they wither and you see them turn yellow, then He makes them crumble? Surely in that is a reminder for people of understanding.","Is the one whose chest God has opened to submission, so that he is upon a light from his Lord — then woe to those whose hearts are hardened against the remembrance of God. Those are in clear misguidance.","God has sent down the best of speech: a Book, consistent, paired in its passages. The skins of those who fear their Lord shiver from it, then their skins and their hearts soften to the remembrance of God. That is God’s guidance — He guides with it whoever He wills. And whoever God leaves astray, for him there is no guide.","Is the one who shields his face from the worst of the punishment on the Day of Resurrection — the wrongdoers are told, “Taste what you used to earn.”","Those before them denied, and the punishment came upon them from where they did not perceive.","So God made them taste disgrace in the life of this world, and the punishment of the Hereafter is far greater — if only they knew.","We have struck for people in this Quran every kind of example, so that they might reflect.","An Arabic Quran, without any crookedness, so that they might be mindful.","God strikes an example: a man shared by quarreling partners, and a man belonging wholly to one man — are the two equal in comparison? All praise belongs to God. But most of them do not know.","You will die, and they will die.","Then on the Day of Resurrection, before your Lord, you will dispute with one another.","Who is more unjust than one who lies about God and denies the truth when it comes to him? Is there not in Hell a dwelling for the disbelievers?","But the one who brought the truth and the one who believed in it—those are the righteous.","They will have whatever they wish with their Lord. That is the recompense of those who do good.","So that God may absolve them of the worst of what they did and repay them their reward for the best of what they used to do.","Is God not sufficient for His servant? Yet they frighten you with those besides Him. Whoever God leads astray, there is no guide for him.","And whoever God guides, there is none to lead him astray. Is God not Almighty, Possessor of retribution?","If you asked them, “Who created the heavens and the earth?” they would surely say, “God.” Say, “Have you considered what you invoke besides God—if God intended harm for me, could they remove His harm? Or if He intended mercy for me, could they withhold His mercy?” Say, “God is enough for me. In Him the trusting place their trust.”","Say, “O my people, act according to your position—I am acting. Soon you will know.","Who will receive a punishment that disgraces him, and upon whom a lasting punishment will descend.”","Truly, We sent down the Book to you for mankind in truth. Whoever is guided, it is for his own soul, and whoever goes astray, he only strays against it. You are not a guardian over them.","God takes the souls at the time of their death, and those that have not died, during their sleep. He keeps those upon which He has decreed death and releases the others until an appointed term. Surely in that are signs for people who reflect.","Or have they taken intercessors besides God? Say, “Even though they possess nothing and have no understanding?”","Say, “All intercession belongs to God. His is the dominion of the heavens and the earth. Then to Him you will be returned.”","When God alone is mentioned, the hearts of those who do not believe in the Hereafter recoil in disgust, but when those besides Him are mentioned, at once they rejoice.","Say, “O God, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the seen, You will judge between Your servants in what they used to differ over.”","If those who wronged possessed everything on earth and the like of it with it, they would ransom themselves with it from the terrible punishment on the Day of Resurrection. And there will appear to them from God what they never anticipated.","The evils of what they earned appeared before them, and what they used to mock closed in on them.","When hardship touches a person, he calls upon Us. Then when We grant him a blessing from Us, he says, “I was given this only because of my knowledge.” Rather, it is a trial, but most of them do not know.","Those before them said the same, yet what they used to earn availed them nothing.","So the evils of what they earned struck them. And those among these people who have wronged — the evils of what they earned will strike them too, and they cannot escape.","Do they not know that God extends provision to whoever He wills and restricts it? Surely in that are signs for people who believe.","Say, “O My servants who have been excessive against themselves, do not despair of God’s mercy. Truly God forgives all sins. He is the All-Forgiving, the Most Merciful.”","Turn back to your Lord and submit to Him before the punishment comes upon you, and then you will not be helped.","Follow the best of what has been sent down to you from your Lord before the punishment comes upon you suddenly while you are unaware.","Lest a soul should say, “O my regret over what I neglected regarding God, and I was indeed among the mockers!”","Or lest it should say, “If only God had guided me, I would have been among the righteous.”","Or lest it should say when it sees the punishment, “If only I had another chance, so I could be among those who do good.”","But yes, My verses came to you, and you denied them and were arrogant and were among the disbelievers.","On the Day of Resurrection, you will see those who lied about God with their faces blackened. Is there not in Hell a dwelling for the arrogant?","God will deliver the righteous through their triumph. No evil will touch them, nor will they grieve.","God is the Creator of all things, and He is Guardian over all things.","To Him belong the keys of the heavens and the earth. And those who disbelieved in God’s verses—it is they who are the losers.","Say, “Is it other than God you order me to worship, O ignorant ones?”","It was revealed to you and to those before you: “If you associate partners with God, your deeds will surely be voided, and you will surely be among the losers.”","Rather, worship God and be among the grateful.","They have not valued God as He deserves to be valued. The entire earth will be in His grip on the Day of Resurrection, and the heavens will be folded in His right hand. Glory be to Him, and exalted is He above what they associate with Him.","The Trumpet will be blown, and everyone in the heavens and everyone on the earth will collapse, except whom God wills. Then it will be blown again, and at once they will be standing, looking on.","And the earth will shine with the light of its Lord, and the Record will be laid open, and the prophets and the witnesses will be brought, and judgment will be passed between them in truth, and they will not be wronged.","Every soul will be paid in full for what it did, and He knows best what they do.","Those who disbelieved will be driven to Hell in throngs. When they reach it, its gates will be opened and its keepers will say to them, “Did messengers from among you not come to you, reciting to you the verses of your Lord and warning you of the meeting of this Day of yours?” They will say, “Yes, but the decree of punishment was justified against the disbelievers.”","They are told, “Enter the gates of Hell, abiding in it forever.” How wretched is the dwelling of the arrogant!","And those who were mindful of their Lord will be led to Paradise in throngs. When they reach it, its gates will have been opened, and its keepers will say to them, “Peace be upon you. You have been good, so enter it, abiding forever.”","And they will say, “Praise be to God, who fulfilled His promise to us and made us inherit the land, to settle in Paradise wherever we wish.” How excellent is the reward of those who worked!","And you will see the angels surrounding the Throne, glorifying their Lord with praise. Judgment will be passed between them in truth, and it will be said, “Praise be to God, Lord of all worlds.”","Ha Mim.","The revelation of the Book is from God, the All-Mighty, the All-Knowing.","Forgiver of sin, Accepter of repentance, Severe in punishment, Possessor of abundance. There is no god but Him. To Him is the final return.","None dispute God’s verses except those who disbelieve, so do not be deceived by their movement through the lands.","Before them, the people of Noah denied, and the factions after them. Every nation plotted against their messenger to seize him, and they argued with falsehood to defeat the truth with it. So I seized them — and how was My punishment?","And so your Lord’s word was justified against those who disbelieved: that they are the companions of the Fire.","Those who carry the Throne and those around it glorify their Lord with praise, believe in Him, and seek forgiveness for those who believe: “Our Lord, You encompass all things in mercy and knowledge, so forgive those who repented and followed Your path, and shield them from the punishment of the Blazing Fire.","Our Lord, admit them into the Gardens of Eternity that You promised them, and whoever was righteous among their fathers, their spouses, and their descendants. Truly, You are the All-Mighty, the All-Wise.","And shield them from evil deeds. Whoever You shield from evil deeds on that Day — You have shown him mercy. And that is the supreme triumph.”","Those who disbelieved will be called out to: “God’s loathing of you is greater than your loathing of yourselves, when you were called to faith and you rejected.”","They will say, “Our Lord, You gave us death twice and gave us life twice. We confess our sins — so is there any way out?”","“That is because when God alone was invoked, you disbelieved, but when partners were associated with Him, you believed. So judgment belongs to God, the Most High, the Most Great.”","He is the One who shows you His signs and sends down provision for you from the sky. Yet none take heed except those who turn back to Him.","So call upon God, devoting your worship sincerely to Him, even if the disbelievers despise it.","Exalted in rank, Lord of the Throne — He casts the spirit by His command upon whomever He wills of His servants, to warn of the Day of Meeting.","The Day they will all emerge — nothing of them is hidden from God. To whom belongs the dominion today? To God, the One, the Vanquisher.","Today every soul is recompensed for what it earned. No injustice today. Truly God is swift in reckoning.","And warn them of the Approaching Day, when hearts will be at the throats, choking with anguish. The wrongdoers will have no close friend and no intercessor who is obeyed.","He knows the treachery of the eyes and what the chests conceal.","And God judges with truth, while those they call upon besides Him judge nothing at all. Surely God — He is the All-Hearing, the All-Seeing.","Have they not traveled through the land and seen what became of those before them? They were mightier than them in strength and in traces upon the earth, yet God seized them for their sins, and they had no protector against God.","That was because their messengers came to them with clear proofs, but they disbelieved, so God seized them. He is Strong, severe in punishment.","And We sent Moses with Our miracles and a clear authority.","To Pharaoh, Haman, and Korah, but they said, “A sorcerer, a liar!”","When he brought them the truth from Us, they said, “Kill the sons of those who believe with him and spare their women.” But the scheming of the disbelievers is only in futility.","And Pharaoh said, “Let me kill Moses, and let him call upon his Lord. I fear he will change your religion or spread corruption in the land.”","And Moses said, “I seek refuge in my Lord and your Lord from every arrogant one who does not believe in the Day of Reckoning.”","A believing man from Pharaoh’s family, who concealed his faith, said, “Would you kill a man for saying ‘My Lord is God,’ when he has brought you clear proofs from your Lord? If he is a liar, his lie is upon him, but if he is truthful, some of what he promises you will strike you. Surely God does not guide one who is an extravagant liar.","O my people, yours is the kingdom today, dominant in the land — but who will help us against God’s might if it comes upon us?” Pharaoh said, “I only show you what I see, and I only guide you to the path of right conduct.”","The one who believed said, “O my people, I fear for you the like of the day of the factions.","The like of the fate of the people of Noah, Ad, Thamud, and those after them. And God does not intend injustice for His servants.","O my people, I fear for you the Day of Calling Out.","The Day you will turn and flee with no protector from God. And whoever God leads astray, there is no guide for him.","Joseph came to you before with clear proofs, yet you never ceased doubting what he brought you, until when he died, you said, ‘God will never send a messenger after him.’ Thus does God lead astray whoever is extravagant, a doubter.","Those who dispute God’s verses without any authority given to them. Grievously hateful is it in God’s sight and in the sight of those who believe. Thus does God seal every arrogant, tyrannical heart.”","Pharaoh said, “O Haman, build me a tower so that I may reach the pathways.","The pathways of the heavens — and look upon the god of Moses, for I truly think he is a liar.” Thus was the evil of his deed made alluring to Pharaoh, and he was barred from the path. And Pharaoh’s scheming led only to ruin.","The one who believed said, “O my people, follow me and I will guide you to the path of right conduct.","O my people, this worldly life is only a fleeting enjoyment, but the Hereafter — that is the lasting abode.","Whoever does an evil deed will be repaid only its like, but whoever does good — male or female — while being a believer, those will enter Paradise, provided for therein without limit.”","O my people, why is it that I call you to salvation and you call me to the Fire?","You call me to disbelieve in God and to associate with Him what I have no knowledge of, while I call you to the Almighty, the Ever-Forgiving.","Without doubt, what you call me to has no claim in this world or in the Hereafter, and our return is to God, and the transgressors — they are the companions of the Fire.","Soon you will remember what I say to you. And I entrust my affair to God. Truly God is All-Seeing of His servants.","So God shielded him from the evils of what they plotted, and a terrible punishment engulfed Pharaoh’s people.","The Fire, they are exposed to it morning and evening. And on the Day the Hour arrives: “Admit Pharaoh’s people into the most severe punishment.”","When they argue with one another in the Fire, the weak say to those who were arrogant, “We were your followers, so will you relieve us of a share of the Fire?”","Those who were arrogant say, “We are all in it. God has already judged between His servants.”","And those in the Fire say to the keepers of Hell, “Call upon your Lord to lighten for us a day of the punishment.”","They say, “Did your messengers not come to you with clear proofs?” They say, “Yes.” They say, “Then call yourselves.” But the supplication of the disbelievers is only in vain.","Surely We support Our messengers and those who believe in the life of this world and on the Day the witnesses stand.","The Day when the wrongdoers’ excuses will not benefit them, and theirs is the curse, and theirs is the worst abode.","And We gave Moses guidance and bequeathed to the Children of Israel the Scripture.","A guidance and a reminder for people of understanding.","So be patient. Truly God’s promise is true. And seek forgiveness for your sin, and glorify your Lord with praise in the evening and the early morning.","Those who dispute God’s verses without any authority that has come to them — in their chests is nothing but arrogance they will never attain. So seek refuge in God. He is the All-Hearing, the All-Seeing.","Surely the creation of the heavens and the earth is greater than the creation of humankind, but most people do not know.","The blind and the seeing are not equal, nor are those who believe and do good deeds and the evildoer. How little you reflect.","Truly the Hour is coming — there is no doubt about it — but most people do not believe.","Your Lord has said, “Call upon Me and I will answer you. Those who are too arrogant to worship Me will enter Hell humiliated.”","God is the One who made the night for you to rest in and the day bright. Truly God is full of grace toward people, but most people are not grateful.","That is God, your Lord, Creator of all things. There is no god but He. So how are you deluded?","Thus are deluded those who used to reject God’s signs.","God is the One who made the earth a resting place for you and the sky a canopy, and shaped you and perfected your forms, and provided you with good things. That is God, your Lord. So blessed is God, Lord of all worlds.","He is the Ever-Living. There is no god but He. So call upon Him, devoting your worship sincerely to Him. All praise belongs to God, Lord of all worlds.","Say, “I have been forbidden to worship those you call upon besides God, since the clear proofs have come to me from my Lord, and I have been commanded to submit to the Lord of all worlds.”","He is the One who created you from dust, then from a drop, then from a clinging clot, then He brings you out as a child, then so that you reach your full strength, then so that you become old — though some of you die before that — and so that you reach an appointed term, and so that you may understand.","He is the One who gives life and causes death. When He decrees a matter, He only says to it, “Be,” and it is.","Have you not seen those who dispute God’s signs — how they are turned away?","Those who denied the Book and what We sent Our messengers with — they will come to know.","When the shackles are around their necks and the chains — they are dragged.","Through scalding water, then into the Fire they are burned.","Then they are asked, “Where are those you used to associate.","Besides God?” They say, “They have vanished from us. Rather, we never used to call upon anything before.” Thus does God lead the disbelievers astray.","“That is because you used to rejoice on earth without right, and because you used to revel.","Enter the gates of Hell, dwelling therein forever.” How wretched is the abode of the arrogant!","So be patient. Truly God’s promise is true. Whether We show you some of what We promise them or We take your life, to Us they will be returned.","We sent messengers before you — among them are those We have told you about, and among them are those We have not told you about. No messenger could bring a sign except by God’s permission. So when God’s command comes, judgment is passed in truth, and there the followers of falsehood lose.","God is the One who made livestock for you — some you ride and some you eat.","And in them you have benefits, and so that you may reach upon them a need in your hearts, and upon them and upon ships you are carried.","He shows you His signs. So which of God’s signs do you deny?","Have they not traveled through the earth and seen what was the end of those before them? They were greater than them in number and mightier in strength and in traces upon the earth, yet what they used to earn availed them nothing.","When their messengers came to them with clear proofs, they rejoiced in whatever knowledge they had, and what they used to mock closed in on them.","When they saw Our punishment, they said, “We believe in God alone, and we reject what we used to associate with Him.”","But their faith was of no benefit to them once they saw Our punishment. That is God’s way, which has always applied among His servants. And there the disbelievers lost.","Ha Mim.","A revelation from the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.","A Book whose verses have been made clear, an Arabic Quran for people who know.","A bearer of good news and a warner. Yet most of them turned away, so they do not listen.","They said, “Our hearts are in coverings from what you call us to, and in our ears is deafness, and between us and you is a barrier. So do as you will — we too are doing.”","Say, “I am only a human being like you. It is revealed to me that your God is one God, so take a straight path to Him and seek His forgiveness.” Woe to those who associate others with Him.","Those who do not give charity and who deny the Hereafter.","Truly, those who believe and do righteous deeds will have a reward unending.","Say, “Do you truly deny the One who created the earth in two days, and set up rivals to Him? That is the Lord of all worlds.”","He placed firm mountains above it, blessed it, and measured out its sustenance in four days, equal for all who ask.","Then He turned to the sky while it was smoke and said to it and to the earth, “Come, willingly or unwillingly.” They said, “We come willingly.”","So He completed them as seven heavens in two days and assigned to each heaven its command. And We adorned the nearest heaven with lamps and as protection. That is the decree of the All-Mighty, the All-Knowing.","If they turn away, then say, “I have warned you of a thunderbolt like the thunderbolt of Ad and Thamud.”","When the messengers came to them from before them and behind them, saying, “Worship none but God,” they said, “Had our Lord willed, He would have sent down angels. So we deny what you have been sent with.”","As for Ad, they grew arrogant in the land without right and said, “Who is mightier than us in strength?” Did they not see that God, Who created them, is mightier than them in strength? And they used to reject Our signs.","So We sent upon them a howling wind on days of calamity, to make them taste the punishment of disgrace in the life of this world. And the punishment of the Hereafter is more disgraceful, and they will not be helped.","As for Thamud, We guided them, but they preferred blindness over guidance, so the thunderbolt of humiliating punishment seized them for what they used to earn.","And We saved those who believed and were God-conscious.","On the Day God’s enemies are gathered to the Fire, they will be driven in ranks.","Until, when they reach it, their hearing, their eyes, and their skins will testify against them about what they used to do.","They will say to their skins, “Why did you testify against us?” They will say, “God gave us speech—He who gave speech to everything. He created you the first time, and to Him you are returned.”","You could not hide yourselves from the testimony of your hearing, your eyes, and your skins, but you assumed that God did not know much of what you did.","That assumption of yours about your Lord has ruined you, and you have become among the losers.","So whether they endure, the Fire is their dwelling, and if they seek to make amends, they will not be allowed to.","We assigned to them companions who made attractive to them what was before them and what was behind them, and the decree was justified against them among nations of jinn and humans that had passed before them. They were truly losers.","Those who disbelieved said, “Do not listen to this Quran and drown it out, so that you may prevail.”","So We will make those who disbelieved taste a severe punishment, and We will repay them the worst of what they used to do.","That is the recompense of God’s enemies—the Fire. In it they will have the home of eternity, as repayment for their rejection of Our signs.","Those who disbelieved will say, “Our Lord, show us the two who led us astray from among the jinn and humans—we will put them under our feet so they become among the lowest.”","Truly, those who said, “Our Lord is God,” then stood firm—the angels descend upon them: “Do not fear and do not grieve, and rejoice in the Garden you were promised.","We are your allies in the life of this world and in the Hereafter. In it you will have whatever your souls desire, and in it you will have whatever you ask for.","A welcome from an All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.”","Who is better in speech than one who calls to God, does good, and says, “I am truly one of those who submit”?","Good and evil are not equal. Repel with what is better, and the one between whom and you there was enmity will become like a close, intimate friend.","But none is granted this except those who are patient, and none is granted it except one of great fortune.","If a provocation from Satan should stir you, seek refuge in God. He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.","Among His signs are the night and the day, the sun and the moon. Do not prostrate to the sun or the moon, but prostrate to God who created them, if it is Him you worship.","But if they are too proud, then those in the presence of your Lord glorify Him night and day, and they never tire.","Among His signs is that you see the earth barren, but when We send down water upon it, it stirs and swells. Surely He who gave it life will give life to the dead. He is Capable of all things.","Those who distort Our verses are not hidden from Us. Is the one cast into the Fire better, or the one who comes secure on the Day of Resurrection? Do whatever you wish — He is All-Seeing of what you do.","Those who rejected the Reminder when it came to them — truly it is a mighty Book.","Falsehood cannot approach it from before it or behind it — a revelation from the All-Wise, the All-Praiseworthy.","Nothing is said to you except what was said to the messengers before you. Your Lord is certainly One of forgiveness and One of painful punishment.","Had We made it a foreign Quran, they would have said, “Why are its verses not made clear? A foreign tongue and an Arab audience?” Say, “For those who believe, it is guidance and healing. But those who do not believe — in their ears is deafness, and it is blindness upon them.” Those are called from a distant place.","We gave Moses the Scripture, and it was disputed. Were it not for a word that had preceded from your Lord, it would have been decided between them. They are truly in troubling doubt about it.","Whoever does good, it is for his own soul, and whoever does evil, it is against it. Your Lord is never unjust to His servants.","To Him is referred the knowledge of the Hour. No fruit emerges from its sheath, and no female conceives or delivers, except with His knowledge. On the Day He calls to them, “Where are My partners?” they will say, “We declare to You — not one of us can bear witness to that.”","What they used to call upon before will vanish from them, and they will realize there is no escape for them.","Man never tires of asking for good, but if evil touches him, he is despairing, hopeless.","If We let him taste mercy from Us after hardship has touched him, he will surely say, “This is mine by right, and I do not think the Hour will ever come. And if I am returned to my Lord, surely the finest reward awaits me with Him.” We will certainly inform those who disbelieved of what they did, and We will certainly make them taste a harsh punishment.","When We bestow favor upon man, he turns away and distances himself, but when evil touches him, he is full of endless prayer.","Say, “Have you considered — if it is from God and then you rejected it, who is more astray than one in extreme opposition?”","We will show them Our signs on the horizons and within themselves until it becomes clear to them that it is the truth. Is it not enough that your Lord is a Witness over all things?","Truly, they are in doubt about the meeting with their Lord. Truly, He encompasses all things.","Ha Mim.","Ayn Sin Qaf.","Thus does God, the All-Mighty, the All-Wise, reveal to you and to those before you.","To Him belongs what is in the heavens and what is in the earth. He is the Most High, the Most Great.","The heavens nearly split apart from above, and the angels glorify their Lord with praise and seek forgiveness for those on earth. Truly, God is the All-Forgiving, the Most Merciful.","Those who have taken protectors besides Him—God is Watchful over them, and you are not their guardian.","Thus We have revealed to you an Arabic Quran so that you may warn the Mother of Cities and those around it, and warn of the Day of Gathering about which there is no doubt. A group in Paradise and a group in the Blaze.","Had God willed, He would have made them one community, but He admits whom He wills into His mercy. And the wrongdoers have no protector and no helper.","Or have they taken protectors besides Him? God alone is the Protector. He gives life to the dead, and He is Capable of all things.","Whatever you disagree about, its judgment rests with God. That is God, my Lord—in Him I place my trust, and to Him I turn.","Originator of the heavens and the earth. He made for you mates from yourselves, and mates among the livestock, multiplying you through it. Nothing is like Him. He is the All-Hearing, the All-Seeing.","His are the keys of the heavens and the earth. He extends provision to whom He wills and restricts it. Truly, He is All-Knowing of all things.","He has ordained for you of the religion what He enjoined upon Noah, and what We have revealed to you, and what We enjoined upon Abraham, Moses, and Jesus: “Uphold the religion and do not divide over it.” Hard upon the polytheists is what you call them to. God draws to Himself whom He wills and guides to Himself whoever turns back.","They did not divide except after knowledge had come to them, out of rivalry among themselves. Were it not for a word that had preceded from your Lord until an appointed term, it would have been settled between them. And those who inherited the Scripture after them are in deep doubt about it.","So to that, call, and stand firm as you have been commanded. Do not follow their desires. And say, “I believe in every Scripture God has sent down. I have been commanded to judge justly between you. God is our Lord and your Lord. To us our deeds and to you your deeds. There is no argument between us and you. God will bring us together, and to Him is the final return.”","Those who argue about God after He has been answered—their argument is null before their Lord. Upon them is wrath, and for them is a severe punishment.","God is the One who sent down the Book with truth and the balance. And what would make you know? Perhaps the Hour is near.","Those who do not believe in it seek to hasten it, but those who believe are fearful of it and know that it is the truth. Truly, those who dispute about the Hour are in far-gone error.","God is Gentle with His servants. He provides for whoever He wills. And He is the All-Strong, the All-Mighty.","Whoever desires the harvest of the Hereafter, We increase for him his harvest. And whoever desires the harvest of this world, We give him of it, but he has no share in the Hereafter.","Or do they have partners who have prescribed for them in religion what God has not authorized? Were it not for the word of judgment, it would have been decided between them. Surely the wrongdoers will have a painful punishment.","You see the wrongdoers fearful of what they earned, and it will befall them. But those who believed and did righteous deeds are in the meadows of the Gardens — they will have whatever they wish with their Lord. That is the great bounty.","That is what God gives glad tidings of to His servants who believed and did righteous deeds. Say, “I ask you no reward for it, only love for the near kin.” Whoever earns a good deed, We increase for him goodness in it. Truly, God is All-Forgiving, Most Appreciative.","Or do they say, “He has fabricated a lie against God”? If God wills, He will seal your heart. God erases falsehood and establishes truth by His words. He is All-Knowing of what is in the hearts.","He is the One who accepts repentance from His servants and pardons misdeeds, and He knows what you do.","He answers those who believed and did righteous deeds, and increases them from His bounty. But the disbelievers will have a severe punishment.","If God were to spread provision widely for His servants, they would have transgressed in the earth, but He sends down in measured amounts as He wills. He is All-Aware of His servants, All-Seeing.","He is the One who sends down the rain after they have despaired, and spreads His mercy. And He is the Protector, the Praiseworthy.","Among His signs is the creation of the heavens and the earth and the creatures He has scattered throughout them both. And He is fully capable of gathering them whenever He wills.","Whatever calamity strikes you is because of what your hands have earned, and He pardons much.","You cannot escape on earth, and you have no protector or helper besides God.","Among His signs are the ships sailing through the sea like mountains.","If He wills, He stills the wind and they remain motionless on its surface. Surely in that are signs for everyone patient and grateful.","Or He wrecks them for what they have earned, though He pardons much.","And so that those who dispute Our verses may know they have no escape.","Whatever you have been given is but the enjoyment of this worldly life, but what is with God is better and more lasting for those who believe and place their trust in their Lord.","Those who avoid the great sins and indecencies, and when they are angered, they forgive.","Those who answered their Lord, established prayer, conduct their affairs by consultation among themselves, and spend from what We have provided them.","Those who, when oppression strikes them, defend themselves.","The recompense of a wrong is a wrong like it, but whoever pardons and makes amends, his reward rests with God. He does not love the wrongdoers.","Whoever defends himself after being wronged — against those there is no blame.","Blame falls only on those who wrong people and commit aggression in the land without right. For them is a painful punishment.","But whoever is patient and forgives — truly that is among the most resolute of matters.","Whoever God leads astray has no protector beyond Him. You will see the wrongdoers, when they see the punishment, saying, “Is there any way back?”","You will see them exposed to it, humbled by disgrace, looking with a furtive glance. And those who believed said, “Truly the losers are those who lost themselves and their families on the Day of Resurrection.” Surely the wrongdoers are in lasting punishment.","They had no protectors to help them besides God. Whoever God leads astray has no way.","Respond to your Lord before a Day comes that God will not turn back. You will have no refuge that Day, and you will have no denial.","If they turn away, We have not sent you as a guardian over them. Your only duty is to convey. When We give man a taste of mercy from Us, he rejoices in it. But when misfortune strikes them for what their own hands have sent ahead, then truly man is ungrateful.","To God belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth. He creates what He wills. He grants females to whom He wills and grants males to whom He wills.","Or He pairs them, males and females, and He makes whom He wills barren. He is All-Knowing, All-Powerful.","It is not for any human that God should speak to him except through revelation, or from behind a veil, or by sending a messenger who reveals by His permission what He wills. He is Most High, All-Wise.","And so We revealed to you a spirit from Our command. You did not know what the Book was, nor what faith was, but We made it a light by which We guide whom We will among Our servants. And you truly guide to a straight path.","The path of God, to whom belongs all that is in the heavens and all that is in the earth. Surely to God all matters return.","Ha Mim.","By the clear Book.","We made it an Arabic Quran so that you may understand.","And it is in the Mother of the Book, with Us — truly exalted, full of wisdom.","Should We turn the Reminder away from you because you are a people of excess?","How many a prophet We sent among earlier peoples.","Yet no prophet came to them without them mocking him.","So We destroyed those mightier in power than these, and the example of the earlier peoples has passed.","If you asked them, “Who created the heavens and the earth?” they would surely say, “The Almighty, the All-Knowing created them.”","He Who made the earth a cradle for you and made pathways in it for you, so that you may find your way.","And He Who sent down water from the sky in due measure — and We revived with it a dead land. Thus you will be brought out.","And He Who created all the pairs and made for you ships and livestock that you ride.","So that you may settle on their backs, then remember your Lord’s blessing when you have settled upon them, and say, “Glory be to Him Who subjected this to us, for we could never have mastered it on our own.","And to our Lord we will surely return.”","Yet they have made some of His servants a part of Him. Truly, man is clearly ungrateful.","Or has He taken daughters from what He creates and favored you with sons?","When one of them is given news of what he attributes to the Most Merciful as a likeness, his face darkens and he is filled with suppressed rage.","One who is raised amid ornaments and is inarticulate in dispute?","They have made the angels — who are servants of the Most Merciful — females. Did they witness their creation? Their testimony will be recorded, and they will be questioned.","They say, “Had the Most Merciful willed, we would not have worshiped them.” They have no knowledge of that. They are only guessing.","Or did We give them a book before it that they are holding on to?","Rather, they say, “We found our fathers following a tradition, and we are guided in their footsteps.”","Likewise, We never sent a warner to any town before you without its affluent ones saying, “We found our fathers following a tradition, and we are following in their footsteps.”","He said, “Even if I brought you something more guided than what you found your fathers upon?” They said, “We reject what you have been sent with.”","So We took vengeance on them. See how the end was for the deniers.","When Abraham said to his father and his people, “I am free of what you worship.","Except He who created me, for He will guide me.”","He made it an enduring word among his descendants, so that they might return.","Rather, I gave these people and their fathers enjoyment until the truth came to them and a clear messenger.","When the truth came to them, they said, “This is sorcery, and we reject it.”","They said, “Why was this Quran not sent down to a great man from one of the two cities?”","Is it they who distribute your Lord’s mercy? It is We who distributed their livelihood among them in the life of this world and raised some of them above others in rank, so that some might take others into service. Your Lord’s mercy is better than what they accumulate.","Were it not that people would become one community, We would have given those who disbelieve in the Most Merciful roofs of silver for their houses and stairways on which they ascend.","And doors for their houses and couches on which they recline.","And gold ornament. Yet all of that is nothing but the enjoyment of the life of this world, and the Hereafter with your Lord is for the reverent.","Whoever turns blind to the remembrance of the Most Merciful, We assign to him a devil who becomes his constant companion.","They bar them from the path, yet they think they are guided.","Until, when he comes to Us, he says, “If only between me and you were the distance of the two easts! What a wretched companion!”","It will not benefit you today, since you wronged, that you are partners in the punishment.","Can you make the deaf hear, or guide the blind and whoever is in clear misguidance?","Whether We take you away, We will surely take vengeance on them.","Or We show you what We have promised them — We have full power over them.","So hold fast to what has been revealed to you. You are on a straight path.","Truly it is a reminder for you and for your people, and you will be questioned.","Ask those of Our messengers We sent before you: did We ever appoint gods to be worshiped besides the Most Merciful?","Certainly We sent Moses with Our miracles to Pharaoh and his chiefs, and he said, “I am a messenger of the Lord of all worlds.”","But when he brought them Our miracles, they laughed at them.","Every sign We showed them was greater than the one before it, and We seized them with punishment so that they might return.","They said, “O sorcerer, call upon your Lord for us by the covenant He made with you — we will surely be guided.”","But when We lifted the punishment from them, they broke their word.","Pharaoh called out among his people, saying, “O my people, is the kingdom of Egypt not mine, and these rivers flowing beneath me? Do you not see?","Am I not better than this contemptible one who can barely speak clearly?","Why then have bracelets of gold not been cast upon him, or why have the angels not come with him as escorts?”","So he made light of his people, and they obeyed him. They were a defiantly sinful people.","When they provoked Us, We took vengeance on them and drowned them all.","So We made them a precedent and an example for those who came after.","When the son of Mary was cited as an example, your people broke into uproar.","They said, “Are our gods better, or is he?” They only raised this with you to argue. They are nothing but a quarrelsome people.","He was only a servant We blessed and made an example for the Children of Israel.","Had We willed, We could have made from among you angels succeeding one another on earth.","Truly, he is a sign of the Hour, so have no doubt about it and follow Me. This is a straight path.","Let Satan not divert you. He is a clear enemy to you.","When Jesus came with clear proofs, he said, “I have come to you with wisdom and to clarify for you some of what you differ over. So be mindful of God and obey me.","Surely God — He is my Lord and your Lord, so worship Him. This is a straight path.”","But the factions among them differed. So woe to those who wronged, from the punishment of a painful Day.","Are they waiting for anything but the Hour — that it should come upon them suddenly while they are unaware?","Close friends on that Day will be enemies to one another — except the righteous.","O My servants, no fear is upon you today, nor will you grieve.","Those who believed in Our signs and were submissive.","“Enter Paradise, you and your spouses, rejoicing.”","Trays of gold and cups are passed around them, and in it is whatever souls desire and eyes delight in. And you will abide in it forever.","That is the Paradise you have been made to inherit for what you used to do.","In it you have abundant fruit from which you eat.","Surely the criminals will abide in the punishment of Hell forever.","It will not be eased for them, and they will be in utter despair within it.","We did not wrong them, but it was they who were the wrongdoers.","They will cry out, “O Malik, let your Lord finish us off!” He will say, “You are staying.”","We brought you the truth, but most of you despise the truth.","Or have they devised some plan? Then We too are devising.","Or do they think that We do not hear their secrets and their private conversations? Yes indeed, and Our messengers are with them, recording.","Say, “If the Most Merciful had a son, then I would be the first to worship.”","Glory be to the Lord of the heavens and the earth, Lord of the Throne, far above what they describe.","So leave them to wade in falsehood and play until they meet their Day which they are promised.","He is the one who is God in the heaven and God on the earth. And He is the All-Wise, the All-Knowing.","Blessed is He to whom belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth and everything between them, and with Him is the knowledge of the Hour, and to Him you will be returned.","Those they invoke besides Him have no power of intercession — except those who testify to the truth while they know.","If you asked them who created them, they would surely say, “God.” So how are they deluded?","And his cry: “O my Lord, these are a people who do not believe.”","So turn away from them and say, “Peace.” They will come to know.","Ha Mim.","By the clear Book.","Truly, We sent it down on a blessed night. We have always been warners.","On that night every wise matter is determined.","A command from Us. We have always been sending messengers.","A mercy from your Lord. He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.","Lord of the heavens and the earth and everything between them, if you would be certain.","There is no god but He. He gives life and causes death — your Lord and the Lord of your earliest forefathers.","Yet they are in doubt, playing.","So watch for the Day when the sky brings a visible smoke.","It will engulf the people — this is a painful punishment.","“Our Lord, lift this punishment from us — we are believers!”","How can remembrance help them now, when a clear messenger already came to them?","Then they turned away from him and said, “A madman, taught by others!”","We will lift the punishment briefly, but you will return.","The Day We strike with the greatest strike — We will take Our vengeance.","Before them We tested Pharaoh’s people, and a noble messenger came to them.","“Hand over to me God’s servants. I am a trustworthy messenger to you.","Do not exalt yourselves against God. I come to you with clear authority.","I have sought refuge in my Lord and your Lord from your stoning me.","If you do not believe me, then leave me alone.”","So he called upon his Lord, “These are a criminal people.”","“Travel with My servants by night — you will be pursued.","Leave the sea parted. They are an army to be drowned.”","How many gardens and springs they left behind!","And crops and noble dwellings.","And comforts in which they delighted.","So it was. And We made another people inherit it all.","Neither the sky nor the earth wept for them, nor were they given respite.","Truly We saved the Children of Israel from the humiliating punishment.","From Pharaoh. He was arrogant, among the transgressors.","We chose them knowingly over all peoples.","We gave them signs in which was a clear trial.","Surely these people say.","“There is nothing but our first death, and we will not be resurrected.","So bring back our forefathers, if you are truthful.”","Are they better, or the people of Tubba and those before them? We destroyed them — they were criminals.","We did not create the heavens and the earth and what is between them in play.","We created them only in truth, but most of them do not know.","Truly the Day of Separation is the appointed time for all of them.","A Day when no ally will avail another ally in the least, nor will they be helped.","Except whoever God has mercy on. He is the All-Mighty, the Most Merciful.","Truly the tree of Zaqqum.","Is the food of the sinful.","Like molten metal, it boils in the bellies.","Like the boiling of scalding water.","“Seize him and drag him into the midst of the Blaze!","Then pour over his head the torment of scalding water!”","“Taste this! You are the mighty, the noble one!","This is what you used to doubt.”","Truly the righteous are in a secure station.","In gardens and springs.","Wearing fine silk and brocade, facing one another.","So it is. And We paired them with wide-eyed maidens.","They call for every kind of fruit there, in security.","They will not taste death there beyond the first death, and He has shielded them from the punishment of the Blaze.","A grace from your Lord. That is the supreme triumph.","So We have made it easy in your tongue, so that they may take heed.","So watch. They too are watching.","Ha Mim.","The revelation of the Book is from God, the All-Mighty, the All-Wise.","Surely in the heavens and the earth are signs for the believers.","And in your creation and what He scatters of creatures are signs for people who are certain.","And in the alternation of night and day, and what God sends down from the sky of provision, reviving the earth after its death, and the shifting of the winds, are signs for people who reason.","These are God’s verses We recite to you in truth. So in what message after God and His verses will they believe?","Woe to every sinful liar.","He hears God’s verses recited to him, then persists in arrogance as though he never heard them. So give him tidings of a painful punishment.","And when he learns anything of Our verses, he takes them in mockery. For those there is a humiliating punishment.","Beyond them lies Hell. What they earned will not avail them at all, nor will those they took as protectors besides God. For them is a tremendous punishment.","This is guidance. And those who disbelieve in their Lord’s verses — for them is a punishment of painful torment.","God is the One who subjected the sea for you, so that ships may sail through it by His command, and so that you may seek of His bounty, and so that you may be grateful.","And He subjected to you whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth — all from Him. Surely in that are signs for people who reflect.","Say to those who believe that they should forgive those who do not expect the days of God, so that He may recompense a people for what they used to earn.","Whoever does good, it is for his own soul. And whoever does evil, it is against it. Then to your Lord you will be returned.","We gave the Children of Israel the Book, authority, and prophethood, and We provided them with good things, and We favored them over all peoples.","And We gave them clear proofs of the matter. They did not differ except after knowledge had come to them, out of rivalry among themselves. Your Lord will judge between them on the Day of Resurrection concerning what they used to differ over.","Then We set you upon a clear way of the matter, so follow it, and do not follow the desires of those who do not know.","They will never avail you anything against God. Truly the wrongdoers are allies of one another, but God is the Ally of the God-conscious.","This is insight for mankind, and guidance and mercy for people who are certain.","Do those who committed evil deeds think We will make them equal to those who believed and did righteous deeds—equal in their life and their death? How wretched is their judgment!","God created the heavens and the earth in truth, and so that every soul is repaid for what it earned, and they will not be wronged.","Have you seen the one who took his own desire as his god, and God led him astray knowingly, and sealed his hearing and his heart, and placed a veil over his sight? Who then can guide him after God? Will you not reflect?","They said, “There is nothing but our worldly life—we die and we live—and nothing destroys us but time.” They have no knowledge of that. They are only guessing.","When Our verses are recited to them as clear proofs, their only argument is to say, “Bring back our forefathers, if you are truthful.”","Say, “God gives you life, then causes you to die, then gathers you to the Day of Resurrection, about which there is no doubt.” But most people do not know.","To God belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth. The Day the Hour arrives—that Day the followers of falsehood will lose.","You will see every nation on its knees. Every nation will be called to its record: “Today you are repaid for what you used to do.”","“This is Our record—it speaks against you in truth. We were having everything you did transcribed.”","As for those who believed and did righteous deeds, their Lord will admit them into His mercy. That is the clear triumph.","But as for those who disbelieved: “Were My verses not recited to you, yet you grew arrogant and were a criminal people?","When you were told, ‘God’s promise is true, and the Hour—there is no doubt about it,’ you said, ‘We have no idea what the Hour is. We think it is nothing but speculation, and we are not convinced.’”","The evils of what they did became apparent to them, and what they used to mock closed in on them.","They were told, “Today We forget you, just as you forgot the meeting of this Day of yours. Your refuge is the Fire, and you have no helpers.","That is because you took God’s verses as a joke, and the worldly life deluded you.” So today they will not be brought out of it, nor will they be asked to make amends.","So all praise belongs to God, Lord of the heavens and Lord of the earth, Lord of all worlds.","To Him belongs all grandeur in the heavens and the earth, and He is the All-Mighty, the All-Wise.","Ha Mim.","The revelation of the Book is from God, the All-Mighty, the All-Wise.","We did not create the heavens and the earth and what is between them except in truth and for an appointed term. Yet those who disbelieve turn away from what they are warned of.","Say, “Have you considered what you call upon besides God? Show me what they have created of the earth. Or do they have a share in the heavens? Bring me a scripture before this or a remnant of knowledge, if you are truthful.”","Who is more astray than one who calls upon, besides God, those who will not answer him until the Day of Resurrection, and who are oblivious of their prayers?","When people are gathered, they will be enemies to them and will deny their worship.","When Our verses are recited to them as clear proofs, those who disbelieve say of the truth when it comes to them, “This is obvious sorcery.”","Or do they say, “He fabricated it”? Say, “If I fabricated it, you could not protect me from God in the least. He knows best what you indulge in. He suffices as a witness between me and you. And He is the All-Forgiving, the Most Merciful.”","Say, “I am no novelty among the messengers, and I do not know what will be done with me or with you. I only follow what is revealed to me, and I am nothing but a clear warner.”","Say, “Have you considered: if it is from God and you disbelieve in it, and a witness from the Children of Israel has testified to something similar and believed, while you are too arrogant? Truly, God does not guide the wrongdoing people.”","Those who disbelieve say of those who believe, “If it were any good, they would not have preceded us to it.” And since they are not guided by it, they will say, “This is an ancient fabrication.”","Before it was the Book of Moses, a guide and a mercy. And this is a confirming Book in an Arabic tongue, to warn those who do wrong and as good news for those who do good.","Surely those who say, “Our Lord is God,” then remain steadfast — no fear will be upon them, nor will they grieve.","Those are the people of Paradise, dwelling therein forever, as recompense for what they used to do.","We charged man to be good to his parents. His mother carried him in hardship and delivered him in hardship, and his bearing and weaning take thirty months. Until, when he reaches his full strength and reaches forty years, he says, “My Lord, inspire me to be grateful for Your blessing that You bestowed upon me and upon my parents, and to do righteous deeds that please You, and set right for me my offspring. I have turned to You in repentance, and I am among those who submit.”","Those are the ones from whom We accept the best of what they did and overlook their misdeeds, among the people of the Garden — a true promise they were promised.","But the one who says to his parents, “Ugh to you both! Do you promise me that I will be brought out when generations have already passed before me?” — while they both plead to God for help — “Woe to you! Believe! Surely God’s promise is true.” Yet he says, “This is nothing but tales of the ancients.”","Those are the ones against whom the word has come due, among nations of jinn and humans that have already passed before them. They were losers.","For each there are ranks according to what they did, so that He may repay them in full for their deeds, and they will not be wronged.","On the Day those who disbelieved are exposed to the Fire: “You squandered your good things in your worldly life and enjoyed them. So today you are repaid with the punishment of humiliation for your arrogance on earth without right, and for your defiance.”","Mention the brother of Aad, when he warned his people at the sand dunes — and warners had already passed before him and after him — “Worship none but God. I fear for you the punishment of a tremendous Day.”","They said, “Have you come to turn us away from our gods? Then bring us what you promise us, if you are truthful.”","He said, “The knowledge is only with God. I convey to you what I have been sent with, but I see you are a people acting in ignorance.”","When they saw it as a cloud advancing toward their valleys, they said, “This is a cloud bringing us rain.” No, it is what you sought to hasten — a wind carrying a painful punishment.","It destroys everything by its Lord’s command. By morning, nothing could be seen but their dwellings. That is how We repay the criminal people.","We had established them in what We have not established you in, and We gave them hearing and sight and hearts. Yet their hearing, their sight, and their hearts availed them nothing, since they used to reject God’s signs, and what they used to mock closed in on them.","We destroyed the towns around you, and We varied the verses so that they might turn back.","Why then did those they took as gods besides God, as a means of nearness, not help them? Instead, they vanished from them. That was their fabrication and what they used to invent.","When We directed a group of jinn toward you to listen to the Quran, and when they came into its presence, they said, “Be silent!” And when it was finished, they returned to their people as warners.","They said, “O our people, we have heard a Book sent down after Moses, confirming what came before it, guiding to the truth and to a straight path.","O our people, answer God’s caller and believe in him. He will forgive you some of your sins and protect you from a painful punishment.”","Whoever does not answer God’s caller cannot escape on earth, and he has no protectors besides Him. Those are in clear error.","Have they not seen that God, who created the heavens and the earth and was never wearied by their creation, is Capable of giving life to the dead? Yes indeed, He is Capable of all things.","On the Day those who disbelieved are brought before the Fire: “Is this not the truth?” They will say, “Yes, by our Lord!” He will say, “Then taste the punishment for what you used to deny.”","So be patient, as the messengers of firm resolve were patient, and do not seek to hasten it for them. On the Day they see what they are promised, it will be as though they had not lingered but an hour of a day. A proclamation. Will any be destroyed except the defiantly disobedient people?","Those who disbelieved and barred others from God’s path — He has rendered their deeds worthless.","But those who believed, did righteous deeds, and believed in what was sent down upon Muhammad — and it is the truth from their Lord — He has absolved them of their misdeeds and set right their condition.","That is because those who disbelieved followed falsehood, and those who believed followed the truth from their Lord. Thus God sets forth for people their likenesses.","So when you meet those who disbelieved, strike at their necks until, when you have thoroughly subdued them, tighten the bonds. Then either grace or ransom, until the war lays down its burdens. That is so. Had God willed, He could have taken vengeance on them Himself, but it is so that He may test some of you by means of others. And those who are killed in God’s path — He will never render their deeds worthless.","He will guide them and set right their condition.","And He will admit them into Paradise, which He has made known to them.","O you who believe, if you support God, He will support you and plant your feet firm.","But those who disbelieved — ruin upon them! He has rendered their deeds worthless.","That is because they despised what God sent down, so He nullified their deeds.","Have they not traveled through the land and seen what became of those before them? God destroyed them utterly, and the disbelievers will have the like of it.","That is because God is the Protector of those who believe, and the disbelievers have no protector.","Truly God admits those who believe and do righteous deeds into gardens beneath which rivers flow. But those who disbelieve — they enjoy themselves and eat as cattle eat, and the Fire is their dwelling.","How many a town mightier than your town that drove you out have We destroyed, and they had no helper.","Is one who stands on clear proof from his Lord like one whose evil deeds have been made appealing to him, and they followed their desires?","The likeness of Paradise promised to the God-conscious: in it are rivers of water never stagnant, rivers of milk whose taste never changes, rivers of wine delightful to the drinkers, and rivers of purified honey. In it they will have every kind of fruit and forgiveness from their Lord. Is that like one who abides forever in the Fire, given scalding water to drink that tears apart their bowels?","Among them are those who listen to you, but when they leave your presence they say to those given knowledge, “What did he just say?” Those are the ones whose hearts God has sealed, and they followed their desires.","But those who are guided — He increases them in guidance and grants them their righteousness.","Are they waiting for anything but the Hour, that it should come upon them suddenly? Its signs have already come. So how will their reminder benefit them once it has arrived?","So know that there is no god but God, and seek forgiveness for your sin and for the believing men and believing women. God knows your movements and your resting places.","Those who believe say, “If only a chapter were sent down.” But when a decisive chapter is sent down and fighting is mentioned in it, you see those in whose hearts is a disease looking at you with the look of one fainting at death. So woe to them!","Obedience and fitting words. But when the matter is resolved, if they had been true to God, it would have been better for them.","So would you, if you turned away, spread corruption on earth and sever your ties of kinship?","Those are the ones God has cursed, so He made them deaf and blinded their sight.","Do they not reflect on the Quran, or are there locks upon their hearts?","Truly, those who turned back on their heels after guidance had become clear to them — Satan enticed them and gave them false hopes.","That is because they said to those who despised what God sent down, “We will obey you in some matters.” And God knows their secrets.","So how will it be when the angels take them in death, striking their faces and their backs?","That is because they followed what enraged God and despised His pleasure, so He rendered their deeds worthless.","Or do those in whose hearts is a disease think that God will never expose their hatred?","If We willed, We could show them to you, and you would recognize them by their marks. Yet you will surely recognize them by the tone of their speech. And God knows your deeds.","We will certainly test you until We know those among you who strive and those who are steadfast, and We will test your accounts.","Truly, those who disbelieved and turned others from God’s path and opposed the Messenger after guidance had become clear to them will never harm God in the least, and He will render their deeds worthless.","O you who believe, obey God and obey the Messenger, and do not invalidate your deeds.","Truly, those who disbelieved and turned others from God’s path, then died as disbelievers — God will never forgive them.","So do not weaken and call for peace while you have the upper hand. God is with you, and He will never deprive you of your deeds.","The life of this world is only play and amusement. If you believe and are mindful, He will give you your rewards and will not ask you for your wealth.","If He were to ask you for it and press you, you would withhold, and He would expose your hatred.","Here you are, called to spend in God’s path, yet among you are those who withhold. Whoever withholds only withholds from himself. God is the Self-Sufficient, and you are the needy. If you turn away, He will replace you with another people, and they will not be the likes of you.","Truly, We have granted you a clear victory.","So that God may forgive you what preceded of your sins and what followed, and complete His blessing upon you, and guide you to a straight path.","And so that God may grant you a mighty victory.","It is He who sent down tranquility into the hearts of the believers so they would increase in faith upon their faith. To God belong the forces of the heavens and the earth, and God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.","So that He may admit the believing men and believing women into gardens beneath which rivers flow, dwelling therein forever, and erase their misdeeds from them. That, with God, is a supreme triumph.","And so that He may punish the hypocrite men and hypocrite women, and the polytheist men and polytheist women — those who harbor evil assumptions about God. Upon them is the turn of evil. God is wrathful against them, has cursed them, and has prepared for them Hell — what a wretched destination!","To God belong the forces of the heavens and the earth, and God is All-Mighty, All-Wise.","Truly, We have sent you as a witness, a bearer of good news, and a warner.","So that you may believe in God and His Messenger, and support him, and honor him, and glorify Him morning and evening.","Surely those who pledge allegiance to you are only pledging allegiance to God — God’s hand is over their hands. Whoever breaks his pledge breaks it only against himself, and whoever fulfills what he has pledged to God, He will grant him a great reward.","Those desert Arabs who stayed behind will say to you, “Our wealth and our families kept us busy, so ask forgiveness for us.” They say with their tongues what is not in their hearts. Say, “Who can avail you anything against God if He intends harm for you, or intends benefit for you?” Rather, God is fully Aware of what you do.","Rather, you assumed that the Messenger and the believers would never return to their families, and that was made appealing in your hearts, and you harbored evil assumptions, and you were a ruined people.","Whoever does not believe in God and His Messenger — We have prepared a blaze for the disbelievers.","To God belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth. He forgives whom He wills and punishes whom He wills, and God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","Those who stayed behind will say, when you set out toward spoils to take them, “Let us follow you.” They wish to change God’s word. Say, “You will not follow us. Thus God has said before.” Then they will say, “Rather, you are jealous of us.” Rather, they hardly understand at all.","Say to those desert Arabs who stayed behind, “You will be called against a people of great military might — you will fight them or they will submit. If you obey, God will give you a good reward, but if you turn away as you turned away before, He will punish you with a painful punishment.”","No blame falls on the blind, nor on the lame, nor on the sick. Whoever obeys God and His Messenger, He will admit him into gardens beneath which rivers flow, and whoever turns away, He will punish him with a painful punishment.","Truly God was pleased with the believers when they pledged allegiance to you under the tree. He knew what was in their hearts, so He sent down tranquility upon them and rewarded them with a near victory.","And abundant spoils for them to take. God is All-Mighty, All-Wise.","God promised you abundant spoils that you would take, and He hastened this one for you and held back people’s hands from you — so that it would be a sign for the believers and so He would guide you to a straight path.","And another you were not yet able to take — God has already encompassed them. God is over all things All-Powerful.","Had those who disbelieved fought you, they would have turned their backs in flight, then found neither protector nor helper.","Such is God’s way that has passed before, and you will never find any change in God’s way.","He is the One who held back their hands from you and your hands from them in the valley of Mecca, after He had given you victory over them. God is All-Seeing of what you do.","They are the ones who disbelieved and barred you from the Sacred Mosque, and prevented the sacrificial animals from reaching their place. Were it not for believing men and believing women whom you did not know — that you might trample them and guilt would befall you on their account unknowingly — so that God might admit into His mercy whom He wills. Had they been separate, We would have punished those among them who disbelieved with a painful punishment.","When those who disbelieved harbored in their hearts the zealotry—the zealotry of ignorance—God sent down His tranquility upon His Messenger and upon the believers and bound them to the word of righteousness, and they were most deserving of it and worthy of it. God is ever All-Knowing of all things.","God has truly fulfilled His Messenger’s vision in truth: you will surely enter the Sacred Mosque, if God wills, in security, with your heads shaved and hair trimmed, fearing nothing. He knew what you did not know, and He granted, before that, a near victory.","It is He who sent His Messenger with guidance and the religion of truth to make it prevail over all religion. God suffices as a Witness.","Muhammad is God’s Messenger. Those with him are fierce against the disbelievers, merciful among themselves. You see them bowing, prostrating, seeking God’s grace and pleasure. Their mark is on their faces from the trace of prostration. That is their likeness in the Torah. And their likeness in the Gospel is like a plant that sends out its shoot, then strengthens it, then grows thick, then stands firm on its stalk, amazing the sowers—so that through them He may enrage the disbelievers. God has promised those among them who believe and do righteous deeds forgiveness and a great reward.","O you who believe, do not put yourselves ahead of God and His Messenger, and be mindful of God. Truly, God is All-Hearing, All-Knowing.","O you who believe, do not raise your voices above the Prophet’s voice, and do not speak loudly to him as you speak loudly to one another, lest your deeds be rendered worthless while you are unaware.","Those who lower their voices in the presence of God’s Messenger — those are the ones whose hearts God has tested for righteousness. For them is forgiveness and a great reward.","Those who call out to you from behind the chambers — most of them have no sense.","Had they been patient until you came out to them, it would have been better for them. And God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","O you who believe, if a corrupt person brings you news, verify it, lest you harm a people out of ignorance and then become regretful over what you have done.","Know that God’s Messenger is among you. If he were to obey you in much of the matter, you would suffer. But God has endeared faith to you and made it beautiful in your hearts, and He has made hateful to you disbelief, wickedness, and disobedience. Those are the rightly guided.","A grace from God and a blessing. And God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.","If two groups of believers fight each other, make peace between them. But if one of them transgresses against the other, then fight the one that transgresses until it returns to God’s command. If it returns, then make peace between them with justice and be fair. Truly, God loves those who are fair.","The believers are but brothers, so make peace between your two brothers, and be mindful of God so that you may be shown mercy.","O you who believe, let no people ridicule other people — they may be better than them — and let no women ridicule other women — they may be better than them. Do not defame one another, and do not insult one another with nicknames. Wretched is the name of wickedness after faith. Whoever does not repent — those are the wrongdoers.","O you who believe, avoid much suspicion — truly, some suspicion is sin. Do not spy, and do not backbite one another. Would any of you love to eat the flesh of his dead brother? You would detest it. Be mindful of God. Surely God is Ever-Accepting of repentance, Most Merciful.","O humanity, We created you from a male and a female and made you into peoples and tribes so that you may know one another. Truly, the most noble of you before God is the most righteous of you. God is All-Knowing, All-Aware.","The Bedouins said, “We believe.” Say, “You have not believed, but say ‘We have submitted,’ for faith has not yet entered your hearts. If you obey God and His Messenger, He will not diminish anything of your deeds.” Surely God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","The believers are only those who believed in God and His Messenger, then never doubted, and strove with their wealth and their lives in God’s cause. Those are the truthful.","Say, “Are you informing God of your religion, when God knows what is in the heavens and what is in the earth?” God is All-Knowing of all things.","They consider it a favor to you that they have submitted. Say, “Do not consider your submission a favor to me. Rather, it is God who favors you by guiding you to faith, if you are truthful.”","God knows the unseen of the heavens and the earth. God is All-Seeing of what you do.","Qaf. By the glorious Quran.","But they marvel that a warner has come to them from among themselves, and the disbelievers say, “This is a strange thing.","When we have died and become dust? That is a far-fetched return!”","We know what the earth consumes of them, and with Us is a preserving record.","But they denied the truth when it came to them, so they are in a confused state.","Have they not looked at the sky above them — how We built it and adorned it, and it has no rifts?","And the earth — We spread it out and cast upon it firm mountains and grew in it every beautiful kind.","As insight and a reminder for every servant who turns back.","And We sent down blessed water from the sky, and with it We grew gardens and the grain of harvest.","And tall palm trees with clustered dates piled high.","As provision for the servants. And with it We gave life to a dead land. Such is the emergence.","Before them, the people of Noah denied, and the companions of the Well, and Thamud.","And Ad, and Pharaoh, and the brothers of Lot.","And the companions of the Thicket, and the people of Tubba. Each denied the messengers, so My threat was fulfilled.","Were We then wearied by the first creation? No, they are in confusion about a new creation.","Certainly We created man, and We know what his soul whispers to him. We are closer to him than his jugular vein.","When the two receivers receive, seated on the right and on the left.","He does not utter a word without a vigilant watcher ready beside him.","The stupor of death came with the truth. That is what you were trying to escape.","The Horn was blown. That is the Day of the Threat.","Every soul came with a driver and a witness.","“You were heedless of this, so We removed your cover, and your sight today is sharp.”","And his companion said, “This is what I have, ready.”","“Cast into Hell every stubborn disbeliever.","Withholder of good, transgressor, doubter.","Who set up another god beside God. Cast him into the severe punishment.”","His companion said, “Our Lord, I did not make him transgress, but he was in deep error.”","He said, “Do not dispute before Me. I had already sent you the warning.","The word is not changed before Me, and I am not unjust to My servants.”","On the Day We say to Hell, “Are you full?” and it says, “Is there more?”","And Paradise was brought near to the righteous, not far off.","“This is what you were promised — for every penitent, vigilant one.","Whoever feared the Most Merciful unseen and came with a heart turning back.","Enter it in peace. That is the Day of Eternity.”","They will have whatever they wish therein, and with Us is more.","How many a generation We destroyed before them, mightier than them in power! They searched through the lands — was there any escape?","Surely in that is a reminder for whoever has a heart or lends an ear while he is present.","We created the heavens and the earth and everything between them in six days, and no weariness touched Us.","So be patient with what they say, and glorify your Lord with praise before the rising of the sun and before its setting.","And in the night glorify Him, and after the prostrations.","And listen for the Day when the caller calls from a near place.","The Day they hear the blast in truth. That is the Day of Emergence.","It is We who give life and cause death, and to Us is the final return.","The Day the earth splits open away from them, swiftly. That is a gathering easy for Us.","We know best what they say, and you are not a tyrant over them. So remind with the Quran whoever fears My warning.","By the scattering winds, scattering.","Then the burden-bearers, bearing loads.","Then the gliders, gliding with ease.","Then the distributors of the matter.","Truly what you are promised is sure.","And the Judgment will certainly come to pass.","By the sky full of pathways.","You are in conflicting speech.","Turned away from it is whoever was turned away.","Destroyed be the speculators.","Those who are drowning in heedlessness.","They ask, “When is the Day of Judgment?”","The Day they are tormented over the Fire.","“Taste your torment. This is what you used to hasten.”","The reverent are in gardens and springs.","Receiving what their Lord has given them. They were, before that, doers of good.","Little of the night did they sleep.","And in the hours before dawn they would seek forgiveness.","And in their wealth was a rightful share for the beggar and the deprived.","And in the earth are signs for those of certainty.","And in yourselves. Do you not see?","And in the sky is your provision and what you are promised.","So by the Lord of the sky and the earth, it is as true as the fact that you speak.","Has the story of Abraham’s honored guests reached you?","When they entered upon him and said, “Peace.” He said, “Peace — unfamiliar people.”","Then he slipped away to his family and came back with a fattened calf.","He set it before them and said, “Will you not eat?”","Then he felt a fear of them. They said, “Do not be afraid,” and they gave him glad tidings of a knowledgeable son.","Then his wife came forward with a cry, struck her face, and said, “A barren old woman!”","They said, “So has your Lord spoken. He is the All-Wise, the All-Knowing.”","He said, “What is your mission, O messengers?”","They said, “We have been sent to a criminal people.","To rain upon them stones of clay.","Marked by your Lord for the transgressors.”","So We brought out whoever was in it of the believers.","But We found in it only one household of those who had submitted.","And We left in it a sign for those who fear the painful punishment.","And in Moses, when We sent him to Pharaoh with clear authority.","But he turned away with his might and said, “A sorcerer or a madman!”","So We seized him and his soldiers and cast them into the sea, and he was blameworthy.","And in Aad, when We sent against them the barren wind.","It left nothing it came upon without turning it to dust.","And in Thamud, when they were told, “Enjoy yourselves for a while.”","But they defied their Lord’s command, so the thunderbolt seized them while they looked on.","They could not stand, nor could they defend themselves.","And the people of Noah before them — truly they were a defiantly disobedient people.","And the sky — We built it with might, and We are surely expanding it.","And the earth — We spread it out, and how excellent a spreader We are.","And of everything We created two kinds, so that you might reflect.","So flee to God. I am a clear warner to you from Him.","And do not set up another god alongside God. I am a clear warner to you from Him.","Likewise, no messenger came to those before them without them saying, “A sorcerer or a madman!”","Did they pass this down to one another? No, they are a transgressing people.","So turn away from them, for you are not to blame.","But remind, for truly the reminder benefits the believers.","I did not create the jinn and humankind except to worship Me.","I do not want any provision from them, nor do I want them to feed Me.","Truly God — He is the All-Providing, the Possessor of Strength, the Unshakable.","So those who have wronged will have a share of punishment like the share of their companions, so let them not rush Me.","Woe to those who disbelieved, on that Day of theirs which they are promised!","By the Mount.","And a Book inscribed.","On parchment unrolled.","And the Frequented House.","And the raised canopy.","And the surging sea.","Your Lord’s punishment is sure to fall.","Nothing can avert it.","On the Day the sky churns violently.","And the mountains drift away.","So woe that Day to the deniers.","Who amuse themselves in idle talk.","The Day they are shoved into the Fire of Hell, shoved hard.","“This is the Fire you used to deny.","Is this sorcery, or do you not see?","Burn in it — be patient or impatient, it is all the same to you. You are only repaid for what you used to do.”","Truly, the reverent are in gardens and bliss.","Delighting in what their Lord has given them, and their Lord has shielded them from the punishment of the Blaze.","“Eat and drink with pleasure for what you used to do.”","Reclining on couches arranged in rows. And We paired them with wide-eyed maidens.","Those who believed, and whose descendants followed them in faith — We joined their descendants with them and did not diminish anything of their deeds. Every person is held in pledge for what he earned.","And We supplied them with fruit and meat, whatever they desire.","They pass among themselves a cup — no idle talk in it and no sin.","And circling among them are boys of their own, like hidden pearls.","They turned to one another, asking.","They said, “We used to live among our families in fear.","So God graced us and shielded us from the punishment of the scorching wind.","We used to call upon Him before. Truly, He is the Most Kind, the Most Merciful.”","So remind, for by your Lord’s grace you are no soothsayer and no madman.","Or do they say, “A poet — we await for him the calamity of time”?","Say, “Wait, for I too am waiting with you.”","Or do their minds command them to this, or are they a transgressing people?","Or do they say, “He fabricated it”? Rather, they do not believe.","Then let them produce a discourse like it, if they are truthful.","Or were they created from nothing, or are they the creators?","Or did they create the heavens and the earth? Rather, they have no certainty.","Or do they possess your Lord’s treasuries, or are they in control?","Or do they have a ladder on which they listen? Then let their listener bring a clear authority.","Or does He have daughters while you have sons?","Or do you ask them for a payment, so they are burdened with debt?","Or do they have the unseen, and they write it down?","Or do they intend a plot? It is the disbelievers who are the ones entrapped.","Or do they have a god other than God? Glory be to God, far above what they associate with Him.","If they saw a fragment falling from the sky, they would say, “Piled-up clouds.”","So leave them until they meet their Day in which they will be struck down.","A Day when their scheming will avail them nothing, and they will not be helped.","And for those who wronged, there is a punishment before that, but most of them do not know.","Be patient for your Lord’s judgment, for you are under Our watchful eyes. And glorify your Lord with praise when you rise.","And in the night glorify Him, and at the fading of the stars.","By the star when it descends.","Your companion has not strayed, nor has he erred.","He does not speak from desire.","It is nothing but revelation revealed.","One mighty in power taught him.","Possessing great strength — he rose to his true form.","And he was at the highest horizon.","Then he drew near and descended.","He was at a distance of two bow-lengths or closer.","And He revealed to His servant what He revealed.","The heart did not lie about what it saw.","Will you then dispute with him over what he sees?","He saw him at another descent.","At the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary.","Near it is the Garden of Refuge.","When there covered the Lote Tree what covered it.","The sight did not swerve, nor did it overreach.","He truly saw some of the greatest signs of his Lord.","Have you considered al-Lat and al-Uzza?","And Manat, the third, the other one?","Is the male for you and the female for Him?","That, then, would be an unjust division.","They are nothing but names you and your fathers have invented. God sent down no authority for them. They follow nothing but conjecture and what their souls desire, even though guidance has come to them from their Lord.","Or does man get whatever he wishes?","To God belongs the Hereafter and the first life.","How many an angel in the heavens whose intercession avails nothing, except after God gives permission to whom He wills and is pleased with.","Truly, those who do not believe in the Hereafter name the angels with female names.","They have no knowledge of it. They follow nothing but conjecture, and conjecture avails nothing against the truth.","So turn away from whoever turns his back on Our remembrance and desires nothing but the life of this world.","That is the extent of their knowledge. Your Lord knows best who has strayed from His path, and He knows best who is guided.","To God belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth, so that He may repay those who did evil for what they did, and repay those who did good with the finest reward.","Those who avoid the major sins and indecencies, except for minor lapses — your Lord is vast in forgiveness. He knew you best when He produced you from the earth and when you were embryos in your mothers’ wombs. So do not claim purity for yourselves. He knows best who is God-conscious.","Have you seen the one who turned away.","And gave a little, then held back?","Does he have knowledge of the unseen, so that he sees?","Or has he not been told of what is in the scriptures of Moses.","And Abraham, who fulfilled—","That no bearer of burdens bears the burden of another.","And that man has nothing except what he strives for.","And that his striving will be seen.","Then he will be repaid for it the fullest recompense.","And that to your Lord is the final end.","And that it is He who makes one laugh and makes one weep.","And that it is He who causes death and gives life.","And that He created the two mates, the male and the female.","From a drop when it is emitted.","And that upon Him falls the second creation.","And that it is He who enriches and grants possessions.","And that it is He who is the Lord of Sirius.","And that He destroyed the first Ad.","And Thamud — He spared none.","And the people of Noah before them; they were more unjust and more tyrannical.","And the overturned cities, He hurled down.","So there covered them what covered them.","So which of your Lord’s blessings do you dispute?","This is a warner among the warners of old.","The Imminent Hour draws near.","None besides God can unveil it.","Is it at this message that you marvel.","And you laugh and do not weep.","While you are heedlessly amusing yourselves?","So prostrate before God and worship.","The Hour has drawn near, and the moon has split.","Yet if they see a sign, they turn away and say, “Persistent sorcery.”","They denied and followed their desires, but every matter will settle.","Certainly there has come to them from the reports what contains deterrence.","Far-reaching wisdom — yet warnings avail nothing.","So turn away from them. The Day the caller calls to something dreadful.","Their eyes humbled, they will emerge from the graves like scattered locusts.","Racing toward the caller. The disbelievers will say, “This is a hard day.”","Before them the people of Noah denied — they denied Our servant and said, “A madman!” and he was rebuked.","So he called upon his Lord, “I am overpowered, so help me!”","So We opened the gates of the sky with torrential water.","And We caused the earth to burst with springs, and the waters met for a matter already decreed.","And We carried him on a vessel of planks and nails.","Sailing under Our watchful eyes — a recompense for him who had been rejected.","And We left it as a sign. So is there anyone who will remember?","So how were My punishment and My warnings?","And We have made the Quran easy for remembrance. So is there anyone who will remember?","Aad denied. So how were My punishment and My warnings?","We sent upon them a screaming wind on a day of unrelenting misfortune.","Tearing people away as if they were uprooted trunks of palm trees.","So how were My punishment and My warnings?","And We have made the Quran easy for remembrance. So is there anyone who will remember?","Thamud denied the warnings.","They said, “Are we to follow a single man from among us? We would then be in error and madness.","Was the reminder cast upon him alone out of all of us? No, he is an insolent liar.”","Tomorrow they will know who the insolent liar is.","We are sending the she-camel as a trial for them, so watch them and be patient.","And inform them that the water is to be shared between them — each drink attended in turn.","So they called their companion, and he took hold and hamstrung her.","So how were My punishment and My warnings?","We sent upon them a single blast, and they became like the dry stubble of a fence-builder.","Certainly We have made the Quran easy for remembrance — so is there anyone who will remember?","The people of Lot denied the warnings.","We sent upon them a storm of stones, except the family of Lot — We saved them at dawn.","As a grace from Us. Thus do We recompense whoever is grateful.","He had warned them of Our grip, but they disputed the warnings.","They demanded his guests from him, so We blinded their eyes: “Taste My punishment and My warnings!”","And by early morning, a lasting punishment settled upon them.","So taste My punishment and My warnings!","Certainly We have made the Quran easy for remembrance — so is there anyone who will remember?","The warnings came to Pharaoh’s people.","They denied all Our signs, so We seized them with the seizing of One Almighty, All-Powerful.","Are your disbelievers better than those, or do you have immunity in the scriptures?","Or do they say, “We are a united force, victorious”?","Their forces will be routed, and they will turn their backs in flight.","No, the Hour is their appointed time, and the Hour is more devastating and more bitter.","Truly the criminals are in error and blazing fire.","The Day they are dragged into the Fire on their faces: “Taste the touch of Hell!”","We created everything in precise measure.","Our command is but one — like the blink of an eye.","We have destroyed your kind before — so is there anyone who will remember?","Everything they did is in the records.","Every matter, small and great, is written down.","Surely the reverent are in gardens and rivers.","In a seat of truth, before a Sovereign, All-Powerful.","The Most Merciful.","He taught the Quran.","He created the human being.","He taught him clear expression.","The sun and the moon follow a precise reckoning.","The stars and the trees bow down.","The sky — He raised it and set the balance.","That you not transgress in the balance.","So establish weight with justice and do not short the balance.","The earth — He laid it down for all living creatures.","In it are fruits and palm trees with sheathed clusters.","And grain with husks and fragrant herbs.","So which of your Lord’s blessings will you two deny?","He created the human being from dried clay like pottery.","And He created the jinn from a smokeless flame of fire.","So which of your Lord’s blessings will you two deny?","Lord of the two easts and Lord of the two wests.","So which of your Lord’s blessings will you two deny?","He released the two seas, meeting one another.","Between them is a barrier they do not overrun.","So which of your Lord’s blessings will you two deny?","From them both emerge pearls and coral.","So which of your Lord’s blessings will you two deny?","And His are the ships, raised high in the sea like mountains.","So which of your Lord’s blessings will you two deny?","Everyone upon it will perish.","But the face of your Lord will remain — full of majesty and honor.","So which of your Lord’s blessings will you two deny?","Everyone in the heavens and the earth asks of Him. Every day He is in a matter.","So which of your Lord’s blessings will you two deny?","We will attend to you, O two weighty beings.","So which of your Lord’s blessings will you two deny?","O assembly of jinn and humans, if you can pass beyond the regions of the heavens and the earth, then pass. You will not pass except with authority.","So which of your Lord’s blessings will you two deny?","There will be sent upon you both a flame of fire and molten copper, and you will not be helped.","So which of your Lord’s blessings will you two deny?","When the sky splits open and turns crimson like oil.","So which of your Lord’s blessings will you two deny?","On that Day no human or jinn will be asked about his sin.","So which of your Lord’s blessings will you two deny?","The criminals will be recognized by their marks, and they will be seized by their forelocks and their feet.","So which of your Lord’s blessings will you two deny?","This is Hell, which the criminals denied.","They will circle between it and scalding water, seething hot.","So which of your Lord’s blessings will you two deny?","But for whoever feared standing before his Lord — two gardens.","So which of your Lord’s blessings will you two deny?","Both with spreading branches.","So which of your Lord’s blessings will you two deny?","In them both are two flowing springs.","So which of your Lord’s blessings will you two deny?","In them both are two kinds of every fruit.","So which of your Lord’s blessings will you two deny?","Reclining on couches lined with thick brocade, and the fruit of both gardens hanging near.","So which of your Lord’s blessings will you two deny?","In them are women of modest gaze, untouched before them by any human or jinn.","So which of your Lord’s blessings will you two deny?","As if they were rubies and coral.","So which of your Lord’s blessings will you two deny?","Is the reward of excellence anything but excellence?","So which of your Lord’s blessings will you two deny?","And besides those two, two other gardens.","So which of your Lord’s blessings will you two deny?","Dark green.","So which of your Lord’s blessings will you two deny?","In them both are two gushing springs.","So which of your Lord’s blessings will you two deny?","In them both are fruits, and palm trees, and pomegranates.","So which of your Lord’s blessings will you two deny?","In them are good and beautiful women.","So which of your Lord’s blessings will you two deny?","Fair ones, sheltered in pavilions.","So which of your Lord’s blessings will you two deny?","Untouched before them by any human or jinn.","So which of your Lord’s blessings will you two deny?","Reclining on green cushions and fine beautiful carpets.","So which of your Lord’s blessings will you two deny?","Blessed is the name of your Lord, full of majesty and honor.","When the Inevitable Event occurs.","None can deny its occurrence.","Bringing low, raising high.","When the earth is shaken violently.","And the mountains are crushed to pieces.","And become scattered dust.","And you are sorted into three groups.","The People of the Right—what are the People of the Right?","The People of the Left—what are the People of the Left?","And the forerunners, the forerunners.","Those are the ones brought near.","In Gardens of Bliss.","A multitude from the earlier generations.","And a few from the later ones.","On woven couches.","Reclining on them, facing one another.","Eternal youths circulate among them.","With cups, pitchers, and a goblet of flowing wine.","No headache from it, nor are they intoxicated.","And fruit of their choosing.","And bird meat of whatever they desire.","And fair women with large eyes.","Like hidden pearls.","As recompense for what they used to do.","They hear no idle talk therein, nor any sinful speech.","Only the saying, “Peace, peace.”","And the People of the Right—what are the People of the Right?","Among thornless lote trees.","And clustered acacias.","And extended shade.","And flowing water.","And abundant fruit.","Neither cut off nor forbidden.","And raised couches.","Truly We created them anew.","And made them virgins.","Loving, of equal age.","For the People of the Right.","A multitude from the earlier generations.","And a multitude from the later ones.","And the People of the Left—what are the People of the Left?","In scorching wind and scalding water.","And shade of black smoke.","Neither cool nor refreshing.","They had been, before that, living in luxury.","And they persisted in the great sin.","And they used to say, “When we have died and become dust and bones, will we really be resurrected?","And our ancient forefathers too?”","Say, “Surely the earlier and the later generations.","Will all be gathered for the appointment of a known Day.”","Then you, O misguided deniers.","Will eat from the tree of Zaqqum.","Filling your bellies with it.","Then drinking scalding water on top of it.","Drinking like thirst-crazed camels.","This is their welcome on the Day of Judgment.","We created you, so why do you not believe?","Have you considered what you ejaculate?","Is it you who create it, or are We the Creators?","We have decreed death among you, and We are not to be outrun.","From replacing you with your likes and producing you in what you do not know.","You already know the first creation, so why do you not remember?","Have you considered what you sow?","Is it you who make it grow, or are We the Growers?","If We willed, We could turn it into debris, and you would be left lamenting.","“Surely we are ruined!","No, we are deprived!”","Have you considered the water you drink?","Is it you who sent it down from the clouds, or are We the Senders?","If We willed, We could make it bitter, so why are you not grateful?","Have you considered the fire you kindle?","Is it you who produced its tree, or are We the Producers?","We made it a reminder and a provision for the travelers.","So glorify the name of your Lord, the Magnificent.","I swear by the positions of the stars.","And truly it is a mighty oath, if only you knew.","It is surely a noble Quran.","In a protected Book.","None touch it but the purified.","A revelation from the Lord of all worlds.","Is it this discourse you take lightly?","And you make your provision denial?","So why, when the soul reaches the throat.","And you are at that moment looking on.","And We are nearer to him than you, but you do not see.","So why, if you are not subject to judgment.","Do you not bring it back, if you are truthful?","As for him, if he is among those brought near.","Then comfort, fragrance, and a Garden of Bliss.","And if he is among the people of the right.","Then peace to you, from the people of the right.","But if he is among the deniers, the astray.","Then a welcome of scalding water.","And burning in Hellfire.","Truly this is the certain truth.","So glorify the name of your Lord, the Magnificent.","Everything in the heavens and the earth glorifies God, and He is the All-Mighty, the All-Wise.","To Him belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth. He gives life and causes death, and He has power over all things.","He is the First and the Last, the Manifest and the Hidden, and He has knowledge of all things.","It is He who created the heavens and the earth in six days, then rose over the Throne. He knows what penetrates the earth and what emerges from it, what descends from the sky and what ascends into it. He is with you wherever you are, and God sees all that you do.","To Him belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth, and to God all matters are returned.","He merges the night into the day and merges the day into the night, and He knows what lies within the hearts.","Believe in God and His Messenger, and spend from what He has made you successors over. Those among you who believe and spend will have a great reward.","Why would you not believe in God when the Messenger is calling you to believe in your Lord, and He has already taken your covenant — if you are believers?","It is He who sends down clear verses upon His servant to bring you out of darkness into light. Truly, God is Compassionate and Merciful to you.","Why would you not spend in God’s cause when to God belongs the inheritance of the heavens and the earth? Not equal among you are those who spent and fought before the conquest — they are greater in rank than those who spent and fought after it. Yet God has promised each of them the best reward, and God is All-Aware of what you do.","Who will lend God a good loan, that He may multiply it for him, and he will have a generous reward?","On the Day you see the believing men and believing women, their light streaming before them and on their right: “Your glad tidings today are gardens beneath which rivers flow, dwelling therein forever.” That is the supreme triumph.","On the Day the hypocrite men and hypocrite women say to those who believed, “Wait for us, let us borrow from your light.” They are told, “Go back behind you and seek a light.” Then a wall is set up between them with a gate — inside it is mercy, and outside it, facing them, is punishment.","They call out to them, “Were we not with you?” They say, “Yes, but you tempted yourselves, you waited and watched, you doubted, and wishful thinking deluded you until God’s command came, and the Deceiver deceived you about God.”","So today no ransom is accepted from you, nor from those who disbelieved. Your refuge is the Fire — it is your master. What a wretched destination!","Has the time not come for those who believe that their hearts should humble themselves at the remembrance of God and what has come down of the truth, and that they should not be like those who were given the Scripture before them? Time stretched long upon them, and their hearts hardened. Many of them are defiantly disobedient.","Know that God gives life to the earth after its death. We have made the signs clear to you, so that you may understand.","Truly, the men who give in charity and the women who give in charity, and who lend God a good loan — it will be multiplied for them, and theirs is a generous reward.","Those who believe in God and His messengers — they are the truthful ones. And the martyrs, before their Lord, will have their reward and their light. But those who disbelieve and deny Our signs — they are the companions of the Blaze.","Know that the life of this world is but play and amusement, adornment and mutual boasting among you, and competition in wealth and children. It is like a rain whose growth delights the tillers, then it withers and you see it turning yellow, then it becomes debris. In the Hereafter is severe punishment, and forgiveness from God and good pleasure. The life of this world is nothing but the enjoyment of delusion.","Race toward forgiveness from your Lord and a Garden whose width is like the width of the heaven and the earth, prepared for those who believe in God and His messengers. That is God’s grace — He grants it to whom He wills. God is the Possessor of immense grace.","No calamity strikes upon the earth or within yourselves except that it is in a record before We bring it into being. That is easy for God.","So that you may not grieve over what has passed you by, nor exult over what He has given you. God does not love anyone conceited and boastful.","Those who are stingy and command people to be stingy — whoever turns away, then surely God is the Self-Sufficient, the Praiseworthy.","Certainly We sent Our messengers with clear proofs and sent down with them the Scripture and the balance, so that people may uphold justice. And We sent down iron — in it is great might and benefits for people — and so that God may know who supports Him and His messengers unseen. Truly, God is All-Strong, All-Mighty.","And We sent Noah and Abraham and placed among their descendants prophethood and Scripture. Some of them were guided, but many of them were defiantly disobedient.","Then We followed in their footsteps with Our messengers, and We followed with Jesus son of Mary and gave him the Gospel. And We placed in the hearts of those who followed him compassion and mercy. But monasticism — they invented it; We did not prescribe it for them — only seeking God’s pleasure. Yet they did not observe it as it should have been observed. So We gave those among them who believed their reward, but many of them were defiantly disobedient.","O you who believe, be mindful of God and believe in His Messenger — He will give you a double share of His mercy, and He will make for you a light by which you walk, and He will forgive you. God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","So that the People of the Scripture may know that they have no power over anything of God’s grace, and that grace is in God’s hand — He gives it to whom He wills. God is the Possessor of immense grace.","God has heard the words of the woman who pleads with you concerning her husband and complains to God. God hears your exchange. Truly, God is All-Hearing, All-Seeing.","Those among you who declare their wives unlawful by comparing them to their mothers — they are not their mothers. Their mothers are only those who gave birth to them. They are surely uttering what is detestable in speech and false. Yet God is truly All-Pardoning, All-Forgiving.","Those who declare their wives unlawful by comparing them to their mothers, then retract what they said, must free a slave before the two of them touch one another. This is what you are admonished with. God is All-Aware of what you do.","Whoever cannot find one, then fasting two consecutive months before the two of them touch one another. Whoever is unable, then feeding sixty needy people. That is so you may believe in God and His Messenger. These are God’s limits. For the disbelievers there is a painful punishment.","Those who oppose God and His Messenger are humiliated just as those before them were humiliated. We have sent down clear verses. For the disbelievers there is a humiliating punishment.","On the Day God resurrects them all and informs them of what they did — God has kept count of it while they forgot it. God is a Witness over all things.","Do you not see that God knows what is in the heavens and what is in the earth? There is no secret conversation among three but He is their fourth, nor among five but He is their sixth, nor fewer than that nor more but He is with them wherever they are. Then He will inform them of what they did on the Day of Resurrection. Truly, God is All-Knowing of all things.","Do you not see those who were forbidden from secret conversation, then return to what they were forbidden from, conspiring in sin, aggression, and disobedience to the Messenger? When they come to you, they greet you with what God has never greeted you with, and say to themselves, “Why does God not punish us for what we say?” Hell is enough for them — they will burn in it. What a wretched destination!","O you who believe, when you converse privately, do not converse in sin, aggression, and disobedience of the Messenger, but converse in righteousness and God-consciousness, and be conscious of God, to whom you will be gathered.","Secret conversation is only from Satan, to grieve those who believe, yet it cannot harm them at all except by God’s permission. So let the believers place their trust in God.","O you who believe, when you are told to make room in gatherings, then make room — God will make room for you. And when you are told to rise, then rise. God will raise those among you who believe and those who have been given knowledge by degrees. God is All-Aware of what you do.","O you who believe, when you wish to speak privately with the Messenger, offer a charity before your private consultation. That is better for you and purer. But if you cannot find the means, then God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","Were you afraid to offer charities before your private consultation? Since you did not do so and God has turned to you in mercy, then establish the prayer, give the charity, and obey God and His Messenger. God is All-Aware of what you do.","Have you not seen those who allied themselves with a people God is wrathful toward? They are neither of you nor of them, and they swear to lies knowingly.","God has prepared for them a severe punishment. Truly, evil is what they used to do.","They took their oaths as a shield and turned others from God’s path, so for them is a humiliating punishment.","Neither their wealth nor their children will avail them anything against God. Those are the companions of the Fire — they will remain in it forever.","On the Day God resurrects them all, they will swear to Him just as they swear to you, thinking they stand on something. Surely, it is they who are the liars.","Satan has overtaken them and made them forget the remembrance of God. Those are Satan’s party. Truly, it is Satan’s party who are the losers.","Those who oppose God and His Messenger — those are among the most debased.","God has decreed, “I will surely prevail, I and My messengers.” Certainly, God is All-Powerful, All-Mighty.","You will not find a people who believe in God and the Last Day showing affection to those who oppose God and His Messenger, even if they are their fathers, their sons, their brothers, or their kin. Those — He has inscribed faith in their hearts and strengthened them with a spirit from Him. He will admit them into gardens beneath which rivers flow, dwelling in them forever. God is pleased with them and they are pleased with Him. Those are God’s party. Truly, it is God’s party who are the successful.","Whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth has glorified God. He is the All-Mighty, the All-Wise.","He is the One who expelled those who disbelieved among the People of the Book from their homes at the first gathering. You did not think they would leave, and they thought their fortresses would protect them from God. But God came at them from where they never expected, and He cast terror into their hearts. They demolished their houses with their own hands and the hands of the believers. So take heed, O people of insight.","Had God not decreed exile for them, He would have punished them in this world. And in the Hereafter they will have the punishment of the Fire.","That is because they opposed God and His Messenger. And whoever opposes God — truly God is severe in punishment.","Whatever palm trees you cut down or left standing on their roots, it was by God’s permission, and so that He might disgrace the defiantly disobedient.","Whatever God restored to His Messenger from them — you spurred neither horse nor camel for it, but God gives His messengers authority over whomever He wills. God is Capable of all things.","Whatever God restored to His Messenger from the people of the towns belongs to God, to the Messenger, to the relatives, the orphans, the needy, and the traveler — so that it does not circulate solely among the wealthy among you. Whatever the Messenger gives you, take it, and whatever he forbids you, refrain from it. And be mindful of God. Surely God is severe in punishment.","It is for the poor emigrants who were driven from their homes and their wealth, seeking bounty from God and His pleasure, and supporting God and His Messenger. Those are the truthful.","And those who settled in the homeland and in faith before them love those who emigrated to them and find no need in their hearts for what they were given, and they prefer others over themselves even if they themselves are in need. Whoever is shielded from the greed of his own soul — those are the successful.","And those who came after them say, “Our Lord, forgive us and our brothers who preceded us in faith, and place no resentment in our hearts toward those who believed. Our Lord, You are truly Most Compassionate, Most Merciful.”","Have you not seen those who practiced hypocrisy, saying to their brothers who disbelieved among the People of the Book, “If you are expelled, we will surely leave with you, and we will never obey anyone against you, and if you are fought, we will surely help you”? God bears witness that they are truly liars.","If they are expelled, they will not leave with them. If they are fought, they will not help them. And if they do help them, they will surely turn their backs, then they will not be helped.","You strike greater fear in their hearts than God. That is because they are a people who do not understand.","They will not fight you all together except in fortified towns or from behind walls. Their hostility among themselves is fierce. You think they are united, but their hearts are divided. That is because they are a people who do not reason.","Like those shortly before them — they tasted the dire consequence of their affair, and for them is a painful punishment.","Like Satan, when he said to man, “Disbelieve.” But when he disbelieved, he said, “I disown you. I fear God, Lord of all worlds.”","So the end for both of them was that they are in the Fire, dwelling in it forever. That is the recompense of the wrongdoers.","O you who believe, be mindful of God, and let every soul look to what it has sent ahead for tomorrow. Be mindful of God. Truly, God is All-Aware of what you do.","Do not be like those who forgot God, so He made them forget themselves. Those are the defiantly disobedient.","The people of the Fire and the people of Paradise are not equal. The people of Paradise — they are the triumphant.","Had We sent down this Quran upon a mountain, you would have seen it humbled, splitting apart from the fear of God. These are the parables We set for people, so that they may reflect.","He is God, there is no god but Him, Knower of the unseen and the seen. He is the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.","He is God, there is no god but Him, the King, the Holy, the Peace, the Granter of Security, the Guardian, the Almighty, the Compeller, the Supreme. Glory be to God, far above what they associate with Him.","He is God, the Creator, the Originator, the Shaper. To Him belong the most beautiful names. All that is in the heavens and the earth glorifies Him. He is the Almighty, the All-Wise.","O you who believe, do not take My enemy and your enemy as allies, extending affection to them when they have rejected the truth that has come to you. They drive out the Messenger and you because you believe in God, your Lord. If you have gone out striving in My cause and seeking My pleasure, you secretly show them affection — I know what you have concealed and what you have revealed. Whoever among you does this has strayed from the right path.","If they gain the upper hand over you, they will be your enemies and stretch out their hands and tongues against you with malice, and they wish you would disbelieve.","Your relatives and your children will never benefit you. On the Day of Resurrection He will separate you. And God is All-Seeing of what you do.","There was certainly a fine example for you in Abraham and those with him, when they said to their people, “We are free of you and of what you worship besides God. We reject you, and enmity and hatred have appeared between us and you forever, until you believe in God alone” — except for Abraham’s saying to his father, “I will surely ask forgiveness for you, though I have no power to protect you from God in any way.” “Our Lord, in You we place our trust, and to You we turn, and to You is the final return.","Our Lord, do not make us a trial for those who disbelieve, and forgive us, our Lord. You are the All-Mighty, the All-Wise.”","Certainly there was a fine example in them for you — for whoever hopes in God and the Last Day. And whoever turns away, then surely God is the Self-Sufficient, the Praiseworthy.","Perhaps God will place affection between you and those of them you have treated as enemies. God is All-Capable, and God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","God does not forbid you from being kind and just to those who have not fought you over religion and have not driven you from your homes. Truly, God loves those who are just.","God only forbids you from allying yourselves with those who have fought you over religion, driven you from your homes, and supported your expulsion. Whoever allies with them — those are the wrongdoers.","O you who believe, when believing women come to you as emigrants, test them. God knows best their faith. If you find them to be believers, do not return them to the disbelievers. They are not lawful for them, nor are they lawful for them. Give them what they spent. There is no blame on you in marrying them if you give them their bridal gifts. Do not hold on to the marriage ties of disbelieving women, and ask for what you spent, and let them ask for what they spent. That is God’s judgment; He judges between you. God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.","If any of your wives have gone over to the disbelievers and you then retaliate, give those whose wives have left the equivalent of what they spent. Be mindful of God, in whom you believe.","O Prophet, when believing women come to you pledging to you that they will not associate anything with God, nor steal, nor commit adultery, nor kill their children, nor bring a slander they have fabricated between their hands and their feet, nor disobey you in what is right, then accept their pledge and ask God to forgive them. Truly God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","O you who believe, do not ally yourselves with a people upon whom God’s wrath has fallen. They have despaired of the Hereafter just as the disbelievers have despaired of those in the graves.","Whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth has glorified God. He is the Almighty, the All-Wise.","O you who believe, why do you say what you do not do?","How hateful it is to God that you say what you do not do.","Truly, God loves those who fight in His cause in ranks, as though they were a solid structure.","And when Moses said to his people, “O my people, why do you hurt me when you know that I am God’s messenger to you?” So when they deviated, God caused their hearts to deviate. God does not guide the defiantly disobedient people.","And when Jesus son of Mary said, “O Children of Israel, I am God’s messenger to you, confirming what came before me of the Torah and bringing good news of a messenger to come after me whose name is Ahmad.” But when he came to them with clear proofs, they said, “This is obvious sorcery.”","Who is more unjust than one who fabricates lies against God while being invited to submission? God does not guide the unjust people.","They want to extinguish God’s light with their mouths, but God will perfect His light, even if the disbelievers despise it.","He is the One who sent His messenger with guidance and the religion of truth to make it prevail over all religions, even if the polytheists despise it.","O you who believe, shall I point you to a transaction that will save you from a painful punishment?","You believe in God and His messenger and strive in God’s cause with your wealth and your lives. That is better for you, if only you knew.","He will forgive your sins and admit you into gardens beneath which rivers flow, and pleasant dwellings in the Gardens of Eternity. That is the supreme triumph.","And another thing you love: help from God and a near victory. So give good news to the believers.","O you who believe, be God’s helpers, just as Jesus son of Mary said to the disciples, “Who are my helpers for God?” The disciples said, “We are God’s helpers.” So a group of the Children of Israel believed and a group disbelieved. Then We supported those who believed against their enemy, and they became dominant.","Everything in the heavens and everything on the earth glorifies God—the King, the Holy, the All-Mighty, the All-Wise.","It is He who raised among the unlettered a messenger from among them, reciting to them His verses, purifying them, and teaching them the Book and wisdom, though before they were clearly astray.","And others among them who have not yet joined them. He is the All-Mighty, the All-Wise.","That is God’s grace—He grants it to whom He wills. God is the Possessor of immense grace.","The example of those who were entrusted with the Torah then failed to carry it is like a donkey carrying volumes of books. Wretched is the example of the people who denied God’s verses. God does not guide the wrongdoing people.","Say, “O you who are Jewish, if you claim that you are God’s allies to the exclusion of all other people, then wish for death, if you are truthful.”","But they will never wish for it because of what their hands have sent ahead. God is All-Knowing of the wrongdoers.","Say, “Truly, the death you flee from will meet you. Then you will be returned to the Knower of the unseen and the seen, and He will inform you of what you used to do.”","O you who believe, when the call to prayer is made on the day of congregation, hasten to the remembrance of God and leave off trade. That is better for you, if you only knew.","When the prayer is concluded, disperse through the land and seek God’s grace, and remember God often, so that you may prosper.","Yet when they saw a transaction or amusement, they rushed toward it and left you standing. Say, “What is with God is better than amusement and trade. God is the Best of providers.”","When the hypocrites come to you, they say, “We bear witness that you are truly God’s Messenger.” God knows that you are His Messenger, but God bears witness that the hypocrites are surely liars.","They have taken their oaths as a shield and turned others from God’s path. Truly evil is what they used to do.","That is because they believed, then disbelieved, so their hearts were sealed and they do not comprehend.","When you see them, their bodies impress you, and when they speak, you listen to their words. They are like propped-up timbers. They think every shout is against them. They are the enemy, so beware of them. May God destroy them! How deluded they are!","When they are told, “Come, let God’s Messenger ask forgiveness for you,” they turn their heads aside, and you see them pulling away in arrogance.","It is the same for them whether you ask forgiveness for them or do not ask forgiveness for them — God will never forgive them. God does not guide the defiantly disobedient people.","They are the ones who say, “Do not spend on those with God’s Messenger until they disperse.” To God belong the treasuries of the heavens and the earth, but the hypocrites do not comprehend.","They say, “If we return to Medina, the mightier will surely drive out the lowlier.” Yet might belongs to God, to His Messenger, and to the believers, but the hypocrites do not know.","O you who believe, do not let your wealth or your children distract you from the remembrance of God. Whoever does that — those are the losers.","Spend from what We have provided you before death comes to one of you and he says, “My Lord, if only You would delay me for a short while so I could give in charity and be among the righteous.”","But God will never delay a soul when its time has come. God is All-Aware of what you do.","Everything in the heavens and everything on the earth glorifies God. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is Capable of all things.","It is He who created you, yet among you are disbelievers and among you are believers. And God is All-Seeing of what you do.","He created the heavens and the earth in truth and shaped you, perfecting your forms. And to Him is the return.","He knows what is in the heavens and the earth, and He knows what you conceal and what you reveal. And God is All-Knowing of what lies within the hearts.","Has the news not reached you of those who disbelieved before? They tasted the consequences of their affair, and for them is a painful punishment.","That was because their messengers came to them with clear proofs, but they said, “Are mere humans going to guide us?” So they disbelieved and turned away. And God had no need. God is Self-Sufficient, All-Praiseworthy.","Those who disbelieve claim they will never be raised. Say, “Yes, by my Lord, you will surely be raised, then you will surely be informed of what you did.” And that is easy for God.","So believe in God and His Messenger and the light that We have sent down. And God is All-Aware of what you do.","The Day He gathers you for the Day of Gathering — that is the Day of Mutual Loss. Whoever believes in God and does good, He will erase his misdeeds and admit him into gardens beneath which rivers flow, dwelling therein forever. That is the supreme triumph.","But those who disbelieved and denied Our signs — those are the companions of the Fire, dwelling therein forever. What a wretched destination!","No calamity strikes except by God’s permission. And whoever believes in God, He guides his heart. And God is All-Knowing of all things.","Obey God and obey the Messenger. But if you turn away, then Our Messenger’s only duty is clear delivery.","God — there is no god but He. And in God let the believers place their trust.","O you who believe, among your spouses and your children are enemies to you, so beware of them. But if you pardon, overlook, and forgive, then God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","Your wealth and your children are only a trial. And with God is a great reward.","So be mindful of God as much as you are able, and listen, obey, and spend — it is better for yourselves. Whoever is shielded from the greed of his own soul, those are the successful.","If you lend God a good loan, He will multiply it for you and forgive you. God is Most Appreciative, Most Forbearing.","Knower of the unseen and the seen, the All-Mighty, the All-Wise.","O Prophet, when you divorce women, divorce them at the start of their waiting period and keep count of the waiting period. And be mindful of God, your Lord. Do not expel them from their homes, nor should they leave, unless they commit a clear indecency. These are God’s limits. Whoever transgresses God’s limits has wronged himself. You never know—perhaps God will bring about something new after that.","When they reach the end of their term, either retain them honorably or part with them honorably. And have two just men among you witness, and uphold the testimony for God. That is what those who believe in God and the Last Day are advised. Whoever is mindful of God—He will make a way out for him.","And He will provide for him from where he never expected. Whoever puts his trust in God—He is enough for him. Truly, God carries out His command. God has set a measure for everything.","As for those of your women who have passed the age of menstruation—if you are in doubt—their waiting period is three months, and likewise for those who have not yet menstruated. And for those carrying children, their term is until they deliver. Whoever is mindful of God—He will make his affair easy for him.","That is God’s command, which He has sent down to you. Whoever is mindful of God—He will erase his misdeeds and magnify his reward.","House them where you live, according to your means, and do not harm them to make life difficult for them. If they are pregnant, spend on them until they deliver. Then if they nurse your child, give them their payment, and consult together honorably. But if you disagree, then another woman may nurse for him.","Let the wealthy man spend from his wealth, and let the one whose provision is restricted spend from what God has given him. God does not burden a soul beyond what He has given it. God will bring ease after hardship.","How many a town defied the command of its Lord and His messengers, so We held it to a severe account and punished it with a terrible punishment.","It tasted the consequence of its affair, and the outcome of its affair was ruin.","God has prepared for them a severe punishment. So be mindful of God, O people of understanding—you who have believed. God has sent down to you a reminder.","A messenger reciting to you God’s verses, made clear, to bring those who believe and do righteous deeds out of darkness into light. Whoever believes in God and does righteous deeds—He will admit him into gardens beneath which rivers flow, dwelling there forever. God has truly granted him an excellent provision.","It is God who created seven heavens and of the earth their like. His command descends through them, so that you may know that God has power over all things and that God has encompassed all things in knowledge.","O Prophet, why do you forbid what God has made lawful for you, seeking to please your wives? God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","God has ordained for you the dissolution of your oaths. God is your Protector, and He is the All-Knowing, the All-Wise.","When the Prophet confided something to one of his wives, and she disclosed it, and God made it known to him, he acknowledged part of it and overlooked part. Then when he told her about it, she said, “Who told you this?” He said, “The All-Knowing, the All-Aware told me.”","If you two repent to God, your hearts have truly deviated. But if you band together against him, then God is his Protector, and Gabriel, and the righteous among the believers — and the angels, beyond that, are his supporters.","Perhaps his Lord, if he divorces you, will give him in your place wives better than you — submitting, believing, devoutly obedient, repentant, worshipping, fasting — previously married and virgins.","O you who believe, protect yourselves and your families from a Fire whose fuel is people and stones, over which are angels, harsh and severe, who never disobey God in what He commands them and do what they are commanded.","O you who disbelieve, make no excuses today. You are only repaid for what you used to do.","O you who believe, repent to God with sincere repentance. Perhaps your Lord will remove your misdeeds from you and admit you into gardens beneath which rivers flow, on the Day when God will not disgrace the Prophet and those who believed with him. Their light will run before them and on their right. They will say, “Our Lord, perfect our light for us and forgive us. Truly, You are Capable of all things.”","O Prophet, strive against the disbelievers and the hypocrites and be harsh with them. Their refuge is Hell — what a wretched destination!","God sets an example for those who disbelieve: the wife of Noah and the wife of Lot. They were under two of Our righteous servants, yet they betrayed them, and the two availed them nothing against God. And it was said, “Enter the Fire with those who enter.”","And God sets an example for those who believe: the wife of Pharaoh, when she said, “My Lord, build for me a house near You in Paradise, and save me from Pharaoh and his deeds, and save me from the wrongdoing people.”","And Mary, daughter of Imran, who guarded her chastity, so We breathed into it of Our spirit. She believed in the words of her Lord and His scriptures, and she was among the devoutly obedient.","Blessed is He in whose hand is the dominion, and He is Capable of all things.","He who created death and life to test you—which of you is best in deed. He is the All-Mighty, the All-Forgiving.","He who created seven heavens in layers. You see no flaw in the Most Merciful’s creation. So look again—do you see any cracks?","Then look again, twice. Your sight will return to you humbled and exhausted.","We adorned the nearest heaven with lamps and made them missiles against the devils, and We have prepared for them the punishment of the Blaze.","For those who disbelieved in their Lord is the punishment of Hell—what a wretched destination!","When they are cast into it, they hear it shrieking as it boils over.","It nearly bursts with rage. Every time a group is cast into it, its keepers ask them, “Did a warner not come to you?”","They say, “Yes, a warner did come to us, but we denied and said, ‘God has not sent down anything. You are in nothing but great error.’”","They say, “Had we listened or reasoned, we would not be among the companions of the Blaze.”","So they confess their sin. Away with the companions of the Blaze!","Truly, those who fear their Lord in the unseen—for them is forgiveness and a great reward.","Whether you conceal your words or speak them aloud, He knows what is in the hearts.","Does He who created not know? He is the All-Subtle, the All-Aware.","It is He who made the earth tame for you, so walk its paths and eat of His provision. To Him is the resurrection.","Do you feel secure that the One who is in the heaven will not cause the earth to swallow you, and suddenly it churns?","Or do you feel secure that the One who is in the heaven will not send upon you a storm of stones? Then you will know how My warning was.","Those before them denied, and how was My condemnation!","Have they not looked at the birds above them, spreading their wings and folding them? None holds them up but the Most Merciful. Truly He is All-Seeing of everything.","Who is this that could be an army for you to help you besides the Most Merciful? The disbelievers are in nothing but delusion.","Who is this that could provide for you if He withheld His provision? Yet they persist in defiance and aversion.","Is one who walks fallen on his face better guided, or one who walks upright on a straight path?","Say, “He is the One who brought you into being and made for you hearing, sight, and hearts. How little you give thanks.”","Say, “He is the One who scattered you across the earth, and to Him you will be gathered.”","They say, “When will this promise come to pass, if you are truthful?”","Say, “The knowledge is only with God, and I am only a clear warner.”","When they see it drawing near, the faces of those who disbelieved will turn wretched, and they are told, “This is what you used to call for.”","Say, “Have you considered: whether God destroys me and those with me, or shows us mercy, who will shelter the disbelievers from a painful punishment?”","Say, “He is the Most Merciful; we believe in Him and in Him we place our trust. You will soon know who is in clear error.”","Say, “Have you considered: if your water were to sink into the ground, who could bring you flowing water?”","Nun. By the pen and what they inscribe.","You are not, by your Lord’s grace, a madman.","Truly, for you is a reward unending.","And you are certainly of a magnificent character.","So you will see, and they will see.","Which of you is the afflicted one.","Your Lord knows best who has strayed from His path, and He knows best the guided.","So do not obey the deniers.","They wish you would compromise, so they could compromise.","And do not obey every habitual swearer, contemptible.","Slanderer, going about with gossip.","Withholder of good, transgressor, sinful.","Brutal, and on top of all that, illegitimate.","Just because he has wealth and sons.","When Our verses are recited to him, he says, “Legends of the ancients!”","We will brand him on the snout.","We have tested them as We tested the owners of the garden, when they swore they would harvest it at dawn.","Making no exception.","So a calamity from your Lord swept over it while they slept.","And by morning it was as if stripped bare.","They called out to one another at dawn.","“Go early to your crop if you would harvest it.”","So they set off, whispering to one another.","“No poor person must enter it today against you.”","And they went early, determined and able.","But when they saw it, they said, “We are surely lost!","No—we are deprived!”","The most moderate among them said, “Did I not tell you, why do you not glorify God?”","They said, “Glory be to our Lord! We were truly wrongdoers.”","Then they turned on one another, blaming each other.","They said, “Woe to us! We were truly transgressors.","Perhaps our Lord will give us something better in its place. To our Lord we turn in hope.”","Such is the punishment. And the punishment of the Hereafter is far greater, if only they knew.","Surely for the reverent, with their Lord, are Gardens of Bliss.","Should We then treat those who submit like the criminals?","What is wrong with you? How do you judge?","Or do you have a scripture in which you study.","That you will have in it whatever you choose?","Or do you have oaths binding upon Us, lasting until the Day of Resurrection, that you will have whatever you decree?","Ask them which of them will vouch for that.","Or do they have partners? Then let them bring their partners, if they are truthful.","On the Day when the shin is bared and they are called to prostrate, but they will not be able.","Their eyes humbled, humiliation covering them. They used to be called to prostrate when they were sound.","So leave Me with whoever denies this message. We will lead them step by step from where they do not know.","And I will give them time. Surely My plan is firm.","Or do you ask them for a payment, so they are burdened with debt?","Or do they have the unseen, so they write it down?","So be patient for your Lord’s judgment, and do not be like the companion of the whale, when he called out in anguish.","Had a blessing from his Lord not reached him, he would have been cast onto the barren shore, disgraced.","But his Lord chose him and made him one of the righteous.","The disbelievers nearly strike you down with their glares when they hear the Reminder, and they say, “He is surely a madman.”","But it is nothing other than a reminder to all the worlds.","The Inevitable Reality.","What is the Inevitable Reality?","And what could make you know what the Inevitable Reality is?","Thamud and Ad denied the Striking Calamity.","As for Thamud, they were destroyed by the overwhelming blast.","And as for Ad, they were destroyed by a screaming, relentless wind.","He unleashed it upon them for seven nights and eight days without cease. You would have seen the people lying fallen like hollow trunks of palm trees.","Do you see any of them remaining?","Pharaoh came, and those before him, and the overturned cities, with sin.","They disobeyed their Lord’s messenger, so He seized them with a crushing grip.","When the waters surged, We carried you in the sailing vessel.","So that We might make it a reminder for you, and so that a retentive ear might retain it.","When the Horn is blown with a single blast.","And the earth and the mountains are lifted and crushed with a single crushing.","On that Day the Event will come to pass.","And the sky will split apart, for on that Day it will be frail.","And the angels will be at its edges, and eight will bear your Lord’s throne above them on that Day.","On that Day you will be exposed — no secret of yours will stay hidden.","As for the one given his record in his right hand, he will say, “Here, read my record!","I knew I would meet my reckoning.”","So he will be in a pleasing life.","In a lofty garden.","Its fruits hanging near.","“Eat and drink with pleasure for what you sent ahead in days gone by.”","But as for the one given his record in his left hand, he will say, “If only I had never been given my record!","And had never known my reckoning!","If only it had been the end!","My wealth has not helped me at all.","My authority has perished from me.”","“Seize him and shackle him.","Then burn him in the Blaze.","Then insert him in a chain seventy cubits long.”","He never believed in God, the Great.","And never urged the feeding of the destitute.","So today he has no close friend here.","And no food except filthy discharge.","None eat it but the sinners.","I swear by what you see.","And what you do not see.","It is truly the word of a noble messenger.","It is not the word of a poet — how little you believe!","Nor the word of a soothsayer — how little you reflect!","A revelation from the Lord of all worlds.","Had he fabricated any sayings against Us.","We would have seized him by the right hand.","Then We would have severed his life-vein.","And none of you could have shielded him.","It is surely a reminder for the reverent.","And We know that among you are deniers.","And it will surely be a source of anguish for the disbelievers.","And it is certainly the truth of certainty.","So glorify the name of your Lord, the Great.","A questioner asked about a punishment bound to fall.","Upon the disbelievers — none can repel it.","From God, Possessor of the Stairways of Ascent.","The angels and the Spirit ascend to Him in a Day whose span is fifty thousand years.","So be patient with a gracious patience.","They see it as distant.","But We see it as near.","The Day the sky will be like molten metal.","And the mountains will be like tufts of wool.","And no close friend will ask about a close friend.","They will be shown to each other. The criminal will wish he could ransom himself from that Day’s punishment with his children.","And his wife and his brother.","And his clan that sheltered him.","And everyone on earth — if only it would save him.","No! It is the Raging Blaze.","A stripper of scalps.","Calling whoever turned his back and walked away.","And gathered and hoarded.","Truly, man was created anxious.","When evil touches him, distressed.","And when good touches him, withholding.","Except those who pray.","Who are constant in their prayer.","And those in whose wealth is a recognized right.","For the beggar and the deprived.","And those who affirm the Day of Judgment.","And those who are fearful of their Lord’s punishment.","Surely their Lord’s punishment is not to be felt safe from.","And those who guard their chastity.","Except with their spouses or what their right hands possess, for then they are without blame.","But whoever seeks beyond that — those are the transgressors.","And those who are faithful to their trusts and their pledges.","And those who stand firm in their testimonies.","And those who safeguard their prayer.","Those will be honored in gardens.","So what is wrong with those who disbelieve, rushing toward you.","From the right and from the left, in clusters?","Does every one of them expect to be admitted into a Garden of Bliss?","No! We created them from what they know.","I swear by the Lord of the Easts and the Wests, We are certainly Able.","To replace them with better than them, and We cannot be outdone.","So leave them to wade in idle talk and play until they meet their Day which they are promised.","The Day they will emerge from the graves in haste, as though racing toward markers.","Their eyes humbled, humiliation covering them. That is the Day they were promised.","We sent Noah to his people: “Warn your people before a painful punishment comes upon them.”","He said, “O my people, I am a clear warner to you.","Worship God, be mindful of Him, and obey me.","He will forgive you some of your sins and grant you respite until an appointed time. Truly, God’s appointed time, when it comes, cannot be delayed — if only you knew.”","He said, “My Lord, I have called my people night and day.","But my calling only increased their flight.","And every time I called them so that You might forgive them, they thrust their fingers in their ears, wrapped themselves in their garments, persisted, and grew ever more arrogant.","Then I called them openly.","Then I proclaimed to them publicly and confided to them privately.","I said, ‘Seek your Lord’s forgiveness — He is ever Forgiving.","He will send the sky upon you in abundant rain.","And supply you with wealth and children, and make for you gardens, and make for you rivers.","What is wrong with you that you do not revere God’s majesty?","When He created you in stages?","Do you not see how God created seven heavens in layers?","And placed the moon among them as a light, and made the sun a lamp?","God grew you from the earth like a plant.","Then He will return you to it and bring you out again.","God made the earth a spread for you.","So that you may travel its wide paths.’”","Noah said, “My Lord, they have disobeyed me and followed those whose wealth and children only increased them in loss.","They schemed a tremendous scheme.","And said, ‘Do not abandon your gods! Do not abandon Wadd, nor Suwa, nor Yaghuth, nor Yauq, nor Nasr!’","They have led many astray. So increase the wrongdoers in nothing but misguidance.”","Because of their sins they were drowned, then cast into a Fire, and they found no helpers for themselves besides God.","Noah said, “My Lord, do not leave upon the earth a single one of the disbelievers.","If You leave them, they will lead Your servants astray and will beget none but wicked disbelievers.","My Lord, forgive me and my parents and whoever enters my house as a believer, and the believing men and believing women, and increase the wrongdoers in nothing but ruin.”","Say, “It has been revealed to me that a group of jinn listened and said, ‘We have heard a wondrous Quran.","It guides to right conduct, so we have believed in it, and we will never associate anyone with our Lord.","And exalted is the majesty of our Lord — He has taken neither a companion nor a child.","And the foolish among us used to speak outrageous lies about God.","And we had thought that humans and jinn would never speak a lie about God.","And there were men among humans who sought refuge with men among the jinn, so they increased them in burden.","And they assumed, as you assumed, that God would never raise anyone.","And we touched the sky and found it filled with fierce guards and flaming missiles.","And we used to sit in positions there to listen, but whoever listens now finds a flaming missile lying in wait for him.","And we do not know whether evil is intended for those on earth, or their Lord intends right guidance for them.","And among us are the righteous, and among us are those less than that — we have been of divided paths.","And we have realized that we can never escape God on earth, nor can we escape Him by fleeing.","And when we heard the guidance, we believed in it. Whoever believes in his Lord will fear neither loss nor oppression.","And among us are those who have submitted, and among us are the unjust. Whoever submits — those have sought right guidance.’”","As for the unjust, they will be firewood for Hell.","Had they stayed firm on the path, We would have given them abundant water to drink.","To test them through it. And whoever turns away from the remembrance of his Lord, He will drive him into an ever-mounting punishment.","The places of worship belong to God, so do not call upon anyone alongside God.","When God’s servant stood calling upon Him, they nearly swarmed over him in crowds.","Say, “I call upon my Lord alone and associate no one with Him.”","Say, “I have no power to bring you harm or right guidance.”","Say, “No one can protect me from God, and I will never find a refuge apart from Him.","Only delivery from God and His messages.” Whoever disobeys God and His Messenger — truly, for him is the fire of Hell, dwelling in it forever.","Until, when they see what they are promised, they will know who is weaker in helpers and fewer in number.","Say, “I do not know whether what you are promised is near, or whether my Lord will set a distant term for it.”","He is the Knower of the unseen, and He does not reveal His unseen to anyone.","Except a messenger He has chosen, for He places guards before him and behind him.","So that He may know that they have delivered their Lord’s messages. He has encompassed all that is with them and counted everything in number.","O you wrapped in garments.","Stand in prayer through the night, all but a little.","Half of it, or reduce from it a little.","Or add to it, and recite the Quran in measured recitation.","We will cast upon you a weighty word.","Truly the rising by night is firmer in tread and more upright in speech.","You have in the day prolonged occupation.","Remember the name of your Lord and devote yourself to Him completely.","Lord of the east and the west—there is no god but Him—so take Him as your Guardian.","Be patient over what they say, and part from them graciously.","Leave Me with the deniers, those of luxury, and give them a brief respite.","With Us are shackles and a blazing fire.","And food that chokes and a painful punishment.","On the Day the earth and the mountains quake, and the mountains become a heap of shifting sand.","We have sent to you a messenger as a witness over you, just as We sent to Pharaoh a messenger.","But Pharaoh disobeyed the messenger, so We seized him with a devastating grip.","How will you guard yourselves, if you disbelieve, against a Day that turns children gray-haired?","The sky will split apart by it. His promise is always fulfilled.","This is a reminder. So whoever wills, let him take a path to his Lord.","Your Lord knows that you stand nearly two-thirds of the night, or half of it, or a third of it, as does a group of those with you. God measures the night and the day. He knew that you would never keep exact count of it, so He turned to you in mercy. So recite what is easy for you of the Quran. He knew that some of you will be sick, and others traveling through the land seeking God’s bounty, and others fighting in God’s cause. So recite what is easy of it, and establish the prayer and give the charity and lend God a good loan. Whatever good you send ahead for yourselves, you will find it with God—better and greater in reward. And seek God’s forgiveness. Truly God is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","O you wrapped in your cloak.","Arise and warn.","And your Lord — magnify Him.","And your garments — purify them.","And defilement — shun it.","And do not give, expecting more in return.","And for your Lord, be patient.","When the trumpet is blown.","That Day will be a difficult day.","Not easy for the disbelievers.","Leave Me with the one I created alone.","I granted him vast wealth.","And sons present at his side.","And I smoothed everything for him.","Then he desires that I give him more.","No! He has been stubborn toward Our verses.","I will drive him up a grueling ascent.","He thought and he calculated.","May he be destroyed — how he calculated!","Then may he be destroyed — how he calculated!","Then he looked.","Then he frowned and scowled.","Then he turned away and grew arrogant.","And said, “This is nothing but sorcery handed down.","This is nothing but the word of a mortal.”","I will cast him into Saqar.","And what will make you know what Saqar is?","It spares nothing and leaves nothing.","It scorches the skin.","Over it are nineteen.","We have made none but angels as keepers of the Fire, and We have made their number only as a trial for those who disbelieve — so that those given the Scripture may be certain, and those who believe may grow in faith, and those given the Scripture and the believers may not doubt, and so that those in whose hearts is disease and the disbelievers may say, “What did God mean by this as a parable?” Thus God leads astray whoever He wills and guides whoever He wills. None knows the armies of your Lord but He. And it is nothing but a reminder for humankind.","No! By the moon.","And the night as it retreats.","And the morning as it shines.","Truly it is one of the greatest.","A warning to humankind.","For whoever among you wishes to advance or fall behind.","Every soul is held hostage by what it has earned.","Except the people of the right.","In gardens, they will ask one another.","About the criminals.","“What drove you into Saqar?”","They will say, “We were not among those who prayed.","And we did not feed the poor.","And we used to plunge into falsehood with those who plunged.","And we used to deny the Day of Recompense.","Until the certainty came to us.”","So no intercession of intercessors will benefit them.","What is wrong with them that they turn away from the reminder?","As if they were startled wild donkeys.","Fleeing from a lion?","Rather, each one of them wants to be given scriptures spread open.","No! Rather, they do not fear the Hereafter.","No! It is truly a reminder.","So whoever wills may heed it.","But they will not heed unless God wills. He is worthy of mindfulness and He is worthy of forgiveness.","I swear by the Day of Resurrection.","And I swear by the self-reproaching soul.","Does man think We will not reassemble his bones?","Yes — We are able to restore even his fingertips.","But man wants to go on sinning ahead of him.","He asks, “When is the Day of Resurrection?”","So when the sight is dazed.","And the moon is eclipsed.","And the sun and the moon are joined together.","Man will say on that Day, “Where is the escape?”","No! There is no refuge.","To your Lord on that Day is the final settlement.","Man is informed on that Day of what he sent ahead and left behind.","Rather, man is a witness against himself.","Even if he throws up his excuses.","Do not move your tongue with it to hasten it.","Upon Us is its collection and its recitation.","So when We recite it, follow its recitation.","Then upon Us is its explanation.","No! But you love the immediate.","And neglect the Hereafter.","Faces on that Day will be radiant.","Looking at their Lord.","And faces on that Day will be grim.","Expecting that a back-breaking calamity will be done to them.","No! When it reaches the collarbones.","And it is said, “Who is a healer?”","And he knows that it is the parting.","And leg is entwined with leg.","To your Lord on that Day is the driving.","He neither affirmed the truth nor prayed.","But he denied and turned away.","Then he went to his family, strutting.","Woe to you, and woe!","Then woe to you, and woe!","Does man think he will be left neglected?","Was he not a drop of emitted semen?","Then he became a clinging clot, and He created and proportioned.","And made from him the two mates — the male and the female.","Is not that One Capable of giving life to the dead?","Has there not come upon man a period of time when he was nothing worth mentioning?","We created man from a mixed drop, testing him, and We made him hearing, seeing.","We guided him to the path — whether grateful or ungrateful.","We have prepared for the disbelievers chains, shackles, and a blazing fire.","Truly the righteous will drink from a cup whose mixture is camphor.","A spring from which God’s servants drink, making it gush abundantly.","They fulfill their vows and fear a Day whose evil spreads far and wide.","And they feed the needy, the orphan, and the captive out of love for Him.","“We feed you only for God’s face. We want from you no recompense and no thanks.","We fear from our Lord a Day grim and overwhelming.”","So God shielded them from the evil of that Day and granted them radiance and joy.","And He repaid them for their patience with a Garden and silk.","Reclining there on couches, they see in it neither sun nor bitter cold.","Its shade hangs close over them, and its fruit clusters are made perfectly easy to reach.","They are served with vessels of silver and cups that are crystal.","Crystal of silver, measured to perfection.","And they are given to drink a cup whose mixture is ginger.","A spring there called Salsabil.","And circling among them are immortal youths — when you see them, you would think them scattered pearls.","And when you look around, you see bliss and a vast kingdom.","Upon them are garments of fine green silk and brocade, and they are adorned with bracelets of silver, and their Lord gives them a pure drink.","“This is your recompense, and your striving has been appreciated.”","It is We who sent down the Quran to you, a gradual revelation.","So be patient for your Lord’s judgment, and do not obey any sinner or ungrateful one among them.","And remember your Lord’s name morning and evening.","And in the night, prostrate to Him and glorify Him through a long night.","Truly these people love the fleeting life and leave behind them a heavy Day.","We created them and strengthened their form, and whenever We will, We can replace them with others like them.","This is a reminder — so whoever wills, let him take a path to his Lord.","But you do not will unless God wills. Truly God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.","He admits whom He wills into His mercy, and for the wrongdoers He has prepared a painful punishment.","By those sent in succession.","Then raging in tempest.","By those spreading wide.","Then separating decisively.","Then delivering a reminder.","As excuse or warning.","What you are promised will surely come to pass.","When the stars are blotted out.","And when the sky is split open.","And when the mountains are blown to dust.","And when the messengers are gathered at their appointed time.","For what Day were they appointed?","For the Day of Separation.","And what will make you know what the Day of Separation is?","Woe that Day to the deniers!","Did We not destroy the former peoples?","Then We follow them up with the later ones.","That is how We deal with the criminals.","Woe that Day to the deniers!","Did We not create you from a worthless fluid?","Then We placed it in a secure resting place.","Until a known term.","So We measured, and how excellent are We at measuring!","Woe that Day to the deniers!","Did We not make the earth a gathering place.","For the living and the dead?","And We set in it towering mountains and gave you sweet water to drink.","Woe that Day to the deniers!","“Proceed to what you used to deny!","Proceed to a shadow of three branches.","No shade, and no relief from the flame.”","It hurls sparks like a fortress.","As if they were tawny camels.","Woe that Day to the deniers!","This is a Day they will not speak.","Nor will they be permitted to make excuses.","Woe that Day to the deniers!","This is the Day of Separation. We have gathered you and the former peoples.","So if you have any scheme, then scheme against Me!","Woe that Day to the deniers!","Truly the righteous will be in shades and springs.","And fruits of whatever they desire.","“Eat and drink in pleasure for what you used to do.”","This is how We recompense the doers of good.","Woe that Day to the deniers!","“Eat and enjoy yourselves a little—you are criminals.”","Woe that Day to the deniers!","When they are told, “Bow down,” they do not bow.","Woe that Day to the deniers!","So in what message after this will they believe?","What are they asking one another about?","About the great news.","Over which they disagree.","No! They will come to know.","Then no! They will come to know.","Did We not make the earth a cradle?","And the mountains as stakes?","And We created you in pairs.","And We made your sleep a rest.","And We made the night a covering.","And We made the day a livelihood.","And We built above you seven mighty ones.","And We placed a blazing lamp.","And We sent down from the rain clouds pouring water.","To bring out with it grain and vegetation.","And dense gardens.","Truly the Day of Separation is an appointed time.","The Day the Horn is blown and you come in crowds.","And the sky is opened and becomes gateways.","And the mountains are set in motion and become a mirage.","Surely Hell lies in ambush.","A destination for the transgressors.","Remaining in it for ages.","They will taste in it no coolness and no drink.","Except scalding water and foul discharge.","A fitting recompense.","They never expected a reckoning.","And they utterly denied Our verses.","But everything We have recorded in a book.","So taste! We will never increase you in anything but torment.","Surely for the reverent is triumph.","Gardens and grapevines.","And full-breasted companions of equal age.","And a cup overflowing.","They will hear in it no idle talk and no lies.","A reward from your Lord, a generous gift.","Lord of the heavens and the earth and all between them, the Most Merciful—none possess the power to address Him.","The Day the Spirit and the angels stand in rows, none will speak except whom the Most Merciful permits, and who will say what is right.","That is the true Day. So whoever wills, let him take a path back to his Lord.","We have warned you of a near torment—the Day a man will see what his hands have sent ahead, and the disbeliever will say, “If only I were dust!”","By those who wrench violently.","By those who draw out swiftly.","By those who glide smoothly.","Then those who race ahead.","Then those who govern all affairs.","The Day the quaking quakes.","Followed by the subsequent one.","Hearts that Day will be pounding.","Their eyes cast down.","They say, “Will we really be returned to our former state?","Even when we are decayed bones?”","They say, “That, then, would be a losing return!”","It will be but a single shout.","And at once they are on the open plain.","Has the story of Moses reached you?","When his Lord called to him in the sacred valley of Tuwa.","“Go to Pharaoh—he has transgressed.","And say, ‘Would you purify yourself?","And I will guide you to your Lord so that you may fear Him.’”","So he showed him the greatest sign.","But he denied and disobeyed.","Then he turned away, striving.","And gathered and proclaimed.","And said, “I am your lord, the most high!”","So God seized him with the punishment of the Hereafter and the first life.","Surely in that is a lesson for whoever fears.","Are you harder to create or the sky? He built it.","He raised its canopy and perfected it.","He darkened its night and brought out its morning light.","And the earth after that He spread it out.","He brought out from it its water and its pasture.","And the mountains He anchored firmly.","A provision for you and your livestock.","But when the Great Catastrophe arrives.","The Day man remembers what he strove for.","And Hellfire is laid bare for all to see.","As for whoever transgressed.","And preferred the life of this world.","Then Hellfire will be the refuge.","But as for whoever feared standing before his Lord and restrained the soul from desire.","Then Paradise will be the refuge.","They ask you about the Hour: when will it arrive?","What do you have to do with mentioning it?","To your Lord is its final end.","You are only a warner for those who fear it.","The Day they see it, it will be as though they had lingered only an evening or its morning.","He frowned and turned away.","Because the blind man came to him.","And what would make you know? Perhaps he would purify himself.","Or remember, and the reminder would benefit him.","As for the one who considers himself self-sufficient.","To him you give your attention.","Though it is not upon you if he does not purify himself.","But as for the one who came to you striving.","And he fears.","From him you are distracted.","No! It is a reminder.","So whoever wills may remember it.","In honored scriptures.","Exalted, purified.","By the hands of scribes.","Noble, righteous.","Cursed is man — how ungrateful he is!","From what thing did He create him?","From a drop He created him, then proportioned him.","Then He eased the path for him.","Then He caused him to die and buried him.","Then when He wills, He will resurrect him.","No! He has not yet fulfilled what He commanded him.","Let man look at his food.","We poured water in abundance.","Then We split the earth open.","And We caused grain to grow in it.","And grapes and fresh herbage.","And olives and palm trees.","And dense gardens.","And fruit and pasture.","A provision for you and your livestock.","Then when the Deafening Blast comes.","The Day a man flees from his brother.","And his mother and his father.","And his wife and his children.","Every one of them that Day will have a matter to preoccupy him.","Faces that Day will be radiant.","Laughing, rejoicing.","And faces that Day will be covered with dust.","Shrouded in darkness.","Those are the disbelievers, the wicked.","When the sun is wrapped up.","When the stars fall down.","When the mountains are set moving.","When the pregnant camels are abandoned.","When the wild beasts are gathered.","When the seas are set ablaze.","When the souls are paired.","When the buried infant girl is asked.","For what sin she was killed.","When the scrolls are spread open.","When the sky is stripped away.","When the Hellfire is set ablaze.","When the Garden is brought near.","Every soul will know what it has brought.","I swear by the retreating stars.","The ones that move and disappear.","By the night as it departs.","By the dawn as it breathes.","Truly it is the word of a noble messenger.","Possessed of strength, secure in rank with the Lord of the Throne.","Obeyed there, and trustworthy.","Your companion is not mad.","He certainly saw him on the clear horizon.","He is not withholding of the unseen.","It is not the word of an accursed devil.","So where are you going?","It is nothing but a reminder to all the worlds.","For whoever among you wills to walk straight.","But you cannot will unless God wills—Lord of all the worlds.","When the sky is split open.","When the stars are scattered.","When the seas are burst open.","When the graves are overturned.","Every soul will know what it sent ahead and what it left behind.","O human, what has deluded you about your Generous Lord?","He who created you, proportioned you, and balanced you.","In whatever form He willed, He assembled you.","No! Rather, you deny the Judgment.","Yet over you are guardians.","Noble, recording.","They know whatever you do.","Truly the righteous will be in bliss.","And the wicked will be in a Blaze.","Burning in it on the Day of Judgment.","They will never be absent from it.","And what will make you realize what the Day of Judgment is?","Then again, what will make you realize what the Day of Judgment is?","A Day when no soul will avail another soul in anything, and the command that Day belongs to God.","Woe to those who give short measure.","Who, when they take a measure from people, take it in full.","But when they measure for them or weigh for them, give less.","Do those not think that they will be raised.","For a tremendous Day.","The Day mankind will stand before the Lord of all worlds?","No! Truly the record of the wicked is in Sijjin.","And what will make you know what Sijjin is?","A written record.","Woe on that Day to the deniers.","Who deny the Day of Judgment.","None denies it but every sinful transgressor.","When Our verses are recited to him, he says, “Tales of the ancients!”","No! Rather, what they used to earn has rusted over their hearts.","No! Surely they will be veiled from their Lord on that Day.","Then they will burn in the Blazing Fire.","Then they are told, “This is what you used to deny.”","No! Truly the record of the righteous is in Illiyyun.","And what will make you know what Illiyyun is?","A written record.","The ones brought near witness it.","Surely the righteous are in bliss.","On couches, gazing.","You recognize in their faces the radiance of bliss.","They are given to drink from a sealed, pure wine.","Its seal is musk. So let the competitors compete for this.","Its mixture is from Tasnim.","A spring from which the ones brought near drink.","Those who committed crimes used to laugh at those who believed.","When they passed by them, they would wink at one another.","When they returned to their own people, they returned amused.","When they saw them, they said, “These are surely astray.”","Yet they were not sent as guardians over them.","So Today, those who believed laugh at the disbelievers.","On couches, gazing.","Have the disbelievers been repaid for what they used to do?","When the sky splits open.","And heeds its Lord — as it must.","And when the earth is stretched flat.","And casts out what is within it and empties itself.","And heeds its Lord — as it must.","O human being, you are toiling toward your Lord, a hard toiling, and you will meet Him.","As for whoever is given his record in his right hand.","He will be given an easy reckoning.","And will return to his people joyful.","But as for whoever is given his record behind his back.","He will cry out for destruction.","And burn in a blaze.","He used to be joyful among his people.","He thought he would never return.","But yes! His Lord was ever Seeing him.","So I swear by the twilight glow.","And the night and what it gathers.","And the moon when it grows full.","You will surely pass from stage to stage.","So what is wrong with them that they do not believe?","And when the Quran is recited to them, they do not prostrate?","Rather, those who disbelieve deny.","And God knows best what they harbor.","So give them tidings of a painful punishment.","Except those who believe and do righteous deeds — for them is a reward unending.","By the sky with its great constellations.","By the promised Day.","By a witness and what is witnessed.","Destroyed were the makers of the trench.","The fire full of fuel.","When they sat beside it.","And they were witnesses to what they did to the believers.","They resented them only because they believed in God, the Almighty, the Praiseworthy.","To whom belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth. And God is Witness over all things.","Truly, those who persecuted the believing men and believing women, then never repented—for them is the punishment of Hell, and for them is the punishment of burning.","Surely, those who believed and did righteous deeds—for them are gardens beneath which rivers flow. That is the great triumph.","Certainly, your Lord’s grip is severe.","It is He who originates and restores.","And He is the All-Forgiving, the All-Loving.","Lord of the Throne, the All-Glorious.","Doer of whatever He wills.","Has the story of the legions reached you?","Pharaoh and Thamud?","Yet those who disbelieve persist in denial.","And God encompasses them from behind.","Rather, it is a glorious Quran.","In a preserved tablet.","By the sky and the night-comer.","And what will make you realize what the night-comer is?","The piercing star.","Every soul has a guardian over it.","So let man consider what he was created from.","He was created from a gushing fluid.","Emerging from between the backbone and the ribs.","Surely He is Able to bring him back.","On the Day when secrets are laid bare.","Then he will have no strength and no helper.","By the sky with its recurring rain.","And the earth that splits open.","It is truly a decisive word.","And it is no jest.","They are plotting a plot.","And I am plotting a plot.","So give the disbelievers respite — let them be, for a little while.","Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High.","He who created and proportioned.","He who determined and guided.","He who brought out the pasture.","Then turned it to dark debris.","We will make you recite, and you will not forget.","Except what God wills. He knows what is declared and what is hidden.","We will ease you to the easiest way.","So remind, if the reminder benefits.","Whoever fears will be reminded.","But the most wretched will avoid it.","He who will burn in the greatest Fire.","Then neither dying in it nor living.","Truly successful is he who purifies himself.","And remembers the name of his Lord and prays.","Yet you prefer the life of this world.","While the Hereafter is better and more lasting.","This is surely in the earliest scriptures.","The scriptures of Abraham and Moses.","Has the news of the Overwhelming reached you?","Faces that Day will be humbled.","Laboring, exhausted.","Burning in a scorching Fire.","Given to drink from a boiling spring.","They will have no food except thorny shrubs.","That neither nourishes nor satisfies hunger.","Faces that Day will be radiant.","Pleased with their striving.","In a lofty Garden.","Where they hear no idle talk.","In it is a flowing spring.","In it are raised couches.","And goblets set ready.","And cushions lined in rows.","And carpets spread about.","Do they not look at the camels — how they were created?","And at the sky — how it was raised?","And at the mountains — how they were set firm?","And at the earth — how it was spread out?","So remind — you are only a reminder.","You have no authority over them.","But whoever turns away and disbelieves.","God will punish him with the greatest punishment.","Truly, to Us is their return.","Then truly, upon Us is their reckoning.","By the dawn.","By the ten nights.","By the even and the odd.","By the night as it passes.","Is there in that an oath for one of reason?","Have you not seen how your Lord dealt with Ad?","Iram of the pillars.","The like of whom were never created in the land?","And Thamud, who carved the rocks in the valley?","And Pharaoh of the stakes?","Those who tyrannized throughout the land.","And spread much corruption in it.","So your Lord poured upon them a scourge of punishment.","Truly your Lord is ever on the watch.","As for man, when his Lord tests him and honors him and blesses him, he says, “My Lord has honored me.”","But when He tests him and restricts his provision, he says, “My Lord has humiliated me.”","No! Rather, you do not honor the orphan.","And you do not urge one another to feed the poor.","And you devour inheritance with greedy consumption.","And you love wealth with an excessive love.","No! When the earth is crushed, pounding upon pounding.","And your Lord comes, and the angels, rank upon rank.","And Hell is brought near that Day—that Day man will remember, but how will remembrance help him?","He will say, “If only I had sent ahead for my life!”","On that Day, none will punish as His punishment.","And none will bind as He binds.","O tranquil soul.","Return to your Lord, pleased and pleasing.","So enter among My servants.","And enter My Garden.","I swear by this city.","And you are free in this city.","And by a father and what he fathered.","Certainly We created man in hardship.","Does he think no one has power over him?","He says, “I have squandered vast wealth.”","Does he think no one sees him?","Did We not give him two eyes?","And a tongue and two lips.","And guided him to the two paths?","Yet he has not attempted the steep pass.","And what will make you know what the steep pass is?","It is the freeing of a slave.","Or feeding on a day of hunger.","An orphan of close kin.","Or a destitute person in the dust.","Then being among those who believed and urged one another to patience and urged one another to compassion.","Those are the people of the right.","But those who rejected Our signs—they are the people of the left.","Over them is a Fire, sealed shut.","By the sun and its morning brightness.","By the moon as it follows it.","By the day as it reveals it.","By the night as it covers it.","By the sky and He who built it.","By the earth and He who spread it.","By the soul and He who fashioned it.","Then inspired it with its wickedness and its righteousness.","Truly he succeeds who purifies it.","And truly he fails who corrupts it.","Thamud denied in their transgression.","When the most wretched of them rose up.","God’s messenger said to them, “This is God’s she-camel, so let her drink.”","But they denied him and hamstrung her, so their Lord crushed them for their sin and leveled it.","And He fears no consequence of it.","By the night as it covers.","By the day as it shines.","By Him who created the male and the female.","Surely your strivings are diverse.","As for he who gave and was mindful.","And affirmed the ultimate good.","We will ease him toward ease.","As for he who was stingy and thought himself self-sufficient.","And denied the ultimate good.","We will ease him toward hardship.","His wealth will not avail him when he plummets.","Truly, upon Us is the guidance.","To Us belongs the Hereafter and the first life.","So I have warned you of a Fire that blazes.","None will burn in it but the most wretched.","Who denied and turned away.","The most righteous will be kept far from it.","Who gives his wealth to purify himself.","Not owing anyone a favor to be repaid.","But seeking only the face of his Lord, the Most High.","He will surely be satisfied.","By the morning light.","And the night when it grows still.","Your Lord has not abandoned you, nor has He hated you.","Surely the Hereafter is better for you than the present.","And your Lord will give you, and you will be satisfied.","Did He not find you an orphan and give you shelter?","And He found you lost and guided you.","And He found you in need and made you self-sufficient.","So as for the orphan, do not oppress him.","And as for the one who asks, do not rebuke him.","And as for your Lord’s blessing, proclaim it.","Did We not open your chest for you?","And lifted from you your burden.","Which broke your back.","And raised high your mention?","So truly, with hardship comes ease.","Truly, with hardship comes ease.","So when you are done, toil on.","And to your Lord turn your longing.","By the fig and the olive.","And by Mount Sinai.","And by this secure city.","We created man in the finest form.","Then We reduced him to the lowest of the low.","Except those who believe and do good deeds—for them is a reward unending.","So what after this could make you deny the Judgment?","Is God not the most just of judges?","Read in the name of your Lord who created.","Created man from a clinging clot.","Read, and your Lord is the Most Generous.","He who taught by the pen.","Taught man what he did not know.","No! Truly man transgresses.","When he sees himself self-sufficient.","Surely to your Lord is the return.","Have you seen the one who forbids.","A servant when he prays?","Have you seen if he was upon guidance.","Or commanded God-consciousness?","Have you seen if he denied and turned away?","Does he not know that God sees?","No! If he does not stop, We will drag him by the forelock.","A lying, sinful forelock.","So let him call his associates.","We will call the angels of Hell.","No! Do not obey him. Prostrate and draw near.","Truly, We sent it down on the Night of Decree.","What will make you know what the Night of Decree is?","The Night of Decree is better than a thousand months.","The angels and the Spirit descend in it, by their Lord’s permission, with every command.","It is peace until the rising of dawn.","Those who disbelieved among the People of the Book and the polytheists were not going to desist until the clear proof came to them.","A messenger from God, reciting purified scrolls.","In them are upright scriptures.","Those who were given the Book did not divide except after the clear proof had come to them.","They were commanded only to worship God, devoting the religion sincerely to Him, as monotheists, and to establish prayer and give charity. That is the upright religion.","Truly, those who disbelieved among the People of the Book and the polytheists are in the fire of Hell, abiding there forever. Those are the worst of creation.","Truly, those who believed and did righteous deeds — those are the best of creation.","Their reward with their Lord is Gardens of Eternity beneath which rivers flow, abiding there forever. God is pleased with them and they are pleased with Him. That is for whoever feared his Lord.","When the earth is shaken with its ultimate quaking.","And the earth brings out its burdens.","And man says, “What is wrong with it?”","That Day it will report its news.","Because your Lord inspired it.","That Day people will emerge in scattered groups to be shown their deeds.","So whoever does an atom’s weight of good will see it.","And whoever does an atom’s weight of evil will see it.","By the charging horses, panting.","Striking sparks with their hooves.","Raiding at dawn.","Raising clouds of dust.","Plunging into the midst of the foe.","Truly, man is ungrateful to his Lord.","He himself is a witness to that.","And in his love of wealth, he is fierce.","Does he not know that when what is in the graves is overturned.","And what is in the hearts is laid bare.","Surely their Lord, that Day, is fully Aware of them?","The Striking Calamity.","What is the Striking Calamity?","And what will make you know what the Striking Calamity is?","A Day when people will be like scattered moths.","And the mountains will be like carded wool.","As for the one whose scales are heavy.","He will be in a pleasing life.","But as for the one whose scales are light.","His mother is the Abyss.","And what will make you know what it is?","A scorching Fire.","Rivalry in amassing distracted you.","Until you visited the graves.","No! You will come to know.","Then no! You will come to know.","No! If only you knew with the knowledge of certainty.","You will surely see the Blazing Fire.","Then you will surely see it with the eye of certainty.","Then on that Day you will surely be questioned about every pleasure.","By time.","Truly, mankind is in loss.","Except those who believe, do righteous deeds, urge one another to truth, and urge one another to patience.","Woe to every backbiter, slanderer.","Who amassed wealth and counted it.","Thinking his wealth will make him immortal.","No! He will be hurled into the Crusher.","And what will make you know what the Crusher is?","God’s kindled Fire.","Which leaps up to the hearts.","It will be sealed over them.","In towering columns.","Have you not seen how your Lord dealt with the People of the Elephant?","Did He not render their scheme utterly futile?","He sent against them birds in flocks.","Pelting them with stones of baked clay.","And made them like devoured husks.","For the solidarity of Quraysh.","Their solidarity in the winter and summer journeys.","Let them worship the Lord of this House.","Who fed them against hunger and secured them against fear.","Have you seen the one who denies the Judgment?","That is the one who shoves the orphan aside.","And does not urge the feeding of the poor.","So woe to those who pray.","Those who are heedless of their prayer.","Those who show off.","And withhold small kindnesses.","Truly, We have given you abundance.","So pray to your Lord and sacrifice.","Surely it is the one who hates you who is cut off.","Say, “O disbelievers.","I do not worship what you worship.","Nor do you worship what I worship.","Nor will I worship what you have worshipped.","Nor will you worship what I worship.","To you your religion, and to me mine.”","When God’s help comes and the victory.","And you see people entering God’s religion in crowds.","Then glorify your Lord with praise and seek His forgiveness. Truly He is ever accepting of repentance.","May the hands of Abu Lahab perish, and may he perish!","His wealth did not avail him, nor what he earned.","He will burn in a fire of blazing flame.","And his wife, the carrier of firewood.","Around her neck is a rope of twisted fiber.","Say, “He is God, the One.","God, the Eternal Refuge.","He never begot, nor was He begotten.","And no one is comparable to Him.”","Say, “I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak.","From the evil of what He created.","From the evil of darkness when it settles.","From the evil of those who blow on knots.","From the evil of an envier when he envies.”","Say, “I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind.","The King of mankind.","The God of mankind.","From the evil of the retreating whisperer.","Who whispers into the hearts of people.","From among the jinn and mankind.”"]);
